not sure I have the notes anymore, but I'll try and remember any interesting details. Mostly, it was an attempt at &quot;this Ability can be clearly used for a Lunar-y thing; can we make a new Charm out of it?&quot;<br /> <br /> The reason we ended up in the Attribute situation in the first place was that all of the players had initially said they wanted to play Solars, but one of them later flipped through the art book and decided Lunars were too cool for school. So I attempted to build a stealth-and-gnawing Lunar template based on the rules I'd already done for Solars.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;failure,&quot; I might be being too harsh. We actually had very few mechanical problems, it just always felt like the Solar Charms (which ran closer to the canonical ones) flowed more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 11-02-2013, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:06:23-07:00","id":1141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=1111#post1111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I have come here to fuck horses and chew bubblegum, and Creation never invented bubblegum.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to ask if you knew Loki but then...he got fucked rather than the other way round <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:59:11-07:00","id":1168,"title":"","content":"My second-ever Exalted character was a Lunar. Only all we had back then was the core book and Storyteller's Guide. It was pretty sweet! I had all these recolored Solar charms with the few limitations placed on Lunars by the existing canon (Celestial circle sorcery maximum, dice-adder cap limited to attributes) and a pretty radical batch of physical bonuses for the warform (as per then-unnamed Magnificent Jaguar's [I think!] stat block).<br /> <br /> Then I chose to play a No Moon, which was <i>less</i> supported by the then total lack of Lunar support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":17,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","user":"Metrophelean","date":". 11-02-2013, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:23:43-07:00","id":1209,"title":"","content":"I have been compelled to use Lunars in a game on my own volition only once in my threeish? years of running Exalted. It was in a Modern Sidereals game where the Lunar in question was the mate of the party's Infernal handler. I had originally planned to use him as the go-between but he really only got screen time as just some guy, and also as a house cat on the order of his mate.<br /> <br /> Alas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:25:38-07:00","id":1210,"title":"","content":"Lunars are awesome, once we can figure out what they actually are/do. I'm willing to take that on faith.<br /> <br /> What isn't awesome, is Lunar Bond/Bond/Past Life Attachment. It's worse than Samsara combined with the Reclamation combined with Scion 1E's mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:38:46-07:00","id":1308,"title":"","content":"so i've never actually gotten to play exalted before but if i ever get the chance i plan on running a lunar, probably full moon caste. i'll assume (hope) that they wouldn't be a bad splat to be playing as as an introduction to exalted, yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2649","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/403-mabufufu","name":"mabufufu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar403_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:25:28-07:00","id":1398,"title":"","content":"I hope to get a 3Ex game up and running in the new year and hopefully some time after that I'll be able to play as a character while someone else runs the game. That way I can play as the Full Moon Lunar who has been haunting my brain for the last four months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T19:01:09-07:00","id":1437,"title":"","content":"As an old school Werewolf player I'll always have a soft spot for Lunars. I really hope they can be done well while still retaining ties to their inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T20:00:15-07:00","id":1463,"title":"","content":"My wife loves Lunars, so I'm hoping we get some solid news about them and their awesome new dynamic soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T20:42:50-07:00","id":1483,"title":"","content":"I made a couple of Lunars.<br /> They were fun. But I suspect they will be more fun in 3e.<br /> Because people tell me things. And I hope they aren't lying to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T01:40:55-07:00","id":1599,"title":"","content":"I played precisely one Lunar, and unfortunately the game didn't last six pages on a forum, IIRC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T11:57:50-08:00","id":1921,"title":"","content":"Was reading a book by one of my favorite Zen authors and came across a few quote-worthy lines that immediately made me think of the Lunars:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you identify rigidly with certain aspects of yourself you're actively suppressing those aspects that don't fit that identity. </div> </div> </div>I could see an elder teaching this to a new Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Daigan told me, &quot;People in some forms of Buddhism say you have to get rid of your identity. But for me, I spent a lot of time getting molested over my identity. What do you mean get rid of it? This is what we got. But later on I saw that it's not the identity we get rid of. We change our relationship to it. We try not reify it or lock it into some place. It's seeing identity as empty. It's just there. It doesn't have any intrinsic value. it's not good, and it's not bad.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Ignoring that this is specifically related to Buddhism, the part about changing your relationship with your identity strikes me as being very much a Lunar ideal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defining oneself as straight, gay, bisexual, kinky or whatever designation you prefer is one way for the ego to try and delineate itself. Such a definition may be provisionally true and may have some use. But ultimately it's not who you are. Buddhist practice is about trying to uncover something fare more fundamental. </div> </div> </div>Ignoring that this is specifically related to sexuality, the idea of using self-identifiers as the way the ego tries to delineate itself, and how while that may be the way you provisionally perceive yourself in a given context, it's not who you really are you. You are not your identity; you have an identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T12:24:54-08:00","id":1961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=1921#post1921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was reading a book by one of my favorite Zen authors and came across a few quote-worthy lines that immediately made me think of the Lunars:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I could see an elder teaching this to a new Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ignoring that this is specifically related to Buddhism, the part about changing your relationship with your identity strikes me as being very much a Lunar ideal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ignoring that this is specifically related to sexuality, the idea of using self-identifiers as the way the ego tries to delineate itself, and how while that may be the way you provisionally perceive yourself in a given context, it's not who you really are you. You are not your identity; you have an identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, and I can totally see it fitting into Lunars, mostly at least.<br /> <br /> I wonder though, how much of that would apply to Lunars as opposed to, say, the chosen of Masks. That's not to say that there isn't possibility for overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T14:15:48-08:00","id":2029,"title":"","content":"Well, the Chosen of Masks is inasmuch as we can tell a single Exigent. Who may or may not be relevant to canon.<br /> <br /> ...before we learned what Exigents were, I thought this was going to be a splat that ran with the &quot;multiple identities, but none of them real&quot; thing that some people suggested for Lunars. So the Lunar Exalted could embrace the idea that they did have core identities, and losing that was where something went wrong, see chimera...<br /> <br /> But obviously that ended up being wrong. Soooo...we'll see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T14:56:53-08:00","id":2073,"title":"","content":"My avatar is a Lunar, zomg, evacuate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:53:59-08:00","id":2124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=1141#post1141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going to ask if you knew Loki but then...he got fucked rather than the other way round <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds just like Lunars, really (not really).<br /> <br /> I had this neat idea, using a character with a really small totem, like a praying mantis. The Character would need <i>Deadly Mantis Practise</i>, <i>Heaven-Expanding Staff of the Monkey King</i>, and <i>Lunar Blade Reconfiguration</i>. For equipment, he would need two Moonsilver Artefact weapons. Use <i>Lunar Blade Reconfiguration</i> to turn the Artefacts into Warstrider Grand Daiklaves, use <i>Heaven-Expanding Staff</i> to wield them while in the form of a common praying mantis, and use <i>Deadly Mantis Practise</i> so you can dual-wield them.<br /> <br /> Enjoy.<br /> <br /> For extra lulz, <i>Lunar Blade Reconfiguration</i> into Warstrider Grand Daiklave works <i>wonders</i> when used on Flying Silver Dream, you know, the weapon which can attack by itself... And either add the Wings mutation using <i>Hybrid Body Rearrangement</i>, or just switch the totem for something flight-capable; you now have two (or three, or more if you feel like it - hey, insects have six legs, go for broke with seven total) flying six-metre-long Behemoth-slicers!<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Beyond how any sensible ST should slap me silly if I suggest it (luckily, I am the ST in my group - guess what they'll be facing?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T19:12:13-08:00","id":2293,"title":"","content":"I've long had the desire to make a Lunar who from time to time chooses to humiliate the hell out of his adversaries. He does so by assuming the form of a mouse. And then commencing the ass-kicking of a lifetime. With or without brandishing the giant moonsilver daiklave. I don't recall that being especially viable in 2nd edition, but I'm hopeful for EX3.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd be psyched for a much greater emphasis on the trickster side of Lunars in general. I mean, that's the archetype that stands out to me when I think of a lot of shapeshifter myths Lunars draw upon. I'm hopeful they work off of <i>that</i> at least as much as the warrior archetype.<br /> <br /> Which I actually feel fairly confident and excited about; I remember Holden spelling out that the Lunar castes embody Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman for a reason. Like, all in the same breath. As though the latter two <i>aren't</i> going to feel like throwaway afterthoughts this time!<br /> <br /> I'd be happier still with more examples of stuff in those two wheelhouses -- I admit I still don't feel I have a solid grasp of the Lunar Charm paradigm, altogether -- but I'm happy enough with the reassurance they won't be neglected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 11-03-2013, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T06:30:09-08:00","id":2557,"title":"","content":"I made a brutal tiger Lunar brawler once.<br /> I'd like to resurrect him for 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T06:50:00-08:00","id":2568,"title":"","content":"Being a kick-ass mouse is no problem; if it's a false form (and really, your ST is a jerk if you can't do it in your Spirit Form), you can still add Strength, and that's without a custom Knack letting you use your Human Strength in mouse form (no less believable than a Dexterity 6 Yeddim, I'd say). <i>Inexplicable Lunar Wonders</i> makes <i>Claws of the Silver Moon</i> not-Obvious, and then there are all the various damage-enhancers... Don't forget the -3 external penalty to anyone trying to hit you, the +3 success bonus to anything applicable (like re-establishing surprise) or the massive stunt potential.<br /> <br /> Add in Crane Style, with a touch of Victorious Concession and Disco Ninja- I mean, Crystal Chameleon, for extra humiliation. Give a verbal commentary on their form as you take them apart. Double humiliation if you use <i>Armor-Rending Claw Fist</i> or similar to strip them while doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:15:38-08:00","id":2733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=2557#post2557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a brutal tiger Lunar brawler once.<br /> I'd like to resurrect him for 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he will dig getting a chance to sink his claws into the new Tiger Style. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:38:26-08:00","id":2760,"title":"","content":"My one and only Lunar didn't last a single session before getting killed; admittedly, it was my very first character, and I didn't have a clue what to do about getting ganked while everyone else was hiding, but he did get killed really easily. Never played a Lunar since, even though I think I'd like to, I just can't get myself to do it since I don't actually enjoy Lunars charms in 2e. Hopefully, though, 3e will make all that better.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I hope to God Lunars can heal other people this time around...that was so annoying. &gt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/339-armstrong-thunderbolt","user":"Armstrong Thunderbolt","date":".  also 11-04-2013, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/339-armstrong-thunderbolt","name":"Armstrong Thunderbolt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar339_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:52:49-08:00","id":2773,"title":"","content":"I want kickass magical moonsilver tattoos that do cool things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:56:07-08:00","id":2776,"title":"","content":"well. lunar tattoos do do cool things! like stop you from turning into a chimera!<br /> <br /> ..that's close enough, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2649","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/403-mabufufu","name":"mabufufu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar403_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:25:01-08:00","id":2794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want kickass magical moonsilver tattoos that do cool things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just by reading this, I pictured a Lunar shedding their tattoos like blood (splattering those around them) to enter some kind of protean super mode.<br /> <br /> Which is weird, because I keep thinking of the tattoos as just an extended Caste mark with some neat fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T00:31:12-08:00","id":3251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=2733#post2733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he will dig getting a chance to sink his claws into the new Tiger Style. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>He' ll be delighted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:50:09-08:00","id":3815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=2794#post2794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just by reading this, I pictured a Lunar shedding their tattoos like blood (splattering those around them) to enter some kind of protean super mode.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7NZESmjjJM\" target=\"_blank\">ZA BEAST</a><br /> <br /> (not hinting at anything, just really dig that scene)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:51:39-08:00","id":3816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabufufu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=2776#post2776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well. lunar tattoos do do cool things! like stop you from turning into a chimera!<br /> <br /> ..that's close enough, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahahahaha-nope. All of my nope. Because that would mean Wyld Taint is still a thing. And that would mean that <i>the</i> Shapeshifter Splat still cannot actually Shapeshift without having to worry that they'll wind up like a Chaos Spawn, unless they join the super-special secret club. Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:17:48-08:00","id":3833,"title":"","content":"Lunars are such an archetype treasure trove! I've always wanted to play either the classic face-ripping werewolf headhunter, or go for the exact opposite, of a deer-shaped healer-sorcerer. Anybody here seen Princess Mononoke? That.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/792-karpattata","name":"Karpattata","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:23:02-08:00","id":3835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=3816#post3816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahahahaha-nope. All of my nope. Because that would mean Wyld Taint is still a thing. And that would mean that <i>the</i> Shapeshifter Splat still cannot actually Shapeshift without having to worry that they'll wind up like a Chaos Spawn, unless they join the super-special secret club. Nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flawed Exaltations ftl. The way 2e chimerae were done always bugged me (As well as the tell UMI). <br /> <br /> For 3e I can't wait to bring back my Crocodile-totemed, man-eating Changing Moon. Oh the shenanigans he and his crocodile familiar got up to. Especially after Sharing the Gifts of Luna.<br /> <br /> Good Timest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T17:55:31-08:00","id":3895,"title":"","content":"Personally, I could take Chimerism if it was actually tied into the Limit mechanic or something else that made it more interesting than just &quot;get tattoos or eventually turn into a psychopathic monster.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:10:04-08:00","id":4160,"title":"","content":"I had a very fun Lunar once. A changing moon wolf pack mother. Inspired a little by Holo (yes, Emperor-Ox Expansion), a little by the Last Unicorn, and a little by Spirits (nWoD) and Raksha.<br /> <br /> To her, life was an ongoing story that was always better in the telling. She never told the truth when an interesting tale would do. She never allowed herself to regret her actions, no matter what became of them. She never let herself be bound; not physically nor by oaths, promises or titles. And finally she never took straightforward action when cunning and cleverness could be substituted.<br /> <br /> Of course, true to her nature, all of these rules were broken at one point or another. Such was her urge for freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:46:51-08:00","id":4237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=3815#post3815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7NZESmjjJM\" target=\"_blank\">ZA BEAST</a></div> </div> </div> </div> It was almost precisely that scene I had in mind, albeit with more arms.<br /> <br /> (I love the sound of AT Fields.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:48:43-08:00","id":4239,"title":"","content":"I have also a Changing moon character stored somewhere in my hd based on Deathmaster Snitch, from Warhammer's Skaven...I'll have to upgrade him to new edition.<br /> Three short Daiklaves with poisonous evocations will be a <i>must have</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:30:00-08:00","id":4258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=4239#post4239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also a Changing moon character stored somewhere in my hd based on Deathmaster Snitch, from Warhammer's Skaven...I'll have to upgrade him to new edition.<br /> Three short Daiklaves with poisonous evocations will be a <i>must have</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three?<br /> ... oh, right. The Tail.<br /> I did a similar thing with a desert monitor lizard totem in a shogunate game.<br /> I miss her.<br /> Maybe I'll play a default time incarnation in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:49:04-08:00","id":4367,"title":"","content":"While it probably has minimal relevance, today I thought of the idea of a Lunar who acted as a guardian of one of the fortress-cities of humanity during the Primordial War, as specifically depicted in a Lunar's past life memory of the time when the city was found and the wall was breached and the Lunar stood alone in the pass tearing apart everything that tried to push its way through.<br /> <br /> His spirit shape is a rabbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:58:04-08:00","id":4376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=4237#post4237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I love the sound of AT Fields.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain they're intended to sound like church bells, because if we're going to pretend there's meaningful religious symbolism here, might as well go all the way, right?<br /> <br /> EDIT: By which I mean the substantive core of Evangelion has never been the (pseudo) religious aspect, it's been the characterization and subversion of traditional mecha archetypes. Which people seem to forget, sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","user":"MrInsecure","date":". 11-06-2013, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:19:55-08:00","id":4397,"title":"","content":"Oh, Australia. Truly, you are the gift that keeps on giving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:21:09-08:00","id":4398,"title":"","content":"For...god, maybe a whole decade now, I have wanted to play a Lunar who seems like a protector of humanity until you notice he never actually helps anyone; he just hurts things that prey on humans, which is not the same thing at all (and the longer it's been since he's had a chance to indulge his rage addiction, the broader his definition of &quot;prey on humans&quot; becomes). He doesn't like taking animal shapes, so he channels his shapeshifting prowess into control of his own body down to a cellular level so he can shrink momentarily when dodging or add some weight to his fist to give it a little extra centrifugal force on a punch.<br /> <br /> Never really had the mechanics for it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:36:02-08:00","id":4414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=4397#post4397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Australia. Truly, you are the gift that keeps on giving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you suppose that it's too late to add this to the megafauna list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:33:14-08:00","id":4456,"title":"","content":"Zeruel's AT Field is actually unique in making that sound; the <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Sqj_lShuQos?t=2m\" target=\"_blank\">classic sound</a> is quite different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T17:49:26-08:00","id":6497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=3815#post3815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7NZESmjjJM\" target=\"_blank\">ZA BEAST</a><br /> <br /> (not hinting at anything, just really dig that scene)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I can't get excited about that scene.<br /> <br /> It just seemed to me like, &quot;Sure, DBT and RLF are cute tricks, especially when used together. But the Solar / Infernal laughs at the adorable little kitten and curbstomps the enemy on his own.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:41:11-08:00","id":6784,"title":"","content":"As I was falling asleep last night a couple ideas popped into my head.<br /> <br /> <b>Luna as the Horned God Archetype</b><br /> We are told that Luna appears as female just as often as she appears to be male. The 2E Lunars Book presents five of her most common personae: Three female, one male and one intersexed. I also find the one male persona to be feminine in both appearance and demeanour. I think it would be really interesting if one of Luna's persona would be a well-known one, and he would take the form of a wild god of the forests sporting animal horns. Most often this muscular brute would have the horns of a stag, but in cultures further south there'd be depictions of him with ram horns. This isn't Luna masquerading as a male divinity, this is the real deal as well. In this way, one must use various pronouns when speaking broadly of the Silver Celestine.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fire Blood Charm</b><br /> This one came closer to actually falling asleep in something of a dream sequence. In it, I saw a Lunar shed blood in a circle around a Celestial God, then ignite his blood. The circle burned with silver fire and prevented that God from leaving or using any Spirit Charms. In the dream it felt as though the Lunar was going to be interrogating this God for reasons I never got into before the dream faded and I was awake enough to write this down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T19:19:05-08:00","id":7143,"title":"","content":"Silver Fire Blood sounds like a cool interpretation of Devil-Restraining Grip - maybe an upgrade, sacrifice a health level to trap the victim in a circle? Could also be a spirit ward using thaumaturgy and a meta-charm so it doesn't take an hour to cast.<br /> <br /> On a side note, am I the only one who wanted to add expansion charms to Devil-Restraining Grip to give it some of the effects Alchemicals get with Mind-Ripping Probe thingamajig? Primarily being able to devour spirits whole, trapping them in the Lunar Labyrinth of your subconscious and digest them over time - also a great way to get (unwilling) tutors for abilities, spells and martial arts. Add a Stamina upgrade that lets you do the same to non-spirits, because Chimeras shouldn't have all the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T20:42:44-08:00","id":7163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=6497#post6497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I can't get excited about that scene.<br /> <br /> It just seemed to me like, &quot;Sure, DBT and RLF are cute tricks, especially when used together. But the Solar / Infernal laughs at the adorable little kitten and curbstomps the enemy on his own.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilsport!<br /> <br /> Guess I'll just have to wait for someone to upload Asuka going Beast Mode in 02-Dash onto youtube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T21:44:58-08:00","id":7180,"title":"","content":"So is Alex Mercer still a valid character concept for 3E Lunars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:16:01-08:00","id":7190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7180#post7180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Alex Mercer still a valid character concept for 3E Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly appears so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:17:51-08:00","id":7209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=3815#post3815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7NZESmjjJM\" target=\"_blank\">ZA BEAST</a><br /> <br /> (not hinting at anything, just really dig that scene)</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I've never seen Evangelion, so maybe I'm missing some context. But... entering a super mode, taking great stress and damage in the process, then failing to even injure your foe and getting dismembered?<br /> <br /> ...yaay. Inspiring. &lt;/sarcasm&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:46:29-08:00","id":7218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7180#post7180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Alex Mercer still a valid character concept for 3E Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T01:22:14-08:00","id":7228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7209#post7209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, I've never seen Evangelion, so maybe I'm missing some context. But... entering a super mode, taking great stress and damage in the process, then failing to even injure your foe and getting dismembered?<br /> <br /> ...yaay. Inspiring. &lt;/sarcasm&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. On the other hand, this was a side of the mecha that hadn't been previously seen, and...a little bit later someone else uses it--or at least something terrifyingly similar--to far, far greater effect, but I can't find a clip of it with any translation on Youtube. The one I linked on the last forums some time ago got taken down.<br /> <br /> I don't think I can do any justice to it in words, especially if you haven't seen any Evangelion before. Suffice it to say that when the next person uses it, he unleashes unstoppable apocalyptic force and just generally manages to be both effective and awesome. Especially given that he's heretofore been the most obviously psychologically unsteady of the main cast, and when this scene played out last time...well, something <i>similar</i> happened, but he wasn't the one in control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T01:28:07-08:00","id":7231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7218#post7218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kimberian and Metagaoiyn Infernal always get all the fun :&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T02:07:36-08:00","id":7245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7218#post7218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give us some examples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T02:08:58-08:00","id":7246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7228#post7228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair. On the other hand, this was a side of the mecha that hadn't been previously seen, and...a little bit later someone else uses it--or at least something terrifyingly similar--to far, far greater effect, but I can't find a clip of it with any translation on Youtube. The one I linked on the last forums some time ago got taken down.<br /> <br /> I don't think I can do any justice to it in words, especially if you haven't seen any Evangelion before. Suffice it to say that when the next person uses it, he unleashes unstoppable apocalyptic force and just generally manages to be both effective and awesome. Especially given that he's heretofore been the most obviously psychologically unsteady of the main cast, and when this scene played out last time...well, something <i>similar</i> happened, but he wasn't the one in control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so naturally this is the Solar doing it this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T05:02:33-08:00","id":7293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7218#post7218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I know the first thing about those. The only mythic shapeshifter who comes to mind is Zeus turning into animals and fucking around with mortal women behind Hera's back and Loki getting impregnated by a horse.<br /> <br /> I was referring more to the approach to shapeshifting -- Mercer doesn't turn into animals so much as he customizes his human form with mutations according to what he needs. I know the devs are moving away from Lunars being the Animorph Exalted but is Hybrid Body Rearrangement or a similar ability included in that approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T06:48:34-08:00","id":7314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7180#post7180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Alex Mercer still a valid character concept for 3E Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting out as an anti-hero who can't go to the shops without there being a body count involved and after a lot of soul searching and eating people decides the problem is everyone else in the world and basically becomes Albert Wesker so that a protagonist who is actually likable can save the day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:07:31-08:00","id":7323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7293#post7293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say I know the first thing about those. The only mythic shapeshifter who comes to mind is Zeus turning into animals and fucking around with mortal women behind Hera's back and Loki getting impregnated by a horse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he means specific deities so much as general bodies of folklore featuring people who turn into animals or animals that turn into people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:41:42-08:00","id":7334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7323#post7323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think he means specific deities so much as general bodies of folklore featuring people who turn into animals or animals that turn into people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what he meant, what I'm saying is that I don't have any context for what shapeshifter mythology entails beyond a whole lot of bestiality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though &quot;animals that turn into people&quot; at least lets me add some vague knowledge of kitsune myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:52:03-08:00","id":7340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7231#post7231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kimberian and Metagaoiyn Infernal always get all the fun :&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Turning into a Lovecraftian monstrosity is what Infernals do, not Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:59:48-08:00","id":7346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7340#post7340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. Turning into a Lovecraftian monstrosity is what Infernals do, not Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, chimera were still a thing that existed and might even be playable this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T09:18:32-08:00","id":7387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7245#post7245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give us some examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think Raven, Coyote, Loki and Zeus immediately. Azrahn from Night's Master is a demon but does some pretty badass animal form stuff about, as do some sorcerers in the setting. Beast Boy from DC stuff, and there's some anime who have shapeshifters like that, although I admit not having immediate examples on hand to work with.<br /> <br /> There's also bits of skinwalkers in various legends stuff. And I remember when I was in junior high reading a collection of werewolf stories from around the world and a lot of stuff of witches in Africa turning into hyenas and leopards and terorizing local populations. Raksi is based on Indian rakshasa. <br /> <br /> So there's stuff to work with I think.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:30:16-08:00","id":7528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7387#post7387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think Raven, Coyote, Loki and Zeus immediately. Azrahn from Night's Master is a demon but does some pretty badass animal form stuff about, as do some sorcerers in the setting. Beast Boy from DC stuff, and there's some anime who have shapeshifters like that, although I admit not having immediate examples on hand to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only anime example who immediately springs to mind is Eve from Black Cat, and she's far more in Mercer's vein of modifying the human form rather than discarding it altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:46:46-08:00","id":7538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7346#post7346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked, chimera were still a thing that existed and might even be playable this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of &quot;Lunars who hybridize their spirit shape&quot; maybe.<br /> <br /> I won't quite point out how chimerae as Lunars who had turned into nondescript blobs was out of place (it was out of place), but it certainly didn't exactly make them interesting or distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:17:13-08:00","id":7557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7538#post7538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of &quot;Lunars who hybridize their spirit shape&quot; maybe.<br /> <br /> I won't quite point out how chimerae as Lunars who had turned into nondescript blobs was out of place (it was out of place), but it certainly didn't exactly make them interesting or distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what a &quot;nondescript blob&quot; has to do with Alex Mercer, who takes a human or at least humanoid form for about 99% of the story and alters it only according to what he needs at any given moment. He's no more Lovecraftian than any given primordial for that matter.<br /> <br /> That's the Lunar I want to play: if he channels animal themes then he does so only through his charms and his actions, like the warrior who invokes the unstoppable force of a runaway yeddim when he plows down a the middle of a street and tackles a dynast through a teahouse and the three buildings behind it. Actually turning into said yeddim is entirely unnecessary because his essence is doing the work just fine without any superficial physical changes. Those are reserved for shaping your figure into whatever form you need it to be -- giant razor-edged shovel claws for an edge in kung-fu duels, talons on the feet for extra traction when running across icy terrain, a furnace rhino's carapace armor for tanking hits, and all of these things you have at the same time because no single animal has all those mutations in a single form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 11-10-2013, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:52:15-08:00","id":7586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7557#post7557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what a &quot;nondescript blob&quot; has to do with Alex Mercer</div> </div> </div> </div>Then citing Second Edition chimerae as a reference point to him is even less suitable.<br /> <br /> When I look at Alex Mercer, I see a bunch of visual signifiers that feel so much more appropriate to the Infernal Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">giant razor-edged shovel claws for an edge in kung-fu duels, talons on the feet for extra traction when running across icy terrain, a furnace rhino's carapace armor for tanking hits, and all of these things you have at the same time because no single animal has all those mutations in a single form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess those specifics are, with slight modification, fine enough as things for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Honestly, when conversations like this come up and people say they want Alex Mercer, I think every person has a different picture of what that actually means.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of perplexed as to what makes that character so damn memorable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:03:17-08:00","id":7595,"title":"","content":"I've never played a Prototype game, and I obviously can't speak for anyone but myself, but at a guess, I'd say people who reference Alex Mercer as a Lunar are people who want to be able to shapeshift while keeping their general human shapes; to use arterial blood jets to fly instead of turning into a bird, to use finger claws to climb instead of turning into a spider, to...uh...I actually don't know anything else Alex Mercer can do, but pretend I said whatever it was and added a &quot;instead of turning into [an appropriate animal].&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:11:41-08:00","id":7601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7586#post7586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I look at Alex Mercer, I see a bunch of visual signifiers that feel so much more appropriate to the Infernal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the whole point of his character arc (in the first game anyways, the second screws him up like whoa from what I'm told) is that despite being a sentient virus he's actually more human than the guy he copied his memories from. Alex Mercer the virus has more compassion and care for his intimacies than Alex Mercer the human ever demonstrated for anything. If you don't make him chew on civilians for a health boost he restricts his targets to the guys who are shooting at him for the most part. Human qualities are things Infernals are much more likely to get rid of as their essence rises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess those specifics are, with slight modification, fine enough as things for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Honestly, when conversations like this come up and people say they want Alex Mercer, I think every person has a different picture of what that actually means.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of perplexed as to what makes that character so damn memorable. </div> </div> </div>Well he's the most mainstream example I can think of of a shapeshifter who primarily uses hybrid body rearrangement as opposed to full-on animal transformations. I could have cited Eve and gotten the same meaning but I thought she was too obscure for Holden to have any idea who I was referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:12:52-08:00","id":7606,"title":"","content":"Mercer always felt Abyssal to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:36:35-08:00","id":7636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7601#post7601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the whole point of his character arc</div> </div> </div> </div>His what now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">is that despite being a sentient virus he's actually more human than the guy he copied his memories from. Alex Mercer the virus has more compassion and care for his intimacies than Alex Mercer the human ever demonstrated for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't remember much of that game's story mode, because it frequently managed to be less compelling to me than rampaging around a Manhattan shaped sandbox, but I'm pretty sure the two or three people Mercer is supposed to care about kind of vaguely disappear about halfway through with little fanfare.<br /> <br /> He's so gruff and nondescript (except for that point towards the end where he occasionally breaks it up by inexplicably screaming his head off with the name of some general character, who isn't the general character in charge of the stupid evil military unit) that I don't really get a sense of what he feels towards anything.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I guess there wasn't much room for development when they had to portion the story out to that weird &quot;eat people for plot&quot; mechanic, which takes a really long time to tell a story that amounts to maybe three lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human qualities are things Infernals are much more likely to get rid of as their essence rises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, that was your point? That's a <i>terrible</i> thing to base Infernals around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:58:04-08:00","id":7652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7636#post7636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His what now?</div> </div> </div> </div>His character arc. You know, the part where he starts off as an amnesiac trying to figure out why he woke up in a morgue and ended with him having all the answers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7636#post7636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, that was your point? That's a <i>terrible</i> thing to base Infernals around!</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what are you basing your assertion on besides &quot;his powers look weird and he has elements of transhumanism in his design&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 11-10-2013, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T14:12:33-08:00","id":7659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7652#post7652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His character arc. You know, the part where he starts off as an amnesiac trying to figure out why he woke up in a morgue and ended with him having all the answers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh. I suppose that basically fits the definition of character arc of &quot;we know more about the character at the end than we did at the beginning&quot;, but when that knowledge amounts to &quot;there was no person before the beginning&quot; and there's hardly much of a person at the end, it feels like a technicality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what are you basing your assertion on besides &quot;his powers look weird and he has elements of transhumanism in his design&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Nothing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T23:18:45-08:00","id":7896,"title":"","content":"The best Lunar mate I've seen lately is non other than... JAKE THE DOG.<br /> <br /> Although he doesn't shift into other animals (he can sometimes emulate them), he has complete control over the shape of his body. Lots of times while I watch Adventure Time, I start wondering how could all those stunts Jake pulls could be done in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Jake's best buddy is kinda like a solar and he even has a girlfriend who seems like she came out of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I wonder if powers similar to Jake's will be available in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T00:27:41-08:00","id":7914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7218#post7218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not tremendously so. We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be both. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:42:28-08:00","id":8060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7218#post7218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure hope one will be able to invest into the spirit shape to turn it into a <a href=\"http://canime.files.wordpress.com/2012/03/princess-mononoke-deer04.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">proper</a> <a href=\"http://canime.files.wordpress.com/2012/03/princess-mononoke-05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">god-beast</a>, because that's what I imagine every time you say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7896#post7896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jake's best buddy is kinda like a solar and he even has a girlfriend who seems like she came out of the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Land of Ooo is absolutely a Creation driven mad by the rising tides of the Wyld.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:57:48-08:00","id":8078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7914#post7914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can be both. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just because something can be the case doesn't mean it's obligated to be so. The authors and devs probably have an idea of where they want to go with them and part of that seems to be &quot;tightening-up&quot; the Lunar aesthetic. Part of this seems to be less Mercer or <i>The THING</i> and more classical and primative sources.<br /> <br /> Part of an annoyance some folks have about Lunar fans is how much of everyone's hopes and dreams, despite the divergence, got mixed into them. Such that for some people there is this entire &quot;alternate Lunar&quot; idea out there that can subsist on its own if we were to delete everything originally printed about Lunar Exalted. The Venn diagram of what folks wnat from the splat is complicated as shit and the team seems to be in the mindset of putting their foot odwn and picking a cross section to stick to rather than please everyone.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:06:51-08:00","id":8122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8078#post8078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because something can be the case doesn't mean it's obligated to be so. The authors and devs probably have an idea of where they want to go with them and part of that seems to be &quot;tightening-up&quot; the Lunar aesthetic. Part of this seems to be less Mercer or <i>The THING</i> and more classical and primative sources.<br /> <br /> Part of an annoyance some folks have about Lunar fans is how much of everyone's hopes and dreams, despite the divergence, got mixed into them. Such that for some people there is this entire &quot;alternate Lunar&quot; idea out there that can subsist on its own if we were to delete everything originally printed about Lunar Exalted. The Venn diagram of what folks wnat from the splat is complicated as shit and the team seems to be in the mindset of putting their foot odwn and picking a cross section to stick to rather than please everyone.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The way 2e Lunars were written is particularly unhelpful for this transition. They seemed to have a bit of just about everything, but all very inconsistently. It's like they were using a really weird version of <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Charms%3ARiver_Reflects_Desire\" target=\"_blank\">River Reflects Desire</a> where almost nobody* is happy with what they see, but they see whatever combination of deletions and emphasis they individually favor as the obvious fixes to make.<br /> <br /> * Of those who pipe up on these boards, anyway.<br /> <br /> This is why I find it particularly important to get the idea of what EX3 Lunars are to be clear as crystal. And for this to happen as far out from their book as possible. Those who go into the Lunars book really looking forward to a radically different idea of Lunars than the book will give them will find some level of unnecessary disappointment. If they know clearly what Lunars are well in advance, they won't be expecting something they're not going to get. Some may have an amount of disappointment, anyway, but it will at least be further removed; they'll be able to better appreciate EX3 Lunars for what they actually are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:29:58-08:00","id":8142,"title":"","content":"Something to consider. I don't remember there ever being an incentive to give Lunars an ability to transform parts of their bodies, on the spot, acording to the situation.<br /> <br /> As far as I remember, when it comes to transformation, it was always complete. The only &quot;partial transformation&quot; is the hybrid form, but arguably that's just the third, complete and integral form Lunars can assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-11-2013, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:34:08-08:00","id":8147,"title":"","content":"Post-errata that's basically what Hybrid Body Rearrangement was.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:46:05-08:00","id":8157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8147#post8147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post-errata that's basically what Hybrid Body Rearrangement was.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you are correct. Interesting, interesting. The question is: is it something to be expected in 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-11-2013, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:08:02-08:00","id":8237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8157#post8157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you are correct. Interesting, interesting. The question is: is it something to be expected in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>As questions go I sincerely hope that one was rhetorical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:12:15-08:00","id":8241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8237#post8237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As questions go I sincerely hope that one was rhetorical. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you think about it, we haven't seen anything like that pre-errata and we've seen but a single such thing post-errata. The only reason to even consider the possibility that an ability to change parts of your body on the spot might be expanded in the 3e, is that the current Dev team made the aformentioned errata. But that's all. It's really uncertain. I wouldn't assume it to be a staple power of the Lunars, it never seemed to be important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:39:09-08:00","id":8410,"title":"","content":"If you dig into Werewolf shapeshifting inspiration, you'll hit partial transformations right out of the gate. Holden even wrote in more Gifts involving partial transformation mechanics for W20. Seems fairly reasonable, given the sorts of inspiration they likely plan on mining. I suspect that it might even end up more widespread than Rage inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:54:39-08:00","id":8532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7323#post7323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think he means specific deities so much as general bodies of folklore featuring people who turn into animals or animals that turn into people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully also those featuring people that turn other people into animals.<br /> <br /> Wolves transmitting uncontrollable lycanthropy with a bite, and witches who turn people into newts (who may or may not get better).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, to clarify my earlier comment: It's not that Za Beasto isn't cool on its own, and Mari was also kind of cool. Sure, she failed, but she tried something risky and gave it her all. The animation and action were awesome.<br /> <br /> But that utter failure to even harm the enemy, followed by Shinji's semi-ascension and one-man victory, apparently followed by someone else (who is apparently a Solar?) using Unit 02 better than Mari... It just stinks so damn much of Second Edition's &quot;only Solars matter&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-11-2013, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:56:10-08:00","id":8533,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd be happy if we could just hear more about what Lunars <i>are</i> and less about what they <i>aren't</i>. 'Primal Gods' doesn't sound all that distinctive, what with Creation having lots of those in its <i>actual</i> gods, and as for 'Mythic Shapeshifters'...well, I agree that Charm-sharing is generally bullshit. That said, a lot of things have most of their power tied up in Charms, and it'd be neat if a Lunar could get something out of killing a dragon with her bare hands other than bragging rights and another shape that isn't as good as DBT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:20:38-08:00","id":8543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7346#post7346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked, chimera were still a thing that existed and might even be playable this time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=7538#post7538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of &quot;Lunars who hybridize their spirit shape&quot; maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Platypus.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any other real-life creatures which can so easily be seen as just mash-ups of other real creatures right now. Maybe the pangolin, which is an anteater, armadillo and tree sloth rolled into one? Or maybe the tree-dwelling spider-crab things?<br /> <br /> On top of those real creatures, Creation features beasts like griffons as completely normal species. So, I hope &quot;chimera&quot; means something other than &quot;start out as a lion and then become a griffon later because your ST won't let you be a griffon from the start.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, the devs were talking about using the Spirit Shape as an avenue of additional power in regards to Charms, so maybe the more important aspect of Chimera is grabbing more potential avenues of power than a Lunar should normally enjoy, at a price?<br /> <br /> That's different from 2ndEd Chimerism, which gated off specific kinds of powers rather than a general level of power. In which regard, my suggestion is more analogous to Infernal Monster Style's Apocalyptic Rage Beast or whatever -- the Charms which sacrificed more and more of the player's control over the character in return for greater power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, Alex Mercer was dead on a slab and then woke up with hardly any memories from the brain he inheritted (though with some muscle memories from the parkour enthusiasts who got absorbed into his body) and with a completely different personality than he had in life. He's something very much not natural or human, though he's human enough to understand and interact with people. He also improves himself by incorporating the flesh of other people into his own body.<br /> <br /> So, I figure he's very much a Liminal Exalt. Born from a dead man's body as a new, abominable creature that will never really fit in among natural human beings. He's also the quintessential Flesh Aspect, being a figure of violence and rage and revenge, whose powers revolve around superhuman physique, using his flesh as a weapon, and more efficiently incorporating the bodies of his victims into himself (ie: absorbing them whole and directly, without the need for surgery).<br /> <br /> <br /> Eve, from Black Cat, is more of an Alchemical Exalt of the Moonsilver Caste and the Modern Shard stripe, going by her origins and the technological aesthetic of her powers. But who knows? Maybe she'll fall under the auspices of the Lunar-complementary Exalted Host that's yet to be described.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8533#post8533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Charm-sharing is generally bullshit. That said, a lot of things have most of their power tied up in Charms, and it'd be neat if a Lunar could get something out of killing a dragon with her bare hands other than bragging rights and another shape that isn't as good as DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the previous forum, I suggested that Heart's Blood forms might have a mechanic similar to artifact Evocations. A Lunar PC who kills and eats a fire god might spend XP to develop fire-magic Evocations which he can only use while wearing that fire-god's form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-11-2013, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:03:06-08:00","id":8585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8543#post8543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, Alex Mercer was dead on a slab and then woke up with hardly any memories from the brain he inheritted (though with some muscle memories from the parkour enthusiasts who got absorbed into his body) and with a completely different personality than he had in life. He's something very much not natural or human, though he's human enough to understand and interact with people. He also improves himself by incorporating the flesh of other people into his own body.<br /> <br /> So, I figure he's very much a Liminal Exalt. Born from a dead man's body as a new, abominable creature that will never really fit in among natural human beings. He's also the quintessential Flesh Aspect, being a figure of violence and rage and revenge, whose powers revolve around superhuman physique, using his flesh as a weapon, and more efficiently incorporating the bodies of his victims into himself (ie: absorbing them whole and directly, without the need for surgery).<br /> <br /> Eve, from Black Cat, is more of an Alchemical Exalt of the Moonsilver Caste and the Modern Shard stripe, going by her origins and the technological aesthetic of her powers. But who knows? Maybe she'll fall under the auspices of the Lunar-complementary Exalted Host that's yet to be described.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great, but what I was saying was &quot;I want to make a character who can do this thing that character Bob does,&quot; not &quot;I want to make character Bob as an Exalt.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:36:54-08:00","id":8601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8543#post8543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Platypus.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any other real-life creatures which can so easily be seen as just mash-ups of other real creatures right now. Maybe the pangolin, which is an anteater, armadillo and tree sloth rolled into one? Or maybe the tree-dwelling spider-crab things?<br /> <br /> On top of those real creatures, Creation features beasts like griffons as completely normal species....</div> </div> </div> </div>The griffin is given as an example Wyld mutant or magical creature from the Wyld that survives in Creation purely by force of will.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself, I'd get to griffin by having a Lunar with a protoceratops totem. But then, that is just me. (Crumbled fossils near gold deposits were thought to have inspired real-life griffin legends.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:45:04-08:00","id":8603,"title":"","content":"As a note, platypus aren't that weird when you get a better idea of how what bits are put together weird. Mind, they are still weird, just not <i>that</i> weird. At least not compared to things like mospids about.<br /> <br /> Griffons, manticores, Chinese phoenixes and Ki-Rens are kind of what I think of mroe when I think of weird hodgepodge animals.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T22:04:14-08:00","id":8612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8603#post8603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, platypus aren't that weird when you get a better idea of how what bits are put together weird. Mind, they are still weird, just not <i>that</i> weird. At least not compared to things like mospids about.<br /> <br /> Griffons, manticores, <b>Chinese phoenixes</b> and Ki-Rens are kind of what I think of mroe when I think of weird hodgepodge animals.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Copy-pasta from wikipedia (does goose have boobs thought ? ):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A common depiction of fenghuang was of it attacking snakes with its talons and its wings spread. According to the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erya\" target=\"_blank\">Erya</a>'s chapter 17 Shiniao, fenghuang is made up of the beak of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rooster\" target=\"_blank\">rooster</a>, the face of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swallow\" target=\"_blank\">swallow</a>, the forehead of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fowl\" target=\"_blank\">fowl</a>, the neck of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snake\" target=\"_blank\">snake</a>, the breast of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose\" target=\"_blank\">goose</a>, the back of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tortoise\" target=\"_blank\">tortoise</a>, the hindquarters of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer\" target=\"_blank\">stag</a> and the tail of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish\" target=\"_blank\">fish</a>.<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenghuang#cite_note-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a> Today, however, it is often described as a composite of many birds including the head of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Pheasant\" target=\"_blank\">golden pheasant</a>, the body of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandarin_Duck\" target=\"_blank\">mandarin duck</a>, the tail of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peafowl\" target=\"_blank\">peacock</a>, the legs of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crane_%28bird%29\" target=\"_blank\">crane</a>, the mouth of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parrot\" target=\"_blank\">parrot</a>, and the wings of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swallow\" target=\"_blank\">swallow</a>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T06:41:17-08:00","id":8767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8601#post8601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The griffin is given as an example Wyld mutant or magical creature from the Wyld that survives in Creation purely by force of will.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the Flame Griffin. The mundane griffin is described as an offshoot of Flame Griffins that became viable in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:23:28-08:00","id":8793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8767#post8767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's the Flame Griffin. The mundane griffin is described as an offshoot of Flame Griffins that became viable in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex2 core, page 291. The gryphon is a mutant, much like the buck-ogre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:33:31-08:00","id":8795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8532#post8532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully also those featuring people that turn other people into animals.<br /> <br /> Wolves transmitting uncontrollable lycanthropy with a bite, and witches who turn people into newts (who may or may not get better).</div> </div> </div> </div>Big-time. With such a huge chunk of human-animal dualism stories they make up, it's bewildering how little attention that got in the past. I mean, they had, what a Charm and two Kna-- three Charms in 2e?<br /> <br /> It's conceivable that thematic restructuring could leave this on the cutting room floor, but I'd be very surprised. It would feel like such a missed opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:40:26-08:00","id":8840,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to make a Sheep Lunar who is a master of infiltration and blending in. Is this idea stupid as all get out? That's what I'm going?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/87-faller3","name":"Faller3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:45:54-08:00","id":8842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faller3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8840#post8840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to make a Sheep Lunar who is a master of infiltration and blending in. Is this idea stupid as all get out? That's what I'm going?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure Creation has sheep to begin with, number one. Number two, for infiltration you probably want some kind of chameleon or other creature with natural camoflauge, and that will change depending on where you are -- a snow leopard blends in with his surroundings pretty well in the north, but not so much in Wavecrest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:52:39-08:00","id":8847,"title":"","content":"The direction of previous editions and the setting info for Exalted 3 gives enough information to answer a few of the questions above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to consider. I don't remember there ever being an incentive to give Lunars an ability to transform parts of their bodies, on the spot, acording to the situation.<br /> <br /> As far as I remember, when it comes to transformation, it was always complete. The only &quot;partial transformation&quot; is the hybrid form, but arguably that's just the third, complete and integral form Lunars can assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't count on anything like Hybrid Body Rearrangement. There are several approaches to shapeshifting, and the one that allows you to customize your limbs / organs whatever on the fly to perform a particular task is <b>not</b> what Lunars have ever been about. It's <b>not</b> what any of the mythic shapeshifters (e.g., Loki) that Lunars are supposedly drawing inspiration from were about. If tools for this appear in the Lunar manual, they'll be a minor and comparatively-unimportant part of shapeshifting. What you have to look forward to should be clear enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that utter failure to even harm the enemy, followed by Shinji's semi-ascension and one-man victory, apparently followed by someone else (who is apparently a Solar?) using Unit 02 better than Mari... It just stinks so damn much of Second Edition's &quot;only Solars matter&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going in with this attitude I can guarantee that Exalted 3 Lunars will feel like a disappointment to you. The facts of the matter are that they were left out of the cozy arrangement that Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded brewed up, were hunted down like animals by the Wyld Hunt, and have not succeeded in bringing their enemy down. The writing team will write this to sound good (&quot;it is only by the constant erosion of Lunar sabotage that the Realm has been brought down this low&quot;), but it does not change that the defining narrative of Lunars is about their failure. The narrative in the standard Exalted game will be &quot;Lunars fought the Realm constantly for hundreds of years, but it was only when the Solar Exalted arrived that the tide turned and the Empire fell&quot;.<br /> <br /> I encourage you to read what Holden has revealed about Lunars again. In his essay, he describes &quot;barbarians&quot; as being defined by oppression from an empire: their infrastructure is broken, their treasures are looted, and they are chased off to live in the ruins of their former cities and make their living in resource-poor lands that the empire doesn't want. That is what Lunars are. Using your perspective as detailed in that previous post, Lunars are the beast-mode Eva making a show and buying time until the Solar Exalted return and punch the Realm down.<br /> <br /> If you don't find this appealing (I don't find anything about the new direction of Lunars appealing), I suggest that you drop Lunars. Your attachment is to your own memories and conception of them, which will never come to pass in official material. Lunars are not being written for you, but for some audience that is a fan of pulp fantasy and will hopefully want to play leather-clad, shapeshifting barbarians on a warpath. So, leave it to them. With the new Exalted and the Exigent Exalted being introduced this edition, you don't have to care: you can tailor what you want in a way that's consistent with the setting. Please believe me when I say that doing this will do wonders for your mood. The amount of worry, care and hope-seasoned-by-despair that I've read in this thread horrifies me, not least because I used to share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","user":"Black Paper Moon","date":". 11-12-2013, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:53:35-08:00","id":8848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8842#post8842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure Creation has sheep to begin with, number one. Number two, for infiltration you probably want some kind of chameleon or other creature with natural camoflauge, and that will change depending on where you are -- a snow leopard blends in with his surroundings pretty well in the north, but not so much in Wavecrest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation has cows and goats, IIRC.<br /> <br /> Sheep aren't that far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/87-faller3","name":"Faller3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:58:04-08:00","id":8849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8842#post8842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure Creation has sheep to begin with, number one. Number two, for infiltration you probably want some kind of chameleon or other creature with natural camoflauge, and that will change depending on where you are -- a snow leopard blends in with his surroundings pretty well in the north, but not so much in Wavecrest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, why <i>wouldn't</i> Creation have sheep? That would seem an oddly specific exclusion, barring some broader explanation I'm not seeing. I mean, yes, it has fauna our Earth doesn't have. That doesn't preclude fauna it does. Yeddims, for instance: they're its most prominent pack animals, but it'd be silly to think that means there are no <i>other</i> beasts of burden at all.<br /> <br /> Getting to the question, a sheep is a perfectly solid thematic choice for a Lunar meant to blend in with others. It's also nice in that I don't think I've heard of such a Lunar before. Unfortunately, with 2e's handling of it, a sheep spirit shape isn't of much use to a Lunar, other than a cheaper time blending in near other livestock.<br /> EDIT: And the fun of embarrassing others by getting the better of them while using Deadly Sheepman Transformation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Luckily, with what's been said of EX3's spirit shape, I get the impression thematic ties in an animal are meant to be a big help, giving your Lunar cheaper and easier access to Charms. There may be other perks. It's one of the new Lunar takes I'm most interested in seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 11-12-2013, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:28:40-08:00","id":8874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8849#post8849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily, with what's been said of EX3's spirit shape, I get the impression thematic ties in an animal are meant to be a big help, giving your Lunar cheaper and easier access to Charms. There may be other perks. It's one of the new Lunar takes I'm most interested in seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much as to what's up with New Lunars, but I am certainly excited about Spirit Shape being more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/87-faller3","name":"Faller3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:36:46-08:00","id":8881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faller3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8874#post8874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much as to what's up with New Lunars, but I am certainly excited about Spirit Shape being more important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely with ya, there. ^_^ Here's the big blurb where John talked about his plans for the Spirit Shape. That was many months ago, so things may have changed, as he notes. Still, it's very promising.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is still the animal you choose to be the basis for your DBT. How much I force it into your character's appearance remains to be seen. If you don't want to be a DBT Lunar, I'd rather you think of DBT / spirit shape as the tool you relied on when your Lunar was still young, inexperienced, and less powerful, rather than ignoring it entirely. I want to help people build away from a DBT-based character through powers that work when you are in your human form and don't work when you are in DBT.<br /> <br /> Once you reach that point, it is my intention that the spirit shape, through a clever use of keywords and associations, provide you a favored discount on Charms whose Attributes you don't favor, going so far as to change the Charm's prerequisites and shift it to a logical place in your current Charm trees (if one exists). So even if you ignore your spirit shape in roleplay, its themes are there helping you by providing a framework to power up your character.<br /> <br /> I also realize that one of the reasons people search so furiously for meaning beyond DBT is because a single animal is so constraining, so I am looking at completely redoing Chimeraism so that it is an accepted state, so that players can make cool-looking hybrid monsters with lots of different traits.<br /> <br /> Note that everything I've said here is &quot;Maybe&quot; not &quot;I promise&quot; and is subject to change. This is about as far as I am willing to reach into my giant vault of future noise to show people, but I feel like the general tone of acceptance and readiness for big new ideas has reached a level where such a classified view won't confuse and upset anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:57:08-08:00","id":8898,"title":"","content":"I am currently playing a Lunar in a long-term mixed-group Heaven's Reach game (passed 150XP not too long ago). He's the group's pilot, but per Lunar norms is actually fairly proficient at a wide variety of things. I think this is the niche Lunars are meant to occupy in mixed groups: the best at moving between places quickly and competent-to-great at nearly everything else.<br /> <br /> He's about 50% custom Charms at this point, excluding excellencies, simply because they're necessary to realize the character fully. To be entirely blunt, this character is an iteration of Lunar that exceeds even 2.5 in liberal application of the rules.<br /> <br /> Our imagining of HR has all but 9 Lunar exaltations under the thumb of the Emperor. So almost every Lunar you encounter is or was an Imperial operative (this character included). Lunars frequently work with Sidereals to stabilize problems inside the Empire and occasionally outside the Empire, depending on the Lunar in question. They can work in opposition, of course, if the Emperor's will doesn't match what the Grand Central Mountain foresees/cultivates as necessary.<br /> <br /> So we opted to throw out basically all of the form-related Knacks. They don't seem relevant in the least to any of the Lunar characters and it means Lunars have much more interesting and varied totems. (We have: a legendary giant bird (that can fly in vacuum because magic), a space wyrm, a colossal predatory weasel, and a swarm of insects.) It also means Lunars change forms at their leisure, and change their clothes like other characters change their expressions, and move freely through society, making them ideal in their role as embedded agents of the Emperor. The Knacks we did keep are: form changing speed Knacks, ritual form acquisition Knacks, and Fate-related Knacks. This means a Lunar at outset is pretty robust from a shapeshifting perspective, but one who invests deeply in it doesn't leave a trail of bodies, digital detritus, and snarled threads of Fate behind them. They're literally ghosts in the machine. Which seems a fair trade for 50+ XP in my estimation.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Knacks will conform to this dynamic, where you're basically buying an ability that is expressed through shapeshifting, rather than the opportunity to break game mechanics if you can convince everyone it's worth their time to let you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T12:25:28-08:00","id":9058,"title":"","content":"I doubt Knacks still exist as a thing separate from Charms, but still, I get your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:40:59-08:00","id":9119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9058#post9058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt Knacks still exist as a thing separate from Charms, but still, I get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that the game has gone from 'Eclipse Open Season' with Native being the 'Eclipse-No' tag, to a general Eclipse-No game with the occasional spirit-charm 'Eclipse-Ok' tag, I very much doubt Knacks need to be separated from Charms.<br /> They might still be their own CharmWeb, though. Stamina, Perception, Dexterity, and Apearance all sound likely Attibutes to file it under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:29:38-08:00","id":9180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8847#post8847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going in with this attitude I can guarantee that Exalted 3 Lunars will feel like a disappointment to you. The facts of the matter are that they were left out of the cozy arrangement that Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded brewed up, were hunted down like animals by the Wyld Hunt, and have not succeeded in bringing their enemy down. The writing team will write this to sound good (&quot;it is only by the constant erosion of Lunar sabotage that the Realm has been brought down this low&quot;), but it <b>does not change that the defining narrative of Lunars is about their failure.</b> The narrative in the standard Exalted game will be &quot;Lunars fought the Realm constantly for hundreds of years, but it was only when the Solar Exalted arrived that the tide turned and the Empire fell&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a deeply-unsatisfying implementation, and I hope you don't take it personally when I say I REALLY hope you're off the mark here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:50:18-08:00","id":9202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8847#post8847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't count on anything like Hybrid Body Rearrangement. There are several approaches to shapeshifting, and the one that allows you to customize your limbs / organs whatever on the fly to perform a particular task is <b>not</b> what Lunars have ever been about. It's <b>not</b> what any of the mythic shapeshifters (e.g., Loki) that Lunars are supposedly drawing inspiration from were about. If tools for this appear in the Lunar manual, they'll be a minor and comparatively-unimportant part of shapeshifting. What you have to look forward to should be clear enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> <br /> So, do you also feel that Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick will be abandoned, at least in its current form? If HBR is unthematic, I don't see how briefly growing an ovipositor would be appropriate. If Lunars are going to be primal barbarian beast-gods, then perhaps the Charm would invoke a Voudoun ritual, with chants, gris-gris and other fetishes and ritual trappings?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going in with this attitude I can guarantee that Exalted 3 Lunars will feel like a disappointment to you. The facts of the matter are that they were left out of the cozy arrangement that Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded brewed up, were hunted down like animals by the Wyld Hunt, and have not succeeded in bringing their enemy down. </div> </div> </div>Don't care. That's fine. That's not my issue.<br /> <br /> Morke said he intends Lunars to be able to throw down with Infernals on equal ground in combat. If an Infernal Shinji shows up a Lunar Mari <i>that badly</i>, it's going to be because of an XP differential, a character build more effective in that particular situation, or just plain having the better Warstrider courtesy of the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> It's not going to be because Lunars are inherently chumps. Not that they were in Second Edition, mind. Not mechanically.<br /> <br /> But I'm still remembering that one poster, where each of the signature Solar circle is facing off against one other Exalted opponent. Except for Panther, who was fighting two beastmen.<br /> <br /> Not <i>one</i> obvious Exalt, like anyone else in the picture. <i>Two </i>naked, unarmed beastmen who might have been Lunars in warform, except neither one of them featured any anima display or Castemark at all, so they could have been just mortal beastmen.<br /> <br /> So either the Lunar Exalted got no representation at all in a picture that was otherwise exclusively casted with Exalts, or they were deemed the only Exalted that needed to double-team a Solar (or bring along a mortal helper) to provide a challenge. Despite Mnemon, of the Terrestrial Exalted designed specifically to rely on numbers, dueling Ariana by her lonesome. Mnemon was also clothed and displaying obvious signs of supernatural power.<br /> <br /> That poster has nothing to do with the Lunar history of disenfranchisement and exile. The poster is meant to say, &quot;Being an Exalt is awesome!&quot; Unless you're a Lunar.<br /> <br /> And Lunars don't really appear anywhere but their own book in Second Edition (excepting Shards), and their own book whines too much about History Is What Was Done To Us to make it sound awesome to be a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, I consider the cover of <i>Scroll of Exalts </i>to be more of an unfortunate coincidence rather than &quot;more of the same&quot; (and certainly not as part of a non-existent conspiracy). Sure, it could have been a Dragon-King filling in for &quot;lizardperson laying slain on the altar&quot;, but that would have broken the pattern of only Exalted being the characters on the cover, and they were already stretching the visual homage by adding a second thief going for the idol's gemstone eyes. There really wasn't much room left on the page for yet another not-dead character.<br /> <br /> I also thought Madame Vert was a fool and would have felt no great loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't find this appealing (I don't find anything about the new direction of Lunars appealing), I suggest that you drop Lunars. Your attachment is to your own memories and conception of them, which will never come to pass in official material. </div> </div> </div>My conception of Lunars has always been as fluid as the execution of them. I've only ever been searching and searching for &quot;what Lunars SHOULD be&quot; without any particular attachment to one concept or another, so long as that concept was strong, well-executed, and made sense in the context of the setting.<br /> <br /> I've proposed a various different versions of them, since my First Edition days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars are not being written for you, but for some audience that is a fan of pulp fantasy and will hopefully want to play leather-clad, shapeshifting barbarians on a warpath. </div> </div> </div>And I'm interested to see how that plays out!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the new Exalted and the Exigent Exalted being introduced this edition, you don't have to care: you can tailor what you want in a way that's consistent with the setting. </div> </div> </div>I definitely am looking forward to making my Changeling Exalted a reality, once I get my hands on the new rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:13:42-08:00","id":9221,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> And they call <i>me</i> incessantly negative.<br /> <br /> Actually, scratch that, write my name just beneath Black Paper Moon's, I agree with what he said. This is exactly how I feel about Lunars and how I predict them to be presented in 3e.<br /> <br /> The only difference being that I probably am the group this idea is targeted at, because that sounds fucking cool to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-12-2013, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:04:46-08:00","id":9322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8847#post8847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[The Lunars]were left out of the cozy arrangement that Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded brewed up, were hunted down like animals by the Wyld Hunt, and have not succeeded in bringing their enemy down. The writing team will write this to sound good (&quot;it is only by the constant erosion of Lunar sabotage that the Realm has been brought down this low&quot;), but it does not change that the defining narrative of Lunars is about their failure. The narrative in the standard Exalted game will be &quot;Lunars fought the Realm constantly for hundreds of years, but it was only when the Solar Exalted arrived that the tide turned and the Empire fell&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I've been getting is not yours. This is not the saga of Lunars holding on with their teeth while the Realm is repeatedly kicking them in the face to knock them off the edge of the world. Remember they have a giant landmass that the Realm has a single toehold on, maintained only by levels of paranoia that would be insane under other circumstances. And this is only the largest of the Lunar territories.<br /> <br /> When the Realm loses a legion, it takes with it artifacts, resources, and men who they invested time and further resources in training. When the Exalted Previously Known As The Stewards lose a tribe, they lose a bunch of dudes they can replace when they go off for the next round.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are playing the long game, pretending at being the wild and savage barbarians, but they've been playing chess all along. It's a war of attrition the Lunar Exalted are better-equipped for, and they probably aren't losing. <br /> <br /> The return of the Solars isn't turning the tide, it's knocking over the chessboard at a time when things are getting unpredictable. How would the Lunars handle the sudden civil war in the Realm, and its pouring-out into their satrapies, in the absence of the returning Lawgivers?<br /> <br /> I don't know.<br /> <br /> But I expect they'd adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:26:16-08:00","id":9335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=8847#post8847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going in with this attitude I can guarantee that Exalted 3 Lunars will feel like a disappointment to you. The facts of the matter are that they were left out of the cozy arrangement that Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded brewed up, were hunted down like animals by the Wyld Hunt, and have not succeeded in bringing their enemy down. The writing team will write this to sound good (&quot;it is only by the constant erosion of Lunar sabotage that the Realm has been brought down this low&quot;), but it does not change that the defining narrative of Lunars is about their failure. The narrative in the standard Exalted game will be &quot;Lunars fought the Realm constantly for hundreds of years, but it was only when the Solar Exalted arrived that the tide turned and the Empire fell&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except this is entirely wrong. We've yet to see the relationship between Lunars and Solars in the new edition, but there's a good reason as to why they weren't included in the deal. They weren't hunted down like animals, there are still to this day First-Age Lunars that live and plot against the Realm and their conspirators. They're still 300 hundred strong and likely the most common example of Anathema known to current day Creation. They are not a unified force, but have still persevered in the face of the Realm and the Sidereals. They're the main opponent of the Sidereals of a cold war that's been going on since the Usurpation. They aren't defined by their failures, they're defined by their adaptability and perseverance. Their theme is change, they've changed since the Primordial War, the First Age, and the Usurpation. The Solar Exalted aren't getting the credit, they're just the wildcard that has been introduced into a secret conflict that's been going on for thousands of years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T19:42:34-08:00","id":9411,"title":"","content":"&quot;leather-clad, shapeshifting barbarians on a warpath.&quot;.......Well at least the leather gonna be form-fitting so my Ichor Flux Tendrils won't feel too bad about penetrating the Lunar's delicious abs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T20:15:10-08:00","id":9433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9202#post9202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I'm still remembering that one poster, where each of the signature Solar circle is facing off against one other Exalted opponent. Except for Panther, who was fighting two beastmen.<br /> <br /> Not <i>one</i> obvious Exalt, like anyone else in the picture. <i>Two </i>naked, unarmed beastmen who might have been Lunars in warform, except neither one of them featured any anima display or Castemark at all, so they could have been just mortal beastmen.<br /> <br /> So either the Lunar Exalted got no representation at all in a picture that was otherwise exclusively casted with Exalts, or they were deemed the only Exalted that needed to double-team a Solar (or bring along a mortal helper) to provide a challenge. Despite Mnemon, of the Terrestrial Exalted designed specifically to rely on numbers, dueling Ariana by her lonesome. Mnemon was also clothed and displaying obvious signs of supernatural power.<br /> <br /> That poster has nothing to do with the Lunar history of disenfranchisement and exile. The poster is meant to say, &quot;Being an Exalt is awesome!&quot; Unless you're a Lunar.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or...maybe a person just drew a picture, and didn't think too hard about it! Like what usually happens with the minimalist art directions people get from RPG art directors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T21:44:35-08:00","id":9455,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that the fall of the Realm, as I gather, isn't so much solely a fault of the return of the Solar Exalted, but more likely greatly an effect of the disappearance of the Scarlet Empress. Her Redness being missing is a lot more to do with the upcoming Civil War and collapse than the Celestial Exalted, who are more able to be the threat they are now in teh wake of the legions more or less collapsing.<br /> <br /> If she were still around, I would think that the Solars gunning for the undermining fo the Realm and setting up their own domions int he world would be no small bit harder than it is now.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T23:24:11-08:00","id":9496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9180#post9180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a deeply-unsatisfying implementation, and I hope you don't take it personally when I say I REALLY hope you're off the mark here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will only be unsatisfying in the way I wrote if you approach Lunars with a keen sensitivity to &quot;but what have they accomplished&quot; and &quot;but despite all the sound and fury they're still the guys being hunted down like animals&quot;. If those are concerns of yours (and it seems they're not concerns of Sunder the Gold, which made my reading of his post a misinterpretation?) then you'll have issues with Lunars. However, being defined as the dudes who were driven to the edges of Creation and oppressed, and have been fighting back from a position of inferiority ever since, is not necessarily a bad thing. It takes you to a different place from most other Exalted, which gives them variety and a distinct identity. It gives them a history and a purpose. And, even in this thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arrakiz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only difference being that I probably am the group this idea is targeted at, because that sounds fucking cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>... some people dig it. You can be sure the writers will try to make it sound good and empowering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar Exalted are playing the long game, pretending at being the wild and savage barbarians, but they've been playing chess all along. It's a war of attrition the Lunar Exalted are better-equipped for, and they probably aren't losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This provokes the same reaction as the &quot;aha! Lunars were secretly manipulating all these cultures all along!&quot; reveals of Exalted 2 in me: a shrug and a &quot;really?&quot; Stylistic barbarism also makes me wince, both aesthetically and because it lies somewhere between offensive and silly in the continuum of ideas when you look at actual &quot;barbarian&quot; cultures. None of it works for me, but I'm not their target audience. If this works for you, then I hope they do a good job with the book and leave you satisfied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> So, do you also feel that Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick will be abandoned, at least in its current form? If HBR is unthematic, I don't see how briefly growing an ovipositor would be appropriate. If Lunars are going to be primal barbarian beast-gods, then perhaps the Charm would invoke a Voudoun ritual, with chants, gris-gris and other fetishes and ritual trappings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember what Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick even is. What I can say is that &quot;protean&quot; shapeshifting ala T-1000, Alex Mercer or whatever is pretty different to the shapeshifting you get in traditional mythology, and that HBR is out of place. It might survive there as a nod to previous-edition Lunar players or as a trick to get some bonuses up, but I should not expect it to be meant to be a defining feature (in either coolness or power) of Lunar shapeshifting. Note, of Lunar <i>shapeshifting</i>. If you're asking me about their Charm arsenal, everything's up in the air. Whether any particular trick introduced in Glories: Luna or Ink Monkeys survives, I couldn't say\u2014that depends on a lot of things I don't know, such as whether anything like that has appeared in the source material the devs draw from and whether they find it cool and interesting enough to warrant inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","user":"Black Paper Moon","date":". 11-13-2013, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T23:59:31-08:00","id":9507,"title":"","content":"For Exalted 3rd, I'd like to see some female Luners with bulk and muscle. One of the things I liked about Diablo 3's barbarians is that the female version was roughly the size of the male one. It seems that most fantasy games/art are fine with dudes that are MASSIVE but women are just slightly taller with muscle definition. It seems odd that the body shifting group doesn't have one woman who looks like she could take a hit from Strength-Of-Many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T02:42:46-08:00","id":9543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9507#post9507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Exalted 3rd, I'd like to see some female Luners with bulk and muscle. One of the things I liked about Diablo 3's barbarians is that the female version was roughly the size of the male one. It seems that most fantasy games/art are fine with dudes that are MASSIVE but women are just slightly taller with muscle definition. It seems odd that the body shifting group doesn't have one woman who looks like she could take a hit from Strength-Of-Many.</div> </div> </div> </div>*snip*<br /> <br /> I hope that this Dragon-Blooded war won't escalate through more and more material to the point of everlasting, burning hatred, effectively making cooperation between Lunar and Dragon-Bloo... Lunar and anyone else, completely impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","user":"Storyteller","date":".  Edited by Storyteller to remove rules infraction. 11-13-2013, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T02:52:42-08:00","id":9551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9507#post9507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Exalted 3rd, I'd like to see some female Luners with bulk and muscle. One of the things I liked about Diablo 3's barbarians is that the female version was roughly the size of the male one. It seems that most fantasy games/art are fine with dudes that are MASSIVE but women are just slightly taller with muscle definition. It seems odd that the body shifting group doesn't have one woman who looks like she could take a hit from Strength-Of-Many.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, every Slayer in hatewheel's &quot;Tell me about your fighty Exalted&quot; is female.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T03:31:12-08:00","id":9563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9507#post9507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Exalted 3rd, I'd like to see some female Luners with bulk and muscle. One of the things I liked about Diablo 3's barbarians is that the female version was roughly the size of the male one. It seems that most fantasy games/art are fine with dudes that are MASSIVE but women are just slightly taller with muscle definition. It seems odd that the body shifting group doesn't have one woman who looks like she could take a hit from Strength-Of-Many.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hazard a guess it's because the artists they hire don't want to draw women that way. More than any real intentional outcome.<br /> <br /> Besides, gender norms and physique have very little to do with combat capability in Exalted. My HR Lunar is tall and broad-shouldered and the second weakest fighter in the group (slightly ahead of our Sidereal Princess). He doesn't even have perfects. He is a Full Moon. He's also the only male PC. The other males in the cast are, amusingly enough, all Lunars as well. He unabashedly admits his real talent lies in running away.<br /> <br /> Could I turn him into a combat monster? Yeah, I'd need to make about a dozen Charm purchases; finishing up the Dex tree and starting in the Stamina tree to begin with. But I don't really need to.<br /> <br /> Did you know Cobra Hypnotic Method forces opponents Inactive in combat? (You probably didn't. It does.) Clover Can't Be Found works in combat against Inactive opponents? It does. Honestly I think I've had a lot more fun building a Lunar who specializes in avoiding fights than I did building one who simply crushed everything he came across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T03:33:20-08:00","id":9565,"title":"","content":"I have also made a female slayer (those are the Malfeus ones, right?) but I'm talking about the official artwork and characters in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:33:51-08:00","id":9764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9565#post9565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also made a female slayer (those are the Malfeus ones, right?) but I'm talking about the official artwork and characters in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basphomy in Verdegris, the signature 3E Slayer-equivalent? Was large and in charge if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:40:47-08:00","id":9774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9764#post9764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basphomy in Verdegris, the signature 3E Slayer-equivalent? Was large and in charge if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was chuby and that's definitely sexy, but she wasn't all that bulky or muscular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:39:23-08:00","id":9914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9496#post9496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember what Wasp of the Labyrinth Trick even is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You briefly grow an egg-injecting stinger to stab into a corpse or zombie, which turns corpses into zombies you control or usurps control of a pre-existing zombie.<br /> <br /> If Lunars are more barbarian beast-gods than The Thing, then that implementation might be handed over to some other splat, with the Lunar Exalted getting something more Voudoun or witch-doctory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It will only be unsatisfying in the way I wrote if you approach Lunars with a keen sensitivity to &quot;but what have they accomplished&quot; and &quot;but despite all the sound and fury they're still the guys being hunted down like animals&quot;. If those are concerns of yours (and it seems they're not concerns of Sunder the Gold, which made my reading of his post a misinterpretation?) then you'll have issues with Lunars. </div> </div> </div>Solar Circle Sorcery was part of the &quot;only Solars matter&quot; problem, but was not a problem in and of itself. I'm cool with Lunars being completely incapable of casting Solar Circle Sorcery. Further, if it's possible to mimic Solar Circle Spells through artifacts (even if they must be inconveniently large and troublesome artifacts), I'd be fine with Lunars not having the potential to make such artifacts. Likewise, I'm not bothered that Lunars can't learn Sidereal Martial Arts, or develop Evocations to the extent that Solars can.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with the Lunar Exalted being the seconds to the Solar Exalted in the First Age, or being the exiles and barbarians of the Second.<br /> <br /> <br /> It may be that my problem isn't confined to <i>Exalted</i>. Certainly, it's not confined to Second Edition, since First Edition (and especially <i>Cult of the Illuminated</i>) had a lot of the attitude towards Lunars against which I seethe.<br /> <br /> It's the picture in <i>CotI</i> where the blazing Solar god is frowning imperiously down at two kneeling beastmen, who from the context of the text on that page are Lunar Exalted. It's the aforementioned Solar Exalted versus Other Exalts poster where Panther is fighting what might be two Lunars or merely mortal beastmen. It's First Edition Raksi treating Lunar followers as disposably as she might treat beastmen, not Celestial Exalted. It's Moonsilver-casted Excessively Righteous Blossom being the Token Idiot of the signature Alchemicals, and yet going on to effortlessly murder a seasoned Lunar Exalt in single combat.<br /> <br /> It's in <i>Accel World</i>, where Cyan Pile is the only other male character in a harem-esque story and despite starting out stronger and more experienced than the main character, Silver Crow, Cyan Pile cannot manage a single on-screen victory that doesn't involve a Taking You With Me mutual KO. His purpose is to pad out fights and worf to the enemy to build up tension, while Silver Crow is the one who actually defeats the villain (and gets Cyan Pile's girlfriend without even trying, or even wanting her as a girlfriend).<br /> <br /> I'm just really fucking sick of The Designated Worf and The One Important Protagonist Around Whom All Plot Must Revolve and Through Whom All Plot Must Resolve (And Who Gets All The Women While He's At It). Which is sad, because I like Silver Crow and think he's a truly interesting character -- just not THAT much worthier a character than everyone else in the setting who has a story to tell.<br /> <br /> So, I don't react very well when I see those scenes of Mari trying everything and failing, with Shinji coming along to win easily. Or at least, I don't react well when Za Beasto is pointed out as a Lunar sort of thing, but only because context sours me against the scene's awesomeness. (And Mari and Za Beasto <i>are</i> cool.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Thus, I'm just being harder on Vance's example/allusion than I should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2013, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:29:41-08:00","id":9983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9764#post9764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basphomy in Verdegris, the signature 3E Slayer-equivalent? Was large and in charge if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only artwork I've seen of her has her standing alone, so I'm not sure how big she is or isn't actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:35:54-08:00","id":9988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9563#post9563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hazard a guess it's because the artists they hire don't want to draw women that way. More than any real intentional outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why it's good to comment on it, because if I don't mention it, the assumption is that no one would want a female character who could stand eye-to-eye with Strength-of-Many or who looks like she could take a hit from Stern Whip of Industry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, gender norms and physique have very little to do with combat capability in Exalted. </div> </div> </div>And this comment has very little to do with the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:43:46-08:00","id":9992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9914#post9914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I don't react very well when I see those scenes of Mari trying everything and failing, with Shinji coming along to win easily. Or at least, I don't react well when Za Beasto is pointed out as a Lunar sort of thing, but only because context sours me against the scene's awesomeness. (And Mari and Za Beasto <i>are</i> cool.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Thus, I'm just being harder on Vance's example/allusion than I should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen 3.33 yet? Because it includes both A) some fun facts about Shinji's &quot;easy win&quot; that are not very fun and B) Asuka using Beast Mode to take on something horrifyingly powerful, and winning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:18:55-08:00","id":10018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9992#post9992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen 3.33 yet? Because it includes both A) some fun facts about Shinji's &quot;easy win&quot; that are not very fun and B) Asuka using Beast Mode to take on something horrifyingly powerful, and winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Waiting for it to make it stateside, here. Actually, I've been waiting so long for that--and checking the Wiki page often enough that when I type in &quot;en&quot; in the search bar, the first thing to pop up is Rebuild of Evangelion.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>And it looks like it'll be making it to some theaters come January. I am sincerely hoping that a.) There's a screening somewhere in the D/FW area again, and b.) It's subbed. I've been watching Eva subbed for well over a decade and the dubbed voices just sound wrong to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 11-14-2013, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:42:19-08:00","id":10074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9914#post9914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I don't react very well when I see those scenes of Mari trying everything and failing, with Shinji coming along to win easily. Or at least, I don't react well when Za Beasto is pointed out as a Lunar sort of thing, but only because context sours me against the scene's awesomeness. (And Mari and Za Beasto <i>are</i> cool.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's worth remembering that Shinji's victory comes at the cost of most of the world's population, and that he's losing up until the point where he flips out and <i>initiates Third Impact</i>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:20:56-08:00","id":24010,"title":"","content":"&quot;Doing the impossible to accomplish the excellent&quot;, &quot;cheating by making the task easier rather than being superhumanly excellent&quot;, &quot;treating the world as though made of water, clay or rubber&quot;...<br /> <br /> This was a general theme I was promoting for the Lunar Exalted back in Second Edition, as a way to make sense of their Charmset and provide a direction for new Charms. It covered the mutability of their own bodies (shapeshifting and shapewarping) as well as Charms like Clay-Wetting Practice, Flesh-Sculpting Art, Moonlight Hunt and Blinking Eye of Chaos. Warping matter, time and space.<br /> <br /> But I think that kind of thing is actually going to the reality-hacking Getimians, now. We already know that they achieve super-Athletics, outright flight or weird mobility tricks by screwing with gravity. I think this new splat would be an awesome place to find science-fiction Esper-esque powers like that.<br /> <br /> Which is cool, as that sort of esoteric thing doesn't really fit with the intensely physical Half-Beast God motif that gives rise to Deadly Beastman Transformation and Relentless Lunar Fury.<br /> <br /> Divide up the themes and magnify them to really get the most out of them, rather than dilute them all into one splat. Especially if the new focus for the Lunar Exalted really sells the importance of Totems, Spirit Shapes and Tells rather than leaving them in as odd afterthoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-05-2013, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:58:50-08:00","id":24048,"title":"","content":"Lunars are cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/481-rahsith","name":"rahsith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T17:44:10-08:00","id":24083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24010#post24010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is cool, as that sort of esoteric thing doesn't really fit with the intensely physical Half-Beat God motif that gives rise to Deadly Beastman Transformation and Relentless Lunar Fury.<br /> <br /> Divide up the themes and magnify them to really get the most out of them, rather than dilute them all into one splat. Especially if the new focus for the Lunar Exalted really sells the importance of Totems, Spirit Shapes and Tells rather than leaving them in as odd afterthoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't wait to have that explanation in a book... finally. After over a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T20:56:13-08:00","id":24163,"title":"","content":"<br /> My favorite lunar PC was one who worked with (and in many cases was part of) the Immaculate order. He wasn't an elder, but early in his exalted life had encountered a very old and curse ridden solar who had hidden out in the Wyld. It left him with a burning hatred, and more importantly, fear of the insane chosen of the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T00:31:00-08:00","id":24223,"title":"","content":"I would like to address something from the last forum, a response to Holden's comments that the Lunar hate was misplaced because the Sidereals were more mechanically broken.<br /> <br /> The Lunar's problem, for me, a person who barely touches mechanics, is they have been <i>boring</i>. Sidereals, broken as they might be, were <i>exciting</i>.<br /> <br /> ~ <br /> <br /> Now, on to a suggestion: Lunar did not all pick one side in the Usurpation. The Silver Pact was a pipe dream, Lunar have always been individualistic. Some of them sided with the Solars, some of them opted out, some sided with the Sidereal. These Lunars are not Wyld Hunted, living it up in Heaven or walking around in Creation with a 'I'm not an Anathema' card. Lunars are not organized, not like Deliberative was and definitely not like the Fellowship. Each one is his own guy, doing his own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T03:09:10-08:00","id":24263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24010#post24010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think that kind of thing is actually going to the reality-hacking Getimians, now. We already know that they achieve super-Athletics, outright flight or weird mobility tricks by screwing with gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereal jumping Charm consists of slingshotting yourself using Fate threads.<br /> <br /> I'm not contributing to the conversation or anything, I just think that's cool.<br /> <br /> Though it kind of annoys me that Sids don't get easy access to perfect balance, so they can stand on the very tip of a swaying tree and be all mysterious kung fu master and stuff. The fact that they don't get it in their native Charm set and they need to use supernatural martial arts isn't a problem. But there just isn't anything as good as the Solar Charm Graceful Crane Stance. There's Crane Form, which, well, is a Form Charm. Which means it bars you from using other Form Charms. It also costs twice as much committed Essence, because it does a bunch of other stuff that's not related to balance. Cloud-Treading Method is actually more powerful (it lets you walk on water and smoke and stuff, in addition to solid things that shouldn't be able to bear your weight), but it has a short duration instead of being Scene-long. And I don't remember any other similar Martial Art Charm.<br /> <br /> Which means that Solars are better than Sidereals at standing on improbable things that really shouldn't support them. Actually, now that I think about it, so are Lunars! Since they also get Graceful Crane Stance. So, yep, Lunars. Doing something better than Sidereals. I guess I'm almost on topic for this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T03:09:57-08:00","id":24264,"title":"","content":"I maintain that one of the biggest problems with people's perceptions of Lunars was that they were overpowered compared to several of their more immediate enemies (Dragon-Blooded, Sidereals, Abyssals) for most of the edition.<br /> <br /> If your enemies are a joke it's difficult to take your plight seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T05:07:29-08:00","id":24296,"title":"","content":"I saw this and thought it would make a cool Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://localprocards.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/ink-eyes-servant-of-on2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The ninjitsu power reflects her shapechanging ability. You thought she was a harmless servant but <i>surprise!</i> she's a sneaky rat assassin.<br /> <br /> The regeneration is... regeneration. Reflecting the ability of even a rather scrawny Lunar to take massive amounts of physical punishment. The ability to bring back her enemy's servants from the dead and use them against her enemy is interesting. Probably dipping into necromancy.<br /> <br /> Ink Eyes also sounds like an Exalted name to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T06:46:55-08:00","id":24336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24296#post24296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this and thought it would make a cool Lunar.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://localprocards.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/ink-eyes-servant-of-on2.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://localprocards.com/wp-content/...ant-of-on2.png</a><br /> <br /> The ninjitsu power reflects her shapechanging ability. You thought she was a harmless servant but <i>surprise!</i> she's a sneaky rat assassin.<br /> <br /> The regeneration is... regeneration. Reflecting the ability of even a rather scrawny Lunar to take massive amounts of physical punishment. The ability to bring back her enemy's servants from the dead and use them against her enemy is interesting. Probably dipping into necromancy.<br /> <br /> Ink Eyes also sounds like an Exalted name to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>She would indeed make a fine Lunar, but let's not neglect the possibility of an Abyssal beastman.<br /> <br /> She can disguise her identity with Abyssal Larceny and survive mortal wounds through Abyssal Resistance. And Necromancy is Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I hope that we have a beastman Exalt more prominent than Ophilus Ses in Third Edition, to showcase that beastman can also be Exalted, and don't need to be Lunar Exalted at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T07:39:59-08:00","id":24353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24223#post24223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, on to a suggestion: Lunar did not all pick one side in the Usurpation. The Silver Pact was a pipe dream, Lunar have always been individualistic. Some of them sided with the Solars, some of them opted out, some sided with the Sidereal. These Lunars are not Wyld Hunted, living it up in Heaven or walking around in Creation with a 'I'm not an Anathema' card. Lunars are not organized, not like Deliberative was and definitely not like the Fellowship. Each one is his own guy, doing his own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy this notion. Honestly, some of the best takes on the Lunars looked similar to this. Heck, I even did a variation where there was an ArgentOort Coud of Wyld kingdoms, lots of individualistic personages running around in Creation during the Shogunate, and a faction that actually conspired with the Sidereals. But ultimately, I feel that 'everybody just did whatever they wanted' can be just as boring as 'everybody line up for tattooes'. I actually enjoyed the notion of a Silver Pact, of some sort of organization dedicated to gathering Lunar strength in the Threshold, doing social things there, and/or being a counterbalance to the Dragonblooded Realm-centric political mapping. But that should be a result of the emergence of the Scarlet Empress, of centuries of slow, growing antagonism between factions of Terestrials growing increasingly paranoid of Lunar influence and pushing them towards the Threshold (and the Lunars pushing back) from a homogenous Shogunate, starting with an uneasy, public truce with those Moonchosen who sided with the Uprising (with big names like Ma-Ha-Suchi and/or Leviathan being amongst that number) to Gens treating having a Lunar like the modern world treats having nuclear armaments now in the middle Shogunate (sanctions, embargoes, nuclear deproliferation movements) to outright hostility only really emerging by the end. As opposed to the Solar revolution, which was a whispered conspiracy up until the sudden Calibration Feast slaughter, it should be more of a 700-year slide. Only with the coming of the Realm, and the Immaculate faith post-Contagion, do you get the Silver Pact. Which is perhaps at most half the total Lunars.<br /> <br /> I honestly wish I'd saved my post-essays. Lysdexic, if you're out there, please help me look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:03:07-08:00","id":24362,"title":"","content":"The signature characters would do well to remember all the weird ethnicities of Creation. A beastman Abyssal<sup>1</sup> would be pretty cool, but I'd be content with, say, a green person.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">1: I'm picturing a kind of Kintarou-like character, here</span> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2013 a barbarian or wild child employed by a lord, wearing the trappings of civilisation over a savage heart.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:41:09-08:00","id":24370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24362#post24362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wearing the trappings of civilisation over a savage heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings to mind something I thought recently, as regards &quot;civilization&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been reading a story in which the population of an entire MMORPG was incarnated and transported to a fantasy-alternate counterpart of Earth. (But no, I'm not talking about the excellent new series, <i>Log Horizon</i>.)<br /> <br /> Not only the various player races, but also the nonplayable races like Fox People. While the playable races have adapted better to the situation and have had the numbers to be both visible and strong enough to require and secure a treaty of basic human rights with the nation where they found themselves, the smaller, weaker and less visible Fox People have remained secluded... and thus they will not benefit from legal protection should anyone find them. This is an issue that came up with the Pixie NPC race when they were discovered, with the players pushing to have their &quot;mascots&quot; added to the treaty.<br /> <br /> Recently, I imagined a player finding the Fox People and wanting to extend them the same protection. But I wondered if he might run into a problem trying to explain the point of such a legal agreement.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I envisioned him explaining the whole matter as it really was -- a game of posturing and growling and showing teeth. It's two packs of beasts wanting to plunder, kill and destroy each other out of fear and greed, but recognizing that open warfare would be too costly. The &quot;laws&quot; and &quot;rules&quot; are merely a mutual language of posturing and dominance by which the opposing forces can compete with each other without open warfare, and perhaps even strike a balance of peaceful co-existence.<br /> <br /> That is, yes, in one sense the treaty is only worth the paper it's written on, and yes, the agreement by itself offers no protection, and unscrupulous elements within the local nation WILL try to plunder, kill and destroy them. But it means that these efforts need to be individual and clandestine, and that it's not an act of war to retaliate against such efforts.<br /> <br /> Of course, the treaty is also a promise of mutual protection with the player races; a recognition that they are all in the same dangerous boat, so one defends the other in return for being defended later, and presenting their opponents a larger, more intimidating target. Safety in numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because really, how civil IS &quot;civilization&quot;, when you get right down to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:07:10-08:00","id":24384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24362#post24362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The signature characters would do well to remember all the weird ethnicities of Creation. A beastman Abyssal<sup>1</sup> would be pretty cool, but I'd be content with, say, a green person.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">1: I'm picturing a kind of Kintarou-like character, here</span> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u2013 a barbarian or wild child employed by a lord, wearing the trappings of civilisation over a savage heart.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>And vice versa. Example: my failed attempt to have a Wyld Barbarian Defiler. The idea sorta got carried over as a Seafolk Twilight for a different game; much more civil... like a young version of the desert scholar from Aang's Library Adventure, but in a swimsuit... and most of the ruins were drowned cities in An Teng (long story). But this is a Lunar Thread.<br /> Any word on whether pelegials are human enough for Exaltation? or are they like the alaun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 12-06-2013, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:48:01-08:00","id":24401,"title":"","content":"Ideas involving the Lunars joining the Sidereals in the Usurpation or being passive non-targets leaves me cold. The Lunars could no more opt out of the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation than Daenerys could opt out of King Robert's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:13:36-08:00","id":24416,"title":"","content":"Re: Alex Mercer: No.<br /> <br /> Nor Carnage, the T-1000, or Twelve from Street Fighter, all of which are variations on Reed Richards and the Plastic Man when you boil them down. Fuck those guys.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:18:31-08:00","id":24419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=9507#post9507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Exalted 3rd, I'd like to see some female Luners with bulk and muscle. One of the things I liked about Diablo 3's barbarians is that the female version was roughly the size of the male one. It seems that most fantasy games/art are fine with dudes that are MASSIVE but women are just slightly taller with muscle definition. It seems odd that the body shifting group doesn't have one woman who looks like she could take a hit from Strength-Of-Many.</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:26:33-08:00","id":24423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24401#post24401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas involving the Lunars joining the Sidereals in the Usurpation or being passive non-targets leaves me cold. The Lunars could no more opt out of the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation than Daenerys could opt out of King Robert's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure Lunars could be Daenerys? Because sometimes, it feels like they cap out at Varys or Peter Baelish. Or even Jorah Mormont. Somebody who, even when the Targaryens got dealt with, might have been allowed to linger around as still-sorta-prominent people at court until somebody finally got tired of being reminded the Targaryens existed, and cleaned house.<br /> <br /> Please convince me The Mother Of Dragons can be that prominent on the world stage, and not be a Solar-Only character. I desperately hope what you say is true.... even if it means she has to go through that whole banishement-Reemergence-thing.<br /> Actually, nevermind. it works even by 2e standards.<br /> But you understand what I'm getting at, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:26:57-08:00","id":24424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24416#post24416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Alex Mercer: No.<br /> <br /> Nor Carnage, the T-1000, or Twelve from Street Fighter, all of which are variations on Reed Richards and the Plastic Man when you boil them down. Fuck those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>*totally, sincerely positive tone*<br /> <br /> Oh, so &quot;rubberman, limb-stretchiness&quot; is another feature moving from Lunars to Getimians or Liminals? I can get behind that.<br /> <br /> Dhalism seems more Getimian than Lunar, really. And Alex Mercer is totally a Liminal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:35:01-08:00","id":24433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24423#post24423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure Lunars could be Daenerys? Because sometimes, it feels like they cap out at Varys or Peter Baelish. Or even Jorah Mormont. Somebody who, even when the Targaryens got dealt with, might have been allowed to linger around as still-sorta-prominent people at court until somebody finally got tired of being reminded the Targaryens existed, and cleaned house.<br /> <br /> Please convince me The Mother Of Dragons can be that prominent on the world stage, and not be a Solar-Only character. I desperately hope what you say is true.... even if it means she has to go through that whole banishement-Reemergence-thing.<br /> Actually, nevermind. it works even by 2e standards.<br /> But you understand what I'm getting at, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the comparison I was making. But I'll go ahead and bite: Daenerys's ascent is made possible by dragons, and she is one of the most-beloved fictional heroines in modern memory. Yet if a Lunar depends on the long-extinct and newly resurrected Solar to make a power play, some people throw up in their mouths. I'm not compelled by the stories people think they can't tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:36:49-08:00","id":24435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24423#post24423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure Lunars could be Daenerys? Because sometimes, it feels like they cap out at Varys or Peter Baelish. Or even Jorah Mormont. Somebody who, even when the Targaryens got dealt with, might have been allowed to linger around as still-sorta-prominent people at court until somebody finally got tired of being reminded the Targaryens existed, and cleaned house.<br /> <br /> Please convince me The Mother Of Dragons can be that prominent on the world stage, and not be a Solar-Only character. I desperately hope what you say is true.... even if it means she has to go through that whole banishement-Reemergence-thing.<br /> Actually, nevermind. it works even by 2e standards.<br /> But you understand what I'm getting at, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the T-1000, and the archetypal genius of Reed Richards, I despise pretty much everything about &quot;stretchy guy&quot; characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:42:08-08:00","id":24442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24433#post24433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the comparison I was making. But I'll go ahead and bite: Daenerys's ascent is made possible by dragons, and she is one of the most-beloved fictional heroines in modern memory. Yet if a Lunar depends on the long-extinct and newly resurrected Solar to make a power play, some people throw up in their mouths. I'm not compelled by the stories people think they can't tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>... oh. Okay then.<br /> So it was more a take on 'Lunars don't need MacGuffins and/or Solars to be viable world-conquerors.'<br /> ... I'm still making occidental dragons, though.<br /> Dragons are cool, period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:45:50-08:00","id":24444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=4398#post4398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't like taking animal shapes, so he channels his shapeshifting prowess into control of his own body down to a cellular level so he can shrink momentarily when dodging or add some weight to his fist to give it a little extra centrifugal force on a punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is an interesting idea, and it would be easy enough to do, but it's not how their mechanics will work. This type of logos omits Essence and divinity from the equation, trading it for an ultra-mechanical, ultra-literal depiction of where their strength comes from. We can leave that kind of an expression to the Alchemicals. Very cool idea, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:45:53-08:00","id":24445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24442#post24442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I'm still making occidental dragons, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, dragon-making is a Sidereal thing! You're stealing my niche!<br /> <br /> Help! Help!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:48:02-08:00","id":24446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24416#post24416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Alex Mercer: No.<br /> <br /> Nor Carnage, the T-1000, or Twelve from Street Fighter, all of which are variations on Reed Richards and the Plastic Man when you boil them down. Fuck those guys.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What about Chimera being akin to Plastic Man?<br /> <br /> Failing that, would it be possible to make a Fair Folk in the Stretch Dude style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:53:21-08:00","id":24449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24401#post24401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas involving the Lunars joining the Sidereals in the Usurpation or being passive non-targets leaves me cold. The Lunars could no more opt out of the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation than Daenerys could opt out of King Robert's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're referencing.<br /> <br /> My only idea is that Lunars will have one little teeny bit of Silver Solar in them, and that's that they're free agents.<br /> <br /> Of course, I've also made a homebrew version of the Bond that facilitates this, so I'm coming from, like, a completely different angle here.<br /> <br /> But my problem has been, to an extent, having trouble thinking about where the Lunar's place in the Usurpation is or how their organization worked. The Solar Deliberative worked only because the kind of people who become Solars have such big egos they couldn't share power but basically had to, and therefore needed a forum to butt heads, while Sidereals and DBs were in a situation that encouraged cooperation. That I could buy.<br /> <br /> But Lunars, I couldn't but needing to form some kind of Pact, not by and large. Mutual protection, maybe, plain human 'We're the same color' prejudice combined with a need for mutual protection so the other splats didn't bully them? Yeah, I could buy it. But not that everyone joined up. I just don't see them being as aggressive or successfully aggressive about recruiting a Moon Chosen to the Pact.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand we're going to do this again. I'm so sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:57:21-08:00","id":24451,"title":"","content":"Brasstreader: Mm, no. I'm not talking about what kind of Lunars you can play. I'm talking about the political juxtaposition of the Lunars to everything else at the fall of the First Age, and the assertion that they should be a faction as varied as the Sidereals. This view distances them from the fallen Solar throne and has several boring consequences, starting with their further diminished relevance and continuing on to them being more like Sidereals and less like a unique actor.<br /> <br /> This sort of logic overlooks just how deeply the Lunars were entrenched in the political and social rule of the old Realm, and how inextricably they were connected to Solar rule. Lunars were the hands, eyes, and mouths of the Solars. They could even wear their faces! If the usurpers considered everything the Solars touched to have been tainted, Lunars would be at the top of the list. And through their power and influence, and their very nature, they represented a massive personal threat to the Sidereal Exalted, and always had\u2014the Lunars were always much, much closer to the throne than the Sidereals were.<br /> <br /> You could no more ignore the Lunars than Westeros could ignore Daenerys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:17:20-08:00","id":24467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24451#post24451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could no more ignore the Lunars than Westeros could ignore Daenerys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me for being thick.<br /> Yes. If I remember correctly, Tywin and Robert were rather pissed that the Targaryen kids 'escaped'. That was practically the first thing they attempted to address.<br /> So... this was just a full cleaning of the house, then, the Uprising. Like sweeping Akhenaten or Hatshepsut from the record of pharohs. Or just forgeting the pharohic lineages ever existed, and all their enforcers too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:19:30-08:00","id":24470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24416#post24416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Alex Mercer: No.<br /> <br /> Nor Carnage, the T-1000, or <b>Twelve from Street Fighter</b>, all of which are variations on Reed Richards and the Plastic Man when you boil them down. Fuck those guys.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Twelve was low tier, and perceived to be a gimmicky garbage tier character who only preyed on the match-up ignorance of his opponents. So the comparison to past Lunar perceptions here is a lot more accurate than at first glance!<br /> <br /> Glad to see you are feeling spirited enough to engage in a Lunars thread again, John.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:20:57-08:00","id":24472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24467#post24467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive me for being thick.<br /> Yes. If I remember correctly, Tywin and Robert were rather pissed that the Targaryen kids 'escaped'. That was practically the first thing they attempted to address.<br /> So... this was just a full cleaning of the house, then, the Uprising. Like sweeping Akhenaten or Hatshepsut from the record of pharohs. Or just forgeting the pharohic lineages ever existed, and all their enforcers too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Lunars are the Chosen of the Chosen, first and select princes of the universe. Ignoring them would be a hilarious oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:21:58-08:00","id":24475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24446#post24446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Chimera being akin to Plastic Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimera will look very, very different from how they did in 2e, and are basically just a means for Lunars to have multiple animals in their spirit shapes. Chimerism as Lunars devolving into (ironically) uniform big ol' blobs of flesh and murder is mercifully on the out.<br /> <br /> Can't speak for raksha, since we haven't heard a ton about their EX3 powers.* &gt;.&gt; In an act of high selfishness, I will personally prefer wordcount doesn't go toward stretchiness for them, either. Dreams and glamour and esoteric-weirdness-that-differs-from-Sidereal-esoteric-weirdness all/much of the way, please.<br /> <br /> * Though they seem to have the hamster excited. This is good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 12-06-2013, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:29:18-08:00","id":24490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24446#post24446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Chimera being akin to Plastic Man?<br /> <br /> Failing that, would it be possible to make a Fair Folk in the Stretch Dude style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me think about that. <a href=\"http://lagorama.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/_41909670_plasticman_220_ap.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://lagorama.com/wp-content/uploa...man_220_ap.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:34:17-08:00","id":24494,"title":"","content":"Thanks for speaking to us on the matter, John.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:38:15-08:00","id":24499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24423#post24423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please convince me The Mother Of Dragons can be that prominent on the world stage, and not be a Solar-Only character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scarlet Empress already showed that. ANYONE can be prominent on the world stage as long as they have the power, whatever form that power may take. For The Mother of Dragons, it was dragons. For the Scarlet Empress, it was the Realm Defense Grid. Heck, that one totally-mortal guy created the Guild with nothing more powerful than <i>an idea</i>.<br /> <br /> For a Lunar Exalt, it could be the returning Solar Exalted. Or anything else powerful enough to change the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24433#post24433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daenerys's ascent is made possible by dragons, and she is one of the most-beloved fictional heroines in modern memory. Yet if a Lunar depends on the long-extinct and newly resurrected Solar to make a power play, some people throw up in their mouths. I'm not compelled by the stories people think they can't tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I don't mind.<br /> <br /> A Lunar attempting to use a Solar to turn the tables and finally conquer the world is a more feasible strategy than we've yet seen ANY Lunar NPC attempt in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24435#post24435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the T-1000, and the archetypal genius of Reed Richards, I despise pretty much everything about &quot;stretchy guy&quot; characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that's a no on the &quot;rubberman&quot; Getimians and Liminals? Or is it pretty much limited to Dhalism's limb-extention?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24446#post24446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Chimera being akin to Plastic Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on developer comments, I think Chimera is going to be more like a Lion-totemed Lunar adding Goat and Snake to his Totem than like becoming effectively formless like Clayface or Inque.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Failing that, would it be possible to make a Fair Folk in the Stretch Dude style? </div> </div> </div>That seems more likely, but I think the developers are moving away from depicting the Fair Folk as fourth-wall breaking cartoonish figures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2013, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:38:27-08:00","id":24500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24433#post24433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the comparison I was making. But I'll go ahead and bite: Daenerys's ascent is made possible by dragons, and she is one of the most-beloved fictional heroines in modern memory. Yet if a Lunar depends on the long-extinct and newly resurrected Solar to make a power play, some people throw up in their mouths. I'm not compelled by the stories people think they can't tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is a bit of an oversimplification. There's nothing wrong with a lunar or another type using a solar or even a dragon-blooded to make a power play. The problem is 2e had a definitely lean towards solars to the extent that they were they only exalted type that was relevant as the gameline progressed. Which was an issue for a majority of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:42:12-08:00","id":24506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24490#post24490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me think about that. <a href=\"http://lagorama.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/07/_41909670_plasticman_220_ap.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://lagorama.com/wp-content/uploa...man_220_ap.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I could be imagining things, but I think Plastic Man is forming the letters &quot;N&quot; with his neck and &quot;O&quot; with his arm.<br /> <br /> Which, you know, might clarify the answer for some people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:49:33-08:00","id":24514,"title":"","content":"I also find something unsatisfying in the assertion that a sizable number of Lunars would join the Sidereals just to live it up in Heaven, because, well, they were already living it up in Creation, with greater prestige than they would have had in this theoretical arrangement with the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> That and it doesn't lend much thought to why Sidereals should have accepted or made such overtures, unless it was for some reason that amounted to &quot;they wanted Lunars to just step out of the way&quot;, which doesn't really lend much credibility to the Lunars, and seems like the kind of thing that, carried to its logical conclusion, leaves you with Lunars with no impact just as they had in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> It's like the Silver Faction; it's a concept for the sake of forced symmetry without really considering the context or implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:51:05-08:00","id":24517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24435#post24435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting aside the T-1000, and the archetypal genius of Reed Richards, I despise pretty much everything about &quot;stretchy guy&quot; characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Jake the Dog?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:51:47-08:00","id":24518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24514#post24514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like the Silver Faction; it's a concept for the sake of forced symmetry without really considering the context or implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please. Don't get on this topic I'll just annoy to death with a long and needless debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T11:55:16-08:00","id":24524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24446#post24446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failing that, would it be possible to make a Fair Folk in the Stretch Dude style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've always been put off by how many of the offensive raksha tricks relied on them undermining their own aesthetic values.<br /> <br /> You can be an incomparably beautiful and graceful swordsman clothed in fire and poetic accounts of your own exploits, and yet you've probably still got to go in for some stretchy arm stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:02:04-08:00","id":24527,"title":"","content":"Another thing that might help separate Lunars from beastmen in the minds of the audience would be if the books (the art, in particular) depicted DBTs that weren't just big blokes with animal heads. After all, &quot;blokes with animal heads&quot; is how the books depict beastmen, too, which kind of blurs the line between one and the other, to the detriment of both.<br /> <br /> So, personally, I'd like to see the occasional warform that invokes things like manticores or Howl's monster-bird form in the Ghibli film, in addition to the classic look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:16:08-08:00","id":24537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24419#post24419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Challenge accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happiness!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:23:23-08:00","id":24544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24517#post24517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Jake the Dog?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can behave like the most Lunar Mate to have ever lunar mated to a Solar, and yet not have abilities which act anything like a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Was it you or someone else who twiced mentioned Zero, from <i>Mega Man X</i>, behaving very much like X's older and more experienced Lunar Mate? When both of them are otherwise staple Alchemical inspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:27:57-08:00","id":24548,"title":"","content":"I'm not necessarily concerned with whether Jake's ability set would resemble what a Lunar could do.<br /> <br /> Just... does John not like him?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:44:56-08:00","id":24559,"title":"","content":"But then who <i>do</i> I use when I want to toss Carnage at my players?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:46:13-08:00","id":24560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24548#post24548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not necessarily concerned with whether Jake's ability set would resemble what a Lunar could do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, <a href=\"http://youtu.be/31ygWdAG0QU?t=9m51s\" target=\"_blank\">it<i> should</i></a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:49:14-08:00","id":24564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24559#post24559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then who <i>do</i> I use when I want to toss Carnage at my players?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Carnage.<br /> <i>Carnage.<br /> <b>Carnage.<br /> <u>Carnage.</u></b></i><br /> <br /> You'd think with a name like that, Abyssals would be all over that. there's even a Martial Arts Charm in their core with blood-chain-making tentacles. I'd think the answer was obvious.<br /> That being said, Fair Folk and Liminals would also be neat Carnages. Especially since Fair Folk have a suite of Assumption Charms that let them appeal as Artifacts, markings on willing mortals, and other nifty items. Why not a Symbiote?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:53:23-08:00","id":24567,"title":"","content":"Which would mean a Chimera would look more like... A Chimera. Meaning the mythical creature. And less like a play-doh turd. I like that, because working chimerism might be something, I'd want to explore for a Lunar. Because I like my Lunars to be far away from Garou. This is a personal preference, nothing else. But it's a strong personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:53:42-08:00","id":24568,"title":"","content":"It's a shame my Chimera treatment on the old forums got erased : it was the post I came out of a 'retirement' from the forums on, and it was fairly well recieved.<br /> <br /> In essence, I felt that Chimerism should focus not on erosion of body or thematic form cohesion but rather the soul - Chimera were willing to sacrifice the 'Self' in the sense of individuality, become more like the Wyld and those that inhabited it. By shedding trappings of identity, they gained mutability. By becoming a force of nature rather than a living creature with consistant dreams, goals and values... they gained adaptability.<br /> <br /> A Chimera abandons her name, abandons her family, abandons her virtues and abandons everything about herself. She becomes pure whim and fancy, but throughout all this she is gifted with an immutable and eternal Exaltation. This allows her a strange paradox. The Chimera, alone of all beings in Creation, can 'melt' completely in the Wyld... and yet remain a cohesive entity, not undone. They can 'die' as the Wyld eats them, yet live on forever.<br /> <br /> It's a strange paradox that many Lunars would find terrifying. That said, this philosophy cannot be said to be -innately- evil... unless you take into account that such a being would probably not ascribe to any form of human (or Exalted) morality at all, and would be capable of actions that would shock even the most cold hearted. As a further irony, the being would be able to undertake these actions with even a sort of quasi-innocence, childlike and incorruptible...<br /> <br /> ... in this way, the state of Chimerism could even have unique benifits. A Chimera would have immense control over Intimacies (or no intimacies at all, alternately), rendering them immune to many conventional methods of control or domination.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of such a transition are simple enough to envision. By abandoning parts of your sheet... your 'dots'... you gain become more of a Chimera. When you abandon you set Attributes, you've begun the path. Abandoning set Abilities is a further erosion of self. But the true challenges come beyond that - abandoning your Intimacies, abandoning your Virtues, abandoning your very name. These steps are so final, so changing, that few Chimera ever complete the journey. Those that do become relatively blase about the fate of Creation or those within it... unless, of course, the mood strikes them to care for a short time before they shift into a new paradigm of ideology and psychology.<br /> <br /> A true Chimera, who has pursued this philosophy to the ultimate extreme, has fed the Wyld everything about her that once defined her - every dot on the sheet, every notation, every specialty, ever merit. All except for the single thing she cannot ever truly dissolve in the Wyld essence - the words 'Lunar Exalted', immutable on the very fabric of her being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-06-2013, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T12:57:45-08:00","id":24571,"title":"","content":"<br /> In Ars Magica there is a house of wizards called the Bjornaer who have the ability to change into their heartbeast by will alone.<br /> <br /> In the white wolf edition of the game (in several ways regarded as the worst one) people thought about what they could do to expand this ability and came up with- change into other things by will alone.<br /> <br /> This was pretty lame in that your character who's essential nature was tied in with their animal decided to work with their inner spirit and as a result they could became less thematically tied to their animal (and therefore more lame). Perhaps this was exacerbated by the fact that turning into an animal by means of the magic that all wizards in the game get is pretty straightforward and while not especially easy neither is it the most difficult thing to do.<br /> <br /> In the present edition the character who delves into the mysteries of the heartbeast has the option of making their heart beast a more perfect example of the platonic ideal of that animal, an elementally associated version of that animal or a combination of that animal with one additional animal. Further study does not dilute the conceptual core of the character. This is far more rewarding.<br /> <br /> For lunars I don't want my choice of a mouse heart shape to prevent me from growing wings, but I also don't want my heart shape to become irrelevant. I'd like to see some mechanical uniqueness to the heart shape. It should be qualitatively different from other forms. On the other hand the min-maxer in me has in previous editions had a difficult time choosing a heart shape without thought to its effectiveness for DBT.<br /> <br /> I want heart shape to be important (to give the character a tight theme) but also irrelevant (in that it doesn't have any significant effects on how much rear I can kick, therefore I can feel free to choose something other than brown bear, tyrant lizard, or saber toothed vampire dire badger without feeling that I am walking away from a much more efficient use of my points). How hard can that be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 05-09-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:02:06-08:00","id":24574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24401#post24401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas involving the Lunars joining the Sidereals in the Usurpation or being passive non-targets leaves me cold. The Lunars could no more opt out of the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation than Daenerys could opt out of King Robert's.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with that is &quot;Ok, the Sidereals decided they could trust the vast majority of Dragon-Blooded to go along with this, but didn't even once consider asking a few Lunars they were pretty sure they could trust to join the coup? Heck, maybe they had to have all the Sids join together to do the prophesy, but some of those guys ended up siding with the Solars. Why wouldn't you think you could get some Lunars to side with you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically it all boils down to the fact that I don't think there has ever been a satisfactory answer to why the Sids decided they had to kill/drive off all the Lunars, other than &quot;The Lunars weren't a playable splat until just before we finished the book, so we basically forgot about them.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 3e the question becomes even bigger, because there are going to be more Exalted out there and at least some of them were active in the First Age. I mean, I really don't see the UCS setting up the Exigence after the Primordial War was over, so there must have been some of those guys out there at the bare minimum. Also the Niobraran Exalted types presumably still existed in one form or another. And so on.<br /> <br /> What happened to them? Did the Sids kill everyone but the DBs? Why did they do that? Why not keep some of the Exigents around? And so on.<br /> <br /> John, please tell me that we will get an actual answer for why the Sids did what they did this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:03:30-08:00","id":24575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24568#post24568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a shame my Chimera treatment on the old forums got erased : it was the post I came out of a 'retirement' from the forums on, and it was fairly well recieved.<br /> <br /> In essence, I felt that Chimerism should focus not on erosion of body or thematic form cohesion but rather the soul - Chimera were willing to sacrifice the 'Self' in the sense of individuality, become more like the Wyld and those that inhabited it. By shedding trappings of identity, they gained mutability. By becoming a force of nature rather than a living creature with consistant dreams, goals and values... they gained adaptability.<br /> <br /> A Chimera abandons her name, abandons her family, abandons her virtues and abandons everything about herself. She becomes pure whim and fancy, but throughout all this she is gifted with an immutable and eternal Exaltation. This allows her a strange paradox. The Chimera, alone of all beings in Creation, can 'melt' completely in the Wyld... and yet remain a cohesive entity, not undone. They can 'die' as the Wyld eats them, yet live on forever.<br /> <br /> It's a strange paradox that many Lunars would find terrifying. That said, this philosophy cannot be said to be -innately- evil... unless you take into account that such a being would probably not ascribe to any form of human (or Exalted) morality at all, and would be capable of actions that would shock even the most cold hearted. As a further irony, the being would be able to undertake these actions with even a sort of quasi-innocence, childlike and incorruptible...<br /> <br /> ... in this way, the state of Chimerism could even have unique benifits. A Chimera would have immense control over Intimacies (or no intimacies at all, alternately), rendering them immune to many conventional methods of control or domination.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of such a transition are simple enough to envision. By abandoning parts of your sheet... your 'dots'... you gain become more of a Chimera. When you abandon you set Attributes, you've begun the path. Abandoning set Abilities is a further erosion of self. But the true challenges come beyond that - abandoning your Intimacies, abandoning your Virtues, abandoning your very name. These steps are so final, so changing, that few Chimera ever complete the journey. Those that do become relatively blase about the fate of Creation or those within it... unless, of course, the mood strikes them to care for a short time before they shift into a new paradigm of ideology and psychology.<br /> <br /> A true Chimera, who has pursued this philosophy to the ultimate extreme, has fed the Wyld everything about her that once defined her - every dot on the sheet, every notation, every specialty, ever merit. All except for the single thing she cannot ever truly dissolve in the Wyld essence - the words 'Lunar Exalted', immutable on the very fabric of her being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from some weird devotion to the abstract concept of adaptability, what does a Lunar get out of any of this?<br /> <br /> Also, it might be okay for a kind of one-off antagonistic monster (which really makes it seem better suited as a behemoth then), but you can't really make interesting characters out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:09:22-08:00","id":24583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24559#post24559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then who <i>do</i> I use when I want to toss Carnage at my players?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be an Infernal. Or a Fae. Or an exalted of some god of slaughter/madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:14:11-08:00","id":24592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24559#post24559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then who <i>do</i> I use when I want to toss Carnage at my players?!</div> </div> </div> </div>An Infernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:32:25-08:00","id":24601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24574#post24574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with that is &quot;Ok, the Sidereals decided they could trust the vast majority of Dragon-Blooded to go along with this, but didn't even once consider asking a few Lunars they were pretty sure they could trust to join the coup? Heck, maybe they had to have all the Sids join together to do the prophesy, but some of those guys ended up siding with the Solars. Why wouldn't you think you could get some Lunars to side with you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically it all boils down to the fact that I don't think there has ever been a satisfactory answer to why the Sids decided they had to kill/drive off all the Lunars, other than &quot;The Lunars weren't a playable splat until just before we finished the book, so we basically forgot about them.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 3e the question becomes even bigger, because there are going to be more Exalted out there and at least some of them were active in the First Age. I mean, I really don't see the UCS setting up the Exigence after the Primordial War was over, so there must have been some of those guys out there at the bare minimum. Also the Niobraran Exalted types presumably still existed in one form or another. And so on.<br /> <br /> What happened to them? Did the Sids kill everyone but the DBs? Why did they do that? Why not keep some of the Exigents around? And so on.<br /> <br /> John, please tell me that we will get an actual answer for why the Sids did what they did this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's obvious - all the Lunars were wearing the trademarked 'TEAM LUNAR' T-shirts, which clearly indicated that they belonged to a splat that could never have any ideological or political sympathy for the Sidereal cause, regardless of context.<br /> <br /> The fact that all Lunars think alike and are very difficult to tell apart from one another helped a great deal with this.<br /> <br /> The 'Team (whatever)' T-shirts were apparently selling like hotcakes around Usurpation time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:44:38-08:00","id":24613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24601#post24601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any ideological or political sympathy for the Sidereal cause, regardless of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what context do the Lunars support the Dragon Blooded being elevated above them in control of the Realm?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:46:55-08:00","id":24615,"title":"","content":"One possibility IS to simply write-off the Lunars' impact on the setting as a whole coherent splat and emphasize the impact individual Lunars have made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:56:02-08:00","id":24623,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's kind of like being annoyed at how the people murdered in the French Revolution were primarily the nobility, and mostly by the working and lower middle classes, and thinking that this means that the nobles were all wearing &quot;Team Ancien Regime&quot; shirts and asking where all the nobles who supported the Revolutionary cause were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:57:51-08:00","id":24626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24574#post24574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it all boils down to the fact that I don't think there has ever been a satisfactory answer to why the Sids decided they had to kill/drive off all the Lunars, other than &quot;The Lunars weren't a playable splat until just before we finished the book, so we basically forgot about them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24601#post24601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's obvious - all the Lunars were wearing the trademarked 'TEAM LUNAR' T-shirts, which clearly indicated that they belonged to a splat that could never have any ideological or political sympathy for the Sidereal cause, regardless of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guys, Hatewheel already TOLD us why. <i>In this thread.</i> On the previous page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24451#post24451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of logic overlooks just how deeply the Lunars were entrenched in the political and social rule of the old Realm, and how inextricably they were connected to Solar rule. Lunars were the hands, eyes, and mouths of the Solars. They could even wear their faces! If the usurpers considered everything the Solars touched to have been tainted, Lunars would be at the top of the list. And through their power and influence, and their very nature, they represented a massive personal threat to the Sidereal Exalted, and always had\u2014the Lunars were always much, much closer to the throne than the Sidereals were.<br /> <br /> You could no more ignore the Lunars than Westeros could ignore Daenerys.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's also not saying exceptions were impossible; he's rejecting the idea that enough Lunars could be trusted to work with the Usurpation to form any kind of trend. Exceptions would have been exceptional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:59:31-08:00","id":24630,"title":"","content":"In fact, there were tons of noble sympathetic to or directly supporting the Revolutionary cause! Mostly they died too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T14:11:13-08:00","id":24640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24626#post24626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's also not saying exceptions were impossible; he's rejecting the idea that enough Lunars could be trusted to work with the Usurpation to form any kind of trend. Exceptions would have been exceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably much like how we get a sample Getimian said to be disillusioned with Thulio's cause and so working alongside Yu-Shan, and yet the summary of Getimians as a whole does not tell us about the great faction apart from the War on Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T14:29:02-08:00","id":24648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24640#post24640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably much like how we get a sample Getimian said to be disillusioned with Thulio's cause and so working alongside Yu-Shan, and yet the summary of Getimians as a whole does not tell us about the great faction apart from the War on Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Only I didn't use that example because I couldn't be sure if that really WAS so exceptional. There very well could be a small trend of Getimians working for Heaven rather than against it as part of Thulio's agenda.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation is different in that it only had one shot and absolutely needed to succeed. The on-going war over heaven between the Bureau of Destiny and Rakan Thulio, on the other hand, has no particular time-limit and it's unlikely that one single lost battle or set-back can win that war.<br /> <br /> Further, given how thoroughly Morke says that Lunar Exalted as a whole were invested in the First Age's power structure, I'm pretty sure that the number of them that would support the Usurpation's WHOLE agenda was vanishingly rare. Since that whole agenda not only involved killing off some asshole Solars, but ALL Solars, good and bad, and ensuring they would NEVER return, which pretty much destroys the whole world as the Lunars know it... and it's a world of which they live at the top and have no where to go but DOWN.<br /> <br /> Plus, the agenda of the Usurption included the destruction of the Lunar Exalted AS WELL, because of the Solar Bond. The Sidereals could not leave a single Lunar Exalted in power, because they absolutely could not risk a Star-Crossed Lovers situation in which a Solar Mate gained the Lunar's sympathy. Plus, the Sidereals needed the Terrestrials in control, and ANY Lunar left in power would create even more conflict and power-struggling than would have happened between the Dragon-Blooded alone.<br /> <br /> A Lunar truly on-board with the Usurpation would have to accept the idea that the Sidereal Exalted could not afford to let HIM live either, and I just can't see many Lunars being okay with getting exiled and hunted to death for the rest of their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Returning to Getimians, however, well... Getimians aren't bonded to Solar Exalted. Getimians are relative new kids on the block without a massive entrenched power-structure that the Sidereals want to utterly destroy and keep from ever returning.<br /> <br /> Getimians can probably be trusted within arm's reach because they can get a pretty sweet deal working with Heaven rather than against it.<br /> <br /> OR... maybe it really is just that one guy -- and your PC(s) -- as the special snowflake exception(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T15:00:19-08:00","id":24666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24574#post24574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened to them? Did the Sids kill everyone but the DBs? Why did they do that? Why not keep some of the Exigents around? And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The broader points on Lunars have been addressed by others, but this one -- and by extension the question of what happened with all other Exalted -- was touched on by Holden:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since people have asked quite a few times-- no, Exigents aren't Anathema. The Immaculate Order and its Sidereal architects aren't simpletons and in the bigger, wider setting of EX3, &quot;all non-DB Exalts&quot; isn't a workable Anathema definition. Exigents basically fall under the same heading as God-Blooded-- the result of improper congress between gods and mortals, and thus shameful and karmically banjaxed, but not the end of the world or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all other Exalted were dealt with or not dealt with as it made sense. None were as tightly connected to and entrenched with the Solars as Lunars, so none of them -- with possibly vanishingly few exceptions -- were painted with the Anathema brush.<br /> <br /> Also, while off-topic,<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I really don't see the UCS setting up the Exigence after the Primordial War was over, so there must have been some of those guys out there at the bare minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think it likely Exigents were around during the War, I wouldn't assume that. We know too little about the Exigence. For all we know, setting it up may not have even been possible -- or at least feasible -- until the end of the War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T15:37:35-08:00","id":24697,"title":"","content":"One thing that probably helps the Silver Pact is to view it at least partially in terms of a collective response to conditions imposed upon them, rather than something that all Lunars just happen to stumble upon independently.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Blooded and the Sidereals are the ones who started this, the ones who cast the Solars down and saw the Lunars, the raging, storming Lunars who had been closer to the crazed, tainted Solars than anybody, as a threat to their new order and drove them out and continue to hound them.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact would probably be at least partially a reactionary movement.<br /> <br /> And the thing about reactionary movements is that since they're all reacting to something, the opposition is probably the same.<br /> <br /> But when you look closer at them, everything else they want tends to be rather different.<br /> <br /> There will probably still be some Lunars who are more actively motivated by the Usurpation, by a desire for revenge for themselves and their Solars and a desire to reclaim their old possessions.<br /> <br /> And such Lunars will be old and powerful, and reactionary movements tend to elevate such figures, so their personal agendas will bleed into a lot of collective rhetoric.<br /> <br /> But still, on a practical level, most of them are being motivated more by the fact that they're living in a world controlled by the enemy. An enemy who, in the course of setting themselves up on their stolen thrones, developed a lot of demonising retroactive justification, that's become so pervasive, and backed up by lifetimes of mutual violence, that it's hard to just turn around and say &quot;no, wait, let's judge each Lunar on their merits and make open friends with the acceptable ones&quot;, because it's gone too far for that.<br /> <br /> At least until somebody goes and does it, but history is one long wait for people to do things that are smart and right.<br /> <br /> And all of this makes for a Silver Pact which is likely to be fractious and constantly shifting and filled with various, often contradictory, ideas about what exactly to do next (that won't be hashed out until tomorrow because there's a war to fight today), and more than a bit of resolving internal disputes through various unpleasant means.<br /> <br /> That they have a mutual enemy does not mean that they won't have disagreements with one another, but it also doesn't mean that there are necessarily lots of separate Silver Pacts all doing their own thing, or that there are bunches of Lunars who align with the enemy (who don't want them anyway), although there conflicts amongst themselves probably inadvertently help the enemy (the same as conflicts within the single Scarlet Dynasty and single Fivescore Fellowship probably help the Lunars, without those also being cases where those are Exalted who are generally viewed as a collective, bound by ties extending from, but not limited to, their mutual category).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:01:59-08:00","id":24716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24648#post24648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Further, given how thoroughly Morke says that Lunar Exalted as a whole were invested in the First Age's power structure, I'm pretty sure that the number of them that would support the Usurpation's WHOLE agenda was vanishingly rare. Since that whole agenda not only involved killing off some asshole Solars, but ALL Solars, good and bad, and ensuring they would NEVER return, which pretty much destroys the whole world as the Lunars know it... and it's a world of which they live at the top and have no where to go but DOWN.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this proposes that the TEAM SIDEREAL shirts have a detailed synopsis of the Usurpation on the back that fully and completely explains the plans they have.<br /> <br /> They don't have to do that. They can just lie and manipulate, like they are infamous for doing/being able to do.<br /> <br /> I have observed in history that...<br /> <br /> A) Very few revolutions are undertaken for the reasons that the people who undertake them believe,<br /> B) Very few people participating in the revolution have any idea what will eventually happen after it succeeds,<br /> C) People who are making a revolution happen are interested in gathering as many allies as possible.<br /> D) People who are making a revolution happen are not interested in being honest beyond whatever amount of honesty serves the goal.<br /> E) Environments which are ripe for revolution usually have lots of dissatisfied people, even amongst the elite, who are envious of others.<br /> F) These people are often manipulated to achieve the aims of the revolution.<br /> G) Said elites are often instrumental to the actual accomplishment of revolutionary gains, even if they are sometimes (often) discarded after.<br /> <br /> I frankly find the idea that the Lunar Exalted of the time of the Usurpation were 'so entrenched' with the Solars that they had no issue with the government ridiculous. It proposes a single unified Solar powerbase, which is in and of itself silly ; multiple Solar 'camps' would exist, each using rhetoric and ideology to paint competing factions as dangerous and ineffective.<br /> <br /> Obviously, multiple factions of Lunar Exalted would have also existed that had huge slights against the existing power structure ; either because they didn't have a big enough seat at the table, Solar Joe fucked her sister, or just because they don't like the same music that Joe does.<br /> <br /> The idea that the SOLARS are a big happy family come usurpation time is silly. The idea that the Lunars are ALSO such a big happy family is also silly. Finally, the idea that the Sidereals... who needed every advantage they could get... would hesitate to ensare these people in the battle is also ridiculous. They don't give one shit about Team Lunar T-shirts. The goal is political, not splatist. They need to eliminate the state so they can take control ; they will weaken it in any way they possibly can, through devious manipulation and conspiracy, which they are obviously predisposed towards.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals should be taking advantage of a dangerous time of political uncertainty and change that allowed them the singular opportunity to leverage a number of discorporate elements into a Usurpation ; probably much more suddenly than they liked, probably much more dangerously than they liked, and probably not as effectively as they liked.<br /> <br /> The conspiracy should have a LARGE PORTION of Solar / Lunar participants, who are later discarded, but are brought into the whole thing with promises of Everything They Ever Dreamed once this is all over.<br /> <br /> This would mirror ACTUAL revolutions rather than comic book battles between the X-Men and the League of Evil Mutants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-06-2013, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:47:48-08:00","id":24745,"title":"","content":"Don't use offensive words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:01:06-08:00","id":24752,"title":"","content":"Offensive words are the best thing ever.<br /> <br /> But alas, while Miss Maddy's idea sounds plausible, I guess I kinda agree with a reactionary Silver Pact. Still, I wanna see Lunars jerking around doing their own thing to not only be an option but an option no one is surprised by and only a minority of people they meet think it's a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:04:02-08:00","id":24753,"title":"","content":"As for factions:<br /> <br /> The factions of the Solars were irrelevant; the Prophecy said that they would destroy the world, and had to be replaced by the Dragon Blooded to stop it.<br /> <br /> The factions of the Lunars were irrelevent; they were peers and partners of the Solars, and were too strong to be left unchecked in a world ruled by the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Would trying to use some Solars and Lunars against the others have helped?<br /> <br /> If everything went according to plan, every single Solar would have died at the Calibration Feast, because the might of the Solars was such that drawing a fight out of them would cause devastation.<br /> <br /> Considering this plan according to a model of &quot;we should save some of the Solars for later&quot; seems... odd. That the Solars weren't all destroyed at once, and some of them got to drag the fighting out, was first blood for the Shogunate. Why should they want to make use of that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:12:02-08:00","id":24759,"title":"","content":"B-b-b-but (reflexive qualifying statement) makes for weak, shitty writing and unclear communication of ideas. There's always exceptions to any idea. Don't get mad because I don't take the time to spell them out for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:19:08-08:00","id":24763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24574#post24574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with that is &quot;Ok, the Sidereals decided they could trust the vast majority of Dragon-Blooded to go along with this, but didn't even once consider asking a few Lunars they were pretty sure they could trust to join the coup?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right up there with asking a few trusted Solars to join the coup. I really mean that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:20:13-08:00","id":24765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24716#post24716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I frankly find the idea that the Lunar Exalted of the time of the Usurpation were 'so entrenched' with the Solars that they had no issue with the government ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyranny is pretty awesome when you sit at the right hand of the tyrant, and that makes it way easier to overlook things that bother you about the whole thing, or try to deal with those issues in a way that doesn't also collapse your mode of living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:21:29-08:00","id":24767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24745#post24745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't use offensive words.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean using All Caps repeatedly to emphasis words?<br /> <br /> That's what jumped out at me, skimming over Maddy's post... and then I looked back at my own post and was properly ashamed.<br /> <br /> Especially now that I can just Ctrl+I for emphasis, resorting to All Caps is lazy and too much like shouting at people over the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:25:38-08:00","id":24768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24767#post24767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean using All Caps repeatedly to emphasis words?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty much entirely sure that he means her use of the word &quot;retarded.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:28:08-08:00","id":24769,"title":"","content":"If your goal is to execute a sudden, decisive, as-close-to-overnight-as-you-can-get-it toppling of the Bureau of Destiny, execution of its employees, and destruction of the Loom of Fate, how many Sidereals do you approach to join your venture, assuming that the whole plan doesn't start off revolving around the aid of a willing traitor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:37:26-08:00","id":24774,"title":"","content":"Personally, my model for the First Age accommodates the potential and actuality for Lunars to be dissatisfied with any relative Solar government, and to act on such, within the boundaries one would expect of their relationship with any given Solar.<br /> <br /> My model for the First Age has it that, at various periods, there have been revolutions against Solars (often sanctioned or aided on some level by other Solars, especially in those cases where the latter is Chosen within troublesome circumstances prompted by the former). These include occasions where Dragon Blooded families (or other Exalted) rebel against ruling Solars for one reason or another; the response this brings from other Solars, including the Deliberative, varies with the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Maybe these occasions were becoming less common as the Age drew to a close, and the Solars became more uniform in their excesses, but the concept was not unknown.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation was not those things. The Usurpation was a changing of the order of the world on a mythic scale. The Usurpation was ending the Age of the Solars to usher in the Age of the Dragon Blooded, to change the definition of &quot;mightiest of the Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> This isn't smaller nations sometimes beating the United States, this is all the smaller nations collectively ganging up to literally wipe the United States from the map.<br /> <br /> It's a revolution, but it's also the Twilight of the Gods.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Dragon Blooded were acting on certain personal or political issues, but they wouldn't have done so to such a degree and with such a coordination if there hadn't been Sidereals whispering encouragements and instructions in their ears, and the Sidereals were motivated by a vision saying &quot;if the Solars remain, the world is doomed&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Lunars did not have so much to gain from such a dramatic reversal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:43:18-08:00","id":24779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24435#post24435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting aside the T-1000, and the archetypal genius of Reed Richards, I despise pretty much everything about &quot;stretchy guy&quot; characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't like Jake from Adventure time? Come on, Dimaggio!<br /> <br /> Man, now you've got me thinking about where to draw the line around this archetype, and what defines it as a thing. The comic archetype seems a bit distinct from things like the T-1000 or Odo from Deep Space Nine, because they have a similar power, but rather than presenting that power in a serious way they use it as a sort of...physical punning? I think the reason those characters tend to be kind of jokey is that the power tends to be used as a way to use exaggeration and blur the lines between people and objects for comedic energy, which puts them in the same concept space as a lot of classic American cartooning (animated or otherwise). I think the reason you see them so much in comics is that the style of humour they use is leveraging the &quot;pseudo-realism&quot; of the medium, where a lot of its energy comes from representing reality in a distorted or metaphorical way. In that context I think the stretchiness is not so much <i>about</i> shapeshifting as it is a justification for a kind of image-play. I think <i>in theory</i> that's a rich concept space for raksha, because it has that aspect of relying on the real while subverting it. In practice I can't see a good way to make it work, though, both because it's a nonvisual medium and because it's hard to throw Plastic Man into a fantasy epic without leaving everybody irritated.<br /> <br /> But then, aside from those guys, you've got a bunch of other characters who mostly play the gimmick straight -- the T-1000 is the granddaddy here and has many derivatives, but at the lower-power/higher-realism end I would include, say, Dhalsim from Street Fighter. I think Exalted has room for published material that explores this space, but I would tend to give it to different people depending.<br /> <br /> T-1000-style &quot;amorphous blob that can redistribute its mass at will&quot; shapeshifting feels very modern: there's little precedent for it before the modern era, and it's one of those superpowers where people take an idea with internal, physical consistency and explore what it would be like if it existed, which is not something you saw a lot of before science fiction. I lump it in with telekinesis, teleportation, and so forth, for that reason. I wouldn't say that nothing in Exalted should work that way, but it feels very far from the earthy sword-and-sandal animism the game is built around, so I think if I were going to add it, I'd give it to one of the &quot;weird otherworldly&quot; types, like Abyssals or Infernals. I don't like it for Lunars because to me Lunars feel very worldly and rooted in the &quot;ancient myth&quot; motif, and it has dissonance with that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I <i>do</i> like Lunars to have some stuff at the low end of this scale, like that Dhalsim-stretch range enhancer Charm whose name I can't remember. I definitely think there's room for appropriately specialized Lunars to be <i>weirdly fluid</i>: bending like they don't have bones, snapping upright from a prone position like a bent switch, weaving back and forth with an animation-style stretch/smear that makes it hard to hit their weak points, surviving killing blows by just not having their organs where they're supposed to be, etc. I think a lot of Lunar players would be unhappy being forced into that aesthetic, but it seems like a legitimate place to allow people to explore if they want to, particularly in Dexterity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:51:24-08:00","id":24783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24779#post24779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I <i>do</i> like Lunars to have some stuff at the low end of this scale, like that Dhalsim-stretch range enhancer Charm whose name I can't remember. I definitely think there's room for appropriately specialized Lunars to be <i>weirdly fluid</i>: bending like they don't have bones, snapping upright from a prone position like a bent switch, weaving back and forth with an animation-style stretch/smear that makes it hard to hit their weak points, surviving killing blows by just not having their organs where they're supposed to be, etc. I think a lot of Lunar players would be unhappy being forced into that aesthetic, but it seems like a legitimate place to allow people to explore if they want to, particularly in Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is some concept space between Flesh Shintai from KotE, and Monkey D. Luffy or Plastic Man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:56:19-08:00","id":24786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24783#post24783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is some concept space between Flesh Shintai from KotE, and Monkey D. Luffy or Plastic Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh shit now I'm imagining a Plastic Man expy Tzimisce","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:08:26-08:00","id":24794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24626#post24626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Guys, Hatewheel already TOLD us why. <i>In this thread.</i> On the previous page.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He's also not saying exceptions were impossible; he's rejecting the idea that enough Lunars could be trusted to work with the Usurpation to form any kind of trend. Exceptions would have been exceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I missed that post. I'm good then!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:11:05-08:00","id":24801,"title":"","content":"In the end, efforts to justify the lazy writing of the 1e Usurpation just kinda fall flat for me because... as we all know... it was just badly written, before much of this was really defined or thought through.<br /> <br /> 3e presents perhaps the best and most salient opportunity to correct some of these issues, but instead, we're struggling to justify a pretty silly history.<br /> <br /> The tone of our gritty, serious, deconstructive game feels weird when we combine it with a 'secretive, epic history' that is about as sophisticated as the history from the 80s 'Transformer' cartoon.<br /> <br /> We should just be honest and self-critical about how overly simplistic the 1e story was. It comes from the era of Vampire where that sorta thing was happening a lot at WW. Nothing to be defensive about.<br /> <br /> This can change. If we're spending so much time 'making the mechanics perfect', a pass at some of these basic story issues would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:13:12-08:00","id":24804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24769#post24769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your goal is to execute a sudden, decisive, as-close-to-overnight-as-you-can-get-it toppling of the Bureau of Destiny, execution of its employees, and destruction of the Loom of Fate, how many Sidereals do you approach to join your venture, assuming that the whole plan doesn't start off revolving around the aid of a willing traitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is a serious question?<br /> <br /> As many as I feel that I can count on being loyal to my cause. Depending on the specific incentives provided by context, and the specific personalities involved in the Sidereal host, this might involve quite a few people... <i>perhaps even a majority of Sidereals</i>.<br /> <br /> It really all depends on if Kejak took a crap in the punch bowl recently.<br /> <br /> <br /> Certainly, if I have lovers or people I have hung out with every day for CENTURIES, and I know them REALLY WELL, then yeah... those guys are gonna stand with me. We're sworn comrades.<br /> <br /> ... of course, this all assumes a world where I ignore the T-shirts, and actually measure my allies and enemies by like... personal accomplishments, ideology, bias, personal history, and sometimes just raw 'gut feeling'. But that'd never happen to Exalted human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-06-2013, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:14:16-08:00","id":24806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24794#post24794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I missed that post. I'm good then!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Pretty much sold me as well.<br /> 'Course, I'm biased because one of my favorite characters to play was a Shogunate Gens soldier/televised monster hunter... who they knew was a Changing Moon. She Exalted, post-Uprising, right in front of her men during a raksha attack, and might have been a war hero if not for the fact. Was it a tightrope to walk? Yes it was. But it felt like it <i>could</i> have worked. At least during the first two centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:18:36-08:00","id":24810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24769#post24769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your goal is to execute a sudden, decisive, as-close-to-overnight-as-you-can-get-it toppling of the Bureau of Destiny, execution of its employees, and destruction of the Loom of Fate, how many Sidereals do you approach to join your venture, assuming that the whole plan doesn't start off revolving around the aid of a willing traitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>None, obviously, but you might consider approaching some gods who work in said bureau, especially if you can get them cushy jobs in the bureau of heaven afterwards. <br /> <br /> Going by what we know from 1e and 2e, there were enough abandoned, dissatisfied, and just plain ready to pitch the whole system Lunars that it was reasonable for the Sids to consider it. That said, on that same basis, I'd be willing to bet there was at least one Solar who would have built up enough self-loathing that they'd have been good to go along with the thing and committed suicide after.<br /> <br /> It sounds like 3e will be quite different in that respect and I'm glad to hear it, because that always kinda bugged me. I hope that, when you finally get to the Sids books and go into a bit more detail on the great prophesy, it will mention more than just the Solars and DBs too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:32:03-08:00","id":24824,"title":"","content":"Again, Brilliantrain, the presumption that Solars 'won't throw in' because they understand they will 'all be killed' kinda relies upon the idea that the Sidereals are going to be honest about what they are doing.<br /> <br /> They don't need to motivated by self-loathing at all. They probably have no idea what they are actually contributing to.<br /> <br /> Remember, those that participate in the Usurpation probably do so <i>envisioning personal gains</i> that are promised to them <i>without having a very comprehensive idea of what the inner circle of conspirators really wants.</i><br /> <br /> ... just like pretty much every other coup in our history.<br /> <br /> It's not so black and white, not so simple as 'bad guys good guys', not so simple as 'us and them'. Not in the real world of actual coups.<br /> <br /> Obviously, if the Sidereals are transparant and honest, they will find few allies amongst the Celestials they plan to slaughter. This is why... they probably won't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-06-2013, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:40:18-08:00","id":24829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24801#post24801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, efforts to justify the lazy writing of the 1e Usurpation just kinda fall flat for me because... as we all know... it was just badly written, before much of this was really defined or thought through.<br /> <br /> 3e presents perhaps the best and most salient opportunity to correct some of these issues, but instead, we're struggling to justify a pretty silly history.<br /> <br /> The tone of our gritty, serious, deconstructive game feels weird when we combine it with a 'secretive, epic history' that is about as sophisticated as the history from the 80s 'Transformer' cartoon.<br /> <br /> We should just be honest and self-critical about how overly simplistic the 1e story was. It comes from the era of Vampire where that sorta thing was happening a lot at WW. Nothing to be defensive about.<br /> <br /> This can change. If we're spending so much time 'making the mechanics perfect', a pass at some of these basic story issues would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, for one, am comfortable with your judgements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:43:10-08:00","id":24830,"title":"","content":"If the Sidereals mention the possibility of the coup to a single wrong person, then it all comes crashing down and the world dies. If a single one of the Solars can see through their lie or deceit, it all comes crashing down and the world dies. If a single informed Lunar decides that loyalty to their Solar companion should prevail, it all comes crashing down and the world dies. No. It is not worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:47:22-08:00","id":24832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24801#post24801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people I have hung out with every day for CENTURIES, and I know them REALLY WELL</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know them well enough to know how difficult it's going to be to kill them if they have a heads up?<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget the Jade Prison; that thing was probably working on a fairly tight schedule, and they only get one of them. The plan isn't just predicated on killing the current Solars, but on preventing the incarnation of future Solars. If they delay closing the box, then the Essences escape and the whole thing starts over again. How many cycles of that do you think they can take?<br /> <br /> And what happens if your conspirator Solars realise that the Exaltations of the fallen are not returning to Lytek, and figure the Jade Prison out? What if they break it?<br /> <br /> If you can't get the vast majority of the Solars inside that thing and then dump it where it will never be found, then the whole endeavor has been for nothing.<br /> <br /> That's why they missed some Solars; they couldn't afford to delay locking the Prison.<br /> <br /> And look at how much trouble twenty Solars caused.<br /> <br /> How many do you want to escape the Prison and trouble the Shogunate and the Realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T19:02:31-08:00","id":24838,"title":"","content":"Really, while the growing appeal of Exalted is in its anthropological nuance, the initial and core premise is pretty simple:<br /> <br /> &quot;You are the glorious returned hero from the fallen golden age come to bring light to an Age of Sorrows.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Usurpation does not exist for itself; it exists to provide the background for that premise; for why the golden age fell and where the glorious heroes went.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be the Usurpation; Heaven's Reach and The Modern Age go for entirely different explanations.<br /> <br /> But the Usurpation fits the genre aesthetics, and it prioritises that over exact anthropological emulation.<br /> <br /> The game has <i>so much else</i> to put that in; the Usurpation can get by without it.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation also provides the background for the Sidereals and the Scarlet Dynasty, and they're widely beloved.<br /> <br /> Add to it a little, and it'll provide for the new Lunars; they're somewhat untested, and not everybody is taking to them, but they'll probably work out.<br /> <br /> But still; the Usurpation isn't there for itself, it's there for the decadent elemental samurai nobility, and the shadowy hidden mystic and prophets, and maybe the dread monster-men baying outside the walls.<br /> <br /> The Time of Tumult comes first; the Usurpation has the details it needs to create that Time, and no more.<br /> <br /> Unless you make a Shard of your own.<br /> <br /> Somehow, despite the bad writing of First Edition's Time of Tumult, it captured the imaginations of everybody who made the game a success.<br /> <br /> So you'll forgive me if I don't assume that your Shard is intrinsically superior to the Exalted that people bought and liked.<br /> <br /> Finally; not all coups and revolutions and overturns are complex.<br /> <br /> Some of them are exceedingly simple.<br /> <br /> To assume that complexity is automatically better is to do a disservice to everything that was simple that ever shook the world to the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T19:57:17-08:00","id":24849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24838#post24838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow, despite the bad writing of First Edition's Time of Tumult, it captured the imaginations of everybody who made the game a success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not like one of the most popular forum thread of the last decade was complaints about the Usurpation or anything.<br /> <br /> I mean, if that sorta thing happened, they might have to put a sticky at the top of the forum telling us all 'YES WE KNOW' so that we stop posting about it.<br /> <br /> What a weird world that would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:30:56-08:00","id":24866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24769#post24769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your goal is to execute a sudden, decisive, as-close-to-overnight-as-you-can-get-it toppling of the Bureau of Destiny, execution of its employees, and destruction of the Loom of Fate, how many Sidereals do you approach to join your venture, assuming that the whole plan doesn't start off revolving around the aid of a willing traitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted to topple the Bureau of Destiny, and I had the same advisory position that the Sidereals had with the Solars, I wouldn't try to do it overnight. I'd work to strengthen the inherent bureaucratic turf conflicts, making their system as dysfunctional and backbitting as possible, keeping them weak and distracted, so that when I did have all my pieces assembled, the strike would be at it's most devastating and hardest to respond to. You don't need to directly recruit Solars or Lunars into things to effectively gain their aid in your plans. Creating a cold war between groups of Solars and Lunars at the height of their insanity probably wouldn't be that hard for the Sidereals to pull off.<br /> <br /> So you don't frame it as &quot;Hey wanna help take out the Solars?&quot;, you phrase it as &quot;this small group of your peers are up to some crazy stuff, you should stop them!&quot; while convincing the other groups that the group you're talking to is also crazy, and you do all of this in such a way as to make it seem like they're discovering this on their own. Nothing ties back to you, you rely on existing fault lines and distrust, and nothing hints at the final hammer blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 12-06-2013, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:34:19-08:00","id":24868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24866#post24866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating a cold war between groups of Solars and Lunars at the height of their insanity probably wouldn't be that hard for the Sidereals to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a moment to think about why the Sidereals organized the Usurpation in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:48:04-08:00","id":24873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24868#post24868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take a moment to think about why the Sidereals organized the Usurpation in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider what it'd mean to the setting if some of the worst excesses of the First Age were actually prompted by some of the Sidereals as part of their plans leading up to the Usurpation, plans that had existed for decades or centuries before fully coming to fruition. Think of what it'd do to the Bronze and Gold faction conflicts if Kejak was implicated in being part of making the Solars so much worse than they would have been because that's what was needed to make sure they fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:56:24-08:00","id":24876,"title":"","content":"Because if the Sidereals need anything, it's to be made even more incompetent than they already are.<br /> <br /> The Solars were consuming Creation in their madness.<br /> The Sidereals chose the most likely solution over the best solution.<br /> That is the premise of the Usurpation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:59:03-08:00","id":24877,"title":"","content":"You realize that setting assumption works just as well as Sidereal propaganda, and that a desire for power and an arrogance to believe that they'd do a better job is sufficient motivation, yeah?<br /> <br /> <br /> The game is stronger if it's ambiguous as to which is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: and I'm pretty sure this particular interpretation makes them ultra competent, not more incompetent, just utter bastards. And I'm okay with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 12-07-2013, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:09:11-08:00","id":24880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24779#post24779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I <i>do</i> like Lunars to have some stuff at the low end of this scale, like that Dhalsim-stretch range enhancer Charm whose name I can't remember. I definitely think there's room for appropriately specialized Lunars to be <i>weirdly fluid</i>: bending like they don't have bones, snapping upright from a prone position like a bent switch, weaving back and forth with an animation-style stretch/smear that makes it hard to hit their weak points, surviving killing blows by just not having their organs where they're supposed to be, etc. I think a lot of Lunar players would be unhappy being forced into that aesthetic, but it seems like a legitimate place to allow people to explore if they want to, particularly in Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you just ask a &quot;I can stretch my body&quot; mutation from your Malefactor friend using Scoured Perfection of Form :'P Making <i>Stretchy Dick Prana </i>is such a waste of space IMO (Yes, I do hate rubber man like Luffy or Reed Richard)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:53:03-08:00","id":24905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24783#post24783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is some concept space between Flesh Shintai from KotE, and Monkey D. Luffy or Plastic Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just imagine - a One Piece where Luffy's skin can't cover the entirety of his stretched-out body! Would have made for quite the grotesque seinen series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T22:44:29-08:00","id":24934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24905#post24905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just imagine - a One Piece where Luffy's skin can't cover the entirety of his stretched-out body! Would have made for quite the grotesque seinen series.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to find much on now because the name is so overloaded (and it was always pretty obscure), but Harvey Comics had a pretty crappy stretchy superhero called <a href=\"http://www.toonopedia.com/jigsaw.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Jigsaw</a> whose skin looked like jigsaw pieces, and when he used his stretchiness, the pieces separated and you could see his muscles or tendons or something stretched out between the &quot;chunks&quot;. It was a weirdly body-horror take on it given that it was a very pedestrian kid-friendly comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T01:13:28-08:00","id":24989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24866#post24866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I wanted to topple the Bureau of Destiny, and I had the same advisory position that the Sidereals had with the Solars, I wouldn't try to do it overnight. I'd work to strengthen the inherent bureaucratic turf conflicts, making their system as dysfunctional and backbitting as possible, keeping them weak and distracted, so that when I did have all my pieces assembled, the strike would be at it's most devastating and hardest to respond to. You don't need to directly recruit Solars or Lunars into things to effectively gain their aid in your plans. Creating a cold war between groups of Solars and Lunars at the height of their insanity probably wouldn't be that hard for the Sidereals to pull off.<br /> <br /> So you don't frame it as &quot;Hey wanna help take out the Solars?&quot;, you phrase it as &quot;this small group of your peers are up to some crazy stuff, you should stop them!&quot; while convincing the other groups that the group you're talking to is also crazy, and you do all of this in such a way as to make it seem like they're discovering this on their own. Nothing ties back to you, you rely on existing fault lines and distrust, and nothing hints at the final hammer blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the comparison is that you are trying to recruit Sidereals to help you destroy their reason for existing. Sure, there's at least one who'll do it. The chances of fucking up your one shot at executing the plan trying to recruit the right one are astronomically high, and in the case of the Usurpation, the risk is not worth the benefit five, ten, hell, a dozen Lunar traitors bring to the table. Not when you already have several armies of Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T01:16:04-08:00","id":24990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24779#post24779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't like Jake from Adventure time? Come on, Dimaggio!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who from what?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T02:16:54-08:00","id":25012,"title":"","content":"Holden! Fix this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T02:56:00-08:00","id":25021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24801#post24801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tone of our gritty, serious, deconstructive game...</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, I have never thought of Exalted as a 'gritty, serious, deconstructive game.' All three of those may appear, but that's typical for the fantasy genre. I don't see it as PnP's Watchman or Black Company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:04:11-08:00","id":25116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24990#post24990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who from what?</div> </div> </div> </div>...You know, I'm genuinely shocked no one from the forum has tried to force Adventure Time down your throat before.<br /> <br /> Long story short: Jake the Dog has near-total control over the size and shape of his body, allowing him to do some... odd things. Like there's one episode that revolves around his ability to stretch noodle thin, and another where he turns his hand into a key to open a locked door. And then there's <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XSkqqQP1aNI\" target=\"_blank\">the Jake Suit...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","user":"MrInsecure","date":". 12-07-2013, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:10:57-08:00","id":25117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24783#post24783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is some concept space between Flesh Shintai from KotE, and Monkey D. Luffy or Plastic Man.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24905#post24905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just imagine - a One Piece where Luffy's skin can't cover the entirety of his stretched-out body! Would have made for quite the grotesque seinen series.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24934#post24934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to find much on now because the name is so overloaded (and it was always pretty obscure), but Harvey Comics had a pretty crappy stretchy superhero called <a href=\"http://www.toonopedia.com/jigsaw.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Jigsaw</a> whose skin looked like jigsaw pieces, and when he used his stretchiness, the pieces separated and you could see his muscles or tendons or something stretched out between the &quot;chunks&quot;. It was a weirdly body-horror take on it given that it was a very pedestrian kid-friendly comic.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those who were also curious, <a href=\"http://kindred-of-the-east-the-song-of-lanterns.obsidianportal.com/wikis/flesh-shintai\" target=\"_blank\">here is there informaiton on Flesh Shintai</a>. Though there's a typo under &quot;Body of the Serpent&quot; where they wrote &quot;strength&quot; instead of &quot;stretch.&quot;<br /> <br /> The disgusting manner of appendage extention seen in &quot;Long Neck&quot; seems a suitable fit for the Liminals (whom, it must be noted, have a Flesh Aspect), though hopefully not the Getimians (whom, it ought be noted, will operate by Yang and Yin &quot;chi / motes&quot; as the Kuejin did).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T09:27:04-08:00","id":25165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24873#post24873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider what it'd mean to the setting if some of the worst excesses of the First Age were actually prompted by some of the Sidereals as part of their plans leading up to the Usurpation, plans that had existed for decades or centuries before fully coming to fruition. Think of what it'd do to the Bronze and Gold faction conflicts if Kejak was implicated in being part of making the Solars so much worse than they would have been because that's what was needed to make sure they fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could imagine seeing some people in the fanon seize on this to exaggerate that the Sidereals mainly engineered the circumstances to justify the Usurpation and combine it with<br /> <br /> - <i>&quot;The Solars were never that bad, rather there were just some disquietening elements of their rule, quiet atrocities&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> - <i>&quot;The Sidereals and Dragonblooded were really just frightened about Solar powers making them obsolete, or threatening their OCD vision of an orderly world. They weren't driven by any concern for humanity&quot;</i><br /> <br /> to make the perfect storm of returning kings who are, in someone's mind, somehow meant to be likeable or rooted for, but are so eternally wronged and betrayed, perfect and never ever in error that they're completely and utterly dislikeable. Maybe that's someone's idea of a good game though, hopefully it's not the norm.<br /> <br /> On attempting to recruit the Solars, yeah, note of the paths of prophecy was &quot;Attempt to reform the Solars and fail&quot; is the one that would leads to the civil war then apocalypse (while doing nothing was what would just lead to continual decline under Solar misrule, a Dying Earth scenario and quieter dying of the world).<br /> <br /> Recruiting the Solars or working with them in any form, in terms of fate mojo, might come too close to putting the world on the path of Gold, which, in its worst case scenario, is about an Exalted civil war and then conquest by the Fair Folk, and which the Sidereals didn't plump for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T11:59:23-08:00","id":25278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24877#post24877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize that setting assumption works just as well as Sidereal propaganda, and that a desire for power and an arrogance to believe that they'd do a better job is sufficient motivation, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't, because if the Vision of Bronze is just Sidereal propaganda, the moral argument surrounding the Great Prophecy is invalidated and the Bronze Faction is automatically evil. The entire point of the Usurpation is that it was morally ambiguous and both sides had perfectly valid points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 12-07-2013, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:19:54-08:00","id":25314,"title":"","content":"I'm incidentally reading some stuff about the Iroquois League right now, and I'm wondering at the idea of the Silver Pact adopting apparent tribalistic terminology and hierarchy, not because they being Lunars are intrinsically inclined towards it, but as a form of appropriation from certain extant lifestyles that, both in resulting organizational principles and somewhat political statement, served their purposes.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking, given the lifestyle they'd been forced into and the people they wound up moving amongst, it might have been a useful model for a group that's internally disagreeable but wishes to present an image of external cohesion.<br /> <br /> Just, another thing that might help the Silver Pact is if it was viewed in terms of the numerous, very different Lunars, independently looking for ways to make use of one another (with an understanding that the strategies employed by any given Lunar will take a form that is most readily helped by the talents of another Lunar), while also having a means to make them look more unified than they really are (helpful for being a terrifying Other to the Dragon Blooded), and maybe have a nebulous overforce to reference in place of their own goals and methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T14:18:50-08:00","id":25345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25012#post25012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden! Fix this!</div> </div> </div> </div>John is soooo not a randomness-comedy person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T14:57:19-08:00","id":25359,"title":"","content":"as long as we're asking the Devs about lunar powers and inspirations, is the <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/42514070\" target=\"_blank\">Witchblade</a> gonna be something that a Lunar could emulate with their native powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T15:35:20-08:00","id":25394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25359#post25359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as long as we're asking the Devs about lunar powers and inspirations, is the <a href=\"http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/42514070\" target=\"_blank\">Witchblade</a> gonna be something that a Lunar could emulate with their native powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>If not Carnage, then not Witchblade. Either might be Infernal, or Abyssal, though. But I don't think the Lunars are going for &quot;amorphous&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> If the devs are really making Totems actually important to the Lunar Exalted, then I'm pretty sure their stuff has to echo with the idea of &quot;Half-Beast God (Warrior/Trickster/Witch)&quot;. They're probably going to be animal shapeshifters with a minor in human shapeshifting (faces). Even the Chimerae are about expanding the concrete starting point of the Totem, which is less &quot;become a shapeless monster&quot; and more &quot;more animals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25345#post25345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John is soooo not a randomness-comedy person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'm in good company.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-07-2013, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T15:53:20-08:00","id":25407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25345#post25345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> John is soooo not a randomness-comedy person.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... the emotional depth and intricacy of character relationships!<br /> <br /> You... bu... the... wha...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://us.123rf.com/400wm/400/400/vlue/vlue1010/vlue101000178/8138990-abstract-minimalistic-texture-of-a-single-line-crack-on-a-large-rock-surface.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> All right then.<br /> <br /> All right then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:17:29-08:00","id":25470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24401#post24401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas involving the Lunars joining the Sidereals in the Usurpation or being passive non-targets leaves me cold. The Lunars could no more opt out of the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation than Daenerys could opt out of King Robert's.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leaves them only as allies of the Solars. If they can't opt out, can't side with the Sidereals, only the Solar side remains, which I detest. I want the tragedy of a Solar being betrayed by it's Lunar mate for various reasons. There is a reason the Usurpation happens, and Lunars shouldn't be blind to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:32:59-08:00","id":25480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25470#post25470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they can't opt out</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, let's sit idly by while our place in the world is torn away never to be recovered. That's what people want from us, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't side with the Sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div>To what purpose?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the tragedy of a Solar being betrayed by it's Lunar mate for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect the Bond will allow relationships flexible enough that betrayal will be possible.<br /> <br /> An individual Lunar betraying an individual Solar is one thing, but a Lunar saying &quot;hey, let's seal this Solar, and all of the others, away from the world forever so that the Dragon Blooded can run things&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a reason the Usurpation happens, and Lunars shouldn't be blind to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're probably complicit in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:50:19-08:00","id":25496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25480#post25480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Hey, let's sit idly by while our place in the world is torn away never to be recovered. That's what people want from us, right?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like &quot;Hey let's bunker down and preserve ourselves so when the storm passes we're ahead of the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25480#post25480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To what purpose?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey so some of these Solars are doing some really screwy stuff, maybe the Sidereals are right&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25480#post25480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect the Bond will allow relationships flexible enough that betrayal will be possible.<br /> <br /> An individual Lunar betraying an individual Solar is one thing, but a Lunar saying &quot;hey, let's seal this Solar, and all of the others, away from the world forever so that the Dragon Blooded can run things&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously it would be a seperate case for each Lunar, and likely dependent on the relationship the Lunar has with Solars. To say that some Lunars wouldn't love to kill and lock away Solars forever is idiotic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25480#post25480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're probably complicit in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They need to be active players in the Usurpation on many sides.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:53:28-08:00","id":25498,"title":"","content":"Just a thought:<br /> <br /> So, you wanna make the Lunar splat as a whole more relevant to the setting, responsible for events in Creation unlike how they were in 2e.<br /> <br /> Consider:<br /> - The Sidereals orchestrated the Usurpation and the DBs fuckin' fought it. Then the DBs ruled Creation with Siddies as their secret... masters? I dunno, but the Siddies were doin' shit, or at least did shit.<br /> - The Usurpation is plain fuckin' ABOUT the Solars and them being crazy assholes, so they did shit right up until the Usurpation and had the excuse of not being around since for inactivity.<br /> - Abyssals and Infernals just started existing, but their patrons shaped Creation. First off, they're all the fucking Primordials, the architects of the worlds. So, there's that but not so important, really. Then the Deathlords are the ones who just Great Contagion'd the place, one of them at least, and the Yozi are the ones who orchestrated breaking the Jade Prison, one of them at least<br /> - And the Lunars just lived through it all. If you consider, like I suggested, that the Lunars are more important as individuals than as a whole, that's not too bad but let's ignore that.<br /> <br /> Alright, so, Usurpation, That's the DBs and Siddies time to shine, before than was the Solar's time and now is that time again for the golden bastards, then the Great Contagion was great for Team Abyssal BEFORE the Abyssal were around, then the DBs put a stop to that shit and created the Realm. Then Abbies and Infernals gets tied right up with the Jade Prison breaking, plus the Solars.<br /> <br /> The Lunars don't HAVE an event. But new history, right, that can be fixed?<br /> <br /> How's it gonna happen?<br /> <br /> A new world shaping event dropped into the time line of Exalted? One with which the Lunars are major players of?<br /> <br /> Players of previous events are replaced with Lunars? Maybe the Lunars were the one to invite in the Fair Folk? Like all the Lunar got together while the Contagion was happening and collectively decided that this was a good idea.<br /> <br /> A new aspect will be added to the events that happened so far that change them greatly from how they were in 2e and tie directly to the Lunar? ES tried this, installing a secret war between the Lunar and the Sidereal that's just been going on forever. That, apparently, did not impress the new Dev.<br /> <br /> What do y'all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:59:38-08:00","id":25499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25278#post25278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it doesn't, because if the Vision of Bronze is just Sidereal propaganda, the moral argument surrounding the Great Prophecy is invalidated and the Bronze Faction is automatically evil. The entire point of the Usurpation is that it was morally ambiguous and both sides had perfectly valid points.</div> </div> </div> </div>First: It's important to look at the perspective of how the Sidereal are being used in game; discussing this out of that context is a waste of time. Exalted's setting is useful only insofar as it informs actual play. If the Vision of Bronze is propaganda, the Sidereals are set up as a major antagonist in a Solar game, or extremely manipulative bastards in a Dragon Blooded game. That is an extremely functional role for them to take; they're already kinda set up that way anyway, but this provides a few layers to peel through when examining their motives. It doesn't assume the entire bronze faction was in on it, opening the doors to a complete re-examining of the Sidereal's position as an act of a Solar Circle; revealing the treachery could be used as a wedge to bring the Sidereals in general back behind the Solars, something that could be a good stepping stone in a campaign centered around unifying groups against massive threats to Creation, or around restoration of first age wonder.<br /> <br /> If you're playing Sidereals, the faction determines where you go: You would almost certainly not have it be propaganda in a Bronze Faction Sidereal game. It'd be a powerful revelation in a Gold Faction game though; that's the sort of secret that'd completely shake up the existing order. There are a lot of stories to be told around that. <br /> <br /> Second: The Great Prophecy taken at face value is overwhelmingly in favor of Bronze. There's barely any moral ambiguity there at all. Gold faction doesn't really gain any strength until after Usurpation for a reason, certainly there is zero dissent at the time Usurpation is decided upon, because it'd have taken one Sidereal breaking ranks to stop the whole thing. In fact most of the ambiguity about the Great Prophecy stems from the Sidereal's version of the great curse, which casts doubt on the whole thing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:06:54-08:00","id":25506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=24989#post24989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point of the comparison is that you are trying to recruit Sidereals to help you destroy their reason for existing. Sure, there's at least one who'll do it. The chances of fucking up your one shot at executing the plan trying to recruit the right one are astronomically high, and in the case of the Usurpation, the risk is not worth the benefit five, ten, hell, a dozen Lunar traitors bring to the table. Not when you already have several armies of Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I was perhaps somewhat inelegantly trying to point out that that comparison doesn't really make a ton of sense in the context of crazy fate ninjas, because 'recruit' doesn't mean 'ask for aid' as much as it means 'xanatos gambit the hell out of'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:56:54-08:00","id":25532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey so some of these Solars are doing some really screwy stuff, maybe the Sidereals are right</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we're back at the point where Sidereals explain their reasoning to Lunars, where a single misstep means that they're exposed and the Vision of Bronze becomes impossible.<br /> <br /> It's probably also kind of hard to bring someone around on a plan that says that your social inferiors need to be elevated above you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25496#post25496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To say that some Lunars wouldn't love to kill and lock away Solars forever is idiotic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar Bond will probably make this unlikely.<br /> <br /> The Lunars seem to have suffered <i>terribly</i> for having lost their Solars.<br /> <br /> On top of those other considerations, the Great Curse probably plays a part; Solars aren't the only ones going crazy.<br /> <br /> Heck, if they keep the self-important and hubristic qualities of the Sidereal Curse intact, that's an explanation all on its own for why they can't see their way to trying to find a more nuanced way to deal with the Lunars.<br /> <br /> Nobody's really to blame for the Great Curse being overlooked, mind, except maybe the writers who neglected it. The current writers will certainly not make that mistake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need to be active players in the Usurpation on many sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do they &quot;need&quot; to be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:10:54-08:00","id":25544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25499#post25499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Prophecy taken at face value is overwhelmingly in favor of Bronze.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I'm not sure I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25499#post25499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's barely any moral ambiguity there at all. Gold faction doesn't really gain any strength until after Usurpation for a reason, certainly there is zero dissent at the time Usurpation is decided upon, because it'd have taken one Sidereal breaking ranks to stop the whole thing. In fact most of the ambiguity about the Great Prophecy stems from the Sidereal's version of the great curse, which casts doubt on the whole thing anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we reading the same book?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOEP: Sidereals p24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth, though, the first deaths of the Usurpation were<br /> not Solar Exalted, or their servants. The fi rst murders were<br /> of Sidereals who could not bend their will to the majority.<br /> Several Seers\u2014including Tammiz Ushun\u2014sought to flee<br /> what they saw as the Five-Score Fellowship\u2019s own descent<br /> into madness and warn the Solar Exalted. None managed<br /> to do so. Gods in the Bureau of Destiny still speak of the<br /> Night of Fallen Stars, when fi ve Sidereals died because they<br /> intended to betray the goals of the Bronze Faction\u2019s so-called<br /> Final Calibration Feast. By the time of the Usurpation itself,<br /> members of the Bronze Faction had arranged the deaths of<br /> at least a dozen of their fellow Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:46:26-08:00","id":25562,"title":"","content":"The Great Prophecy is like in The Avengers, where there's debate over<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">whether it's a better option to nuke Manhattan in order to wipe out an invading army and destroy the power source for their wormhole, or to trust in heroes to be daring and brilliant enough to pull through the overwhelming odds. The Vision of Bronze is the nuke.<br /> <br /> This is a setting where Nick Fury and Iron Man fail to stop the nuke from going off, because the genre is about fighting around in the irradiated ruins of Manhattan.<br /> <br /> This does not mean that launching the nuke is an overwhelmingly favoured option.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:50:46-08:00","id":25564,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten that bit, it's been a while. But that kind of reinforces my point, in any event; the overwhelming majority of Sidereals were bronze faction supporters. The consequences of inaction were too great to ignore, and the consequences of failure for attempting to redeem the Solars, something not at all likely to even be possible in the first place, equally severe. While there's some room for moral rejection of the viewpoint that the Solars all needed to die, from a practical point of view, there is no other choice for the Sidereals to make if they have any consideration for Creation as a whole; Fate is too certain and clear a thing as presented for the Gold position to be viewed as workable. And the vast majority is shown to have accepted that point of view.<br /> <br /> Presenting them doing absolutely awful things for reasons that can be justified to themselves works no matter how you present their motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T20:50:47-08:00","id":25565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25499#post25499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: It's important to look at the perspective of how the Sidereal are being used in game; discussing this out of that context is a waste of time. Exalted's setting is useful only insofar as it informs actual play. If the Vision of Bronze is propaganda, the Sidereals are set up as a major antagonist in a Solar game, or extremely manipulative bastards in a Dragon Blooded game. That is an extremely functional role for them to take; they're already kinda set up that way anyway, but this provides a few layers to peel through when examining their motives. It doesn't assume the entire bronze faction was in on it, opening the doors to a complete re-examining of the Sidereal's position as an act of a Solar Circle; revealing the treachery could be used as a wedge to bring the Sidereals in general back behind the Solars, something that could be a good stepping stone in a campaign centered around unifying groups against massive threats to Creation, or around restoration of first age wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone's ever said that the Vision of Bronze was propaganda, although that might be an interesting idea to pursue in your own game. Rather, the source of tension in the game is a matter of what could have been, had they attempted to bring the Vision of Gold into being, rather than pursuing the Vision of Bronze. A Bronze loyalist would say that the Usurpation was justified and necessary, considering the potential for disaster from pursuing the Vision of Gold; a Gold loyalist, on the other hand, would point out that things aren't exactly going swimmingly right now, and a couple hundred shining heroes might have been able to avert all this disaster.<br /> <br /> The point is not to prove one right or wrong (unless you want there to be a clear answer in your game), but rather to show that <i>there is no way to prove the Gold Faction would've done any better</i>. It is an eternal &quot;what if?&quot;, prone to endless speculation and regret.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: The Great Prophecy taken at face value is overwhelmingly in favor of Bronze. There's barely any moral ambiguity there at all. Gold faction doesn't really gain any strength until after Usurpation for a reason, certainly there is zero dissent at the time Usurpation is decided upon, because it'd have taken one Sidereal breaking ranks to stop the whole thing. In fact most of the ambiguity about the Great Prophecy stems from the Sidereal's version of the great curse, which casts doubt on the whole thing anyway. </div> </div> </div>...what? No, the Great Prophecy is not &quot;overwhelmingly&quot; in favor of Bronze. There's a reason that there was a Gold Faction prior to the Usurpation, and why the Bronze Faction had to <i>straight up murder</i> all of the Golds that got in their way- the Gold Faction were the Sidereals who were willing to take a huge risk for a brighter future, while the Bronze Faction were those Sidereals who thought the potential cost of the Gold Vision failing far outweighed the potential benefits. You see this sort of struggle in governments and businesses all the time, where someone proposes a new, risky idea but gets shot down because everyone else would prefer to do things like they've always done, rather than take a chance on something new (and potentially much better).<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a reason people hate risks: if you fail, you're going to lose something, even if it's &quot;only&quot; sunk costs in terms of time, money or other resources. Sometimes, you can lose <i>a lot</i> more than that, depending on what exactly you're betting on. The Gold Vision was the ultimate gamble, with the ultimate jackpot- and with the whole world as the wager. On the one hand, you can see why a lot of people would turn down that wager, even if it had decent odds... but on the other hand, you can also see why someone might take the wager as well. Which side of the line you fell on likely was a factor of how risk-averse you were... and it doesn't take a lot of risk-aversion to not want to gamble one the fate of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:01:40-08:00","id":25572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25565#post25565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone's ever said that the Vision of Bronze was propaganda, although that might be an interesting idea to pursue in your own game. Rather, the source of tension in the game is a matter of what could have been, had they attempted to bring the Vision of Gold into being, rather than pursuing the Vision of Bronze. A Bronze loyalist would say that the Usurpation was justified and necessary, considering the potential for disaster from pursuing the Vision of Gold; a Gold loyalist, on the other hand, would point out that things aren't exactly going swimmingly right now, and a couple hundred shining heroes might have been able to avert all this disaster.<br /> <br /> The point is not to prove one right or wrong (unless you want there to be a clear answer in your game), but rather to show that <i>there is no way to prove the Gold Faction would've done any better</i>. It is an eternal &quot;what if?&quot;, prone to endless speculation and regret. ~~</div> </div> </div> </div> That's only a source of tension in a Sidereal game; a Solar circle or a Dragon Blooded or a Lunar is highly unlikely to be party to Bronze/Gold politics. The extent to which those groups are exposed to Sidereal thought on the matter of the Usurpation, it'll be in the context of Bronze Faction party line or Gold Faction guilt. That makes that particular conflict relatively meaningless as a matter of actionable choices on the part of those parties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...what? No, the Great Prophecy is not &quot;overwhelmingly&quot; in favor of Bronze. There's a reason that there was a Gold Faction prior to the Usurpation, and why the Bronze Faction had to <i>straight up murder</i> all of the Golds that got in their way- the Gold Faction were the Sidereals who were willing to take a huge risk for a brighter future, while the Bronze Faction were those Sidereals who thought the potential cost of the Gold Vision failing far outweighed the potential benefits. You see this sort of struggle in governments and businesses all the time, where someone proposes a new, risky idea but gets shot down because everyone else would prefer to do things like they've always done, rather than take a chance on something new (and potentially much better).<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a reason people hate risks: if you fail, you're going to lose something, even if it's &quot;only&quot; sunk costs in terms of time, money or other resources. Sometimes, you can lose <i>a lot</i> more than that, depending on what exactly you're betting on. The Gold Vision was the ultimate gamble, with the ultimate jackpot- and with the whole world as the wager. On the one hand, you can see why a lot of people would turn down that wager, even if it had decent odds... but on the other hand, you can also see why someone might take the wager as well. Which side of the line you fell on likely was a factor of how risk-averse you were... and it doesn't take a lot of risk-aversion to not want to gamble one the fate of the world. </div> </div> </div>Except they weren't decent odds, they were terribly long shot odds, with the whole of Creation at stake. Taking that bet would have been extremely irresponsible; Exalted is several shades darker than an action hero movie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T21:54:19-08:00","id":25598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25572#post25572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they weren't decent odds, they were terribly long shot odds, with the whole of Creation at stake. Taking that bet would have been extremely irresponsible; Exalted is several shades darker than an action hero movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Vision of Gold was portrayed as fifty-fifty odds. Not long shot, but no guarantee either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T22:01:52-08:00","id":25601,"title":"","content":"After they decided to kill the Solars they shoulda done a Vision on if they would hunt down the Lunars or spare them to pick up the pieces. As is, they were not even spared a second thought and were treated like they are just collateral damage - when any Exalt deserves more than being the town block smashed as the Kaiju fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T22:31:29-08:00","id":25609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25598#post25598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say the Vision of Gold was portrayed as fifty-fifty odds. Not long shot, but no guarantee either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think they weren't given the odds, nor were they told how much shittier creation would get with the Vision Of Bronze. They all essentially had to go on gut feelings and personal ethics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:23:49-08:00","id":25622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25506#post25506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I was perhaps somewhat inelegantly trying to point out that that comparison doesn't really make a ton of sense in the context of crazy fate ninjas, because 'recruit' doesn't mean 'ask for aid' as much as it means 'xanatos gambit the hell out of'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you paying attention? The 'Team : Sidereal' shirts clearly outline the ultimate goals of the Usurpation in bold type along the back side, along with a complete description of the Great Prophesy.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know what game YOU'VE been playing, but typically Sidereal Exalted are really honest about what they want you to do. They don't really so much manipulate or subtly guide people, they just kinda show up and tell you what they want (usually, by pointing at the T-shirt and exclaiming 'Duh' really loudly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:27:05-08:00","id":25625,"title":"","content":"Did the Sidereals at least get a good designer for their t-shirt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:55:10-08:00","id":25632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25572#post25572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only a source of tension in a Sidereal game; a Solar circle or a Dragon Blooded or a Lunar is highly unlikely to be party to Bronze/Gold politics. The extent to which those groups are exposed to Sidereal thought on the matter of the Usurpation, it'll be in the context of Bronze Faction party line or Gold Faction guilt. That makes that particular conflict relatively meaningless as a matter of actionable choices on the part of those parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, the Bronze/Gold thing is mostly a concern for Sidereals. However, the impact the Usurpation had on Creation is one of the major reasons the landscape looks like it does, and the Bronze and Gold Factions are now in a position to fight the old battle all over again- only this time, it's not as clear who's going to be on whose side.... nd that's going to shape what the coming conflicts look like in the near future of Creation.<br /> <br /> For example, take the Lunars. Back in the First Age, most of them were the undisputed allies and lieutenants of the Solar Exalted, and they were hunted down by the Bronze Faction all the way to the edge of Creation because of that. In the modern era, however, many of the Lunars have established a pretty cozy arrangement for themselves, and the return of the Solar Exalted (not to mention the Infernal and Abyssal Exalted) is going to mean an end to that lifestyle... unless, of course, they can get some allies in Heaven to help watch their backs. This, ironically, might put a few Lunars on the same side as the guys who once hunted them down, just because it will give them a bulwark against the coming tide of Solar-ness.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you might also see a few of the Dragon-Blooded Houses in the Realm rethinking this whole &quot;hunt down the Anathema&quot; thing, in spite of what the Bronze Fa- I mean, the Immaculate Order says, just because having a Solar or two on their side could make a big difference against the other Houses in the coming Civil War. Obviously, this is more likely among the more corrupt or desperate Houses- Iselsi, Tepet, Cynis and Nellens all come to mind- but the Time of Tumult is likely to be a time of strange bedfellows.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, though, one thing is quite clear: the time of the Bronze Faction's dominance is coming to a close. In the face of all this change, it's exceedingly unlikely that the Dragon-Blooded will be able to reassert their dominion, and the Solars (along with their Infernal and Abyssal brethren) will slowly begin their takeover of Creation. At that point, it's just a matter of what the Bronze Faction is willing to do, and what deals it's willing to make, to prevent the ascent of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except they weren't decent odds, they were terribly long shot odds, with the whole of Creation at stake. Taking that bet would have been extremely irresponsible; Exalted is several shades darker than an action hero movie. </div> </div> </div>Well, the actual odds were never stated, but what we do know was that the Bronze Vision was much better odds than the Gold Vision. Exactly how much better is sort of irrelevant, unless you have a very specific threshold of risk that you're not willing to cross. The point was that the Sidereals had two choices: play it safe with the knowledge that the world would probably continue to subsist, albeit in a reduced state, or risk everything on the possibility that you could reunite the Solar Host and bring them back on the straight and narrow.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty classic dilemma, and I'm not entirely sure how I'd resolve it. I guess it's a matter of what you're willing to pay for a chance at paradise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","user":"MrInsecure","date":". 12-08-2013, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:09:24-08:00","id":25707,"title":"","content":"You know, I'm not one for the idea that pursuing the safer Vision of Bronze indicates a form of cowardice, but jeez, is this or is this not a game of audacious and daring heroes?<br /> <br /> What do you think the odds of <i>defeating the Primordials</i> were? 'Cause they probably weren't great.<br /> <br /> Scenarios in which the Exalted lost and the Exalted switched allegiance to the Primordials exist in their own Shards. You could make a Shard in which the Goldstars won the debate and then succeeded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:11:29-08:00","id":25709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25622#post25622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't you paying attention? The 'Team : Sidereal' shirts clearly outline the ultimate goals of the Usurpation in bold type along the back side, along with a complete description of the Great Prophesy.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know what game YOU'VE been playing, but typically Sidereal Exalted are really honest about what they want you to do. They don't really so much manipulate or subtly guide people, they just kinda show up and tell you what they want (usually, by pointing at the T-shirt and exclaiming 'Duh' really loudly).</div> </div> </div> </div><i>How</i> do you subtly manipulate the Lunars into murdering Solars all at once so they can be shoved in a jade box? Do you make the dress code for the Calibration Feast hides and antlers and then tell the Lunars that it's deer season?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:21:25-08:00","id":25713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25709#post25709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>How</i> do you subtly manipulate the Lunars into murdering Solars all at once so they can be shoved in a jade box? Do you make the dress code for the Calibration Feast hides and antlers and then tell the Lunars that it's deer season?</div> </div> </div> </div> They tried that once, but the Eclipses pulled them into this long debate about what season it actually was and the Lunars ended up hunting each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T07:15:06-08:00","id":25780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25622#post25622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I don't know what game YOU'VE been playing, but typically Sidereal Exalted are really honest about what they want you to do. They don't really so much manipulate or subtly guide people, they just kinda show up and tell you what they want (usually, by pointing at the T-shirt and exclaiming 'Duh' really loudly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pssst. You know what Solars and Lunars are really good at? <u><i><b>NOT BEING LIED TO.</b></i></u><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T08:51:56-08:00","id":25809,"title":"","content":"This faction t-shirt thing is a tad hyperolic.<br /> <br /> The Fivescore Fellowship had their visions. One of them was unequivocally agreed upon as &quot;Kill the Solars&quot;. Not kill most of them. Not kill the bad ones. The Solars, all of them. Not all Sidereals in the room thought that was the plan like Tammiz. They didn't make it out of Heaven to tell anyone else. So it wasn't so much &quot;Sidereals united as team Sidereal.&quot; It was &quot;Bronze united as Sidereals who were left.&quot; And frankly, with mass homicide, has a bit of &quot;We're all in&quot; to this.<br /> <br /> As noted also, herding Celestial Exalted via guile and subtlety, while doable, is also like herding cats. Lunar Exalted probably had a range fo positions in relation to Solars. Secondary rulers, Bene Gezerett-style badass righthands, mentors, squires, one man secret police, even the asshole who hates their Solar and spends time on the other side of Creation from his Solar companion (and thus not likely to be contactable in the time scales Siderals might be working with). Regardless of actual job the Lunars are doing for Solars, or lack there of, they are defined as a group as number two. The only way to get higher power is to be the guy in power. This is as a group probably fairly invested in how things are and being human, like being in power and luxury. The guys who don't get along with their Solar probably are still living it fairly large more the sense of reputation, personal power, and maybe a cheque to stay away.<br /> <br /> This is a group defined historically as individualistic, contrarian and is about as good as you at spy games. That asshole in a forest retret in the East while his Solar companion runs her island in the West and they haven't talked for centuries might be spearheading a spying project for her out there and securing supply networks her way. Out of the three hundred or so Lunars, maybe there's one that could side with you. But he has to have a combination of 1) Available, 2) Actually trustworthy, 3) Useful and 4) Having nothing to lose that may simply not be there. And the more caveats you need in a co-conspirator, out of a group that is bound to have folks trying to fuck your conspiracy if they find out, the less helpful it'll be to your goals. Even the seemingly most sympathetic to your cause Lunar might turn around and sell you out for the bonus. Being the Lunar who single-handedly undid the entire SIdereal conspiracy, with lifespans he has to deal with, means that he'll be an issue if things fall through thosuand years from now. And you'll likely still be dead.<br /> <br /> It's all down to risk rewards. The Gold part of the risk is already handled, they're dead or in line with threat of death. The Dragon-Blooded are a bit less of a risk since they seem unhappy with things as-is and the prophecy guarantees they'll get some success. The Solar Exalted aren't on the table as the Prophecy said they have to die and we're not told of any caveats to this. Which leaves of the classical four Lunars, the group that is most entrenched in Solar rule, gets the most out of it, loses the msot in its collapse and on top of all that probably complicit if not outright part of the problem of Solar crazy-personhood. Even discounting the abandonment of all things 2e background, stuff like the Black Nadir Conpact and the Five Metal Shrike I think were enough co Solar-Lunar projects that Lunar Exalted were not an option of replacements due to just likely more of the same.<br /> <br /> To that end, you have a group that has most to lose, least to gain and least to offer in the whole thing. Your conpsiracy needs the least possible issues, as to get rid of the Solars requires you do it right or you start on one of the other paths. It's a bit of Muad'Dib's problem really. The Golden Path was lain with bodies and he wanted nothing to do with it. Too fucking bad, Leto II did what was needed, and it was ugly and threw a lot of folks under the bus. The Sidereals aren't in much better a position in that.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T09:01:13-08:00","id":25818,"title":"","content":"I think it's fine if a Storyteller wants to have a handful of Lunars in on the Usurpation. I also think it's fine if a Storyteller wants to have it be a Sid only affair.<br /> <br /> Both are plausible and there's no need for the books to definitively rule on the matter one way or another. I'd prefer it if the Usurpation remained a back-story element with a paragraph or two devoted to it.<br /> <br /> 'The Sidereals saw that the Solars were going bad, they checked the loom and saw a possible horrible fate for the world, so they conspired with the Dragon-Blooded to overthrow the Solars at the annual Calibration feast.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T10:53:56-08:00","id":25877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25707#post25707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'm not one for the idea that pursuing the safer Vision of Bronze indicates a form of cowardice, but jeez, is this or is this not a game of audacious and daring heroes?<br /> <br /> What do you think the odds of <i>defeating the Primordials</i> were? 'Cause they probably weren't great.<br /> <br /> Scenarios in which the Exalted lost and the Exalted switched allegiance to the Primordials exist in their own Shards. You could make a Shard in which the Goldstars won the debate and then succeeded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting overthrowing the Solar Exalted at the height of their power in such a way as to effectively prevent their return for millennia is not daring and audacious? It may not lead to the daring and audacious future, but the plan itself was far more over-the-top and extreme than the plan for fulfilling the Vision of Gold. Kind of like overthrowing the Primordials, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1415-nonsensicles","name":"Nonsensicles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:01:46-08:00","id":25888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsensicles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25877#post25877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you suggesting overthrowing the Solar Exalted at the height of their power in such a way as to effectively prevent their return for millennia is not daring and audacious?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm arguing against somebody saying that the Great Prophecy seems excessively weighted towards Bronze.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:12:40-08:00","id":25892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25818#post25818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fine if a Storyteller wants to have a handful of Lunars in on the Usurpation. I also think it's fine if a Storyteller wants to have it be a Sid only affair.<br /> <br /> Both are plausible and there's no need for the books to definitively rule on the matter one way or another. I'd prefer it if the Usurpation remained a back-story element with a paragraph or two devoted to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Usurpation should get a paragraph in the core, maybe another paragraph in the Sidereal book, and never be described in any detail.<br /> <br /> That way, if people choose to believe the Usurpation doesn't work, it has nothing to do with the books or the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:18:58-08:00","id":25897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25780#post25780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pssst. You know what Solars and Lunars are really good at? <u><i><b>NOT BEING LIED TO.</b></i></u></div> </div> </div> </div>... the entire premise of the Usurpation seems to contradict this.<br /> <br /> Either way, they got lied to.<br /> <br /> And Blaque, I feel you - but let's just stop defending this kinda badly conceived story element. We've hated it for like a decade. It was seriously up there with threads on Eclipse charms and Lunar theme. The Usurpation got FAR more attention and complaining than say... the 3 spheres cataclysm, did.<br /> <br /> It's ok to take another pass at this thing. It's ok to admit, 'Yeah, elements of this thing kinda don't make much sense, and could be better thought through.'<br /> <br /> The conspiracy of 2 splats against another 1 splat while 1 splat fled into the Wyld is basically a classic WW 'This Chapter Has the Ancient History' hack job. Let's take another look. And the 50 year 'secret conference of murder' required for the Great Prophesy... ugh. It's just so bad, all the way through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:25:27-08:00","id":25901,"title":"","content":"B-but, I wanna see the Usurpation in exact detail.<br /> <br /> And the Primordial War, while we're at it.<br /> <br /> I wanna know what kind of Panoply charms Theion &amp; Co used to forge Creation. The EXACT stats.<br /> <br /> Down to the last d10, goddamn you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T11:54:44-08:00","id":25930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25897#post25897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... the entire premise of the Usurpation seems to contradict this.<br /> <br /> Either way, they got lied to.<br /> <br /> And Blaque, I feel you - but let's just stop defending this kinda badly conceived story element. We've hated it for like a decade. It was seriously up there with threads on Eclipse charms and Lunar theme. The Usurpation got FAR more attention and complaining than say... the 3 spheres cataclysm, did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I missed a lot of the Usurpation threads, but seeing as the setting hinges on it more than the cataclysm, and since there are obvious camps on the matter, it's far from universal. Unlike the Cataclysm or Eclipse Charmshare, it seems also a bit one of thsoe First Prinicples of the game thing. The setting is how it is because the Usurpation happened in a way that looked Solars up, sent Lunars to the periphery and put Dragon-Blooded in charge. I would also say that one thread on it doesn't somehow make i tthe authoratative stance on stuff in the line. I mostly ignored it since after a point it to me felt stupid and circular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25897#post25897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... It's ok to take another pass at this thing. It's ok to admit, 'Yeah, elements of this thing kinda don't make much sense, and could be better thought through.' ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication I get from you is you want it not to be what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25897#post25897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The conspiracy of 2 splats against another 1 splat while 1 splat fled into the Wyld is basically a classic WW 'This Chapter Has the Ancient History' hack job. Let's take another look. And the 50 year 'secret conference of murder' required for the Great Prophesy... ugh. It's just so bad, all the way through.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prophecy took a year. The time from then to actual Usurpation isn't stated. For all we know it happeend within a few weeks and the Dragon-Blooded were that independently ready to perform a coup. This is likely not something we'll ever get much in detail. But the logic still is the logic that it is to justify this instance of splatness. Seeing as the First Age society was built in some part with the Exaltations as societal castes, with each acting like its own branch of government, it makes sense to of played out like it is. But then, save Dragon-Blooded, I see Exaltation type more like a job position and skillset that gets certain people working in it than I see it as something like a Masquerade clan.<br /> <br /> And again, the logic is sound on first principles and plays out in practice. Prophecy said Solars die, Dragon-Blooded rule. Lunars are axed as being directly tied to the first's power and not able to be compatible with the new regime. Sidereals orchestrated the thing and killed dissenters. Seeing as after the Calibration Feast it was a society-destroying global conflict to get who was left, sizable Dragon-Blooded probably were loyal to the Solars and enough Lunars were probably still loyal too that the intiail decision not to try the one out of three-hundred dudes who won't fuck you over was probably validated by the parties that be.<br /> <br /> The issue you seem to have here is the Usurpation uses splat delimination at all, since splats aren't to supposed to have societal weight. Which might work in a game like Requiem, where clan really doesn't do that, but not in Exalted's First Age, where different Exalts were different bodies within a global government, of which the Usurpation represents more or less the collapse of a long term regime. Exaltation has a weird aspect of caste-like impact on career choice and peers and expected privilege in the society. And again, nothing stops there from being Lunars who sided with Sidereals in the end. The issue is those guys are probably going to be the single character who might of been your mentor or previous Exaltation, and so probably left for you to build anyhow. There could of been Sidereals or Terrestrials who tried to side with the Solars: they got killed or simply lost, respectively, as history has shown. And Solars have little to say in it all as the Plan A-Omega was &quot;Solars have to die for this to work at all&quot;.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T12:14:33-08:00","id":25944,"title":"","content":"Maddy, please, <i>please </i>stop patronizing everyone. We're not deluded people trying to hang on to the mistaken idea that the Usurpation is good when it is in fact time to let go. You don't need to tell us that it's &quot;okay to admit&quot; that it's bad. Some of us actually like it and think you are wrong! You don't need to treat those people condescendingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 12-08-2013, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T07:25:06-08:00","id":26485,"title":"","content":"Let's talk more about lunars!<br /> <br /> I DM a Dungeons and Dragons game, and last Sunday we got a new player with her brand new dwarven druid.<br /> <br /> Image!:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://th07.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2013/036/3/7/dwarf_druid_by_vnc_children-d5twcod.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> While I looked over the powers, I didn't help her build the PC and I didn't consider myself an expert on 4e Druids. I was familiar with their ADnD and 3x incarnations though. As the party was making their way through a slave pen, I told her that she'd been captured earlier but was waiting for the right moment to escape.<br /> <br /> She was in a pit, chained by the ankle. <br /> <br /> I assumed she'd transform. Become a panther and use her strength to pull the chain out of the wall? Um, nope, changed into a panther, she still had the same strength. Change into a hawk and fly out of the pit? Um, no, she could turn into a hawk, but it would be the same size as she was and couldn't fly.<br /> <br /> I was shocked! If you've ever played (or seen) a 3x druid, you know they're like a grab bag of animal forms and abilities. Need to swim? Become a shark. Need to pull something heavy? Become an ox. Need to get somewhere quickly? Become a bird. Need to sneak into someone's evil lair? Become a rat.<br /> <br /> That's not to mention that you can become a supernatural animal. I recall the time we were going to attack a city so we slipped into the city's armory, the druid turned into a rust monster, and we rusted away their arms, weapons, and siege engines.<br /> <br /> I realized last night that I tend to think of Lunars as a combination of 3x druids and werewolves from the oWoD. That grab bag of abilities, the monstrous power and aggression, and the reverence for nature. I like the idea that even while rubbing shoulders with socialize and couriers, there's always something untamed within the Lunar. He doesn't really fit in, but he's a master of camouflaging his true nature to blend in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T07:46:18-08:00","id":26496,"title":"","content":"Seeing that picture make me wonder, will Laundry-and-Ivy Prana still exist in Ex3, since you know.....Gaia is know more as a tree-hugging hippy and not a PETA enthusiastic, I await the day I can turn into a strawberry bush before MoW's bedroom and armed with a full-suite of Scorpion-and-Toad charms :&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T07:56:08-08:00","id":26504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25944#post25944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maddy, please, <i>please </i>stop patronizing everyone. We're not deluded people trying to hang on to the mistaken idea that the Usurpation is good when it is in fact time to let go. You don't need to tell us that it's &quot;okay to admit&quot; that it's bad. Some of us actually like it and think you are wrong! You don't need to treat those people condescendingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh, he beat me to it.<br /> <br /> Again.<br /> <br /> Don't ever be alone in a room where there's culinary implements with me G.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T08:19:24-08:00","id":26523,"title":"","content":"You know, it's kind of weird how Maddy keeps referring to the &quot;Team Sidereal&quot; idea derisively, although it's a silly and possibly unintended consequence of poorly considered writing for them...<br /> <br /> When the idea that the Sidereals are more closely knit and homogenous than other Exalted is kind of inherent in their concept, with the whole Fivescore Fellowship and complementary Charms and role in the Divine Bureaucracy things going on. It's part of the idea underlying and distinguishing them, and, for me at least, it's kind of part of their appeal.<br /> <br /> Heck, by my reading, there's a subtext to the whole Bronze-Gold division in which it's supposed to be really kind of weird for the Sidereals to be so partisan, just because they tend to be in the same boat (even if it's a boat that sways around a lot). I can only assume that the addition of a plethora of new antagonists will enhance this.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Dragon Blooded have that whole &quot;gigantic extended family&quot; thing going on also plays into things that could logically hold them closer to each other than to certain outsiders.<br /> <br /> To make this a point relevant to Lunars, I'd imagine that they'd be further distinguished by their particular group context including the tensions that would necessarily underlie a bunch of eminently different people all being kind of shoved together by external pressures.<br /> <br /> Apparently, part of the original concept for each of the different Exalted would be that they kind of formed their own self-contained approaches to the overall genre*, including a capacity to pull in elements that might otherwise be alien to the genre. It's part of what makes them distinct and interesting beyond their aesthetics and powers. It's the premise that is started from, and then a history is worked backwards to produce it.<br /> <br /> This appears to have reasonably appealed to a large number of people, so it has its value.<br /> <br /> When trying to recapture some of that original magic that made the game so distinct and memorable, it's not really best to go &quot;that stuff was dumb and bad, so we need to come up with ways to make it work in spite of that&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's what the Storytelling chapter of Exalted: the Lunars did.<br /> <br /> * Although in the case of Solars, part of their genre is the potential to smash through the barriers separating the other genres, literally and figuratively, and as a presence in the setting they can convey that attitude even into games that don't have people playing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T10:35:42-08:00","id":26589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=26523#post26523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This appears to have reasonably appealed to a large number of people, so it has its value.</div> </div> </div> </div>This logic is interesting to me - one of the all time most criticized and reviled elements of the Exalted metaplot is 'good' because, despite the fact that people have complained about the Usurpation for years, Exalted sold well.<br /> <br /> By that logic, of course, every single decision Exalted ever made reasonably appealed to a large number of people! The number of complaints or topics addressing the possibility of change is irrelevant because the game was clearly perfect. So why even bother with a 3e to begin with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T10:44:17-08:00","id":26596,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Post edited by moderator, no personal attacks please. Darksider</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 12-09-2013, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:17:13-08:00","id":26615,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to patronize, here? I'm just a little astounded at the communal amnesia about the Usurpation situation.<br /> <br /> I had no idea that proposing a second look would provoke such an outpouring of community spite.<br /> <br /> You all COULD try to be a little nicer. I'm presenting my arguments in a straightforward fashion ; if you don't agree, engage me, but try not to get so antagonistic about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-09-2013, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:35:51-08:00","id":26625,"title":"","content":"And for my part, I do kinda love you guys as prickly as you are, so I'll offer a mea culpa as well. I'm a bit sassy of a person and I've certainly been known to try to spice up a comment with ill-advised comedy from time to time. I'm honestly just fishing for a laugh while I make my case. I don't want to hurt any feelings or upset anybody.<br /> <br /> I'm still willing to engage in a more substantive debate about Usurpation realism if anybody feels inclined. (Or, if we need to drive post counts up for the forum war). I'm still very convinced of my position. Heck, we've already delayed immensely on mechanical issues, so a story pass couldn't hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T20:44:38-08:00","id":26967,"title":"","content":"For me, the bottom line of the Usurpation is this: reasonable people will disagree.<br /> <br /> By that I mean that we, as players who know everything that there is to know about the fiction, should be able to reasonably disagree about the moral valence of the actions taken by the major groups/players. Of course, characters in the fiction, PCs and NPCs, will know some subset of what we as players know.<br /> <br /> Sidereal fans should be able to argue that the Great Prophecy means that they've got to do something. Exactly what they should do and what the moral valence of those choices (Gold, Bronze, whatever) should be available for reasonable disagreement.<br /> <br /> Solar fans should be able to argue that the Solars were the hope of Creation and the only ones capable of obtaining the best possible outcomes. Exactly what that means in the face of Great-Currse (and whatever other sources) madness and the fact that they are also capable of the greatest dooms of Creation should be available for reasonable disagreement.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded and Lunars... need more. The Dragon-Blooded need more agency in the Usurpation; being the dupes of the Sidereals is less than interesting. Similarly, the Lunars need more than 'died with their mates or fled to the wild.' It's not that either of these is bad per se, it's that they lack much of any room for reasonable moral disagreement because they either lack agency (in the DB case) or they lack interest or context (in the Lunar case).<br /> <br /> As this is a thread about Lunars, I'll say a bit more about that (and leave DBs for another time). I don't necessarily think that Lunars need to do <i>more, </i>that they need to have a more active role in the Usurpation, though I also wouldn't mind if they did. What the Lunars really need, and perhaps this should really come on in the Lunar book, are <i>reasons</i> for those actions that they do take. I also think that these reasons should be somewhat institutional. This is not because it's necessarily the most accurate depiction of such an event (so far as fiction goes), but because it provides a touchstone for players. Of course individual Lunars might have done whatever just before/during/just after the Usurpation. However, I'm inclined to think that Lunars as a group would do well to have <i>reasons</i> for what they did. To be sure, I'd be perfectly happy for Lunars to take a more active role (whatever that may be) in the Usurpation; I'm just as happy to have their part be, more or less, what it has been... except <i>with reasons and context.</i> Those reasons and that context should also allow for reasonable people to disagree.<br /> <br /> (Note: I would not be completely opposed to the idea of the Usurpation-era Lunars, as a group, being defined by their lack of institutional response in the way that they have been. I'm just inclined to think that some sort of majority reasoning is both easier to write coherently and easier for players to play with. For instance, perhaps the Lunars could have an immediate institutional response, let's GTFO and blah blah, which later falls apart into more individualized stories.)<br /> <br /> That being said, this is my gut reaction to the Usurpation posts (and I apologize for this becoming much longer and more stream-of-consciousness than I intended when I originally started typing; I don't have the energy to actually edit this into something cleaner) ... I'm not trying to get anywhere near whatever's been happening recently in this thread regarding how anyone else has/does/has not/does not feel about the Usurpation as it has existed in Exalted up to this point.<br /> <br /> *I now return to being studious and preparing for exams*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:24:37-08:00","id":27170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=26967#post26967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon-Blooded and Lunars... need more. The Dragon-Blooded need more agency in the Usurpation; being the dupes of the Sidereals is less than interesting. Similarly, the Lunars need more than 'died with their mates or fled to the wild.' It's not that either of these is bad per se, it's that they lack much of any room for reasonable moral disagreement because they either lack agency (in the DB case) or they lack interest or context (in the Lunar case).</div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem the Dragon-Blooded have there is the current perception of elder power levels leading to their role in events being limited to an unheroic Zerg Rush.<br /> To some extent that applies to Lunars as well, Leviathan's stunt with the self destruct might have killed more Dragon-Blooded than all of the Solar Exalted combined but nobody really gives a fuck because people started measuring &quot;how awesome my FA incarnation was in the Usurpation&quot; exclusively in Sidereal kills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:49:35-08:00","id":27188,"title":"","content":"Personally, I view the events of the Shogunate as the main illustration that the rebelling Dragon Blooded had their own issues and ambitions to prompt their actions, and all they needed from the Sidereals was encouragement, guidance, and coordination.<br /> <br /> In my mind, Dragon Blooded in the Usurpation with the least agency weren't dupes of the Sidereals, but gens uninvolved in planning the initial strike who, once word gets around, find their hand kind of forced to raise their banners in support of the new regime (or of surviving, retaliating Solars, for that matter), because they fear what indecision or opposition will bring down upon them.<br /> <br /> But I think that's a lack of agency which is more tragic than denigrating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">their role in events being limited to an unheroic Zerg Rush.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings up a problem people have expressed in ideas relating to the Usurpation and the Terrestrial role in the Primordial War that I finally have the terms to argue against...<br /> <br /> But that I don't really want to do here, because I expect it would be overlooked in the general thrust of the topic, and it doesn't deserve that.<br /> <br /> Ah well... patience patience...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:15:20-08:00","id":27201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27170#post27170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem the Dragon-Blooded have there is the current perception of elder power levels leading to their role in events being limited to an unheroic Zerg Rush.<br /> To some extent that applies to Lunars as well, Leviathan's stunt with the self destruct might have killed more Dragon-Blooded than all of the Solar Exalted combined but nobody really gives a fuck because people started measuring &quot;how awesome my FA incarnation was in the Usurpation&quot; exclusively in<b> Sidereal kills.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remembered the Solar that rushed to Yu-shan in order to call Conky for help managed to kill 9 Sidereals right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:44:59-08:00","id":27216,"title":"","content":"If every Solar who claimed to have killed a Sidereal in the Usurpation actually did then they'd be the Fifty-Score Fellowship.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Oh right... Lunars... uh...<br /> <br /> I was a big fan of the Thousand Streams River. What roll the Lunar's had during the Usurpation is pretty much moot. What is important for giving the Lunar's agency is showing what they did <i>after</i>. And essentially conquering the entire Threshold to bring about a &quot;Vision of Silver&quot; (if you will) where Creation doesn't need Exalted masters (be they Solars or Dragonblooded) is a pretty big thing. It showed the Lunar's weren't sitting in the Wyld twiddling their thumbs, but had in fact taken over <i>most</i> of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-10-2013, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:55:13-08:00","id":27222,"title":"","content":"I've always thought that the Usurpation was more complicated than the official history. I assumed the history spoke in generalities and that there were specific cases that went other ways, but I also assumed that the official history was generally the way things shook out in the end. I feel that any contradicting stories should be left to individual players or ST's to come up with. The Usurpation is supposed to be <i>backdrop</i> on which we paint our own stories. It's almost necessary that anything pre-Age of Sorrow be somewhat less interesting because that's not when the game is set.<br /> <br /> That way when a Lunar player says to me, &quot;Hey, that doesn't make sense!&quot; I can reply, &quot;Oh really? Then what do <i>you</i> think <i>really</i> happened?&quot; and we can build some sort of conspiracy plotline or add some past life shenanigans to his/her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:10:53-08:00","id":27240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27188#post27188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I view the events of the Shogunate as the main illustration that the rebelling Dragon Blooded had their own issues and ambitions to prompt their actions, and all they needed from the Sidereals was encouragement, guidance, and coordination.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Hanging everything off the Usurpation is just going to repeat one of Ex2's main problems. There are centuries of Shogunate history that can be used to flesh out the Dragon-Blooded. And Lunars, for that matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:44:04-08:00","id":27266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27216#post27216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was a big fan of the Thousand Streams River. What roll the Lunar's had during the Usurpation is pretty much moot. What is important for giving the Lunar's agency is showing what they did <i>after</i>. And essentially conquering the entire Threshold to bring about a &quot;Vision of Silver&quot; (if you will) where Creation doesn't need Exalted masters (be they Solars or Dragonblooded) is a pretty big thing. It showed the Lunar's weren't sitting in the Wyld twiddling their thumbs, but had in fact taken over <i>most</i> of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in general terms, I also like the idea of the Thousand Streams River. IIRC, people hate it and it's not coming back in a substantially similar form, but I thought that the concept had potential. In particular, I thought that it could be made made more interesting if pushed more into the idea of a Creation that doesn't depend on Exalted master, as you suggest.<br /> <br /> That is, the Thousand Streams River could be pushed as a response to the greatest failing of the Glorious Solar First Age: that the whole world depends on 300 Solar exalts being there all the time. (Of course, contrivances like the Creation Ruling Mandate actually make it such that the world revolves around Solar masters... but that can be written out of the fiction :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:47:57-08:00","id":27307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27266#post27266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that it could be made made more interesting if pushed more into the idea of a Creation that doesn't depend on Exalted master, <b>as you suggest</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear for anyone who's not familiar with the Thousand Streams River, this is how MoEP: Lunars introduces the concept (literally the first thing it says):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP Lunars</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thousand Streams River is the Silver Pact\u2019s name for its long-term plan to restructure mortal society so that it can function without the aid of the Dragon-Blooded or indeed any other Exalted beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <b>my</b> idea for The Thousand Streams River. It is <b>the</b> idea for The Thousand Streams River. And hate for Halta and the general retconning involved in introducing The Thousand Streams River aside, it is still a fundamentally good idea.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded control the Blessed Isle. Ok, sure. Big whoop. The Lunar's control <b>the rest of Creation</b>. And are making good progress into the Wyld.<br /> <br /> They really don't need a magic island with a Not-Loom-of-Fate made from dirt and rocks. Just a better presentation of The Thousand Streams River.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27266#post27266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, the Thousand Streams River could be pushed as a response to the greatest failing of the Glorious Solar First Age: that the whole world depends on 300 Solar exalts being there all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Vision of Bronze and Solar rule be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-10-2013, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:19:05-08:00","id":27331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27307#post27307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded control the Blessed Isle. Ok, sure. Big whoop. The Lunar's control the Threshold. And are making good progress into the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes yes, and then they slayed the Jabberwocky and went on to save Narnia.<br /> <br /> You know, there are several reasons why the Thousand Streams River lacked credibility, but I'd say one of the more glaring ones was how, given the developmental mandate to all but repeat information from First Edition verbatim, <i>everything else</i> written about the setting was still acting as though the Realm was the great and terrible empire standing astride the world.<br /> <br /> At least where it wasn't transplanting the settings that had been functioning without Dragon Blooded or other Exalted aid since the very beginning of the setting without needing Lunars to teach them how, because hey, if you're going to steal heat, you might as well steal it from everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-10-2013, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:23:04-08:00","id":27333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27240#post27240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hanging everything off the Usurpation is just going to repeat one of Ex2's main problems. There are centuries of Shogunate history that can be used to flesh out the Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nono, I'm getting at the idea that the fact that the Dragon Blooded immediately turned on each other is an indication that they all had their own issues behind their rebellion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:27:25-08:00","id":27338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27201#post27201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vaguely remembered the Solar that rushed to Yu-shan in order to call Conky for help managed to kill 9 Sidereals right ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he was killed by several elder Sidereals, but I'm pretty sure they all lived through it.<br /> <br /> He did pretty much murderize his way through Yu-Shan in a staight line toward the Jade Pleasure Dome though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:49:18-08:00","id":27356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27333#post27333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nono, I'm getting at the idea that the fact that the Dragon Blooded immediately turned on each other is an indication that they all had their own issues behind their rebellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also interesting. We need moar shogunate either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T15:55:13-08:00","id":27584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=25622#post25622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't you paying attention? The 'Team : Sidereal' shirts clearly outline the ultimate goals of the Usurpation in bold type along the back side, along with a complete description of the Great Prophesy.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know what game YOU'VE been playing, but typically Sidereal Exalted are really honest about what they want you to do. They don't really so much manipulate or subtly guide people, they just kinda show up and tell you what they want (usually, by pointing at the T-shirt and exclaiming 'Duh' really loudly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I don't agree with your analysis of the Usurpation in the context of historical revolutions - I do, and I'd really like to see it get a more nuanced treatment, given how amazing Exalted tends to be when it applies modern conceptions of nuance to myth and legend - but your post makes me unironically want to see a Sidereal Charm that lets them foster teamwork and cooperation towards an agenda by passing out T-shirts with cheaply-printed motivational logos or slogans like you'd get at a corporate seminar.<br /> <br /> Regarding the role of Lunars in the Usurpation, I personally favor the explanation that much of the groundwork was done by sowing as much mistrust as possible beforehand using every dirty trick in the book, so that fewer Sids and Deebs would get pureed by their primary targets' mates when the time came. When Solar lie-detection runs up against Lunar perfect lying and vice-versa, the safe option for both of them is to just assume the other is lying (Prisoner's Dilemma, ho!). That said, I'd be leery of spelling out TOO much about how everything went down for one, simple reason: for many players, the Usurpation is as much a part of their character's backstory as their mortal, pre-Exaltation life, if not moreso. Locking in too many details locks out a lot of cool background possibilities, especially when there's a pronounced tendency for player and ST alike to see anything written in a book as ironclad and immutable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T16:50:06-08:00","id":27618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27333#post27333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nono, I'm getting at the idea that the fact that the Dragon Blooded immediately turned on each other is an indication that they all had their own issues behind their rebellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to imagine that the Dragonblooded were promised quite a lot, basically promised that in the absence of the Solars and Lunars that all thousands of them would get the power and rulership and luxury afforded to the elite. It wouldn't surprise me if the Sidereals had cleverly promised the same individual widget or position to six or seven or ten thousand Terrestrials at a time over and over again. It reminds me of the Russian Revolution, where a good half of any history of it is going to be about the revolutionary anti-monarch factions fighting one another. <br /> <br /> With regard to mistrust, if many of the Solars are going power-mad and many of the Lunars are going Chimeric, it seems it'd be quite easy for the Chief Bureaucrats to make the rest of the Celestials extremely paranoid about one another, especially since it's implied in some of the books that certain Primordial War veterans were occupying the highest positions and living for three or four millennia or longer. I wouldn't be surprised if the Sidereals had most of the Solars and Lunars watching other Solars and Lunars at the Calibration Feast. I think this goes along nicely with some of what Maddy has been saying, that thinking of the Exalts as splat-based teams is bound to result in an extremely silly Usurpation. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:10:51-08:00","id":27627,"title":"","content":"I don't mind a Usurpation where not much is specified, but that doesn't really work with a 'not much wil specified EXCEPT for the lame splat story'.<br /> <br /> Personally, I take the High First Age at face value. This is what I know about it from what I have read; which is why I have issues, because many of the things printed about the High First Age seem to contradict one another.<br /> <br /> In the High First Age, the dominant political entity is the Circle, not the splat. Multiple circles command immense influence. Many of those who are in command of these circles are having struggles with the Great Curse ; comrades accept these difficulties based upon long-standing relationships (and the fact they endure the same thing), and generally speaking Circles look out for each other. Mixed circles of multiple Exalt types are extremely common. They are, in fact, the rule... not the exception.<br /> <br /> Absent any real conflict or pressing world-ending threats, the Exalted have turned to insular pursuits. Pet projects... either personal, or circle-based... are the order of the day. Deliberative control is growing more and more tenuous as more and more Elder Solar Exalted declare themselves autonomous tributaries. 'Everybody knows' those guys are doing stuff they shouldn't be, but nobody really does anything about it. It's institutionalized and the Exalted are so august they aren't about to be challenged on this.<br /> <br /> Because they don't have so many REAL battles to fight, the Exalted tend to get very emotional and passionate about various ideological and political issues - let's take a real-world modern example that doesn't translate into Exalted as a hypothetical placeholder example : drug policy. Exalted fight duels over drug policy. They talk shit about drug policy endlessly. They describe people who don't agree with the policy THEY agree with in hyperbolic, inflammatory terms.<br /> <br /> When speaking with Dragonblooded... or anybody else, for that matter... objectively speaking, a description of the Great Prophesy comes across as culty madness. Only Sidereals are going to understand the magnitude and importance of the prophesy; nobody else really appreciates what they do as much. One must also view this in the realm of the established metaphysics, and how silly the prophesy is -to begin with- in a setting that repeatadly emphasis the importance of free will. Destiny is already proven to not-really-apply to Exalted, so forming a coalition based upon a prophesy that the Exalted will do something in some nebulous future is a ridiculous idea.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the far more effective strategy would seem to be to exploit already existing political divisions and bring the Realm down using the same tools and methods the Sidereals have -always- used.<br /> <br /> Instead, we get the 'Red Wedding'. In Game of Thrones, this worked because we were describing a pre-industrial society of far reduced magnitude and complexity... and, we were discussing -people- who were unified behind clan banners, not God-Kings plucked from various eras/locations in Creation of various age half-maddened by limit break.<br /> <br /> It's honestly pretty silly to suggest the Solars would -ever- get in the same room at this point, without serious defenses and paranoia involved that would have made the Usurpation kinda a wash.<br /> <br /> We describe this world experiencing fundamental political angst due to these god-kings going semi-crazy and becoming more and more irrational, but then we have them all act like a unified entity when confronted with other 'splats'.<br /> <br /> I would rather see all of this sillyness completely disregarded in favor of 'A coup happened'. I think the stupid dinner should be gone ; I think the stupid 'over in a day more or less' war should be gone; I think the stupid declarations of Lunar and Dragonblooded motivations on the macro level should be gone.<br /> <br /> It should be declared a mess that the Sidereals came out on top of (probably due more to Machiavellian maneuvers than martial pussiance) and left at that.<br /> <br /> This is Lunars thread, so I'll point out that while I'm focusing on the Usurpation here, that's only because the Lunar 'identity issue' in the first age is a symptom of the greater disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-10-2013, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:23:12-08:00","id":27636,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's honestly pretty silly to suggest the Solars would -ever- get in the same room at this point, without serious defenses and paranoia involved that would have made the Usurpation kinda a wash.&quot;<br /> <br /> Generally, I'd agree with you, but I think the clever idea that &quot;Calibration is effectively mandatory so none of you assholes can try to summon and bind Ligier&quot; helps explain that, and I wouldn't be surprised if the Solars had trusted the Sidereals and Dragonblooded to handle the grunt-work of the defenses for two thousand years without anything going wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:51:53-08:00","id":27638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind a Usurpation where not much is specified, but that doesn't really work with a 'not much wil specified EXCEPT for the lame splat story'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concep that <i>a priori</i> splat-based conflict and events is stupid is kind of the issue I think we're at disagreement here. It sucked in lots of cWoD. It doesn't make sense in nWoD very much either, honestly. It does work in other environments, though. Tribes in Forsaken, for instance, have veins of this between Pure and Forsaken. Exalted sorts are also, again, also positions and offices in the First Age world-spanning infastructure, of which the SIdereals were very speicifically always the most tight-knit. That Exaltation also tends to select certain personality types and imbue one wiht a certain set of skills useful for some endeavors over others also will cause clique forming and general political factioning around some aspects of splat line. Folks aren't their group, but that doens't mean there's no such thing as a group metality. Especially when paycheques and privilege kick in.<br /> <br /> I also question so-called &quot;forum amnesia&quot; on the topic. Infernals and Yozi Charms, Devil-Tigers, the impacts of Solars upon the setting in general, Artifact aesthetics and a perception of Lunar Exalted as pointless and the bamilion ways to try to fix that are what I remember quite a bit more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I take the High First Age at face value. This is what I know about it from what I have read; which is why I have issues, because many of the things printed about the High First Age seem to contradict one another.<br /> <br /> In the High First Age, the dominant political entity is the Circle, not the splat. Multiple circles command immense influence. Many of those who are in command of these circles are having struggles with the Great Curse ; comrades accept these difficulties based upon long-standing relationships (and the fact they endure the same thing), and generally speaking Circles look out for each other. Mixed circles of multiple Exalt types are extremely common. They are, in fact, the rule... not the exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle as by default multi-splat is not actually ever stated anywhere. This is in practice with play since folks like playing mixed-Circle groups, but not the assumptioin in the First Age. Nearly everything ever talked on the issue indicated that Solars and Sidereals formed Circles within their Exalt sorts, with Lunars acting as free agents or attached to Solar mate and Dragon-Blooded doing their own thing with Brotherhoods. This might be how your Creation works, but it has not been the statement of the game as far as Ic an tell forever. There's auspicious weight given to Perfect Circles, there is a thing called the Solar Deliberative and Sidereals have always been the Fivescore Fellowship serving in the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Complaining that the devs are not writing an Usurpation to fit the multi-splat version of the First Age located in your personal canon is not really something that I feel has a lot of weight behind it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absent any real conflict or pressing world-ending threats, the Exalted have turned to insular pursuits. Pet projects... either personal, or circle-based... are the order of the day. Deliberative control is growing more and more tenuous as more and more Elder Solar Exalted declare themselves autonomous tributaries. 'Everybody knows' those guys are doing stuff they shouldn't be, but nobody really does anything about it. It's institutionalized and the Exalted are so august they aren't about to be challenged on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which again, is still how you have built the First Age. It's vague and that's fine, but there is impression I get of large-scale projects, flashbacks in books of Solars going too far and getting hunted down for their crimes to Creation which seem legitimate (large scale crime rings, mass havoc, things like that). The devs are working from First Principles, not headcanon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> When speaking with Dragonblooded... or anybody else, for that matter... objectively speaking, a description of the Great Prophesy comes across as culty madness. Only Sidereals are going to understand the magnitude and importance of the prophesy; nobody else really appreciates what they do as much. One must also view this in the realm of the established metaphysics, and how silly the prophesy is -to begin with- in a setting that repeatadly emphasis the importance of free will. Destiny is already proven to not-really-apply to Exalted, so forming a coalition based upon a prophesy that the Exalted will do something in some nebulous future is a ridiculous idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prophecy runs outside of the &quot;mecahnics = physics&quot; aspects of the game. We have no mechanical reason but we have any amount of metaphysical reason to buy that the nature of the Prophecy being a year long ritual require all 100 Sidereals to be alive and acting in it at expense of other shit probably gives it some weight to be accurate. And as you note, as no one else has an ability to really comprehend what the Sidereals are talking about, they didn't consult anyone else on it anyways. Because the Sidereals as a group probably understood enought hat others don't matter and the Prophecy itsel fmight have issues in self-fulfilling parts if it leaked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, the far more effective strategy would seem to be to exploit already existing political divisions and bring the Realm down using the same tools and methods the Sidereals have -always- used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under what motivation and with what impetus? As noted by others already, while Exalted is a lot of breaking things down in real politik, it still does run on genre tropes and decisions. Great Prophecies of Doom that lead to huge political upheavel are one of them. Arthur was going to save and destroy his nation. The Han were going to fall. Narazen's kingdom would die unless she got a kid. Cantos who are prone to being psychopaths will go and murder everyone. The Golden Path is strewn with bodies. The Usurpation had the visions of Gold, Bronze and Darkness. It plays on those tropes, because Exalted isn't just real world politics with magic physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, we get the 'Red Wedding'. In Game of Thrones, this worked because we were describing a pre-industrial society of far reduced magnitude and complexity... and, we were discussing -people- who were unified behind clan banners, not God-Kings plucked from various eras/locations in Creation of various age half-maddened by limit break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as Sidereal madness is traditionally being a hubritic ass more than anything compared to going Mad Scientist or werewolf, things seem likely that if anyone got united on an agenda it would be Sidereals. And note Sidereals also often could find the guys who would be Sidereals and raise them in Heaven. So there's expeted to be a bit more culturla homogeny there than in the other Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly pretty silly to suggest the Solars would -ever- get in the same room at this point, without serious defenses and paranoia involved that would have made the Usurpation kinda a wash.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what their defenses can total to, how much the Calibration Feast was also a general considered armistice, how much hubris was involved and even how much Eclipse Oath was being tossed about. A lot of the entire idea of the event was, note, based on Solars not trusting <i>one-another</i>. It's also notable that not everyone was there or got killed int he initial alpha strike. Just enough did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We describe this world experiencing fundamental political angst due to these god-kings going semi-crazy and becoming more and more irrational, but then we have them all act like a unified entity when confronted with other 'splats'.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're united in the sense that a lot were in the apparently long established cultural tradition of eating dinner for New Years in the First Age's G8 Summit. They wer eunite din &quot;Needed to be killed by other splats who do tend to unite.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather see all of this sillyness completely disregarded in favor of 'A coup happened'. I think the stupid dinner should be gone ; I think the stupid 'over in a day more or less' war should be gone; I think the stupid declarations of Lunar and Dragonblooded motivations on the macro level should be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are Lunars the way they are now? Why do elders, who fund and train the generations of Lunars after, want to break the whole damned thing down and kill Sidereals? What motivated the uprising? What motivates the people in charge of the Sidereal Host now who remember the whys and what-fors? The Usurpation has a bit of a thing in that it's the watershed moment for the rest of the setting. So it gets described. A genre-appropriate prophecy happened, the genre appropriate events occur. The issue seems, again, this <i>a priori</i> assumption that &quot;splat goals = stupid&quot;, which is not a sound statement. And the setting going and doing something you say it should do, but it has never claimed to be doing in other instnace.s<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be declared a mess that the Sidereals came out on top of (probably due more to Machiavellian maneuvers than martial pussiance) and left at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Chejob, the orchestrator still alive, is a self-serving shill instead of someone who might have had at least some incling of &quot;Ends justifine the means&quot; villain? I think I'll pass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27627#post27627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Lunars thread, so I'll point out that while I'm focusing on the Usurpation here, that's only because the Lunar 'identity issue' in the first age is a symptom of the greater disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>That splats are there at all? Since so far the only thing I get from you is that Exalt sort shouldn't have more impact than say, clan, does in Requiem or Creed in Hunter: the Reckoning. To which I would answer that not all games, or even within Exalt all Exalt sorts, need to treat splats with the same level of ability to have societies, goals and cultural identity.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:53:54-08:00","id":27639,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the Calibration Feast thing (which, by 2.5 considerations, is itself pretty silly)... I'm willing to grant they'd show up.<br /> <br /> I'm just not willing to accept they'd show up and be 'sitting ducks' for assassination. They'd all come loaded for bear, with as much muscle as they could muster, layering dead-man switch nastyness behind them as far as the eye can see.<br /> <br /> ... because they're not just debauched rulers earning a comeuppance. They are manifest God-Kings who are growing increasingly paranoid, unstable and 'weird'... so much so, that the Sidereals feel they will destroy the world.<br /> <br /> If we're going to work with that premise, then we need to work with that premise, not use it selectively, right?<br /> <br /> I mean, think about it - this is far from the 'perfect opportunity' to do this.<br /> <br /> It's literally probably the WORST possible opportunity to do this.<br /> <br /> Simultanious assasination across Creation when the Solars are not expecting knives in the back... and are not gathered together into a glorious super-army that might just unify in the face of a greater foe... is far more feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:09:49-08:00","id":27649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27639#post27639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the Calibration Feast thing (which, by 2.5 considerations, is itself pretty silly)... I'm willing to grant they'd show up.<br /> <br /> I'm just not willing to accept they'd show up and be 'sitting ducks' for assassination. They'd all come loaded for bear, with as much muscle as they could muster, layering dead-man switch nastyness behind them as far as the eye can see.<br /> <br /> ... because they're not just debauched rulers earning a comeuppance. They are manifest God-Kings who are growing increasingly paranoid, unstable and 'weird'... so much so, that the Sidereals feel they will destroy the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>A security force literally <i>thousands</i> of Dragon-Blooded strong was protecting Meru the night of the (yearly!) gathering. How much more secure can you get?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:18:18-08:00","id":27651,"title":"","content":"Paranoia is actually the worst thing to actually come up with good defensive strategies with. The precautions a paranoid person takes are all idiosyncratically tailored to their delusions, rather than an impetus to engage in rational threat assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:23:42-08:00","id":27655,"title":"","content":"Also, this? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One must also view this in the realm of the established metaphysics, and how silly the prophesy is -to begin with- in a setting that repeatadly emphasis the importance of free will. Destiny is already proven to not-really-apply to Exalted, so forming a coalition based upon a prophesy that the Exalted will do something in some nebulous future is a ridiculous idea. </div> </div> </div> Seriously, fuck this. &quot;Hey, let's make a group of prophets who are also advisors to the great heroes, but completely undermine their function by lionising the great heroes as basically beyond the foresight of prophets and also make a big chunk of enemies also arbitrarily immune to prophecy.&quot; Just terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:23:45-08:00","id":27656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27649#post27649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A security force literally <i>thousands</i> of Dragon-Blooded strong was protecting Meru the night of the (yearly!) gathering. How much more secure can you get?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, are the Solars afraid of, if not each other? And thus, the retinues of their compatriots?<br /> <br /> Trusting an army to protect you from that dude two tables over finally deciding to take your cold war hot seems... pretty foolish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:28:10-08:00","id":27657,"title":"","content":"Because it's impolite to air your dirty laundry in front of everybody else like that. Also, hey, see in the U.N. how delegates from India and Pakistan aren't killing each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:35:43-08:00","id":27660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27649#post27649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A security force literally <i>thousands</i> of Dragon-Blooded strong was protecting Meru the night of the (yearly!) gathering. How much more secure can you get?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, how can we forget the thousands of people ALSO in on the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> When we have already described the 'supernal intelligence apparatus' of the High First Age as being a transhumanist terror headed up buy ever-vigilant Night Caste Exalted who have extensive charm portfolios dedicated to figuring out -exactly this sort of thing-, along with extensive pawns / mentally conditioned troops within the 'traitor army'.<br /> <br /> How did we justify that in 2e, again? With that bullshit Dynasty charm, IIRC? Ugh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:39:51-08:00","id":27663,"title":"","content":"Also, just to expand on the paranoia thing, a halfway functional paranoid person will still have habits and routines that override their persecution delusions, or just plain don't intersect with them. Like, maybe a person thinks that somebody's out to get them, but I bet you most such people don't, say, completely randomise the brand of drink they consume and the store they buy it from to keep the person who's out to get them from poisoning all of the drinks of the same brand in the same store in order to get them. And if a person actually was trying to kill them, they could totally exploit that. I mean, sure, one could present the Solars as the non-functional, Howard Hughes kind of paranoid, but it doesn't really fit the genre tone. So instead, whatever paranoia any of them have doesn't extend to them not being used to the big lavish celebration where everybody is conditioned to play nice. Or if it does, it's a tiny minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:40:16-08:00","id":27664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27657#post27657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's impolite to air your dirty laundry in front of everybody else like that. Also, hey, see in the U.N. how delegates from India and Pakistan aren't killing each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya know, just like... 150 years ago, members of congress were challenging each other to duels to the death and beating each other into comas with blunt instruments.... WHILE IN SESSION.<br /> <br /> And that's without Limit Break or super kung-fu!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:42:13-08:00","id":27665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we have already described the 'supernal intelligence apparatus' of the High First Age as being a transhumanist terror headed up buy ever-vigilant Night Caste Exalted who have extensive charm portfolios dedicated to figuring out -exactly this sort of thing-, along with extensive pawns / mentally conditioned troops within the 'traitor army'.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you <i>like</i> this as an image of the First Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:42:18-08:00","id":27666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27655#post27655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this? Seriously, fuck this. &quot;Hey, let's make a group of prophets who are also advisors to the great heroes, but completely undermine their function by lionising the great heroes as basically beyond the foresight of prophets and also make a big chunk of enemies also arbitrarily immune to prophecy.&quot; Just terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, it somewhat deprotagonizes the remaining splats if the Sidereals do in fact have any real prophetic power beyond offering incentives for things.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it's impossible to RUN actual prophesy good with any degree of reliability, as thousands of STs throughout history can attest to.<br /> <br /> This is one of the fundamental 'wrinkles' of Sidereals that can never honestly be fixed. It's particularly grating since much of the 1e fiction was written without these things in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:47:36-08:00","id":27669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27660#post27660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, how can we forget the thousands of people ALSO in on the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> When we have already described the 'supernal intelligence apparatus' of the High First Age as being a transhumanist terror headed up buy ever-vigilant Night Caste Exalted who have extensive charm portfolios dedicated to figuring out -exactly this sort of thing-, along with extensive pawns / mentally conditioned troops within the 'traitor army'.<br /> <br /> How did we justify that in 2e, again? With that bullshit Dynasty charm, IIRC? Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far the 3e one seems to be less about having Investigation Charms that make it so you don't have to have the Ability anymore. My guess would be that part of the issue wiht finding the Terrestrial part of the conspiracy is that:<br /> - It was probably pretty long term planned by Sidereals but short-term planned by Dragon-Blooded, depending on the brass' already inherent dislike of Solars.<br /> - Possibly previous rebellions that were put down due to enough loyalists.<br /> - A bit of spontaneaity.<br /> <br /> <br /> It should be noted, enough Dragon-Blooded decided not to side with the Usurpers that the world got sent through Continental World War II at best. They lost.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that, again, the Calibration Feast was kind of a big alpha strike to gain momentum. An all-out assault without an ambush would have probably not succeeded without the headstart, judging from the damage estimates given on the protracted parts.<br /> <br /> Also, judging from some of the &quot;Dreams of the First Age&quot; chapters we have about, some Solars kind of were dumbstruck the Dragon-Blooded did things on their own, went to their Sidereal advisors for advise and in at least one instance got a knife in the back for it. As already stated, for most Solars, it appears that they thought the only threat anymore was other Solars. The entire point of the Calibration Feast and its paranoia over everyone else doing things kind of demosntrates this.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:50:02-08:00","id":27670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27660#post27660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, how can we forget the thousands of people ALSO in on the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> When we have already described the 'supernal intelligence apparatus' of the High First Age as being a transhumanist terror headed up buy ever-vigilant Night Caste Exalted who have extensive charm portfolios dedicated to figuring out -exactly this sort of thing-, along with extensive pawns / mentally conditioned troops within the 'traitor army'.<br /> <br /> How did we justify that in 2e, again? With that bullshit Dynasty charm, IIRC? Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I woudl assume the Feast had gone on enough centuries or so that folks probably thought better than it at that point. Kind of like Congress or the UN now instead of 150 years ago. more sniping and out of room vendetta-making, less hostility in public. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:50:35-08:00","id":27671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya know, just like... 150 years ago, members of congress were challenging each other to duels to the death and beating each other into comas with blunt instruments.... WHILE IN SESSION. And that's without Limit Break or super kung-fu!</div> </div> </div> </div> It's also without Congress completely disintegrating because nobody attends it anymore, apparently. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it somewhat deprotagonizes the remaining splats if the Sidereals do in fact have any real prophetic power beyond offering incentives for things</div> </div> </div> </div> Not if, a relevent amount of the time, the only response to &quot;you foresee having a giant sword shoved through your jugular in the next three seconds&quot; is to go &quot;Well fuURRK&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's impossible to RUN actual prophesy good with any degree of reliability, as thousands of STs throughout history can attest to.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then don't present prophecies that include details out of your control. Like, if it's a prophecy that's supposed to happen. It's not a bad thing if PCs get told a future they're supposed to change. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's particularly grating since much of the 1e fiction was written without these things in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> None of the setting material has ever assumed paranoia combat either. Concerns about making paranoia combat less of a thing in the system, I'd personally find setting fiction which actually acts like mechanical results are how things are expected to happen in the setting to be deeply unsatisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:53:21-08:00","id":27672,"title":"","content":"I always kind of assumed that the Calibration Feast played specifically on that very paranoia and hubris which, the Sidereals knew, would eventually shatter the world. The Solars were so blinded by their own glory that they cared nothing for those beneath them -- and thus, their fellow Solars were, to their minds, the only rivals or threats worth taking seriously. The Terrestrial and Sidereal Exalted attempting a coup? Ridiculous! They were the Solar's inferiors and knew their place. Surely this is some feint by an old enemy, or a young rival looking to make a name for himself, or a betrayal by the old comrade they always thought might be plotting against them...<br /> <br /> ...and so, in the moment of the Terrestrial attack, Solar blades turned not against their true enemies, but each other. Just as the Sidereals planned. Oh, some certainly realized the truth and fled or tried to rally, and these examples are much of why the Usurpation took many years instead of a single night. But my impression was always that Solars accounted for most of their own casualties during the Calibration Feast; their pride and paranoia would not allow otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27655#post27655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this? Seriously, fuck this. &quot;Hey, let's make a group of prophets who are also advisors to the great heroes, but completely undermine their function by lionising the great heroes as basically beyond the foresight of prophets and also make a big chunk of enemies also arbitrarily immune to prophecy.&quot; Just terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here speaks great truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:53:42-08:00","id":27673,"title":"","content":"This begins to verge into 'Assumptions of Competence' and 'Assumptions of Incomptence' territory for me.<br /> <br /> I prefer to see competence and incompetence more evenly distributed.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals have had issues with Assumptions of Competence for some time. Part of this is due to the way the archetype of the 'Gandalf' character is constructed ; later, we got elegant mechanics that tried to explain how such a character could exist and still be... fallible, or interesting.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, when the history of Exalted was written, those mechanics did not exist.<br /> <br /> So we get Sidereals as strangely infallible masterminds, the 'Illuminati' of the First Age, always one step ahead and never caught unawares. Gandalf is just too awesome for that!<br /> <br /> The problem is, that 'short hand' didn't really mesh when the rest of the game was described... PARTICULARLY, when we saw the Sidereals more in depth and understood exactly how they functioned. The Great Prophesy was written in a time before the 'Player Agency vs Fate' question was even seriously considered. Contemplate that. Back then, it literally was just, 'They tell the future somehow. It works.'<br /> <br /> In order for the Usurpation to work, you need to assume the Sidereals were always exceptionally competent, and those they slaughtered were always exceptionally incompetent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-10-2013, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:55:22-08:00","id":27674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far the 3e one seems to be less about having Investigation Charms that make it so you don't have to have the Ability anymore. My guess would be that part of the issue wiht finding the Terrestrial part of the conspiracy is that: - It was probably pretty long term planned by Sidereals but short-term planned by Dragon-Blooded, depending on the brass' already inherent dislike of Solars. - Possibly previous rebellions that were put down due to enough loyalists. - A bit of spontaneaity.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say that there were plenty of Solars who were aware of conspiracy on the level of the Terrestrials to some degree. Their main problems were that other Terrestrial investigators sent to collate further information on the ground level kept being compromised and, more importantly, the Solars didn't take the threat seriously. To a degree, the Usurpation is like the 9/11 of Exalted (probably including some Lunar and Dragon Blooded conspiracy theorists who find the apparent facts so unbelievable that they compose elaborate narratives that seem more plausible and palatable to them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:03:28-08:00","id":27685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27674#post27674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would say that there were plenty of Solars who were aware of conspiracy on the level of the Terrestrials to some degree. Their main problems were that other Terrestrial investigators sent to collate further information on the ground level kept being compromised and, more importantly, the Solars didn't take the threat seriously. To a degree, the Usurpation is like the 9/11 of Exalted (probably including some Lunar and Dragon Blooded conspiracy theorists who find the apparent facts so unbelievable that they compose elaborate narratives that seem more plausible and palatable to them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do on some level think that might also be a bit of things. Humans have a bery strong tendancy to not care about something when it is shown not to be a threat. See all the times folks text and drive, even if rationally you know one shouldn't do it. The Usurpation and the Solars being blindsided by it seems like a perfect example of the Reverse Tinkerbell Effect at work.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:05:00-08:00","id":27687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27672#post27672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always kind of assumed that the Calibration Feast played specifically on that very paranoia and hubris which, the Sidereals knew, would eventually shatter the world. The Solars were so blinded by their own glory that they cared nothing for those beneath them -- and thus, their fellow Solars were, to their minds, the only rivals or threats worth taking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumptions of Comptenence/Incompetence.<br /> <br /> I believe the Solar Exalted were not reduced to such a degree by the Great Curse. SOME, perhaps, were... but the vast majority were more-or-less mostly lucid. They behaved in a more or less logical fashion, tainted by extreme virtues.<br /> <br /> None of this implies a gross underestimation of the people that serve them, except in perhaps specific cases.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:06:29-08:00","id":27689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27660#post27660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, how can we forget the thousands of people ALSO in on the conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think Gaius Julius went to every soldier in his army and personally talked him into overthrowing the government before crossing the Rubicon, or do you think he just said &quot;Forward!&quot; and his men obeyed, as they'd been trained their whole lives to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:13:51-08:00","id":27695,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that among Paranoid God Kings who have a traditional yearly feast, the worst thing you could do is not show up because that paints a giant target sign on your back as &quot;suspicious&quot;. Sure it's bad if you think people are out to get you and you have to look them in the face, but to galvanize all those people against you because you don't show up? Who knows what you could be plotting!<br /> <br /> The Solars may have been Paranoid God Kings, but given that they were mostly paranoid against each other, that is where tunnel visions can let outrageous things like the Calibration Feast Ambush happen.<br /> <br /> Note: By clicking on this spoiler tag you forfeit the right to get righteously indignant over the contents of it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> In my opinion (allow me to bloviate a moment) this stuff just seems to write itself, honestly, as long as you do not do the following:<br /> <br /> A) Consider that Mechanical Representations of Mythical Events important (or relevant at all). It should be painfully obvious what this does to any White Wolf game. This is definitely not the game for it.<br /> <br /> B) Look for reasons it could work rather than look for reasons it doesn't. <b>The entire setting can be subjected to the same scrutiny and make no sense, if you do not want it to.</b> Looking for reasons it does work gives you the seeds to USE the Ursupation in interesting ways divergent from those reasons it does work.<br /> <br /> For Example:Why do the super secret agent Night Castes not see this coming? MAKE IT UP AND MAKE IT A PLOT HOOK.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":".  Clarification in-spoiler 12-10-2013, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T19:19:23-08:00","id":27696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27687#post27687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assumptions of Comptenence/Incompetence.<br /> <br /> I believe the Solar Exalted were not reduced to such a degree by the Great Curse. SOME, perhaps, were... but the vast majority were more-or-less mostly lucid. They behaved in a more or less logical fashion, tainted by extreme virtues.<br /> <br /> None of this implies a gross underestimation of the people that serve them, except in perhaps specific cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucid beings do not seriously make plans to dissolve the world into chaos so that they can remake it in an improved version. They do not unleash the Wyld upon vast areas of Creation out of boredom and the desire for military readiness. They do not plan to give every single sentient in the world the power to glass a city with a modicum of preparation and study (and yes, that was Salina's ultimate objective -- to reshape the laws of Creation so that the Circle of Adamant was available to any being who wished to learn it).<br /> <br /> More importantly, the <i>point</i> of the First Age -- or so it seems to me -- is that it had grown corrupt, decadent and mad. If the Solars were &quot;more or less mostly lucid&quot;, then why evoke the Great Prophecy at all? Why was the Vision of Gold not the shoe-in answer, if the Solars could, by and large, be reasoned with? This isn't assuming Solar incompetence. This is assuming that they did, in fact, have flaws -- the epic flaws which come with their epic natures in the sword-and-sorcery genre, exaggerated and impelled by the death-curse of the Primordials, which laid on them most heavily of all the Exalted. And the Sidereals -- the prophets, advisors and spymasters among the Exalted Host -- used those flaws to undo them; that's not only in-genre, but also very much in their nature.<br /> <br /> ETA: I am aware that the vast majority of the history of the First Age will be re-mystified in 3E. I do, however, think that it will conform more to the idea of mythic, decadent god-kings, larger than life with flaws to match, than it will to real-world political theory. After all, as far as Creation is concerned, it has long passed into myth, and who but Heaven can truly say what passed in those ancient days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":39,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","user":"ysadrel","date":". 12-10-2013, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:07:18-08:00","id":27717,"title":"","content":"It's possible to come up with all sorts of vaguely-feasible-if-you-squint-hard-enough reasons the Usurpation can fly, but why? Let me make an argument that we should instead rethink it.<br /> <br /> We KNOW the real reason the Usurpation feels weird - Sidereals, and fate, were not yet defined when the 1e history was written.<br /> <br /> Players, and writers, had no idea what the limitations of these beings were or what they could do.<br /> <br /> The default archetype of the Sidereals, the 'Mysterious Xanatos Wizard', was used as shorthand.<br /> <br /> The problem is, Mysterious Xanatos Wizard is hyper competent. Gandalf is not really 'balanced' with everybody else. He's there to motivate the story.<br /> <br /> This becomes an issue later on when Sidereals are actually clearly defined, are somewhat balanced in the context of the other Exalted. Further, they do not have the ability to predict the actions of essence using beings to any serious degree (which they... and everybody else!... are keenly aware of!).<br /> <br /> So we have a fiction that is incompatible with the Sidereals as presented.<br /> <br /> This is an issue we should examine.<br /> <br /> It's very possible to have a Usurpation that does not rely upon the assumptions that were made pre1e Sidereals. Back before Sidereals were defined, they always benefited from 'Assumptions of Competence', excepting incidences of tragic hubris. They did what they needed to do to make the story happen, and nobody could really stop them. They are the Deus Ex Illumanati.<br /> <br /> We should rewrite the fiction with the actual Sidereal Exalted, as we came to understand them when they were actually examined and thought through. This would create a better story that could hew very closely to the original structure and intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-10-2013, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:24:04-08:00","id":27719,"title":"","content":"Couldn't a lot of this be done with the idea that a lot of short term prophecies are reliable, long term gets worn-out when subjected to too much strain (like a weather forecast) and super big powerful once-in-history rituals that take a year probably can take into account enough of those variables to give you a fairly complete Pr(\u03a9) that is nearly 1 enough that these three choices are indeed the three choices? Just saying that the Prophecy seems to work just fine if it isn't assumed to be something you can mechanize from the extent rules isnce it's fairly obviously a unique one-off event.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:46:59-08:00","id":27727,"title":"","content":"I don't believe that the thesis of &quot;Sidereals are hypercompetent Mysterious Xanatos Wizards&quot; is supported by canon as it stands, with the original conception of the Usurpation. The thesis I instead support is &quot;Solars were larger-than-life pulp sorcerer-kings with the flaws of larger-than-life sorcerer-kings, which the Sidereals and Terrestrials used to lay them low in an epic, world-spanning struggle.&quot; I also do not know the reason the Usurpation feels weird, because it doesn't feel weird to me; I would appreciate it if, in future, my feelings were left to me to determine.<br /> <br /> I also find it extremely questionable that the developers of the line -- the original writers who conceived of the Usurpation -- had no idea of Sidereal limitations when they did so. Certainly the execution of certain 1E splats was mangled, but we do know that that was writers acting against the developer's instructions for the most part, and that Grabowski had a clear vision of the gameworld. It seems very reasonable to me that he had a general idea of the capabilities of the Sidereal Exalted when he conceived the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> (I once saw, but cannot now find, a suggestion of how existing Sidereal Charms could, working in concert, be used to approximate the Great Prophecy. I found it believable, with sufficient stuntworthiness. It implies that it wasn't a <i>single</i> prophecy, but rather a continued aggregation of smaller prophecies which led inevitably to the three choices.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:47:48-08:00","id":27728,"title":"","content":"Uh, Maddy, you seem to have been in touch with a different fan community than I have. <br /> <br /> The one I know is constantly complaining that Sidereals are hilariously incompetent, and that their history is a string of fuck-ups mainly caused by the fact that there are three entire universes completely outside their &quot;wise prophet&quot; powers who are all intent on claiming or destroying Creation, two of which have their own Solar-level Exalts. <br /> <br /> I've never seen &quot;Sidereals are described as far too competent&quot; as an actual problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:06:58-08:00","id":27739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27728#post27728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, Maddy, you seem to have been in touch with a different fan community than I have.<br /> <br /> The one I know is constantly complaining that Sidereals are hilariously incompetent, and that their history is a string of fuck-ups mainly caused by the fact that there are three entire universes completely outside their &quot;wise prophet&quot; powers who are all intent on claiming or destroying Creation, two of which have their own Solar-level Exalts.<br /> <br /> I've never seen &quot;Sidereals are described as far too competent&quot; as an actual problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics do not equal story impact, in this case. After all, my entire point here is, 'that's because the story was written before the mechanics'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:13:36-08:00","id":27744,"title":"","content":"I would argue that if the mechanics are derailing a story that's kind of pivotal to the way the setting...is, then the mechanics are probably what's wrong and are what need to be re-evaluated, not the story.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:16:53-08:00","id":27747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27728#post27728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, Maddy, you seem to have been in touch with a different fan community than I have.<br /> <br /> The one I know is constantly complaining that Sidereals are hilariously incompetent, and that their history is a string of fuck-ups mainly caused by the fact that there are three entire universes completely outside their &quot;wise prophet&quot; powers who are all intent on claiming or destroying Creation, two of which have their own Solar-level Exalts.<br /> <br /> I've never seen &quot;Sidereals are described as <b>far too competent</b>&quot; as an actual problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are still some people that think every Solar that set foot in Yu-shan gonna get ganked in 2 seconds so......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:19:07-08:00","id":27749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27739#post27739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanics do not equal story impact, in this case. After all, my entire point here is, 'that's because the story was written before the mechanics'</div> </div> </div> </div>The objections I heard were generally based in the story. You know, the one where the brilliant plan of the Bronze Faction gets screwed by the Great Contagion and the countless threats that might cause Creation to die in like twenty minutes, and the consistent failure of the Sidereals to anticipate, well, basically <i>anything </i>in the history of Creation.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not well-versed enough in Sidereal lore to say if that's an accurate representation of what's in the books, but it's a cry of outrage I have heard countless times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:29:10-08:00","id":27752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27744#post27744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that if the mechanics are derailing a story that's kind of pivotal to the way the setting...is, then the mechanics are probably what's wrong and are what need to be re-evaluated, not the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>No real reason exists for why they can't be in harmony. I, personally, favor mythologizing the Usurpation far more. The Sidereal Usurpation should be much less important, or even just one particular legend about what happened. Part of the danger of defining something so exhaustively in an earlier phase of development is when cool ideas arise later that contradict the original story. With 3e we get a chance to dust off some old questions and give a coat of spit and polish to the whole game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:59:28-08:00","id":27791,"title":"","content":"Is it the Great Prophecy you have a problem with, Maddy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:17:57-08:00","id":27798,"title":"","content":"Not really - though aspects of the execution do irk, in particular the 'year in seclusion' thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:43:07-08:00","id":27807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27717#post27717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible to come up with all sorts of vaguely-feasible-if-you-squint-hard-enough reasons the Usurpation can fly, but why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to come up with the exact mechanics of the Usurpation is like trying to figure out the exact mechanics of Icarus' flight.<br /> <br /> But, you know, many people can appreciate the story of one boy flying too high and falling into the ocean without worrying about the aerodynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T01:01:51-08:00","id":27822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27752#post27752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No real reason exists for why they can't be in harmony. I, personally, favor mythologizing the Usurpation far more. The Sidereal Usurpation should be much less important, or even just one particular legend about what happened. Part of the danger of defining something so exhaustively in an earlier phase of development is when cool ideas arise later that contradict the original story. With 3e we get a chance to dust off some old questions and give a coat of spit and polish to the whole game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be, uh, cutting the entire thesis statement out from under the Sidereals as a thing that exists in the setting. The Great Prophecy and their actions during the Usurpation are the foundations for literally everything about them today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T03:21:46-08:00","id":27863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27747#post27747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there are still some people that think every Solar that set foot in Yu-shan gonna get ganked in 2 seconds so......</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, many of the people who think that refuse to go to The Underworld and/or Malfeas for pretty much the same reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:33:53-08:00","id":27890,"title":"","content":"I, personally, happen to like the Usurpation story, since the basic form of it is mythic (possibly reminiscent of One Thousand and One Nights or Romance of the Three Kingdoms, but that's purely intuitive speculation and I really need to read that stuff), and, considering the amount of history I've read, am not perturbed by the amount of additional details you'd need to add to make it consistent.<br /> <br /> Also, we had a whole thread about the breakdown in society that was entailed by the years of warfare that ensued from Solars who either weren't at the feast or escaped the initial assault, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-11-2013, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:29:38-08:00","id":27938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27798#post27798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really - though aspects of the execution do irk, in particular the 'year in seclusion' thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A year? I could have bought.... well, I could've bought that, considering time skipping that happens in some Exalted games, actually.<br /> <br /> Alright, so it's just how Siddies could execute the whole thing, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:11:37-08:00","id":27984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27752#post27752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No real reason exists for why they can't be in harmony. I, personally, favor mythologizing the Usurpation far more. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a tad hard to do since it is the even that defined modern Sidereal politics, Lunar exile and started the Dragon-Blooded hegemony rule. It should at least get the level of tlak about that the rise of Caesar Augustus tends to get as far as I'm concerned. It's also hard to mythologize something when there's a couple dozen individuals who lived through it alive today and define a lot of what they're doing in &quot;Fuck those guys&quot; and &quot;The Usurpation enver stopped.&quot; These individuals are also the primary backers of most PCs in those splats.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why are there Gold and Bronze Factions at all?&quot; &quot;Stuff happened&quot; is not going ot really motivate anyone to join a Faction at all, which is a big chunk of the Sidereal design thesis. Again, First Principles are in play here, not &quot;Make Creation run like I think it would if I rebooted it and it does in my ehad.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27752#post27752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The Sidereal Usurpation should be much less important, or even just one particular legend about what happened. Part of the danger of defining something so exhaustively in an earlier phase of development is when cool ideas arise later that contradict the original story. With 3e we get a chance to dust off some old questions and give a coat of spit and polish to the whole game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that as stated already, this is of taste. Great Prophecies that due to responses of to them cause great upheavel are huge genre institutes that Exalted draws on. They show up in classical stuff like the Bible and Greek Tragedy, they show up in later stuff liek Romance of the Three Kingdoms and Shakespeare's Julius caesar. They still show up in modern fantasy like in Tanith Lee's Flat Earth and even Dune with Muad'Dib and Leto II. Giant prophecies which define policy and impact history in a huge curse is pretty big. Making it a footnote deflates its point of being in the legend, derails the impetus ofr the Usurpation, and also deflates the reasoning for the current setup beyond petty squabble.<br /> <br /> It might fit more real politk tries to describe Creation, but Creation is also a genre piece. And genre pieces include Great Prophecies, Usurpations and Calibration Feast Betrayals in teh same way it has stuff like the evil empire in the center of the world or armies of the dead.<br /> <br /> In the end, it still boils down to three complaints so far that I see. The ifrst is an <i>a priori</i> belief that splat-based conflict is bad, full stop. Which I have yet to see an argument why that's the case, simply dismissive statements that it is the case. Exalt sort isn't Clan from Vampire, it can matter more than just what your power set is. And in the case of Sidereal Exalted especially, comes with a job descritpion. <br /> <br /> The second is a simple want of making vague the Usurpation. But to be hoenst, it already is vague. We know who played in it, we know why it happened and we know its effects. We know why the Calibration Feast happened. The mechancis of it all? Who cares. WHatever resistance lost. Potential dissentors? They lost or died. Or are unique enough to be left-open for STs to use or not. The Usurpation can be as detailed or thought-out as it needs to be. It seems from my understanding is you thik it's too detailed. But in a weird since, I think it comes from you over-thinking what's going on. The result you want is a watered down Usurpation with little narrative momentum to it. When from the First Principles of the game, it's the watershed moment of the entire setting. It's Shin Huang Di unites China. It's Caesar crossing the Rhine. It's the Duke Ferdenand (sp?) getting shot moment that defiens everything from then out.<br /> <br /> Finally, you seem to think you know better than everyone else on this matter. Yet I have yet to see a substantive description from you on what such a world would be like besides vague &quot;It'd be more legendary.&quot; If the geopolitical landscape looks like neither previosu edition that's a bit odd there. And it seems that there is some revision of First Principles about. Mainly in making it so that Lunars were reasonably impacted by the Usurpation, rather than toss the oe of setting's three major historical events and deleting it. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:07:33-08:00","id":28022,"title":"","content":"My issue isn't, again, so much with the Great Prophesy... despite the fact that multiple posters attempt to straw-man that... and more that DURING the Great Prophesy, everything that has been written or stated about the High First Age and the various Exalted types / characters that populate it is thrown own in favor of a old school splat-based cWoD showdown.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal / Dragonblooded alliance itself is awful ; in specific, it's terrible because it suggests the Dragonblooded rebel 'as a race' because they have just 'had enough'. In pure cWoD fashion, Clan : Dragonblooded has decided that they can no longer tolerate the world as it stands. As a gestalt hive-mind, they flip a switch and suddenly throw in with the rebels.<br /> <br /> Not only is that massively simplistic, but let's talk about this honor guard thing a second. The 10,000 honor guard Dragonblooded at the Red Wedding Usurpation were -all- traitors?<br /> <br /> ... in order to buy this, we need to rely upon assumptions of competence / incompetence : <i><b>every single</b></i> Sidereal who tried to get a Dragonblooded agent near the throne succeeded. <i><b>Every single </b></i>Night Caste / Lunar who had a chance to detect or stop this failed or did not try. No safeguards were in place. None of the spymaster caste were spying. Despite the fact that these were the 'honor guard'... <i>hand-selected personal bodyguards of the Solar Exalted.</i><br /> <br /> Beyond that, we have the reaction of the Lunar Exalted. They stand aside and retreat to the Wyld. Ever since 1e this has made no sense ; it was justified in the original edition by literally suggesting the Sidereals had a mass astrology effect that just made them do that.<br /> <br /> Think about this for a second.<br /> <br /> The Mystic Xanatos Wizards pull off the Red Wedding Usurpation, but that's not all. <i>They literally have a magical spell in the first edition concept which is so powerful it FORCES all the Lunar Exalted into the Wyld, having them abandon lifelong mates and holdings.</i><br /> <br /> Cue the entire history of Lunar Exalted as cWoD Werewolf analogue, as hunted vagabond raiders who never have a home and are always outsider fuzzy angst BLUH I hate it.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but anybody who can't see how the 1e Usurpation is a huge cWoD-style story that relies heavily upon absurd assumptions of competence on behalf of the 'Gandalf' analogues isn't looking closely enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-11-2013, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:26:47-08:00","id":28042,"title":"","content":"So, it's the Calibration Feast you have a problem with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:42:36-08:00","id":28054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28042#post28042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's the Calibration Feast you have a problem with?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's the plausibility of the situation which has always been a major oversight. Unless you are going to limit solar clairvoyance or increase Sidereal subterfuge there's no way that the usurpation should have been possible. And making it possible in a game like this when it clearly isn't, isn't clever or good. It's just a cop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:43:10-08:00","id":28093,"title":"","content":"I thought all other threads were supposed to turn into Lunar threads. How did the Lunar thread turn into a Sidereal/Usurpation thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:56:52-08:00","id":28103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28093#post28093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought all other threads were supposed to turn into Lunar threads. How did the Lunar thread turn into a Sidereal/Usurpation thread?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One might say it was... usurped.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2008/09/04/article-1052367-0103B55A000004B0-847_468x461.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:12:03-08:00","id":28115,"title":"","content":"How is &quot;Rich people becoming complacent and self-involved to the point of believing that nothing can touch them&quot; not plausible? I mean, even Night Castes are fallible. They are human, they can get lazy, drunk, and fall to bangers and mash.<br /> <br /> Sure, they might have charms that can 100% always and forever figure shit out, but it doesn't mean they're always 100% on alert, poised and ready to strike. They're not Mages that always walk around with mage sight and 30 prepared uber-spells <i>just in case</i>. They're not walking paranoia combos (no offence to Paranoia Combo).<br /> <br /> They're humans, they have human brains, brains that reassure them that everything is fine, you can rest and close your eyes, even for a moment. That you are sure there aren't any enemies of the state left, because you did a good job. That reassure you that your people adore you and that you are doing a good job keeping the peace. That tell them that the world won't change over-night, the system is too big and running too well to fail.<br /> <br /> I don't see how it's implausible that <u>100 unified sidereals working specifically on an extermination plan</u> can outsmart 300 complacent, lazy, drugged and <u>divided</u> Solars. Should Sidereals never have any possibility of outsmarting Solars? Even then, if all you need to do is outsmart the Night Castes, you're cutting that number down to 100 vs 60.<br /> <br /> Hell, I get the impression that some of the Lunars that exiled themselves actually helped in covering it up, because they were convinced that letting the Solars perish is better than taking 3000 years of emotional and physical spousal abuse. (though this is only conjecture)<br /> <br /> Yes, it implies a level of Solar incompetence. But that's what happens when there's nothing left for you to do but sit on a throne and have wild parties with your best buds while your catgirl-slave is out fighting a war you've not actually seen in 100 years and that doesn't noticeably affect you other than a +/- 3% fluctuation in tributes from the outlying satrapies.<br /> <br /> It not implausible to me at all. It is in fact very real, and happened repeatedly throughout history.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like the Stadium-riot scene in season 1 of Legend of Korra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:18:35-08:00","id":28123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28022#post28022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal / Dragonblooded alliance itself is awful ; in specific, it's terrible because it suggests the Dragonblooded rebel 'as a race' because they have just 'had enough'. In pure cWoD fashion, Clan : Dragonblooded has decided that they can no longer tolerate the world as it stands. As a gestalt hive-mind, they flip a switch and suddenly throw in with the rebels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that's ridiculous. That's why what you're saying <i>didn't happen</i>. All that's needed is that a sufficient number of DBs went along with it or did nothing for long enough that it was too late by then. There totally would have been DBs loyal to the Solars who fought other DBs. We hardly need a detailed breakdown of how many of them at the Feast were loyal and protected Solars, how many were traitors, how many just followed their leader, how many had been manipulated somehow by Sidereals, etc.<br /> <br /> I just don't think the splat conflicts are as you say it is. There were Dragon-Blooded who would have preferred to keep the Solars. There were Sidereals who were against the plan. To return to the original subject, it's entirely possible that there were some Lunars who were actually fed up enough with their Golden Overlords that &quot;psst, hey, we're going to slaughter all the Solars at the Calibration Feast, you interested?&quot; sounded good to them. For some reasons already mentioned, i.e. Lunars were closer to Solar rule (that one actually surprised me a bit, but I'm curious to see what will be written about the First Age in Ex3), it's much riskier to try and suborn them compared to the Dragon-Blooded (if only because they'd be harder to assassinate if the discussion doesn't go as you wanted it to go :P), etc, trying to turn Lunars traitor against the Solars wouldn't have been a wide-spread tactic in the days leading to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> And hey, if a handful of them DID help at the Feast, they probably got betrayed by the Sidereals at some point so the Vision of Bronze could be realized. Or maybe they left by themselves when they realized they'd been manipulated into helping something worse than they'd thought. Or maybe there's a couple of Lunars who worked with the Sidereals even into the Shogunate and beyond! Maybe they're the past life of a PC or NPC. Maybe they're still alive right now! That's kind of a cool story idea. Good thing there won't be a sidebar in the Ex3 core that says &quot;you cannot do this thing ever, all Lunars reacted to the Usurpation in exactly the same fashion&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, nope, I don't see a problem with the splat-based conflict. I will grant that the Usurpation does need both some incompetence and some competence from certain parties, but between some mitigating factors (Solars were going mad, they were mostly watching for betrayal from their fellow Solars instead of the ever-loyal Sids, etc) and the whole &quot;it's a cool, epic betrayal that happened far enough into the past that the details don't matter all that much unless you decide to base your game around some of it&quot; thing, I'm pretty much okay with it.<br /> <br /> I will also note that I have zero knowledge of what they wrote about it in 1e. And dang, that astrology thing is pretty dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:11:27-08:00","id":28183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28115#post28115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I get the impression that some of the Lunars that exiled themselves actually helped in covering it up, because they were convinced that letting the Solars perish is better than taking 3000 years of emotional and physical spousal abuse. (though this is only conjecture)</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is a Lunar thread, I'm gonna also stick my hand in a whole other beehive here and say that I dislike that the Swan / Lililth dynamic has become the default template for Solar / Lunar relationships.<br /> <br /> It's run so deep that it's actually affected multiple mechanical / design decisions, almost all of which I think are pretty bad.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Lilith / Swan never existed. What would the tone of Lunars have been? What other stories would have been told in that vacuum?<br /> <br /> We should be up to like 10,000 posts in this thread by the end of next week I predict.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:17:58-08:00","id":28189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28183#post28183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since this is a Lunar thread, I'm gonna also stick my hand in a whole other beehive here and say that I dislike that the Swan / Lililth dynamic has become the default template for Solar / Lunar relationships.<br /> <br /> It's run so deep that it's actually affected multiple mechanical / design decisions, almost all of which I think are pretty bad.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Lilith / Swan never existed. What would the tone of Lunars have been? What other stories would have been told in that vacuum?<br /> <br /> We should be up to like 10,000 posts in this thread by the end of next week I predict.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this, I absolutely agree. Nevertheless we're stuck with it for 2e with charms that play off of it.<br /> I dare hope it'll change in 3e, at least to have a slightly more positive portrayal (I can get how it shouldn't necessarily be all good, but it should have at least a modicum of redeeming value).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:54:37-08:00","id":28223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28183#post28183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is a Lunar thread, I'm gonna also stick my hand in a whole other beehive here and say that I dislike that the Swan / Lililth dynamic has become the default template for Solar / Lunar relationships.<br /> <br /> It's run so deep that it's actually affected multiple mechanical / design decisions, almost all of which I think are pretty bad.<br /> <br /> Imagine if Lilith / Swan never existed. What would the tone of Lunars have been? What other stories would have been told in that vacuum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right. Not going to disagree, here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:06:42-08:00","id":28235,"title":"","content":"I can't say there is anything in particular I like about Solar/Lunar Bond at all, not just Swan/Lillith. My experiences with it have been entirely negative. Hopefully EX3 changes it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:34:33-08:00","id":28254,"title":"","content":"I <i>think</i> I remember a statement about it sticking around, but i might just be hallucinating. I'd be happier if it went away (mechanically at the very least) else I'll just be handwaving it away. It <i>can</i> create unique situations where 2 lovers/partners/best friends are a Solar and a Lunar and use that unique facet of their exaltation to fight as one and have charms that depend or affect the other, but I don't believe that something like the Bond is <i>required</i> for it. It could as easily be a facet of Lunar Stewardship or an Intimacy-related charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-11-2013, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:44:11-08:00","id":28263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28022#post28022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only is that massively simplistic, but let's talk about this honor guard thing a second. The 10,000 honor guard Dragonblooded at the Red Wedding Usurpation were -all- traitors?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been addressed, even though you've ignored it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond that, we have the reaction of the Lunar Exalted. They stand aside and retreat to the Wyld. Ever since 1e this has made no sense ; it was justified in the original edition by literally suggesting the Sidereals had a mass astrology effect that just made them do that. </div> </div> </div>Pageref?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:06:44-08:00","id":28291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28115#post28115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're not walking paranoia combos (no offence to Paranoia Combo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Little known fact: Paranoia Combo actually hops wherever she goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28183#post28183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is a Lunar thread, I'm gonna also stick my hand in a whole other beehive here and say that I dislike that the Swan / Lililth dynamic has become the default template for Solar / Lunar relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not aware of anyone who liked that particular combo or its influence on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:45:14-08:00","id":28379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28254#post28254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think</i> I remember a statement about it sticking around, but i might just be hallucinating. I'd be happier if it went away (mechanically at the very least) else I'll just be handwaving it away. It <i>can</i> create unique situations where 2 lovers/partners/best friends are a Solar and a Lunar and use that unique facet of their exaltation to fight as one and have charms that depend or affect the other, but I don't believe that something like the Bond is <i>required</i> for it. It could as easily be a facet of Lunar Stewardship or an Intimacy-related charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Solar/Lunar Bond will still be a thing in EX3, but it mercifully doesn't sound much like 2e's treatment. To the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">gist of what we know to date!</a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: Will Lunar Bond/Lunar-Solar dynamics be revised in any way? <b>(babyseal)</b></i><br /> A: Yes. <b>(Holden)</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [The Solar/Lunar Bond is] a whole big complicated thing with huge bearing on what the Lunars are doing, rather than a very simple brain lasso. <b>(Holden)</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: New lore question:</i> <i>Every Solar has a Lunar mate. Will any of the new Exalted be tied together similar to the Solar-Lunar pairings? <b>(Starglyte)</b></i><br /> A: <u>I would not assume the first statement to be true</u>. The answer to your question, though, is &quot;could be.&quot; <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine on that last one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But yeah, the Lilith/Swan model is potentially okay as one possibility for how it might turn out. Not something I enjoy, but hey, I don't object to it at all if it's a huge outlier. That it is the default is just... Ugh. People who actually like it as the assumed default are vanishingly few, and thank gog for that.<br /> <br /> In other Bond-related notes, it would have been nice to see more variety in representative manifestations. When reading about it in the Core and Lunars Manual, I had no positive feelings for the idea when it emphasized &quot;love at first sight,&quot; up until I read that &quot;incredibly awesome friendship&quot; was an option. That immediately made it not merely okay, but <i>awesome</i>. I had been interested in Lunars before I got the Core and that just made them cooler to me. Cue disappointment that this was never really explored. &quot;Romantic/sexual attraction&quot; is the assumption from most people, while mentioning other possibilities seems to actually make them pause for a moment before maybe saying, &quot;Oh, right, I guess that's an option.&quot;<br /> <br /> For occasions the Bond came up in a story in the books, consider a circle for &quot;The Bond is important to this story&quot; and a circle for &quot;The Bond's context is not of a romantic/sexual nature.&quot; I'm not sure there's any overlap in that Venn diagram. Nor much at all in the second circle, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:06:12-08:00","id":28397,"title":"","content":"I tend to make it possible by boosting Sidereal subterfuge. Thinking on it, the Usurpation would not be successful without he Jade Prison. The Jade Prison wasn't built the night of the Calibration Feast either. Things had been in motion for a long time, and hidden from the Solars. I tend to lend back to that old piece of fluff that there are 200 unused Sidereal Exaltations sealed in Yu-Shan somewhere, the Jade Prison's design comes from that very same prison, which in turn is part of the design of the Monstrances of Celestial Portion.<br /> <br /> The reason Sidereal power has waned was when they broke the Mask they lost their power to manipulate it, capable of making it more than it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 12-11-2013, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:55:39-08:00","id":28480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28397#post28397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to make it possible by boosting Sidereal subterfuge. Thinking on it, the Usurpation would not be successful without he Jade Prison. The Jade Prison wasn't built the night of the Calibration Feast either. Things had been in motion for a long time, and hidden from the Solars. <b>I tend to lend back to that old piece of fluff that there are 200 unused Sidereal Exaltations sealed in Yu-Shan somewhere, the Jade Prison's design comes from that very same prison, which in turn is part of the design of the Monstrances of Celestial Portion.</b><br /> <br /> The reason Sidereal power has waned was when they broke the Mask they lost their power to manipulate it, capable of making it more than it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an old piece of fluff. It's a relatively recent throwaway idea from a book full of throwaway ideas that don't make sense (otherwise known as MoEP: Sidereals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T20:07:08-08:00","id":28490,"title":"","content":"More specifically, it's a &quot;hey, what if&quot; thing from the Storytelling chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T20:34:03-08:00","id":28498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28115#post28115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it's implausible that <u>100 unified sidereals working specifically on an extermination plan</u> can outsmart 300 complacent, lazy, drugged and <u>divided</u> Solars</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part where I note that not all Solars were complacent (Gold Shadowed Arrow for instance) and that quite a few less than all five score of the fellowship were okay with the Usurpation, the dissenters being the first to die, long before the Solars, Lunars or their created races.<br /> <br /> Nitpicking I know, but it's something I don't like being forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T23:08:45-08:00","id":28559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28480#post28480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not an old piece of fluff. It's a relatively recent throwaway idea from a book full of throwaway ideas that don't make sense (otherwise known as MoEP: Sidereals).</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have clairified. I consider it old due to the time the actual book was released, and the new edition looming just ahead of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T02:27:07-08:00","id":28600,"title":"","content":"The cynical side of me thinks that even without Lilith and Swan, heavily unequal power dynamics plus an unbreakable close relationship is going to lead many people to go to abuse or domination pretty quick, unless they're explicitly led otherwise.<br /> <br /> Imagine you had some weird situation where the GSPs weren't corruptions of the Solar Exaltation, but clones of them, and as such, each Solar and GSP had a weird &quot;bond&quot;. That wouldn't go to domination and abuse of power very quickly, because there's not a notion that either GSPs or Solars get overshadowed by one another or are helpless in the face of one another.<br /> <br /> Yes, if we have the Bond it should be be &quot;Just about every close relationship that we could imagine being romantic as well if the physical criteria were right&quot;, than all focused on some abusive thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T04:02:13-08:00","id":28616,"title":"","content":"If Lunars are massively overshadowed by Solars in that way, then their implementation is a failure regardless of what form the Solar Bond takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T06:26:23-08:00","id":28677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=28379#post28379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar/Lunar Bond will still be a thing in EX3, but it mercifully doesn't sound much like 2e's treatment. To the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">gist of what we know to date!</a><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: Will Lunar Bond/Lunar-Solar dynamics be revised in any way? (babyseal)<br /> A: Yes. (Holden)<br /> [The Solar/Lunar Bond is] a whole big complicated thing with huge bearing on what the Lunars are doing, rather than a very simple brain lasso.(Holden) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: New lore question: Every Solar has a Lunar mate. Will any of the new Exalted be tied together similar to the Solar-Lunar pairings? (Starglyte)<br /> A: I would not assume the first statement to be true. The answer to your question, though, is &quot;could be.&quot; (John M\u00f8rke) </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine on that last one.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSounds like a much more interesting and manageable version of it will be making it to 3e - like it might be a ritual type thing (blood oaths, weddings or what not) that could actually be chosen as being a thing by the individual player instead of being forced upon them! Ok, I'm in.<br /> <br /> Now I feel bad for ever having doubted the devs. I must repent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:28:41-08:00","id":29983,"title":"","content":"Alright, this thread ran out of topics. Let's talk about this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor\">[Idea] Lunars Let In Balor</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/27741-idea-lunars-let-in-balor#post27741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Contagion is happening, every asshole is dying and everyone is scrambling for a solution. So, right here around the edge of Creation, at the border of Pure Chaos where most of the Lunars park their summer homes, one Moon Elder looks into the infinite possibility of the Wyld and has himself a vision, as Lunars are want to do in their old age.<br /> <br /> So, it basically spells out the Sidereal dilemma to him: 1. Do Nothing, aka Not An Option. 2. Try to fight the Contagion on yer own, aka Yeah Good Luck With That. 3. Let in the Fair Folk, aka When Did We Exchange Reason For Madness!? Yeah, Option 3 essentially establishes that the infinite possibilities of the Wyld Folk will cancel out with the necrotic stagnation of the Great Contagion and only dissolve a whole heaping big chunk of Creation, but it will be an ALIVE Creation, especially if you play your cards right. Option 2, well y'all have tried option two already, you've been trying it for a while. It hasn't been working. Then again, Option 2 is at least not 'Well, let's let in something JUST AS BAD'.<br /> <br /> So the Lunar aren't the Sidereal, they don't gather up in one place and then duke it out to see who's gonna do what. They are ringed all over Creation. So, instead, this vision just leaks out through the Silver Pact and ever individual Lunar gets to decide what to do. Thing is, most of 'em could go with Option 2. All it takes is a couple of 'em to go look at Option 3, 'Eh, better than nothing.' And suddenly you're up to your eyeballs in Raksha.<br /> <br /> So it gives Lunars something to do as a splat, something they did, something that utterly, literally, shaped Creation. Well, not quite as a splat, but individuals of the splat, emphasizing that the Lunars operate as roving packs of individuals bonded by circumstance and a desire to protect Creation. Or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:53:26-08:00","id":29992,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Caul will go a long way to scratch the itch of something of major relevance done by the Lunars so that they don't need to do something tremendously self-defeating like be responsible for the Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like making the Balorian Crusade a thing of the Lunars from the outset diminishes the raksha within the setting, and I thing that putting it in as a startling revelation in the Lunars' own book is not a good way for Exalted to be written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T11:35:58-08:00","id":30013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=29992#post29992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Caul will go a long way to scratch the itch of something of major relevance done by the Lunars so that they don't need to do something tremendously self-defeating like be responsible for the Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like making the Balorian Crusade a thing of the Lunars from the outset diminishes the raksha within the setting, and I thing that putting it in as a startling revelation in the Lunars' own book is not a good way for Exalted to be written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on this a bit:<br /> <br /> By making the event contingent on the Lunars allowing it, it diminishes the raksha in that it takes their independent narrative and co-ops it for aother PC splat. It diminishes one by simply stealing to prop-up another. A lot of the kind of cool of raksha, especially post Chapter 7, is I think Balor's independent though in it, the once-in-history weigh tit has. Tying it to some psychotic plot by some Lunars seems to be missing a bit of the point.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't really help Lunars at all, since it is simply taking an existing indepenent thing and stealing it for their use, instead of trying to make the Lunars cooler independently. It has all the issues of the Thousand Stream River. It also unequivacally puts the current problems of Creation on the Lunars, rather than the somewhat independent raksha influence. So it also steals the fire from the Fair Folk while at the same time also makes Lunars huge assholes.<br /> <br /> In short....kind of a terrible idea I think in the grnad scheme of things.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 12-14-2013, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:11:15-08:00","id":30118,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it the DL's that let in the Raksha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:30:26-08:00","id":30124,"title":"","content":"Equally bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:38:57-08:00","id":30128,"title":"","content":"But, just to clarify, wasn't that how it was presented?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:52:13-08:00","id":30133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=29992#post29992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Caul will go a long way to scratch the itch of something of major relevance done by the Lunars so that they don't need to do something tremendously self-defeating like be responsible for the Balorian Crusade.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like making the Balorian Crusade a thing of the Lunars from the outset diminishes the raksha within the setting, and I thing that putting it in as a startling revelation in the Lunars' own book is not a good way for Exalted to be written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much agree here. I find a lot to like about the Caul, but then again, we're going off of hints and spoilers at this point so it's hard to really put it under a microscope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T15:54:54-08:00","id":30134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30128#post30128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, just to clarify, wasn't that how it was presented?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Fair Folk book (and possibly the Abyssals book, I haven't seen that one yet), yes.<br /> <br /> Prior to that, it was presented as &quot;lots of people dying left the borders of the world undefended, and also messed up the principles that maintained Wyld-shaped lands&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T16:21:58-08:00","id":30136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30134#post30134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Fair Folk book (and possibly the Abyssals book, I haven't seen that one yet), yes.<br /> <br /> Prior to that, it was presented as &quot;lots of people dying left the borders of the world undefended, and also messed up the principles that maintained Wyld-shaped lands&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can confirm that the Abyssals book* indeed had the Lion and Eye &amp; Seven Despairs explicitly allowing the Fair Folk in.<br /> <br /> * 2e's, at least; no clue if 1e did likewise. Ditto 1e's Fair Folk, though I suspect it looked a lot like 2e's.<br /> <br /> I'm also very interested to know what the original story really was on the raksha side of things. Given <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:secret-history-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">Holden's revelations here</a>, the whole product would have been very different indeed had Grabowski's original outline been followed more faithfully. For years now, I've been quite intrigued by the words, &quot;Balor was implemented as a completely different character than he was supposed to be.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T16:27:32-08:00","id":30138,"title":"","content":"It is impressive the extent the books have gone to make Balor not the hero of his own Crusade, between the Thief of Words and the deathlords letting them in thing.<br /> Poor Balor can't catch a break. Everything wants to turn him into someone else's tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T16:30:41-08:00","id":30142,"title":"","content":"I imagine you get a lot of the gist of it from the depiction of Balor in the Ink Monkeys article, where he's all terrible and regal and engages in a grand mythic feat to solidify his status prior to beginning his war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:18:16-08:00","id":30159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30134#post30134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Fair Folk book (and possibly the Abyssals book, I haven't seen that one yet), yes.<br /> <br /> Prior to that, it was presented as &quot;lots of <b>people</b> dying left the borders of the world undefended, and also messed up the principles that maintained Wyld-shaped lands&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The human casualties themselves wouldn't have done much. They were just one part of the 90% of all life that died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T17:46:43-08:00","id":30169,"title":"","content":"Rodents and sparrows can't man the guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T18:09:37-08:00","id":30176,"title":"","content":"And... we're worried about protecting the protagonist status of the Fair Folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T18:12:34-08:00","id":30181,"title":"","content":"A very important Lunar theme: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vPA0BmlNd20\" data-code=\"vPA0BmlNd20\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vPA0BmlNd20/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T20:50:48-08:00","id":30256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30169#post30169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rodents and sparrows can't man the guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how you defend the borders from the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T22:08:31-08:00","id":30271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30176#post30176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... we're worried about protecting the protagonist status of the Fair Folk?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>An</i>tagonist status, actually. It's hard to take them as a credible threat if all they've done is what the Exalted want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T22:18:10-08:00","id":30274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30176#post30176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... we're worried about protecting the protagonist status of the Fair Folk?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am. If you're going to make them a PC splat, then treat them like one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T23:36:50-08:00","id":30306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30176#post30176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... we're worried about protecting the protagonist status of the Fair Folk?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're worried about stealing heat from the oldest enemies of Creation and leaving them at the same degree of noncredible threat-level as common perception of them has trended towards in previous editions to puff up the achievements of the Exalt type whose achievements have been found lacking in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Robbing Peter to pay Paul is not the soundest of narrative legerdemain even without being so up-front about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T03:19:25-08:00","id":30354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30256#post30256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how you defend the borders from the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several layers of defense against the Wyld. Stability and complexity of civilization is one of them, and an important one, but there also need to be weapon systems for their less abstract and more martial threats. That's likely why the raksha had to resort to breakthroughs more often than straightforward invasion (although breakthroughs are likely strategically useful no matter what you're facing).<br /> <br /> Look no further than the actual Realm Defense Grid.<br /> <br /> Also, remember when Holden talked about losing airships in battle against the fae? Or not having enough battle golems to defend a full border region against the fae? Or needing to deploy a soulbreaker orb when they take control of some <i>other</i> border defense weapon and start turning it around to fire at the South?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T04:14:42-08:00","id":30371,"title":"","content":"I would also note that &quot;the Lunars did the exact same thing as the Sidereals, except with the Balorian Crusade instead of the Usurpation&quot; doesn't sound particularly good to me. You can only lessen Creation to save it so much before it starts to lose it's dramatic import.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:08:19-08:00","id":30457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30354#post30354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are several layers of defense against the Wyld. Stability and complexity of civilization is one of them, and an important one, but there also need to be weapon systems for their less abstract and more martial threats. That's likely why the raksha had to resort to breakthroughs more often than straightforward invasion (although breakthroughs are likely strategically useful no matter what you're facing).<br /> <br /> Look no further than the actual Realm Defense Grid.<br /> <br /> Also, remember when Holden talked about losing airships in battle against the fae? Or not having enough battle golems to defend a full border region against the fae? Or needing to deploy a soulbreaker orb when they take control of some <i>other</i> border defense weapon and start turning it around to fire at the South?</div> </div> </div> </div>And many moons before Holden, there was an offering of alternatives <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\"> from GCG.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:47:15-08:00","id":30484,"title":"","content":"Okaaaaaaaay.<br /> <br /> The point &quot;they needed people to actually man weapons against the Fair Folk&quot;...<br /> <br /> And the point &quot;people (and possibly life in general) create a stability that reinforces the rim against the Wyld&quot;...<br /> <br /> Are <u>separate</u>, but related points.<br /> <br /> If the Great Contagion had only targeted humans, sure, there wouldn't have been large sections of the world that would have catastrophically disintegrated.<br /> <br /> But the lack of soldiers and people with their fingers on the button still means that raksha start pouring in.<br /> <br /> The Realm Defense Grid has, from the very start of the game, been the primary thing keeping the raksha out (and there was the idea to show up later that there weren't as many of them left as everybody thought anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:53:19-08:00","id":30506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30484#post30484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okaaaaaaaay.<br /> <br /> The point &quot;they needed people to actually man weapons against the Fair Folk&quot;...<br /> <br /> And the point &quot;people (and possibly life in general) create a stability that reinforces the rim against the Wyld&quot;...<br /> <br /> Are <u>separate</u>, but related points.<br /> <br /> If the Great Contagion had only targeted humans, sure, there wouldn't have been large sections of the world that would have catastrophically disintegrated.<br /> <br /> But the lack of soldiers and people with their fingers on the button still means that raksha start pouring in.<br /> <br /> The Realm Defense Grid has, <b>from the very start of the game</b>, been the primary thing keeping the raksha out (and there was the idea to show up later that there weren't as many of them left as everybody thought anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the roving autonomous defense systems were envisioned as doing that earlier on. This detail is contained in the quote that I linked.<br /> <br /> For whatever reason, the Wyld doesn't slosh out on its own. Perhaps all the living, defined things in Creation are threatening in what they represent. Perhaps migratory birds can strongly discourage Wyld monsters used to constant change from encroaching, because the Fair Folk or other things catch a whiff of the non-narrative necessity that has molded the world and feel so uneasy that they flee. The howls of wolves might bear the risk, however minuscule, of gaining Luna's attention, a risk that the monster feels pressing down on them like the Curse from W:TA, only angled at alien creatures under the silver light of the moon instead of humans, hunted for millennia, trying to escape the Changers in their midst.<br /> <br /> Alternatives exist. They might be as costly as the various wonders of old that the Scarlet Empress used, but it was by no means the only thing that had that utility. It's not as if the Unconquered Sun, or even the multiplicity of Luna, could be in all places all the time in Creation during the Age of Glory. Else, there could have been no tales of Ahlat leading his force of walruses against Fair Folk and winning. Perhaps there's going to be something like the upshot of heroic mortals in EX3, only for beasts. Certainly, if the Exalted are going to be made to stop and think seriously about having to take on a tyrannosaur, the raksha won't be in a better position when they happen across the territory of a large, angry predator that can kill them for good because said tyrannosaur is Creation-born and thus has that weight behind the force of biting and stomping.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T16:55:27-08:00","id":30644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30506#post30506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever reason, the Wyld doesn't slosh out on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't? I thought it did. Or rather creep/soak into Creation on its own. It's the ocean and Creation is the cliff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T20:50:18-08:00","id":30742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=30644#post30644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't? I thought it did. Or rather creep/soak into Creation on its own. It's the ocean and Creation is the cliff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without massive die-offs. Something has to form within it and then move in. This sentence doesn't match up to the rest of the paragraph so well, anyway. Probably better to say that you can scare the Wyld sufficiently that whatever's sloshing around inside it might be hesitant to come on out... unless Luna baits it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T21:39:12-08:00","id":30766,"title":"","content":"Don't wyld storms blow into Creation in the North regularly? And the Wyld literally washes in and out in the far Western ocean.<br /> <br /> Originally Creation had <i>The River of All Torments</i> to separate it completely from the Wyld. After it was imprisoned, the Solars built the Jade Obelisks and used the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern to ensure Creation's integrity. Following the Balorian Crusade and centuries of neglect and accidents, there's not a lot to keep the chaos at bey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T04:36:31-08:00","id":30896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=27689#post27689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think Gaius Julius went to every soldier in his army and personally talked him into overthrowing the government before crossing the Rubicon, or do you think he just said &quot;Forward!&quot; and his men obeyed, as they'd been trained their whole lives to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading a bit more on the administrative machinery* and history of Rome, I'd think another, and possibly more pertinent, example would be any case in which &quot;the army&quot; contested an emperor's choice of successor.<br /> <br /> Also references to the Senate as a collective, since even when there were divisions within the Senate its actual decrees and appointments were issued from the position of being the will of the entire body (since it's not as if they had anything remotely resembling political parties back then).<br /> <br /> It's probably worth also noting that the Dragon Blooded have the capacity to combine all the cult of personality inherent to a military organisation with all the cult of personality inherent to a family unit; the person calling the shots isn't just your general, she's your great-grandmother, with all the conditioning to obey that that implies.<br /> <br /> * Which, incidentally, is a lot more complex than I had ever known of; I'd always thought that the Senate was the straightforward elected legislature, when... nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T10:04:25-08:00","id":31043,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'll be honest, I'm just not able to grasp being able to care about the Raksha but I've never been a big fan of them anywho, so I'm biased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T10:06:49-08:00","id":31046,"title":"","content":"Nobody expects the Roman Senate... of being complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No boom<i> today</i>. Boom<i> tomorrow</i>. There's always a boom tomorrow. What? Look, somebodys got to have some damn perspective around here. Boom. Sooner or later. Boom!&quot; - Susan Ivanova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/888-thatblueguy","name":"ThatBlueGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar888_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T10:27:20-08:00","id":31054,"title":"","content":"I expect everything with [Ancient] Roman in front of it of being complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T04:56:38-08:00","id":31590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatBlueGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=31046#post31046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody expects the Roman Senate... of being complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Senate itself is fairly uncomplicated (in that it's an appointed board of the most politically experienced individuals in Rome, who collectively determine domestic and foreign policy and control public finance), it's more in the fact that Rome had three or four different democratic legislative bodies who elected the various magistrates, some of whom appointed the members of the Senate, but were all subordinate to it, except for the Plebeian Tribune, who was elected by the lowest ranking legislature but had the power to veto decisions by all other bodies, including the Senate (which it could also force a convening of).<br /> <br /> The Roman Republic seems to have been distinguished from kingdom and empire by the fact that it didn't have a head of state, instead having sovereign power invested in a collection of committees with a kind of multi-layered hierarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T09:35:09-08:00","id":31724,"title":"","content":"It also stood out compared to a democratic body like what the Greeks had in that instead of one big collection of voting citizens on everything (because the rest of the state weren't real people), there's the represenative aspect. You don't have a king who represents you, or a democratic body you had no say in whether or not you get a vote for that does things; you just vote for a guy who does the politicking for you.<br /> <br /> That said, the Deliberative I get a feeling is supposed to have a Senate feel. Or at least a UN one.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T09:56:13-08:00","id":31738,"title":"","content":"As opposed to the Dragon-Bloodeds' elaborate, structured society, and the Solars' complete lack of society, I would like to see the Lunars have a loose, Creation-spanning network. Perhaps a get together for the entire direction every year or so with some Lunars dedicated to keeping people in touch with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T09:59:19-08:00","id":31743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=31724#post31724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, the Deliberative I get a feeling is supposed to have a Senate feel. Or at least a UN one.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current model for the Solar Deliberative is something like a combination between the U.N., the European Union, the Roman government, and the Magisterium from His Dark Materials; a collection of colleges, councils, courts and committees, all functioning as international and intergovernmental organisations, under the overall administration of a council of those most politically minded Solars (technically all Solars are considered members of the Deliberative, and it derives the notion of authority over all the Realm from that conceit, but it's unusual for more than half of them to partake in it consistently, and only about a third of them have big agendas with it). Insofar as &quot;the Realm&quot; is essentially the concept of the dominion of humanity over Creation, the Deliberative endeavors to coordinate and centralise all of human civilization (in its various diverse states, nations, methods of government, and organisations) under the ultimate authority of the Solar Exalted as placed atop Meru.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T06:04:40-08:00","id":39341,"title":"","content":"Was just looking over the Alchemicals, the other ones with Attribute-based Charms, and what struck is how varied the associated Attributes were for the Castes. I <i>think</i> the devs mentioned that all of the Lunars will have some physicality to them. I was thinking that &quot;scrambling&quot; the Caste Attributes so that it's not Full Moon=Physical, Changing Moon=Social and No Moon=Mental, but a bit more varied. Here is the version I came up with<br /> <b>Full Moons</b> as the &quot;pro-active&quot; survivors, those who take the fight to the threats against their enemies and those who hunt the threats to Luna's Children.<br /> -Caste Abilities: Strength, Charisma and Perception<br /> <b>Changing Moons</b> are those who react but are never caught off guard, those who slip away to haunt their foes another day, those who attack unexpectedly.<br /> -Caste Abilities: Dexterity, Wits, Appearance<br /> <b>No Moons</b> the sages, shamans and hoarders of knowledge, those who wait and study and survive until they find and learn the weaknesses of their enemies, be they mortal, spirit or chosen.<br /> -Caste Abilities: Intelligence, Stamina and Manipulation<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not really happy with this spread so far, but I'd like to think it's a start. Thoughts/idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T08:44:28-08:00","id":39408,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much okay with the current separation, but in the interest of discussion...<br /> <br /> Perception goes with No-Moon. I will tolerate no discussion there. They're the shamans who get to see spirits or know everything about you after sniffing you a little. In my mind, it's frankly even more important to them than Intelligence. And, really? You didn't even leave Manipulation to those poor Changing Moons? They're supposed to be the ones using their guile to deal with problems, their anima power is a disguise, and you took Manipulation away from them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T08:56:19-08:00","id":39413,"title":"","content":"Perception for Full Moons because that seemed to fit the theme of hunters the best, and I didn't think either Wits or Intelligence would fit them. I was torn between Manipulation and Appearance for Changing Moons because both fit them, and Appearance fits more in line with them using shapechanging for infiltration.<br /> <br /> Another spread for ideas I had was:<br /> <br /> Full Moon: Strength, Stamina, Perception<br /> Changing Moon: Dexterity, Manipulation Appearance<br /> No Moons: Charisma, Intelligence, Wits<br /> <br /> But that's far from good either way. Maybe Charisma for Full Moons next to Strength and Stamina, Perception and Intelligence to No Moons. But that leaves the following conundrum: I can see Changing Moons having access to Wits, Manipulation, Appearance and Dexterity as well, while I can't really see Charisma or Appearance for the No Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T09:20:35-08:00","id":39425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=39341#post39341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was just looking over the Alchemicals, the other ones with Attribute-based Charms, and what struck is how varied the associated Attributes were for the Castes. I <i>think</i> the devs mentioned that all of the Lunars will have some physicality to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be interpreting a game term beyond the bounds it was intended to apply to. After all, everything about a person is physical. Even their thoughts are physical, occurring as they do from a chemical interaction, with memories stored in a particular arrangement of cells. Damage the cells, damage the memory. What we're probably looking at for a synonym here is visibility or outward notability. You might not be able to see what makes someone persuasive or affable, but it can register to you by vocal distinctions. Understanding and thought are even pricklier to try and make noticeable, but I don't think that the obstacle is even close to insurmountable there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T09:53:46-08:00","id":39459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=31743#post31743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My current model for the Solar Deliberative is something like a combination between the U.N., the European Union, the Roman government, and the Magisterium from His Dark Materials; a collection of colleges, councils, courts and committees, all functioning as international and intergovernmental organisations, under the overall administration of a council of those most politically minded Solars (technically all Solars are considered members of the Deliberative, and it derives the notion of authority over all the Realm from that conceit, but it's unusual for more than half of them to partake in it consistently, and only about a third of them have big agendas with it). Insofar as &quot;the Realm&quot; is essentially the concept of the dominion of humanity over Creation, the Deliberative endeavors to coordinate and centralise all of human civilization (in its various diverse states, nations, methods of government, and organisations) under the ultimate authority of the Solar Exalted as placed atop Meru.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a useful model that I arrived at after thinking about Exalted and how they would 'feel' for a long time, maybe you will like it.<br /> <br /> Exaltation cannot be thought of exactly as a national identity or an occupation ; it implies a sort of judgement of character, an innate litmus test that the candidate has endured. Likewise, Exaltation happens, most often, to individuals who can be regarded by society as 'unique'... those who challenge the everyday, who are defined by unusual beliefs and unusual talents that make them stand out from everybody else.<br /> <br /> So what does this produce? I put forward - These are people who feel very, very entitled. That's not really that difficult to understand, is it? Shit, if I was one of the 300 Solar Exalted, I'd feel pretty entitled too. You were -chosen-. That alone produces a big ego, a big personality that feels they are entitled to weigh in on whatever issue they wish.<br /> <br /> Now, we get to the arguably even more relevant issue - the Exalted are not career politicians. No, in fact, they are nearly impossible to quantify by any specific means - are they soldiers? are they scientists? are they mystics? They are all of these things and none. Each Exalted has a story. Most of these stories are pretty epic and complicated, involving unique challenges they met and overcame that defined them in fundamental ways. These guys aren't Bob Dole and Bill Clinton. They're Indy, Batman, and Luke. So we're talking /even more/ ego, /even more/ personality.<br /> <br /> So, how does this alter the character of Deliberative as a government body?<br /> <br /> I picture Deliberative as being -really- over the top and extreme. Absolute political theater. Madness. Some Deliberative sessions must have been so intense that people literally were like 'wtf is going on' -- when you get these insanely unique people, tell them they are chosen by god and entitled to be the way they are, give them immense power with virtually no checks and balances? You get some blowhards. You get some really, really extreme folks that constantly push reasonable discussion into chaos. You get people that just don't want to play at all, like K'tula over there.<br /> <br /> On good days, the Deliberative saves the world. On bad days, Creation suffers as the godlings quarrel. Very, very rarely, duels are fought and people die, but mostly the only costs are mortal lives waged on gambits of pride and principle.<br /> <br /> But on most days? The chamber roars, the endless drama spins on, and the Exalted accomplish far, far less than they should.<br /> <br /> Who would have thought that these living superweapons, chosen by this specific criteria, might not be particularly adept at cooperative governance?<br /> <br /> One thing I can say though? Is that with these kinda people at the helm, I doubt it looks very much like any other government chamber. Real politicians would run from that room screaming.<br /> <br /> In the REAL WORLD, they make sure that Barabbus the Devourer of Slaves is never let into the upper echelons of power. That guy was a crazy ass canibbal warlord thing that was famous for killing a tyrant lizard by biting it to death! He is totally unqualified to vote on taxes! In a million little ways, Barabbus is excluded from the White House, which honestly in the opinion of lotsa folks (perhaps even Barabbus himself) might be better for everybody!<br /> <br /> ... in Deliberative, Barabbus gets a chance to stand up and bellow out his feelings on any matter he chooses, even those which he is only tangentially informed about. In fact, he might feel he is -obligated- to offer his opinion. After all, he was chosen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 12-30-2013, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:46:21-08:00","id":39481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snipped alternate Attribute breakdowns*</div> </div> </div> </div>Saur Ops gives some good reasoning for why one shouldn't presume every Caste will have a physical Attribute. It's also worth noting that the thematic archetypes the Lunar Castes are meant to cover are Warrior, Trickster, and Shaman. If assigning new Attribute breakdowns, there's merit to bearing these in mind.<br /> <br /> In addition, there may not be just three Attributes per Caste (one way or another). While I'm having trouble finding where, they described a change to Solar Caste Abilities: each Solar Caste has 7 or so Caste Abilities, from which each member of that Caste selects 5. There's no telling if other splats will work this way (Sidereals and Alchemicals having set Caste Abilities/Attributes could work thematically), but if Lunars do, we may be looking at 4-5 Attributes per Caste, from which a Lunar selects 3 or however many, plus the Favored(s?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:13:57-08:00","id":39489,"title":"","content":"This post is kind of long, rambling, and probably not of much interest to anybody besides myself, so I'm just going to tuck it all in here for anybody who wants to see it, and keep it from troubling anybody else.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=39459#post39459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the REAL WORLD, they make sure that Barabbus the Devourer of Slaves is never let into the upper echelons of power. That guy was a crazy ass canibbal warlord thing that was famous for killing a tyrant lizard by biting it to death! He is totally unqualified to vote on taxes! In a million little ways, Barabbus is excluded from the White House, which honestly in the opinion of lotsa folks (perhaps even Barabbus himself) might be better for everybody!<br /> <br /> ... in Deliberative, Barabbus gets a chance to stand up and bellow out his feelings on any matter he chooses, even those which he is only tangentially informed about. In fact, he might feel he is -obligated- to offer his opinion. After all, he was chosen!</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is the kind of model which is why I think the idea of a Deliberative in which all the Solars take part lacks credibility.<br /> <br /> Excepting my idea for what was becoming of it in the final centuries of the First Age, where the centralisation efforts of the Hierophant had largely borne fruit and the Solars were at the height of their madness and excess.<br /> <br /> On that note, I do like your imagery as the way that final phase of the Deliberative might work.<br /> <br /> But still, with my sense of a lack of credibility, my ideas for earlier (and somewhat more functional) forms of the Deliberative kind of amount to a kind of forum where Exalts of different fields and interests come together, discuss ideas as to how Creation should be with the expertise of each informing the rest, and making decisions about what to come away with in contributions with which to pursue their different fields.<br /> <br /> So it's not so much the Engineer Solar taking part in administration and legislation as it is going to talk to Legislator Solar(s) about what kinds of engineering they think should be engaged in and encouraged for the sake of the common good/the agendas of the Solars with the greatest clout.<br /> <br /> In my picture, a semi-formal forum was all the Deliberative was for quite a while (and that forum itself arose from how so many Solars were drawn into the sphere of Merela by her own leveraging of a few privileges she'd managed to wrangle out of the extremely vague &quot;Queen of Creation&quot; title she'd been granted, most notably greater requisition authority over the collective Sidereals than anybody else); it only truly became the Deliberative after some crisis (possibly the Niobraran War) brought every single Solar into the system for a while. They didn't all stay part of it for long after the crisis was resolved, but it provided the resources to convert informal coordination of various groups into true international organisations with a direct administrative hierarchy under a collective of Solars.<br /> <br /> I'm also basing some of my ideas for how the Realm was organised on the Southeast Asian Mandala model, with Meru as the central point that the various other powers and polities revolve around. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> On a slightly related note:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miss Maddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exaltation cannot be thought of exactly as a national identity or an occupation</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably not an <i>accurate</i> way to surmise Exaltation (or rather, certain kinds of Exaltation, since the Sidereals are absolutely an occupation and the Dragon Blooded have some pretty firm foundation for something like a national identity), but I can certainly see it as an idea people would form and push for the sake of certain ideologies.<br /> <br /> Certainly, in my abridged history of the First Age, something like the ideas that the Solar Exalted should be united by their collective relationship to their patron god, and that this conferred certain responsibilities and obligations, was a part of several of the groups that the Solar who became the Hierophant unified into the Church of the Unconquered Sun, and one that he placed significant emphasis on in its creed (motivated by a desire for Solars to rise above provincial concerns that he saw as a basis for a lot of conflicts in the Realm), and the length of the spiritual hegemony of his Church meant that a lot of Solars Exalted having grown up with such ideas and a lot of others who weren't inclined to personally believe them still played into a bit of the ceremony for the sake of broadening their power.<br /> <br /> He <i>intended</i> this as a way to confer the standards usually attached to Solar Exalted vis a vis the rise and fall of ideas and nations and systems to the whole of the Realm, univeralised, broadened to the extent of every Solar's supreme capability, and permanently held up by the Solars collectively so that there would never be a thing that would fail for lack of Solars to champion it. Unfortunately, having brought such an idea to the fore at the time when the Great Curse had become its most extreme, the Solars wound up holding themselves up as a kind of irreproachable reigning caste with the power of each secured by the reinforcement provided by the all; the idea that the Realm would be unquestionably better if the Solars oriented themselves as a collective had become very pervasive in the world's culture, so it became a very powerful rhetorical point by which any given Solar could demand or justify basically anything.<br /> <br /> The Hierophant's Curse was in the hubris that thought he could control the Solar Exalted in such a manner, and the depths of his despair when he realised how wrong it had all gone.<br /> <br /> This also provided a context for stuff that happened with other Exalted, since Solars expressing these ideas also sought to impose a kind of caste system identity on the rest of the Exalted as well. It created a context in which the Terrestrial dissatisfaction with what the world was turning into was expressed via building up their own interconnected identity over their individual root cultures (not just distinct Gentes, but also diverse cultural groups they had disseminated through by intermarriage, an action widely encouraged by the Deliberative), as well as part of why Lunars were widely viewed as a more homogenous group oriented directly below the Solars (which was itself the idea that the more vengefully minded Lunars sought to organise around when disaster came).<br /> <br /> This was the situation the Sidereals were faced with when they had to figure out how to implement their Vision. It was very distressing.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the Solars being so collective as they were was exactly why the sudden removal of <i>all</i> of them led to such a catastrophic collapse as it did, greater than anything that could have come before. If the Hierophant could have anticipated that binding the security of everything to the Solars collectively would mean that the loss of that collective would take all security with it, he still would have been untroubled by the idea that it could actually happen.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So... there, that's a whole bunch of ideas I've come up with for what the First Age could have been. Please forgive my extended digression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:25:02-08:00","id":39493,"title":"","content":"Lunars were originally designed with having four favored Attributes in mind, two of which were meant to be selected outside of their Caste-primary Attributes. This works perfectly fine in my experience. My gut feeling is that five favored Attributes would be too many, but I've never actually tried. The primary thing to keep in mind is that Lunars are basically not going to be purchasing any Abilities at the favored prices, which adds up pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T16:33:12-08:00","id":39682,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> My first character in Exalted was a Lunar.<br /> <br /> She was a Red Fox totem Changing Moon. Basically Marena, but younger, and with a Moonsilver bow.<br /> <br /> And I liked playing that character, even when there was other player with a Dawn Caste that was infinitely better at killing things.<br /> <br /> It also mattered not if Lunars fit well or badly into the game or its story.<br /> <br /> What mattered was that you were playing a devious shapeshifting badass, feared and reviled by Creation, and yet compelled to defend it at all costs.<br /> <br /> And it was awesome.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1850-snake-obsidian","name":"snake obsidian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:45:19-08:00","id":60299,"title":"","content":"I have a secret preview of the Lunars cover art in the works. This is like top secret level shit right here but I believe in giving back to the community. Since we all know 3e is about going back to the roots of the game, the Lunars are taking a few steps back as well, so this is NSFW by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/FRukxNQ.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/FRukxNQ.jpg</a> rejoice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:54:36-08:00","id":60304,"title":"","content":"I like how it both captures the adventure and epic feel of Exalted but also feels mature and uncompromising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T19:01:26-08:00","id":60310,"title":"","content":"I think it really speaks to the soul, challenging the perception of a Lunar's role. Where a picture of a knight on a horse conjures thoughts of abject servitude and expedience, I think the audience here can really appreciate that this is a partnership of the truest sort. Moreover, the contrast of the otherworldly flesh tone of the mythical creature and the alternative use of symbols lends the entire piece a certain conjugal <i>ju ne sais quoi.</i> Clearly, this both illustrates and represents the Lunar experience, I think capturing a hint of their historic treatment.<br /> <br /> Now, if somebody would scribble some silver swirly lines all over it, it'd be perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T19:14:32-08:00","id":60317,"title":"","content":"Hummm, I don't know... <br /> <br /> Oh don't get me wrong, I can fully support the ideas presented and embrace them as the step sideways and then two forward that is the progression of the lunar archetype as presented in this image, that is fully the ideal. <br /> <br /> I'm just not certain about using it as a cover image. You see I look at it and think that by the edge trimming needed to use it as a cover image it's going to lose the proper framing. And without the proper framing, it goes from the perfection of lunar expression to a very very good expression of lunar nature. It's acceptable of course, and better than 2e, but I don't know if it will really *sing* enough for 3e going forward. I mean we're punching the art up all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,