nfernal, dammit!<br /> <br /> Even has the weird devotion to an alien master which is really just a coded way to aggrandize oneself.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of what I see as ideal in &quot;pious&quot; Third Edition Green Sun Princes. &quot;Glorious Malfeas is the true ruler of this Earth! Unfortunately, due to a pressing prior appointment, he can't be here for now, so I shall be governing on his behalf for the next quadrillion years. Now; who wants to get press-ganged into constructing a giant green lantern to hang from the sky dome? It's just that Ligier owns the bonds on my gambling debts, aaaaand...&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T20:50:59-07:00","id":91363,"title":"","content":"I'm watching <b>Thor</b> on TV. It just started, and it's at the scene where Thor, the Warriors Three and the Lady Sif, and Loki are picking fights in Jotunheim. I'm thinking to myself, &quot;Okay, Thor, Fandral, Hogun, Volstagg, and Sif are all Solars, though the last four suffer from a really unfortunate but advanced case of Not Being The Protagonist that makes them kind of pussies. What's Loki, though? Is he a Lunar or a Sidereal?&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to play Tom Hiddleston's Loki (or just as good, Loki from the current <b>Agent of Asgard</b> ongoing series) as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:06:31-07:00","id":222792,"title":"","content":"Reposted from the &quot;Magic Armor: Problematic?&quot; Thread from a post by Aquillion:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Revan058</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221490-magic-armor-problematic?p=221642#post221642\">View Post</a></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">...I. Wait, what? *scrolls up*<br /> <br /> ...I think I blanked that out when I was reading over that post. That. Wj...WHY. Why the fuck would your NATIVE POWERS shut off your equipment, espcally if it's a damn MOONSILVER, SHIFTING WEAPON? You know, the shit that's flowing and shifting and...i have a headach now...</span></span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Several reasons.<br /> <br /> The main one is that Lunars need a reason to not use DBT. This puts the devs in a bind. One one hand, DBT is supposed to be heinously powerful; that's what it has always been, and it's a bit iconic to how it works. So they can't balance it as &quot;just another Lunar charm&quot; and make it one option among many -- it has to leap off the page. But at the same time, if they do that, any Lunar who doesn't use DBT is going to be weaker. This was a problem in previous editions -- you get Lunars balanced around DBT (so they're weak aside from this one strong option) and you get Lunars feeling they have to use this charm that has a very specific ascetic to it that might not be appropriate for everyone.<br /> <br /> The solution is to make DBT require some sort of tradeoff, but to make it a tradeoff in terms of 'options' (so the charm is still powerful as long as you don't intend to rely on those options at this precise moment.) Now, it could trade off with some DBT-incompatible Lunar charms, sure, but that would actually be harder to justify -- you'd have to almost invent un-Lunar Lunar charms in order for it to make sense for them to not work with DBT.<br /> <br /> On top of that, remember that DBT probably gives you huge persistent dice pools. In 3e this is going to be a <i>big deal</i> -- most people do not get persistent die-adders anymore; IAM-type charms are no longer a default part of the system. This makes DBT even more powerful than it was before, given how Exalted dice work -- it means that in some ways it can almost be a win button, provided your opponent has no way to shut it down. More specifically, it means that &quot;general&quot; powersets like Evocations are not necessarily designed and balanced with huge persistent dice-pools in mind; so having DBT limit your general powerset access makes for good balance.<br /> <br /> I will emphasize this again, because I think you're missing it, although I feel it's been heavily implied by everything spoiled so far: <i>In DBT, a Lunar will probably have a much larger persistent dice pool than a Solar</i>. Or anyone else, for that matter, excluding maybe some situational Infernal shintai stuff. I have no idea exactly how they'll balance this -- absent other tweaks, persistently rolling significantly more dice in the Storyteller system is a massive, game-changing advantage, of the &quot;I win automatically&quot; sort -- but it's a huge deal that will need to be designed around. This is probably part of that.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's pure speculation -- maybe Lunars will work entirely differently -- but I think it's reasonable to suspect that &quot;persistently boosted dice pools&quot; will be something Lunars get even if few other people do, since it's fairly inherent in what shapeshifting is. And it's a massively different (and much more defining) power in a setting where nobody else has IAM-equivilants to match those numbers. Turning into a bear now means that most fights against people who can't turn into bears will go down like, well, people trying to fight a bear, as opposed to 1e/2e where everyone had a charm to become as strong as a bear for the scene and shapeshifting was just your version of it.<br /> <br /> In terms of themes... this is the part I expect you won't like, but it's there, and I think they've indicated that this is where Lunars are going. It's a <i>beast</i>man transformation. The thematics are what they are; yes, there are a small number of animals that use tools, but none remotely comparable to humanity. It is therefore entirely thematically reasonable that taking on DBT (and temporarily shifting away from humanity into a hybrid state) could limit your ability to use human tools to their full potential. Keep in mind that by making this loss of evocation access a part of DBT, you allow Lunars to be good with tools <i>while in human form</i> -- human-form Lunars are better at evocations than Sidereals, and probably as good or better than anyone but Solars, despite their increased animal associations in 3e. This is possible because the game is focusing on their flexibility and shapeshifting -- a Lunar can choose to focus on their humanity, or they can choose to combine it with an animal form in exchange for physical power; and they can make that decision on the fly and rapidly switch back and forth between the two modes as the situation calls for it.<br /> <br /> This is more thematically interesting than a Lunar who just gets all their powers all the time in any form.<br /> <br /> (Keep in mind that we're not seeing the full picture here, of course -- DBT will be different; shapeshifting will be different; and we barely even know what Evocations are. But my point is that there are some obvious reasons to make it so Lunars can't use evocation in DBT form.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>Last edited by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\">Aquillion</a>; <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Today, 03:27 AM</span>.</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:37:06-07:00","id":222831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222792#post222792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">In terms of themes... this is the part I expect you won't like, but it's there, and I think they've indicated that this is where Lunars are going. It's a <i>beast</i>man transformation. The thematics are what they are; yes, there are a small number of animals that use tools, but none remotely comparable to humanity. It is therefore entirely thematically reasonable that taking on DBT (and temporarily shifting away from humanity into a hybrid state) could limit your ability to use human tools to their full potential. Keep in mind that by making this loss of evocation access a part of DBT, you allow Lunars to be good with tools <i>while in human form</i> -- human-form Lunars are better at evocations than Sidereals, and probably as good or better than anyone but Solars, despite their increased animal associations in 3e. This is possible because the game is focusing on their flexibility and shapeshifting -- a Lunar can choose to focus on their humanity, or they can choose to combine it with an animal form in exchange for physical power; and they can make that decision on the fly and rapidly switch back and forth between the two modes as the situation calls for it.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You see, that is the part that doesn't sell for me. To say it emphasizes the character's flexibility to invent a rule saying he can't do X while in Y shape. That doesn't enhance his flexibility... it detracts from it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I get miffed when they say preventing Lunars from using evocations in DBT form is a way of giving Lunars more options. No, it's not. It demonstrably removes options. It's like creating a rule saying Lunars can't use sorcery in DBT form. What 'option' does that add? Precisely none. Even though you now have two categories of Lunars - sorcery Lunars and DBT Lunars - in truth you've not actually given Lunars any more options, you've just taken options away and forced them down two arbitrary paths because they can no longer go down both at once. That is, maybe, the illusion of having more options. But in truth it's a net reduction. Previously, a Lunar could do anything in DBT form that he could do in human form. Now, he cannot. That doesn't add flexibility, it removes flexibility.<br /> <br /> I understand that games need balancing, and if they say Lunars will not have the ability to use evocations while DBT because of balancing issues - fine. What I don't like is the sell that it give a Lunar character more flexibility, when demonstrably all it does is place limits on what Lunars can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:56:47-07:00","id":222841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222831#post222831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, that is the part that doesn't sell for me. To say it emphasizes the character's flexibility to invent a rule saying he can't do X while in Y shape. That doesn't enhance his flexibility... it detracts from it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I get miffed when they say preventing Lunars from using evocations in DBT form is a way of giving Lunars more options. No, it's not. It demonstrably removes options. It's like creating a rule saying Lunars can't use sorcery in DBT form. What 'option' does that add?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can interrupt your rhetorical question, the fact that it provides a choice between two alternatives means that it produces an option point. You take one thing, or you concentrate on the other thing, in this case communion with your magic item versus communion with the two halves of the Lunar self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T23:00:59-07:00","id":222844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222841#post222841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can interrupt your rhetorical question, the fact that it provides a choice between two alternatives means that it produces an option point. You take one thing, or you concentrate on the other thing, in this case communion with your magic item versus communion with the two halves of the Lunar self.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because by definition, creating a rule saying <i>X</i> cannot be done in <i>Y</i> form removes as many options as it adds. It gives the option of using <i>X</i> without <i>Y</i>; but it removes the option of using <i>X</i> with <i>Y</i>. There is no net gain in options. And from the individual character's perspective, his functionality has decreased. Previously he could do two things at once; now he can only do one at a time. That's nothing but a decrease to his flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T23:15:56-07:00","id":222847,"title":"","content":"Wow, in the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; RPGnet thread, John confirmed that there are still 100 Sids and 300 Solars...but that there are now about *400* Lunars! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T00:38:04-07:00","id":222926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222847#post222847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, in the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; RPGnet thread, John confirmed that there are still 100 Sids and 300 Solars...but that there are now about *400* Lunars! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This came up, as well(Crossposting myself like a cheap hooker from another thread):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?733370-Exalted-Ask-the-Developers&amp;p=18181808#post18181808\" target=\"_blank\">Well, hello what's this here then</a>.<br /> <br /> For those that don't want to go elsewhere, this question was asked: &quot;So, are Solars and Lunars no longer paired Exaltations since their numbers are different?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mr. S.L. Sheppard has this to say: &quot;I <i>think</i> we're going back to the 1e standard of &quot;In the First Age, diplomatic marriages between Solars and Lunars were common, and these sometimeso-to-often blossomed into meaningful relationships, so you can have a lost romance with your ancient spouse or his/her modern reincarnation if you dig on that sort of thing.&quot; &quot;<br /> <br /> Now, he's not a dev. But nor has he been corrected in thread with both devs there.<br /> <br /> So, I think I can safely say: It's about goddamn time, I'm super glad to hear it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 08-09-2014, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T02:45:18-07:00","id":223039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222831#post222831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, that is the part that doesn't sell for me. To say it emphasizes the character's flexibility to invent a rule saying he can't do X while in Y shape. That doesn't enhance his flexibility... it detracts from it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I get miffed when they say preventing Lunars from using evocations in DBT form is a way of giving Lunars more options. No, it's not. It demonstrably removes options. It's like creating a rule saying Lunars can't use sorcery in DBT form. What 'option' does that add? Precisely none. Even though you now have two categories of Lunars - sorcery Lunars and DBT Lunars - in truth you've not actually given Lunars any more options, you've just taken options away and forced them down two arbitrary paths because they can no longer go down both at once. That is, maybe, the illusion of having more options. But in truth it's a net reduction. Previously, a Lunar could do anything in DBT form that he could do in human form. Now, he cannot. That doesn't add flexibility, it removes flexibility.<br /> <br /> I understand that games need balancing, and if they say Lunars will not have the ability to use evocations while DBT because of balancing issues - fine. What I don't like is the sell that it give a Lunar character more flexibility, when demonstrably all it does is place limits on what Lunars can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just about raw flexibility, it is about the <i>type</i> of flexibility they have -- about determining which choices are significant.<br /> <br /> Since we don't know Lunar design for 3e, I will use 2e Alchemical design as a reference, because I think it illustrates the point really well. Alchemicals have a major constraint on how many charms they can use at once, primarily due to their commitment costs.<br /> <br /> If you removed commitment costs, Alchemicals would be able to install all their charms at once. That would give them more options, right? Well, sort-of. But it would mean that the choice of what charm to <i>install</i> is no longer a meaningful decision (since obviously you just install everything.) And since modularity is vital to the unique Alchemical theme, that choice ought to be important -- hence, commitment costs. Obviously everyone would like to have every potential option, at all times, at no cost; but characters and powersets are defined by their limitations (and the specific, unique choices those limitations force on you) as much as by their strengths.<br /> <br /> Same with Lunars. Yes, a Lunar in DBT who has access to all their evocations has access to ALL THE OPTIONS; but that means that whether or not you take DBT or whether or not you learn evocations is no longer a meaningful choice. <i>Shapeshifting</i> ceases to be a meaningful choice, because there is now one obvious form to always take for combat which every Lunar will always use. And since Lunars are meant to be a shapeshifting splat, that is an undesirable result.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I said it would sort-of give Alchemicals more options; but in fact, it <i>wouldn't</i>. Because another key point to get from Alchemicals is how they're balanced and designed around their limitations, and what that means for the choices available to them. The commitment cost is the reason Alchemicals can get such inexpensive, powerful, low-prerequisite charms; and having those charms, of course, increases Alchemical options. (Or, in other words -- the commitment cost, by allowing that design, ultimately increases the number of interesting choices Alchemicals face.) Remove the commitment cost and you have to nerf and reprice their charms to balance, and the next thing you know they're just generic bottom-tier Celestials. They're not going to actually end up with more absolute choices, because... the splat is balanced as a whole.<br /> <br /> Same for Lunars. The limitation on using DBT with Evocations is part of the core design design of both DBT and Lunar Evocation access; one or both of them would have to be substantially weaker without it. In other words -- your evocation-wielding Lunar has the <i>option</i> to drop their evocations for a moment and turn into an overwhelmingly powerful DBT form; your DBT-using Lunar has the <i>option</i> to switch to human form and use powerful evocations. Without the limitation, neither would be so powerful for you, and therefore neither would be as significant of an option -- even though you could have both running at once, the game would have to be balanced so you don't always want to, which would mean DBT would just be one more generic charm in their charmset rather than an option of nearly game-breaking power.<br /> <br /> eg. Solars, for instance, do <i>not</i> have the option to temporarily trade their Evocation access for increased power. That's something they can't do. The fact that Lunars have that choice is, in some cases, a substantial advantage for them.<br /> <br /> (And in this case I'm using Solars as an example very deliberately -- Solar charms rarely have disadvantages or limitations or trade-offs, which <i>looks</i> like an advantage for them. But it does limit Solar options, in terms of what the Solar charmset can do, because disadvantages and trade-offs in one area can be used to buy power elsewhere -- something non-Solar splats tend to explore in a lot more depth. Lunars can trade their hands for wings; Solars can't.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-09-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T04:43:10-07:00","id":223125,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, quick confession: I always found Deadly Beastman Transformation super boring. Its mechanical effects were fairly limited (even if you were willing to go through the dispersed bookkeeping of Gift Charms), it always felt weird that you were supposed to build the appearance of the form out of points for mutations (except not really, since nobody ever expected your character to look different if you didn't have enough points to cover every mutation that would make it look like it was supposed to), excepting the occasional mutation that had a disproportionately useful effect, usually by stacking stat bonuses. Worst of all, though, is that it didn't really feel like it incentivized or required a character to act in any way different, despite the implications lent by usual interpretations of the motif.<br /> <br /> Put it next to things like the Infernal shintais, or even Martial Art Forms, and it feels especially wanting. It's a skin, an FPS paint job for the guns.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's going to be what it is in the next Edition. All of this talk of emphasizing playstyles and feeling different in Charms makes me think that Deadly Beastman Transformation will have more widgets to get you to act and fight in a certain way that feels appropriate to the motif more. Something a bit more like shintais and Form-Charms.<br /> <br /> There are several reasons why you can't have more than one shintai or Form active at the same time. Some are a matter of excessive mechanical stacking, but to my mind the most important is a sense of diffusion of playstyle.<br /> <br /> I think there's a point, and a not especially difficult to reach one, where your transformed lunatic beast person doesn't really feel like they're fighting in the manner that feels appropriate, if they're slugging around their soul-bonded magical weapon.<br /> <br /> Really, forget Deadly Beastman Transformation and Evocations for a moment. I can just focus on the idea that part of the play experience of being a Lunar is being able to turn into a tyrant lizard, and fighting in the distinct manner given by the stats we got, all tail sweeps and huge bites and roaring and stunts to terrify. You might even supplement it a fair bit with Lunar Charms, albeit still hanging off of the central frame of fighting in the manner of a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> This comes at the cost of having to give up fighting with a sword for a while, I should expect. Partially because it's too much in one place, but mostly because a tyrant lizard fighting with a sword looks quite silly. Or at least diffuses the sense of fighting like a tyrant lizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T05:36:33-07:00","id":223156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223125#post223125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so, quick confession: I always found Deadly Beastman Transformation super boring. Its mechanical effects were fairly limited (even if you were willing to go through the dispersed bookkeeping of Gift Charms), it always felt weird that you were supposed to build the appearance of the form out of points for mutations (except not really, since nobody ever expected your character to look different if you didn't have enough points to cover every mutation that would make it look like it was supposed to), excepting the occasional mutation that had a disproportionately useful effect, usually by stacking stat bonuses. Worst of all, though, is that it didn't really feel like it incentivized or required a character to act in any way different, despite the implications lent by usual interpretations of the motif.<br /> <br /> Put it next to things like the Infernal shintais, or even Martial Art Forms, and it feels especially wanting. It's a skin, an FPS paint job for the guns.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's going to be what it is in the next Edition. All of this talk of emphasizing playstyles and feeling different in Charms makes me think that Deadly Beastman Transformation will have more widgets to get you to act and fight in a certain way that feels appropriate to the motif more. Something a bit more like shintais and Form-Charms.<br /> <br /> There are several reasons why you can't have more than one shintai or Form active at the same time. Some are a matter of excessive mechanical stacking, but to my mind the most important is a sense of diffusion of playstyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want me to be required to <i>behave</i> a certain way in DBT form?<br /> <br /> So not only can I not use all my powers while in DBT, I can't even roleplay in it the way I want to? Dear God, I hope that's not what it's going to be.<br /> <br /> It's because Lunars are so <i>good</i> at shapeshifting that they don't <i>have</i> to behave like a monster just because they take the shape of a monster. Your shape changes, your instincts change, but you, the Lunar, remain in control (until you choose to go into RLF). And I like that. I like playing a cool, methodical, intellectual No Moon who remains cool and methodical and intellectual even when in his war form. If I'm forced to play him as a ragebear it's going to be a serious downgrade to his ability to shapeshift, on top of limiting my roleplaying choices as a player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T05:46:52-07:00","id":223164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223125#post223125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes at the cost of having to give up fighting with a sword for a while, I should expect. Partially because it's too much in one place, but mostly because a tyrant lizard fighting with a sword looks quite silly. Or at least diffuses the sense of fighting like a tyrant lizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean in general, but sometimes fighting a Lunar should feel like this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static-2.nexusmods.com/15/images/162/529489-1354079087.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T05:49:44-07:00","id":223165,"title":"","content":"Well, potentially you'd be the one picking what bonuses go where, so you can still roleplay how you want, it would just give you a reason to adopt a slightly different persona in werewolf mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:10:59-07:00","id":223191,"title":"","content":"My reading of what Levi said was about avoiding the phenomena I call &quot;Adorable Beastman Transformation&quot; in which a Lunar player uses their warform for a bunch of non-combat applications that it clearly wasn't intended for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:12:08-07:00","id":223193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221490-magic-armor-problematic?p=222434#post222434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why are Solars' native charms immune to this basic game design?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be found somewhat in what their Charms actually do, and not so much in what their numbers are.<br /> <br /> Let's think for a moment in terms of Abyssals, because they're another who aren't as good at Evocations, and I have an actual reference point for illustration.<br /> <br /> First off, I have no idea what not being as good at Evocations means; it could be anything from &quot;can't get as deep into the trees&quot; to &quot;can't use all the Materials&quot; to &quot;can't use all of their Evocations in all circumstances&quot;.<br /> <br /> So what do Abyssals have?<br /> <br /> For a start, they might have a Charm to summon a collection of spiked ghost-chains that flail around with a mind of their own (and can eventually be enhanced to have an iron maiden that turns the people it kills into armoured zombie minions). That sounds pretty neat, and fairly useful, weapon things that go around with a logic tangential to actually being wielded by a fighter.<br /> <br /> Do Solars have anything like that? I mean, anything that even follows the broad paradigm, of aspects of themselves flying about independently, maybe altering the conditions of the battlefield, or whatever other tactical benefits it has?<br /> <br /> I can't see how they would, following the logic given for what their Charms are. Nothing that kind of extends outside of themselves.<br /> <br /> Not without an Artifact, at least.<br /> <br /> The Solar is still built holistically around the idea that it's possible for them to overcome the deathknight with the flailing death chains (which is partially based on better use of Evocations), but I can imagine it's still a tactical option unavailable to them; they instead go through things like resistances, reactive powers, or building up their advantages, perhaps.<br /> <br /> But the Abyssal still has those chains. It might be that, if those chains were stacked on top of some things Evocations might do, the possibility of anybody beating them would be reduced drastically.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a Lunar warform might be capable of things that a Solar cannot do, but can still beat, but that would be excessively advantageous if paired with Evocations, even if they're not aesthetically incompatible.<br /> <br /> A Lunar might still have recourse to switching back and forth between them with great speed. A Solar might have recourse to recognising that pattern, and exploiting openings it might provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:24:52-07:00","id":223203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223191#post223191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading of what Levi said was about avoiding the phenomena I call &quot;Adorable Beastman Transformation&quot; in which a Lunar player uses their warform for a bunch of non-combat applications that it clearly wasn't intended for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not let the player decide what his forms are for? Do we need the developers leaning over our shoulder, going &quot;No no, I don't want you to use that form in that situation, here, see this form, this is what you should use.&quot; Who's the shapeshifter here?<br /> <br /> Besides, unless this changes, the DBT form is one of your true forms. You are <i>yourself</i> in your true form; you're as much yourself when in DBT as you are when human. It's not like you're blending yourself with something you're not. The point of a spirit shape is that whatever instincts and nature your totem animal possesses are already instincts and nature that you share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:41:37-07:00","id":223212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223203#post223203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's the shapeshifter here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST, duh - he's gotta be everybody in the world who isn't a PC, and from time to time one or more of the PCs on top of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:47:30-07:00","id":223215,"title":"","content":"I once had a player enter Deadly Beastman Transformation to pick a lock. That wasn't because he had a cool stunt for his DBT form, it was because two extra dice from the warform's +1 Dexterity (and the Dexterity Excellency) were way too good to pass up.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's unreasonable to say that's a flaw rather than a feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:50:31-07:00","id":223220,"title":"","content":"I think it's not entirely silly for each true form to bring different sides of the character to the forefront. Your human &quot;true self&quot; is slightly different from your wolf &quot;true self&quot; and your DBT &quot;true self&quot; is kind of halfway between the two.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking anything drastic, but if say you've got a wolf totem, then your human form will be a bit wolfish, whereas in your wolf form these traits really come to the surface and other traits recede a bit and you end up a particularly humanish wolf. They're both <i>you</i>, but they're not quite the <i>same </i>you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:58:39-07:00","id":223225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222847#post222847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, in the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; RPGnet thread, John confirmed that there are still 100 Sids and 300 Solars...but that there are now about *400* Lunars! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm-... Interested in this.<br /> There was a time where I would have gone at this with torch and pitchfork in hand, but now I just find it extremely interesting and can see some potential in the idea.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this means anything for the Celestial Bond, or not? Though considering we don't even know how the bond will be working in third edition, or even if it still exists as a 'thing'.<br /> I kind of like the bond, the only change I want is for it to become less sucky for the Lunar/not a horribly one-sided chain for the Solar to yank.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I wonder if Lunar-Sidereal bonds will be a thing? Probably not in the way I'm thinking.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aannndd, I just read Shepard's quote. Looks like it will be -entirely- different, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:02:23-07:00","id":223227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223156#post223156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you want me to be required to <i>behave</i> a certain way in DBT form?<br /> <br /> So not only can I not use all my powers while in DBT, I can't even roleplay in it the way I want to?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works so well for Demon Emperor Shintai and the like.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I wasn't even thinking specifically about their mindset (it's not as if Demon Emperor Shintai changes that either), but at the very least give them a tactical profile distinct from how they'd fight when not in the war form that amounts to more than &quot;slightly higher dicepools&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because Lunars are so <i>good</i> at shapeshifting that they don't <i>have</i> to behave like a monster just because they take the shape of a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't care for arguments based on using Lunar shapeshifting as an avenue for their triumphalism. I like that Lunars shapeshift, I'm barely compelled by them beng the best at it, or using it to be the best at something.<br /> <br /> That and turning into a monster and then not doing monster stuff seems to be missing most of the fun, something I'm more concerned about than using it to make a rhetorical point about how great Lunars are at shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Referring back to tyrant lizards, I can't see why one would want to turn into one if they weren't looking to stomp on people and bite them in half; a compulsion to do so seems like it should be wholly unnecessary. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:04:36-07:00","id":223232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223203#post223203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are <i>yourself</i> in your true form; you're as much yourself when in DBT as you are when human. It's not like you're blending yourself with something you're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a Lunar?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:06:13-07:00","id":223234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223220#post223220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's not entirely silly for each true form to bring different sides of the character to the forefront. Your human &quot;true self&quot; is slightly different from your wolf &quot;true self&quot; and your DBT &quot;true self&quot; is kind of halfway between the two.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking anything drastic, but if say you've got a wolf totem, then your human form will be a bit wolfish, whereas in your wolf form these traits really come to the surface and other traits recede a bit and you end up a particularly humanish wolf. They're both <i>you</i>, but they're not quite the <i>same </i>you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes I play it that way, at other times the opposite angle is more fun: you are a wolf at all times, even when you are perfectly human. When you get annoyed by someone, onlookers get the impression of bristling fur or a fanged snarl, even though you have neither fur nor fangs and are as human as anyone. If you seem more feral when in your war form, it's partly that you're relaxing your self-control a bit, but your instincts are the same.<br /> <br /> But you see, currently, two Lunar players can have two different interpretations on things like that; you have the choice to see it how you want and roleplay the way that makes sense to you. I wouldn't like being told I have to roleplay one way or other other. And if it gets to the point where my mechanical capabilities are being restricted for the sake of that, I think it's gone too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:15:04-07:00","id":223236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223215#post223215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once had a player enter Deadly Beastman Transformation to pick a lock. That wasn't because he had a cool stunt for his DBT form, it was because two extra dice from the warform's +1 Dexterity (and the Dexterity Excellency) were way too good to pass up.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's unreasonable to say that's a flaw rather than a feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand if I'm in my super-nimble (small mutation) war form, I do not want to have to shift into human shape to pick a lock. Because are you kidding me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:55:13-07:00","id":223264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223232#post223232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is a Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Throws goblet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T08:28:50-07:00","id":223294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223236#post223236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand if I'm in my super-nimble (small mutation) war form, I do not want to have to shift into human shape to pick a lock. Because are you kidding me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should be better at this than your human form.<br /> <br /> Also the Lunar with Devastating Ogre Enhancement is <b>even better</b> at this, because I know that when I see a 12 foot tall fusion of man and beast I think &quot;clearly this individual is a sneaky thief!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T09:10:40-07:00","id":223311,"title":"","content":"This is the problem with making &quot;move silently&quot; and &quot;hide in tight corners&quot; the same dice pool. I can see a 12 foot beastman having the precise, fluid motions to be silent stalker. The issue is that he's not very good at hiding in a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T09:33:33-07:00","id":223326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223294#post223294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Lunar with Devastating Ogre Enhancement is <b>even better</b> at this, because I know that when I see a 12 foot tall fusion of man and beast I think &quot;clearly this individual is a sneaky thief!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it had the right Dexterity score, I'd think of one of those enormous monsters that nevertheless manages to sneak around the ship (or whatever) because it's just so fast (at action and reaction), and able to blend in so well. Although as Elfive says, this should be an issue of being a bad thief in environments where there isn't a lot of open space to hide in.<br /> <br /> Using DBT to pick a lock really seems like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut. Was this lock really so difficult to pick, and were the consequences of a failed roll that big a deal?<br /> <br /> DBT (and applied sensible GMing) and any shapeshifting that is meant to be of an epic, &quot;breaking out the big guns&quot; scale really, seems like it shouldn't really encourage you to shapeshift for a single, rather mundane task - breaking the sledgehammer out of its case to crack that nut, give him a good enough hammer that its just inefficient. I think that's quite different from the idea that becoming the Weretiger with beyond human reflexes and speed *AND* opposable thumbs shouldn't mean that you're a better swordfighter than humans of a similar level of ability are, in a game were swordfighting ability is, amongst other things, a composite of skill and natural reactions.<br /> <br /> On Lunar evocations - I wonder if they'll have evocation like ability to absorb their weapons into their body and enhance their shapeshifting. It would make sense for their evocation like abilities to follow the tactic of shapeshifting their weapon into a form useful for their transformation, so it's not like, either / or for them.<br /> <br /> I could see Lunar comic lady being able to do something like this.<br /> <br /> Like, you might not want the Lunar to shapeshift into a tyrant lizard and then not be able to use his melee, but if would be nice if there was be a better solution this than &quot;your melee is now dead points&quot;. I mean, it still could clearly be worth the Lunar to invest in melee, for when he has to fight as a mortal, but ideally there should be something beyond &quot;When you're getting serious, your most signature weapon and ability as a mortal doesn't mean anything at *all*&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 08-09-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T09:33:35-07:00","id":223327,"title":"","content":"Don't forget they're automatically better at sneaking in the warform and it doesn't matter if the Lunar's spirit shape is something like a Mammoth or a Rhinoceros. I'm not against huge but stealthy monsters, I just think you should have to work for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223326#post223326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using DBT to pick a lock really seems like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut. Was this lock really so difficult to pick, and were the consequences of a failed roll that big a deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Low Larceny and two Abyssal Exalted in the immediate area.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-09-2014, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:02:55-07:00","id":223389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223227#post223227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and turning into a monster and then not doing monster stuff seems to be missing most of the fun, something I'm more concerned about than using it to make a rhetorical point about how great Lunars are at shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Referring back to tyrant lizards, I can't see why one would want to turn into one if they weren't looking to stomp on people and bite them in half; a compulsion to do so seems like it should be wholly unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Forms like tyrant lizard, sea dragon, snow lion, of course you could use those forms to stomp people, bite them in half, swallow them whole, etc. But of equal utility is the fact that all those things that might happen, those things are flashing vividly through the minds of any mortals and small spirits who happen to be looking at you. Mortals and spirits who, let's say, you would prefer to think of as your friends, if only they could be made amenable to the possibility. And when a tyrant lizard stops and lowers itself to look at you and asks, hey, you wanna be friends? =D<br /> <br /> Typically, the answer you give is yes.<br /> <br /> It's a houserule I use that any overwhelmingly large and terrifying shape automatically grants you an Appearance score of 5 or greater, which gives you an advantage in social combat, as well as a Presence bonus to intimidation. Yes you can talk to a tyrant lizard, you can even joke with it, but all the while you're thinking, teeth, teeth, teeth.<br /> <br /> Moreover, there are other uses for large shapes like that. You might need to convey a couple of friends somewhere in a hurry, in which case a large strix or a great roc or a snow wyrm or simply a very large wolf may be in order. The need to carry people around comes up <b>a lot</b>, especially in mixed games with non-shapeshifting, non-flying Exalts, and when the need arises, being compelled to eat your passengers is probably not something that's going to help you much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223294#post223294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should be better at this than your human form.<br /> <br /> Also the Lunar with Devastating Ogre Enhancement is <b>even better</b> at this, because I know that when I see a 12 foot tall fusion of man and beast I think &quot;clearly this individual is a sneaky thief!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a war form with a Dexterity score of 6, it is, in fact, a creature of superhuman grace and speed. So, in all honestly, why shouldn't it be capable of stealth? Now, if it's being played as a hulking brute, then it's a problem, because it really should have a lower Dexterity score than that. But if it honestly looks like it should be as graceful as its numbers say it is, then is it still a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:07:10-07:00","id":223390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223294#post223294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it should be better at this than your human form.<br /> <br /> Also the Lunar with Devastating Ogre Enhancement is <b>even better</b> at this, because I know that when I see a 12 foot tall fusion of man and beast I think &quot;clearly this individual is a sneaky thief!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the problems is that the rules, while having penalties in them, and equipment bonuses for certain tasks, never really pushed enough the idea that STs should apply situational modifiers: &quot;Sure, you have +2 dexterity, but you are a huge monster now, so here is a penalty to your stealth roll&quot;. If you were sneaky in human form, you can be a sneaky hybrid monster, otherwise, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:18:32-07:00","id":223396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223389#post223389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a war form with a Dexterity score of 6, it is, in fact, a creature of superhuman grace and speed. So, in all honestly, why shouldn't it be capable of stealth? Now, if it's being played as a hulking brute, then it's a problem, because it really should have a lower Dexterity score than that. But if it honestly looks like it should be as graceful as its numbers say it is, then is it still a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>If, as a human being, you have a Dexterity of 5 (which you will, because godstat), then a hybrid form with Devastating Ogre Enhancement has Dexterity 7 <i>regardless of the animal on which the form is based</i>. That means, yes, Dex 7 mammoth/rhino/buffalo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:30:36-07:00","id":223427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223396#post223396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as a human being, you have a Dexterity of 5 (which you will, because godstat), then a hybrid form with Devastating Ogre Enhancement has Dexterity 7 <i>regardless of the animal on which the form is based</i>. That means, yes, Dex 7 mammoth/rhino/buffalo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And someone with Dexterity 7 is inhumanly graceful, fast and agile. If a Solar has Dexterity 7, he is an inhumanly graceful. If a Lunar has Dexterity 7, he is inhumanly graceful. What is the problem, exactly? You think Dexterity should read differently for Lunars?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd allow someone with a mammoth totem to take Dexterity 5 at chargen, though. At least I would insist that he also have Stamina 5 and/or Strength 5. The character's spirit shape must be some reflection of his innate qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:39:35-07:00","id":223434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223427#post223427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. And someone with Dexterity 7 is inhumanly graceful, fast and agile. If a Solar has Dexterity 7, he is an inhumanly graceful. If a Lunar has Dexterity 7, he is inhumanly graceful. What is the problem, exactly? You think Dexterity should read differently for Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it was achieved by turning into a huge monster. It's rather counter-intuitive, like the tiger shapeshifter stats in WoD: Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure I'd allow someone with a mammoth totem to take Dexterity 5 at chargen, though. At least I would insist that he also have Stamina 5 and/or Strength 5. The character's spirit shape must be some reflection of his innate qualities. </div> </div> </div>You're going the same route as the &quot;wouldn't want to hose warthog totem Lunars&quot; route. Don't do that. It results in a total lack of Charms based on Appearance. Also, the qualities of a spirit shape are symbolic and idiosyncratic to the Lunar with the totem. Wolves don't typically go it alone if they can help it, but there are Lunars, so the book says, with that spirit shape because they're &quot;lone wolves&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:47:22-07:00","id":223443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223427#post223427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. And someone with Dexterity 7 is inhumanly graceful, fast and agile. If a Solar has Dexterity 7, he is an inhumanly graceful. If a Lunar has Dexterity 7, he is inhumanly graceful. What is the problem, exactly? You think Dexterity should read differently for Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe, just maybe, a mammoth warform shouldn't increase your dexterity, so that a mammoth-Lunar would stay Dexterity 5 because their human shape is incredibly graceful and agile but gain appropriate mammoth-like qualities, instead of <i>making them even more graceful and agile</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course these mammoth-like qualities should be balanced against the increased Dexterity a more nimble shape would provide, which is a laughable proposition in the current system, so really it's lose/lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:50:02-07:00","id":223446,"title":"","content":"Someone can, to be fair, take a rat totem and transform into a hulking giant rat beast. Rats are not, exactly, known for their might (they're not exactly like hero shrews). What exactly is different about Dex here? What's particularly weird about super acrobat Ganesha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:55:54-07:00","id":223451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223434#post223434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it was achieved by turning into a huge monster. It's rather counter-intuitive, like the tiger shapeshifter stats in WoD: Changing Breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>A large thing is not necessarily a ponderous thing. A large thing can be terrifyingly fast and agile. In fact, I think it's more fearsome and awe-inspiring when it is.<br /> <br /> Picking locks? I don't know, maybe some internal penalties are in order for things that require manipulation of tiny objects, and maybe stealth should be penalized too when you're all but impossible to miss, but that's the kind of thing I would expect normally to fall to storytellers to impose based on circumstances. I mean a 15' Lunar isn't necessarily any worse at picking locks, he may even be better. But a lock sized for a human door, that's naturally going to pose more of a challenge<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223434#post223434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unars&quot; route. Don't do that. It results in a total lack of Charms based on Appearance. Also, the qualities of a spirit shape are symbolic and idiosyncratic to the Lunar with the totem. Wolves don't typically go it alone if they can help it, but there are Lunars, so the book says, with that spirit shape because they're &quot;lone wolves&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If mammoth-Lunar's player could make a good argument, I'd allow it. But offhand, I don't see any good argument for statting a mammoth-totem Lunar with, for example, Str 3 / Dex 5 / Sta 3. The whole point of a spirit shape is that it's supposed to have something in common with your human form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:56:28-07:00","id":223452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223446#post223446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone can, to be fair, take a rat totem and transform into a hulking giant rat beast. Rats are not, exactly, known for their might (they're not exactly like hero shrews). What exactly is different about Dex here? What's particularly weird about super acrobat Ganesha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are examples of how the present system is not handling the matter properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:13:12-07:00","id":223481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223451#post223451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If mammoth-Lunar's player could make a good argument, I'd allow it. But offhand, I don't see any good argument for statting a mammoth-totem Lunar with, for example, Str 3 / Dex 5 / Sta 3. The whole point of a spirit shape is that it's supposed to have something in common with your human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I want to actually be a valid participant in combat&quot; is a pretty good argument as far as I'm concerned","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:15:37-07:00","id":223484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223264#post223264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Throws goblet)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Kill la Kill myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:17:19-07:00","id":223486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223451#post223451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of a spirit shape is that it's supposed to have something in common with your human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard this before, ever. Cite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:24:58-07:00","id":223494,"title":"","content":"I think it's really more the other way round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:27:05-07:00","id":223497,"title":"","content":"Whether or not the character is suitably fast despite their size isn't really the point to me.<br /> <br /> The point is that form is not connecting logically to function; that the war form amounts to a flat spread of bonuses that can be applied to a wide variety of tasks does not seem like a suitable implication of turning into a fearsome beast person. Or impetus to make such a transformation; I mean, the chain of thought that connects something<br /> <br /> Goddammit, why is my brother whinging to me about Harry Potter shit i cantt deeven think striaght.<br /> <br /> I'm sure people can see what Im getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:39:45-07:00","id":223508,"title":"","content":"Thank god.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:46:32-07:00","id":223512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223486#post223486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard this before, ever. Cite?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean you haven't heard that your spirit shape is supposed to represent your innate talents?<br /> <br /> <i>SPIRIT SHAPE<br /> Upon Exaltation, the Chosen of the Moon gains a second shape, which she can assume as readily as her natural human form. Known as the spirit shape, this form is that of a specific animal representing the Lunar\u2019s inner nature and personality.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223497#post223497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that the war form amounts to a flat spread of bonuses that can be applied to a wide variety of tasks does not seem like a suitable implication of turning into a fearsome beast person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course it does. The war form makes you stronger, faster and tougher. Of course that gives you bonuses that can be applied to a wide variety of tasks. That is the essence of what it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223481#post223481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I want to actually be a valid participant in combat&quot; is a pretty good argument as far as I'm concerned</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if I had someone trying to start a mammoth Lunar with Dexterity 5 and with Dexterity as a favored attribute, I'd probably be having second thoughts about inviting that person to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:51:34-07:00","id":223516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222831#post222831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that games need balancing, and if they say Lunars will not have the ability to use evocations while DBT because of balancing issues - fine. What I don't like is the sell that it give a Lunar character more flexibility, when demonstrably all it does is place limits on what Lunars can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try not to think of it in IC terms. It really has more to do with player build options than character &quot;what can I do this turn&quot; options.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's more like, DBT was always a no-brainer for Lunars who wanted to be combat-savvy. Which was in some ways a real shame, because Lunars should be fighting in many forms, not just that one. But practically, with DBT being exempt from the shit that was form-lock, DBT was your go-to fight form unless you had a giant spirit shape and even then, because DBT isn't going to show up on a street in quite the same way that a yeddim might.<br /> <br /> So the game is basically telling you &quot;if you want to be a fight Lunar, you need DBT&quot; (in the same way that the game said &quot;if you want to play an Abyssal, you have to do it this precise way or you get punished&quot;). Which led to basically every person who was going to play a Lunar needing to think about whether or not to invest XP in that Knack and its line, and probably needing to come up with a good reason for &quot;why <i>shouldn't </i>I take this even if I'm a socialite, because at some point I'm going to have to fight and I don't want to suck at it!&quot; <br /> <br /> Now the system could have allowed this to be a real choice. It didn't. Form-lock meant you can't take a combative animal form because if you spend too much Essence, that's gone. The awful tattoos meant you were closed off from some of the better buff effects in the game (sorcery). You can still do Martial Arts, sure, but Martial Arts + DBT persistent bonuses is still better than Martial Arts alone.<br /> <br /> Now going forward, we know that Evocations are a thing, that they offer some degree of doing stuff outside your normal splat thematics. We can also assume DBT will remain because it's an iconic Lunar power, and was historically their best way to fight, or at least a way to fight pretty damn well for relatively minimal XP investment. Paired with the changes to the system as Aquillion pointed out, you go from one One True Build problem to another if Lunars both get a form that gives persistent dice-additions and also get access to Evocation effects.<br /> <br /> At the same time, it's a character-building-flavor thing. Some people want to play Lunars who do shapeshift, but more for utility than combat and don't want to have to go Crinos to fight effectively. Now they have that option by focusing on Evocations instead of the DBT tree, and not feeling behind the ones who go DBT. But it's clear that if DBT and Evocations completely play together perfectly, you've traded last edition's One True Build problem for a new one.<br /> <br /> Iit is a balance thing. But I don't agree that it reduces flexibility. By that I mean it does not reduce overall flexibility - just flexibility on a turn by turn basis which frankly I am OK with. You're not necessarily behind anyone if you invest in both DBT and Evocations, assuming DBT isn't 5th down in a Charm tree or something. If anything you've expanded your toolkit to meet more challenges: fighting with DBT in certain situations may cause a huge panic that simply manifesting Evocations would not, but sometimes you also just need to be a fuzzy chainsaw who doesn't need tools to play the chunky salsa game as well as anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222847#post222847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, in the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; RPGnet thread, John confirmed that there are still 100 Sids and 300 Solars...but that there are now about *400* Lunars! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Meh? I don't know why people think hard numbers were ever necessary.<br /> <br /> Also now you have to justify what 100+ more Celestials have been doing the past 2000 years lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:54:46-07:00","id":223517,"title":"","content":"That doesn't necessarily mean that their physical attributes will be reflected. <br /> <br /> You could have a skinny waif who nonetheless possesses the belligerent temperament of a rhinoceros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:55:26-07:00","id":223518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223512#post223512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>SPIRIT SHAPE<br /> Upon Exaltation, the Chosen of the Moon gains a second shape, which she can assume as readily as her natural human form. Known as the spirit shape, this form is that of a specific animal representing the Lunar\u2019s inner nature and personality.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Which has nothing to do with their physical appearance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, of course it does. The war form makes you stronger, faster and tougher. Of course that gives you bonuses that can be applied to a wide variety of tasks. That is the essence of what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning into a monster person in order to pick locks and things that don't really follow the motif of turning into a monster person is dumb, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if I had someone trying to start a mammoth Lunar at Str 3 / Dex 5 / Sta 3, with Dexterity favored, I'd be having second thoughts about inviting that person to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's just... wow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:57:55-07:00","id":223519,"title":"","content":"Hello all, my search fu seems to be lacking and this seems to be a good place to ask.<br /> <br /> I was wondering is there any reason you couldn't use Limb Shielding Growth and a Thunderbolt Shield? The charm doesn't seem to have been hit with any errata making it about on par with the 2.5 version of Protection of Celestial Bliss?<br /> <br /> Shifting Options<br /> -Covering the shield with a bony carapace directly?<br /> -Ankylosaurus like tail? (This actually would be a lot of fun, I think its DBT would be something like an Aklok.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:00:26-07:00","id":223520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223512#post223512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if I had someone trying to start a mammoth Lunar with Dexterity 5 and with Dexterity as a favored attribute, I'd probably be having second thoughts about inviting that person to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e Exalted, such a decision would merely show how utterly disconnected you would be from the actual game you are presuming to run.<br /> <br /> In one game I'm currently in, a Lunar player started with Dexterity 3, because it suited her character concept of tough, hulking brawler with no finesse.<br /> <br /> Then she bought Dexterity 4, because that was the only way to have a character who would actually <i>function</i> in combat.<br /> <br /> Then she bought Dexterity 5, because, yeah, that's what it took. No real choice.<br /> <br /> She hated every bit of it, but that's the game we have right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:06:25-07:00","id":223528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223517#post223517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't necessarily mean that their physical attributes will be reflected.<br /> <br /> You could have a skinny waif who nonetheless possesses the belligerent temperament of a rhinoceros.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said I'd be open to a good argument. Ideally, though, your spirit shape should reflect your physical attributes as well as mental. For instance, a coyote-Totem Lunar might have very good Perception, Dexterity and Stamina, good Wits and/or Charisma, but mediocre strength. Alternatively, he could go with very high Manipulation, Charisma and Wits, building off of coyote's mythic identity as a trickster. He doesn't <i>have</i> to have all these things, of course. But if he started with 5 Strength and 3 Dexterity, I would ask the player what about a coyote makes him think of someone none too quick but immensely strong.<br /> <br /> Look at Strength of Many's human form and his spirit shape for an example of what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> While I don't demand everyone's attributes conform to my expectations, your spirit shape should bear at least some resemblance to your human self on some level. And going with physical attributes that are pretty much the opposite of your spirit shape's, like a high-Dex, low-Strength mammoth, would be a tough sell for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-09-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:25:24-07:00","id":223557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223520#post223520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e Exalted, such a decision would merely show how utterly disconnected you would be from the actual game you are presuming to run.<br /> <br /> In one game I'm currently in, a Lunar player started with Dexterity 3, because it suited her character concept of tough, hulking brawler with no finesse.<br /> <br /> Then she bought Dexterity 4, because that was the only way to have a character who would actually <i>function</i> in combat.<br /> <br /> Then she bought Dexterity 5, because, yeah, that's what it took. No real choice.<br /> <br /> She hated every bit of it, but that's the game we have right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in my original comment, Dexterity 5 would not necessarily be a problem if they also had Strength 5 or Stamina 5, because then you're just looking at general physical awesomeness. But a low-Strength, low-stamina, high-Dex mammoth, yes, that for me is a problem. Sorry if you don't agree. But I don't think you would ever have wanted to play with me as a storyteller anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:26:03-07:00","id":223559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223528#post223528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said I'd be open to a good argument. Ideally, though, your spirit shape should reflect your physical attributes as well as mental. For instance, a coyote-Totem Lunar might have very good Perception, Dexterity and Stamina, good Wits and/or Charisma, but mediocre strength. Alternatively, he could go with very high Manipulation, Charisma and Wits, building off of coyote's mythic identity as a trickster. He doesn't <i>have</i> to have all these things, of course. But if he started with 5 Strength and 3 Dexterity, I would ask the player what about a coyote makes him think of someone none too quick but immensely strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you'd be kind of a dick for doing it, because the text specifies inner nature and personality, with absolutely no mention of outward appearance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look at Strength of Many's human form and his spirit shape for an example of what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> While I don't demand everyone's attributes conform to my expectations, your spirit shape should bear at least some resemblance to your human self on some level. And going with physical attributes that are pretty much the opposite of your spirit shape's, like a high-Dex, low-Strength mammoth, would be a tough sell for me. </div> </div> </div>He could do as the circus elephant do, and charm people while pocking their pockets with his proboscis. Or she could be a priestess who dances for the spirits, and the mammoth is her guardian. It's so trivially easy to find some kind of resonant situation that you'd be better off not worrying too much about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:33:00-07:00","id":223564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221490-magic-armor-problematic?p=221696#post221696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having them be mutally excusive isn't the way to do it at all. Make viable builts, that people want one or the other.<br /> <br /> Not be forced to have one or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Melee Charms are mutually exclusive from Solar Archery. A Lunar applies pretty much all Strength and Dexterity Charms into either weapon with little to no exclusivity.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can also shapeshift more than once per battle. If he needs an Evocation this round, he shapeshifts back to human. If he doesn't need an Evocation this round, he reassumes or remains in DBT. This is essentially no different from a Solar switching out one magical sword for another magical weapon as the battle changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:36:16-07:00","id":223567,"title":"","content":"On one hand, it seems logical that a war form based on an animal particularly at odds with the lunar's human form could cause some stat juggling, trading dexterity for strength, for example. <br /> <br /> On the other hand this would probably be horrendously broken in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:41:02-07:00","id":223570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223559#post223559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you'd be kind of a dick for doing it, because the text specifies inner nature and personality, with absolutely no mention of outward appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, nothing like that.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Changing Moons favor animals adored for their beauty or grace. Great cats, birds of prey and serpents are common, as are animals whose luxurious fur, skin or feathers are sought by hunters.<br /> <br /> Full Moons favor animals known for their great strength and endurance, or for their speed and agility. Bears, great cats and aurochs are common, as are serpents and large birds of prey.</i></div>&quot;Inner nature&quot; in Exalted pertains to all your Attributes, not just your personality. If personality were all it meant, the phrase &quot;inner nature and personality&quot; would be redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:46:41-07:00","id":223575,"title":"","content":"My general feeling is that DBT should be, above all, a jacked-up war-form you adopt to kill shit. I think it was a mistake to try to make it satisfy a broader niche. I'm okay with Lunars having <i>other</i> tricks to fit those niches, but DBT should not be a terribly attractive option in situations where you don't need shit broken or killed. Obviously, there are various ways of doing this.<br /> <br /> The character art should probably reflect this, rather than being two-thirds DBT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:52:30-07:00","id":223580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223570#post223570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, nothing like that.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Changing Moons favor animals adored for their beauty or grace. Great cats, birds of prey and serpents are common, as are animals whose luxurious fur, skin or feathers are sought by hunters.<br /> <br /> Full Moons favor animals known for their great strength and endurance, or for their speed and agility. Bears, great cats and aurochs are common, as are serpents and large birds of prey.</i></div>&quot;Inner nature&quot; in Exalted pertains to all your attributes, not just your personality. If pesonality were all it was, the phrase &quot;inner nature and personality&quot; would be redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caste blurbs still don't mention how the Exalt has to have their Attributes concentrated. So this doesn't rule out at all the huge guy with little in the way of Dexterity that becomes a weasel because Luna changed him into it while he was running and came across a narrow passageway. Nor does it rule out, say, a beautiful woman who turns into a warthog, which is regarded as looking majestic in her culture... or simply enough, to her, because that's all that matters for her Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there are number of critters that can serve in the capacity of a totem across Castes. All of them, in fact. And how are you going to gauge just what someone with a king cobra totem &quot;should have&quot; for Attributes outside of the Caste's purview, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:55:46-07:00","id":223585,"title":"","content":"I really, really hope that Lunars have other options that are just as good as DBT. I tried playing Lunars a few different ways, and they were always... kinda lacking. I remember getting knocked around quite a bit by enemies that the rest of the Circle took out relatively easily. The day I took DBT, that switched, and I was able to take out enemies the team was struggling with. DBT just upped my abilities so much that the rest of my combat strategy went from underpowered to overpowered. I don't want a whole bunch of Lunar strategies that are basically good strategies, but when you add DBT, its better. Forcing Lunars to not use Evocations while in DBT seems weak, but I would prefer it to a situation where having an Evocation based combat strategy is simply made better by having DBT.<br /> <br /> I do not want a situation where everything a Lunar does is made better by DBT. If that happens, everything Lunars do will have to be balanced around the fact that the Lunar will be in DBT whenever there is no overriding need to NOT be in DBT.<br /> <br /> I am totally ok with DBT. I love DBT. I just don't want every Lunar ever to be DBT all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:56:27-07:00","id":223587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223580#post223580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caste blurbs still don't mention how the Exalt has to have their Attributes concentrated. So this doesn't rule out at all the huge guy with little in the way of Dexterity that becomes a weasel because Luna changed him into it while he was running and came across a narrow passageway. Nor does it rule out, say, a beautiful woman who turns into a warthog, which is regarded as looking majestic in her culture... or simply enough, to her, because that's all that matters for her Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that makes me a dick if I ask a player what about a coyote makes him think of someone of mediocre agility but immense strength? Really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223580#post223580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, there are number of critters that can serve in the capacity of a totem across Castes. All of them, in fact. And how are you going to gauge just what someone with a king cobra totem &quot;should have&quot; for Attributes outside of the Caste's purview, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would start by asking the player to explain it to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:07:19-07:00","id":223594,"title":"","content":"Seriously, those blurbs are <i>awful </i>for what they're trying to do. All Castes &quot;favor&quot; serpents and birds of prey, for different aesthetic reasons; that doesn't change the shape or its stats. There's a good argument for big cats in all Castes: they're mighty hunters, they have beautiful pelts that are sought after by poachers, and they're associated with cleverness or the supernatural. A furnace rhino or desert basilisk could be any Caste: they're powerful and dangerous, absolutely gorgeous or striking in appearance, and supernatural/mystical all in one. Elephants and bears and octopi are strong as well as being culturally viewed as wise (and are in fact quite smart and clever creatures). Etc.<br /> <br /> Hell, most if not all animals are pretty dangerous, from a human perspective, and would therefore be appropriate for any Caste. Deer gore people! Monkeys can tear off your face! Even small and cute animals that you might see in your backyard can hurt you pretty bad if they feel threatened or believe their territory is being infringed on. The distinctions the book makes there are unfortunately meaningless; the book is trying to provide some ideas for &quot;appropriate&quot; spirit shapes for players who might be unsure about the &quot;appropriateness&quot; of their idea in a given Caste but when most animals can fall under multiple Caste umbrellas, the provided examples fall flat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223557#post223557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said in my original comment, Dexterity 5 would not necessarily be a problem if they also had Strength 5 or Stamina 5, because then you're just looking at general physical awesomeness. But a low-Strength, low-stamina, high-Dex mammoth, yes, that for me is a problem. Sorry if you don't agree. But I don't think you would ever have wanted to play with me as a storyteller anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you can acknowledge that this would be a house rule. And hey, go nuts with house rules as far as I'm concerned! It's your table, after all. Just don't make it sound like anything in the books supports let alone requires the notion that human Attributes need to somehow be &quot;appropriately&quot; allocated for a player to choose a particular spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:14:07-07:00","id":223600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223587#post223587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that makes me a dick if I ask a player what about a coyote makes him think of someone of mediocre agility but immense strength? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. If you're sticking with an amazingly literal interpretation of animal capabilities, any animal could value Strength due to the importance of grappling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would start by asking the player to explain it to me. </div> </div> </div>Why enforce requiring a shapeshifter to have a human form with as many literal features in common with the totem as possible? That starts to cut against the concept of shapeshifters, i.e. the other form is not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:28:39-07:00","id":223606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223594#post223594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, those blurbs are <i>awful </i>for what they're trying to do. All Castes &quot;favor&quot; serpents and birds of prey, for different aesthetic reasons; that doesn't change the shape or its stats. There's a good argument for big cats in all Castes: they're mighty hunters, they have beautiful pelts that are sought after by poachers, and they're associated with cleverness or the supernatural. A furnace rhino or desert basilisk could be any Caste: they're powerful and dangerous, absolutely gorgeous or striking in appearance, and supernatural/mystical all in one. Elephants and bears and octopi are strong as well as being culturally viewed as wise (and are in fact quite smart and clever creatures). Etc.<br /> <br /> Hell, most if not all animals are pretty dangerous, from a human perspective, and would therefore be appropriate for any Caste. Deer gore people! Monkeys can tear off your face! Even small and cute animals that you might see in your backyard can hurt you pretty bad if they feel threatened or believe their territory is being infringed on. The distinctions the book makes there are unfortunately meaningless; the book is trying to provide some ideas for &quot;appropriate&quot; spirit shapes for players who might be unsure about the &quot;appropriateness&quot; of their idea in a given Caste but when most animals can fall under multiple Caste umbrellas, the provided examples fall flat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are undoubtedly good arguments. Maybe that's why I said <b>I would be open to an argument.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223594#post223594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you can acknowledge that this would be a house rule. And hey, go nuts with house rules as far as I'm concerned! It's your table, after all. Just don't make it sound like anything in the books supports let alone requires the notion that human Attributes need to somehow be &quot;appropriately&quot; allocated for a player to choose a particular spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the book supports is a matter of opinion. It's my opinion that a character's spirit shape reflects more aspects of his or her nature than merely his personality. If that's not your reading of it, fine. Your interpretation is no more valid than mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223600#post223600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of. If you're sticking with an amazingly literal interpretation of animal capabilities, any animal could value Strength due to the importance of grappling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you've settled down into &quot;you're a dick for reading things that way&quot; I don't think there's anything further to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:42:00-07:00","id":223613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that makes me a dick if I ask a player what about a coyote makes him think of someone of mediocre agility but immense strength? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you ask them to leave should their answer be unsatisfying to you, possibly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:46:34-07:00","id":223616,"title":"","content":"I'd kind of like spirit shapes to be a bit like Anchors in Nobilis; there's an assumption, in-character, that there's a certain relevant link between the nature and powers of the Anchor and the personality or Estate of the Noble, but you don't really need to go in much for what that connection is, and it doesn't really constrain what your Anchors can be, so the Power of Fire can still have a soul bound connection to a flute that causes flourishing business enterprise when played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:04:59-07:00","id":223647,"title":"","content":"I'm really interested in seeing how the No Moons are handled.<br /> <br /> Descriptions of the No Moons in First Edition -<br /> <br /> First Edition Core -<br /> <br /> - &quot;excellent combat sorcerors&quot;<br /> Lunars - <br /> - Masters of the lore and legends of the Lunars.<br /> - &quot;They hold all of the sorceries peculiar to the Beloved of Lunar, remember the tales of the First Age and they have learned almost everything there is to know about the wild environment that is theres&quot;<br /> - &quot;The greatest No Moons are able to mine moonsilver with their bare hands, work it into weapons and armor, fabricate the greatest artifacts and even, it's said, repair and manufacture the Lunars' specialized warstriders.&quot;<br /> - &quot;Quiet thinkers and mighty sorcerors ... trusting in their vast knowledge and mystical might&quot;<br /> - &quot;the caste's role as arbitrator and advisor within the Silver Pact&quot;<br /> <br /> So they make things, know sorcery and carry legends and lore.<br /> <br /> I feel they get sorcery as a primary focus because they are very much not a physical Caste, so shapeshifting is of limited value for them, and very much not able to express skills, to distinguish their approach from Solars. I wonder if this will continue in 3e, and if so, how will their sorcery be other than simply being of the &quot;Silver Solar&quot; variety? I guess taking a page out of the TAW playbook, while limiting the influences it took from Infernals and general cynicism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:37:42-07:00","id":223661,"title":"","content":"No Moons have been described as shamans rather than sorcerers. No Moons suffered from an association with sorcery like none other, given that their anima was useless for anything else until 2e's Lunar manual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:25:19-07:00","id":223742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223613#post223613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you ask them to leave should their answer be unsatisfying to you, possibly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never yet asked a player to leave a game, for that or any reason.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, when you ask a player something during chargen, you're not saying, &quot;Answer the way I like or you're out of the game.&quot; The worst that would happen in the case of mammoth Lunar player, if he had no explanation of why his character had Dexterity 5 and Strength 3 other than &quot;god stat&quot;, is that I might ask him to choose a different totem animal, one that actually had a high Dexterity score and would therefore seem more appropriate for him.<br /> <br /> The reason is because the whole point of the s<i>pirit shape</i> is that it's the animal that best reflects your nature. It's the animal you. It's not some other thing you change into. It's your true form. Is nature is your nature, its instincts are your instincts. You can't separate them. And just as your spirit shape is an animal repreesentation of you, so you, in human form, are a human representation of your spirit shape, because the nature of both is the same.<br /> <br /> It seems the consensus on this thread is that your totem animal only reflects your nature as far as your personality is concerned - but I've never read it that way, because you can't really separate, say, the instincts of a fox, with the Dexterity and Perception a fox relies on to hunt. Physical and social attributes are a large part of an animal's nature, and if your spirit shape reflects your nature then it should reflect your attributes too.<br /> <br /> And in my experience, it's always more enjoyable in a Lunar game the more in common you have with your spirit shape, because you get to play on that in a variety of ways. If the fox Lunar is the one who, even in human form, has the best hearing, the one who always notices a trap, the one with the quickest reflexes, well, it makes you feel like you're actually playing a fox Lunar, someone whose spirit shape actually fits. And it makes the character feel more like it actually works, and the game experience is more enjoyable. Or at least that's how it's always been for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223647#post223647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really interested in seeing how the No Moons are handled.<br /> <br /> Descriptions of the No Moons in First Edition -<br /> <br /> First Edition Core -<br /> <br /> - &quot;excellent combat sorcerors&quot;<br /> Lunars -<br /> - Masters of the lore and legends of the Lunars.<br /> - &quot;They hold all of the sorceries peculiar to the Beloved of Lunar, remember the tales of the First Age and they have learned almost everything there is to know about the wild environment that is theres&quot;<br /> - &quot;The greatest No Moons are able to mine moonsilver with their bare hands, work it into weapons and armor, fabricate the greatest artifacts and even, it's said, repair and manufacture the Lunars' specialized warstriders.&quot;<br /> - &quot;Quiet thinkers and mighty sorcerors ... trusting in their vast knowledge and mystical might&quot;<br /> - &quot;the caste's role as arbitrator and advisor within the Silver Pact&quot;<br /> <br /> So they make things, know sorcery and carry legends and lore.<br /> <br /> I feel they get sorcery as a primary focus because they are very much not a physical Caste, so shapeshifting is of limited value for them, and very much not able to express skills, to distinguish their approach from Solars. I wonder if this will continue in 3e, and if so, how will their sorcery be other than simply being of the &quot;Silver Solar&quot; variety? I guess taking a page out of the TAW playbook, while limiting the influences it took from Infernals and general cynicism?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Moons are my favorite caste to play but I've only played one sorcerer ever, and he was a dragon king. For me, the major flavor of the caste is just... perceptiveness, intellect, deep thinking and strategy. Also darkness and concealment. They work very well as spies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T22:47:46-07:00","id":223888,"title":"","content":"I realize this was a few pages back, but eh, I'll chime in anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=222844#post222844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because by definition, creating a rule saying <i>X</i> cannot be done in <i>Y</i> form removes as many options as it adds. It gives the option of using <i>X</i> without <i>Y</i>; but it removes the option of using <i>X</i> with <i>Y</i>. There is no net gain in options. And from the individual character's perspective, his functionality has decreased. Previously he could do two things at once; now he can only do one at a time. That's nothing but a decrease to his flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a different way to look at it than that. I mean, yes, entering form <i>Y</i> can prevent the use of <i>X</i>, but it's also kinda objectively true of just about any kind of shapeshifting into distinct forms. It's also an incomplete statement. One also generally chooses to enter form <i>Y</i> in order to improve (or quite often <i>allow</i>) the use of <i>Z</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, say a Lunar turns into his spirit shape, a snake. There are some clear disadvantages, there, the lack of limbs topping the list. But that's also not quite the point. If the Lunar's changing into it, he likely has a purpose in mind for which a snake would be well-suited, such as employing its sense of smell, slithering through smaller spaces than his human form could manage, employing a venomous bite, and possibly keeping someone constricted. The form has its pluses and its minuses, so it's the Lunar's job to apply it when its pluses are of greatest use and he's decided its minuses are outweighed by the benefits or he'll be changing to a different shape such that they're non-issues. To one degree or another, this is true of all forms. Picking the right form for the right job is honestly what's struck me as a lot of the fun of such a shapeshifter. If that playstyle is part of the design goal, I fully approve of decisions that better enable the fun in it.<br /> <br /> So, looking at DBT as another form, it stands to reason it, too, would have some minuses to go with its pluses. In EX3, one of those minuses is going to be a lack of Evocation access. It might also help to consider that it may be getting more than just a new minus. Personally, I have a hunch DBT is going to be even more powerful than it's been before. Aquillion had a very good point about one way that might be: in a land without common persistent dice-adders, the physical* Attribute-enhanced DBT-user is all the mightier. But it might extend beyond that. If Evocations are the big deal that they're meant to be and DBT is meant to be balanced against the lack of them, perhaps it could go even further than buffing up Attributes? I could see Charm trees building off of it,** developing powerful effects usable only while in DBT based off the unique synergy of human and beast it allows, much as Evocation arrays draw on the relationship of a wielder and her Artifact.<br /> <br /> From that perspective, a Lunar wouldn't be able to use Evocations while shifted into DBT, but would have access to something that might be seen as analogous, while still being able to shift back to human form if circumstances change and an Artifact's Evocations are needed. In this way, a Lunar swordsmaster with Evocations unlocked in a daiklave and great proficiency in DBT would be much like a Solar swordsmaster with Evocations unlocked in two daiklaves: neither can use both at once, but can gain clear benefits from being able to switch from one to the other as circumstances demand. It'd also be reasonable that such a hypothetical DBT-rooted Charm tree might be able to go places that Evocations wouldn't.<br /> <br /> * Sidebar: I wonder if it will still be restricted to Strength, Dexterity and Stamina next time. Perhaps it might be &quot;pick whichever 3 (or whatever) to boost and justify how;&quot; e.g. reaction time may quicken (Wits), as senses heighten (Perception) and the Lunar becomes all the more visually striking (Appearance). Even if the form is generally meant for combat, if there are numerous capabilities across the Lunar Charmset that would be great for battle and would benefit from heightened Attributes, I could see something like this working out. Eh, just musing.<br /> <br /> ** Fair warning: anyone who says something like, &quot;It's a Knack&quot; will make me laugh at them. We don't know if Knacks will even be a thing in EX3, much less if DBT will be among their number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T02:57:11-07:00","id":223987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223661#post223661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Moons have been described as shamans rather than sorcerers. No Moons suffered from an association with sorcery like none other</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're making a point about the problem of tying them excessively to the use of Sorcery, but I still want to make a point out of my hope that this Edition won't get excessively hung up on providing major delineations between different titles for broadly similar social roles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T07:51:52-07:00","id":224101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223742#post223742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never yet asked a player to leave a game, for that or any reason.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, when you ask a player something during chargen, you're not saying, &quot;Answer the way I like or you're out of the game.&quot; The worst that would happen in the case of mammoth Lunar player, if he had no explanation of why his character had Dexterity 5 and Strength 3 other than &quot;god stat&quot;, is that I might ask him to choose a different totem animal, one that actually had a high Dexterity score and would therefore seem more appropriate for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mammoths would have a size variance in the species. That character could be a skinny, relatively lithe mammoth that's clever about using the old snoot proboscis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason is because the whole point of the s<i>pirit shape</i> is that it's the animal that best reflects your nature. It's the animal you. It's not some other thing you change into. It's your true form. Is nature is your nature, its instincts are your instincts. You can't separate them. And just as your spirit shape is an animal repreesentation of you, so you, in human form, are a human representation of your spirit shape, because the nature of both is the same. </div> </div> </div>The spirit shape comes to a Lunar due to some symbolic reason. Hence why so many of the entries don't just mention the animal, either in the anima banner entry or the spirit shape entry. Tamuz isn't just a gazelle hound - he's a sleek, fit gazelle hound. Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't just a wolf, he's an oversized wolf with goat features. Anja Silverclaws has an anima banner that forms a housecat out of shadows. What the totem represents varies from character to character, as you can see with Ma-Ha-Suchi's oversized brute compared to Red Jaws's shadowy, skulking lupine manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems the consensus on this thread is that your totem animal only reflects your nature as far as your personality is concerned - but I've never read it that way, because you can't really separate, say, the instincts of a fox, with the Dexterity and Perception a fox relies on to hunt. Physical and social attributes are a large part of an animal's nature, and if your spirit shape reflects your nature then it should reflect your attributes too. </div> </div> </div>And again, those animals will vary. There are larger and smaller examples of an animal within the same species. There are beasts of the same type that nonetheless differ from each other in a wide variety of other ways, too - coloration, dietary preference, dietary requirements, etc. Those can serve as markers of the totem, not just one ideal view of the species.,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in my experience, it's always more enjoyable in a Lunar game the more in common you have with your spirit shape, because you get to play on that in a variety of ways. If the fox Lunar is the one who, even in human form, has the best hearing, the one who always notices a trap, the one with the quickest reflexes, well, it makes you feel like you're actually playing a fox Lunar, someone whose spirit shape actually fits. And it makes the character feel more like it actually works, and the game experience is more enjoyable. Or at least that's how it's always been for me. </div> </div> </div>Superlatives are risky business for Lunars, recall. That's why personal symbolism plays a factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-10-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:46:25-07:00","id":224166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223742#post223742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Moons are my favorite caste to play but I've only played one sorcerer ever, and he was a dragon king. For me, the major flavor of the caste is just... perceptiveness, intellect, deep thinking and strategy. Also darkness and concealment. They work very well as spies.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224101#post224101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait... you played a character with a spirit shape that wasn't an animal? And you're lecturing about how the book requires certain qualities of the spirit shape? You didn't even choose one that was selectable by the book for that character. Dragon Kings are mergings of spirit and flesh that are most emphatically not a mortal beast, and the only Knacks that widen the choice of spirit shape are Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form. You dragged us all the way out into houserules country.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I disagree with TSk on many things, too, but come on. It seems really obvious he's saying, &quot;I haven't played any Lunar who was a Sorcerer. The only Sorcerer I have played was an actual Dragon King.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:47:20-07:00","id":224167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224166#post224166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dude, I disagree with TSk on many things, too, but come on. It seems really obvious he's saying, &quot;I haven't played any Lunar who was a Sorcerer. The only Sorcerer I have played was an actual Dragon King.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Edited accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:50:21-07:00","id":224170,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Also, I think my tone may have come off as harsh or accusatory about your motives, so sorry about that if it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T08:50:58-07:00","id":224171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224101#post224101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait... you played a character with a spirit shape that wasn't an animal? And you're lecturing about how the book requires certain qualities of the spirit shape? You didn't even choose one that was selectable by the book for that character. Dragon Kings are mergings of spirit and flesh that are most emphatically not a mortal beast, and the only Knacks that widen the choice of spirit shape are Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form. You dragged us all the way out into houserules country.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMG, no. I said that I'd only played one actual sorcerer ever, and that he was a dragon king. Read that again, please. One sorcerer, who was a dragon king. Not a Lunar Exalt with &quot;dragon king&quot; as a spirit shape. The character I refer to was a Pterok dragon king who happened to be a sorcerer and had no dealings whatsoever with Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T10:58:27-07:00","id":224304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223616#post223616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Power of Fire can still have a soul bound connection to a flute that causes flourishing business enterprise when played.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no I'm still unsatisfied with this, successful business still feels to much like it references symbolic connotations of fire.<br /> <br /> More like being the Sovereign of Fire and having a nautilus shell that, when sounded, summons octopuses from bodies of water (including the film of tears over an eyeball), with &quot;octopus&quot; being a category that also includes mythic krakens, octopus spirits, concepts and ideas of octopuses, and things that are octopuses metaphorically, such as far-reaching and grasping criminal organisations.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I wonder if spirit shape should be a bit like Caste, something only properly determined after you're already Exalted for a while. Might also include a bit of the old Casteless problems with chimerism; on top of ones who tried to change their totem, there are ones who took too long to settle it (or just weren't really suitable to a single one) and so got a bit stuck between.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm a little bit cold towards the idea of Lunar spirit shapes being informed by romantic or literary conceptions of animals, partially because I think it's a bit overdone, partially because I feel that Lunars are a bit more suited to being more unvarnished about beasts, partially because I think it limits the range of imagined totems a bit (there are some animals one might just be hard pressed to find symbolic meaning for). I'm guided in somewhat by Lea's idea that it would be better if Ma-Ha-Suchi had originally been a goat totem.<br /> <br /> Also might help focus a bit more on what Lunars are; an owl as a spirit shape doesn't indicate wisdom, it's silent death on wings. The association with the No Moon Caste is because of the acute senses of sight and hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:07:34-07:00","id":224311,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's kinda weird to think of a character and puzzle out, &quot;Now, how is his soul like an ocelot?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:11:35-07:00","id":224316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224304#post224304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also might help focus a bit more on what Lunars are; an owl as a spirit shape doesn't indicate wisdom, it's silent death on wings. The association with the No Moon Caste is because of the acute senses of sight and hearing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait. You're saying the owl's acute senses (Perception) make it suitable for a high-Perception No Moon.<br /> <br /> Are you actually agreeing with me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:34:16-07:00","id":224323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224304#post224304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'm a little bit cold towards the idea of Lunar spirit shapes being informed by romantic or literary conceptions of animals, partially because I think it's a bit overdone, partially because I feel that Lunars are a bit more suited to being more unvarnished about beasts, partially because I think it limits the range of imagined totems a bit (there are some animals one might just be hard pressed to find symbolic meaning for). I'm guided in somewhat by Lea's idea that it would be better if Ma-Ha-Suchi had originally been a goat totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idealised and grounded interpretations of beasts are equally valid, and the game has no business favouring one over the other \u2013 that's for individual players to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:55:18-07:00","id":224334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224311#post224311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's kinda weird to think of a character and puzzle out, &quot;Now, how is his soul like an ocelot?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars aren't the only Exalted with totemic anima displays. Even the ones that don't directly show animals could still provide the basis for a spirit shape, if the character were a Lunar. It sort of helps that Arianna's anima banner is very similar to Lilith's own totemic display (both gain a cape-like pair of feathered wings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:09:46-07:00","id":224342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224311#post224311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's kinda weird to think of a character and puzzle out, &quot;Now, how is his soul like an ocelot?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the soul of a hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:16:59-07:00","id":224352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223888#post223888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyone who says something like, &quot;It's a Knack&quot; will make me laugh at them. We don't know if Knacks will even be a thing in EX3, much less if DBT will be among their number.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt there will be Knacks. The whole concept of the &quot;Knack&quot; arose out of (1) the belief that Eclipse Charmshare should allow an Eclipse to acquire any and all things-called-Charms possessed by any supernatural creature in the game; (2) Lunar-style shapeshifting and Charm effects like DBT are completely out of theme for Solars, even through Charmshare, and should be completely impossible for Eclipses to learn with Charmshare. The result was creating a new non-Charm term of art for the category of effects, since not calling them Charms locks them out of being acquired with Charmshare. It was a distinction created as a workaround for a specific problem, instead of just addressing the problem itself.<br /> <br /> 2 is as true as it ever was, but 1 is no longer a problem, since 3e Eclipse Charmshare does not allow Eclipses to learn the Charms of other Exalt types, &quot;only&quot; specific kinds of spirit Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:22:23-07:00","id":224357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224352#post224352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt there will be Knacks. The whole concept of the &quot;Knack&quot; arose out of (1) the belief that Eclipse Charmshare should allow an Eclipse to acquire any and all things-called-Charms possessed by any supernatural creature in the game; (2) Lunar-style shapeshifting and Charm effects like DBT are completely out of theme for Solars, even through Charmshare, and should be completely impossible for Eclipses to learn with Charmshare. The result was creating a new non-Charm term of art for the category of effects, since not calling them Charms locks them out of being acquired with Charmshare<br /> <br /> 2 is as true as it ever was, but 1 is no longer a problem, since 3e Eclipse Charmshare does not allow Eclipses to learn the Charms of other Exalt types, &quot;only&quot; specific kinds of spirit Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yes and no. Knacks were basically charms that did stuff to shapeshifting, and were separated for two reasons: Keep Eclipse dirty hands off of them, and different xp rates. The first reason is fixed. Eclipse can keep their grubby little fingerprints away from it without needing a rule saying they can't have it. however, the different xp cost might still be a thing. It might be a useful shorthand to assign these types of Charms a keyword of some sort to differentiate them from other Charms as well. Knack is probably not a good one, because it wasn't a keyword, but some sort of keyword might help.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I don't know what keywords will be doing in 3, or even if they exist. I also don't think the developers can say with confidence what they will do in 3, because Lunars are a long ways away. Maybe they will rebalance the Shapeshifting knacks to be more closely in line with Charms. Maybe these charms will simply get a keyword that reduces the cost to buy them. I do expect them to be put aside a little bit at least, even if it is only into their own trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:30:25-07:00","id":224368,"title":"","content":"They were Charms in 1e, right?<br /> <br /> Really I think normalization of Charm costs across the board will go a long way, and yes I agree that &quot;be able to hunt and turn into smaller/larger things than normal&quot; is probably more of a 4 XP power than an 8 XP power. Then again, I'd say DBT is definitely worth 8 XP, as is &quot;have sex with target instead of eating their heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Solar XP is still a thing, maybe let that pay for &quot;Knacks&quot; along with Sorcery, Evocations, etc...since everyone wants their &quot;normal&quot; XP for Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:34:21-07:00","id":224374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224368#post224368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were Charms in 1e, right?<br /> <br /> Really I think normalization of Charm costs across the board will go a long way, and yes I agree that &quot;be able to hunt and turn into smaller/larger things than normal&quot; is probably more of a 4 XP power than an 8 XP power. Then again, I'd say DBT is definitely worth 8 XP, as is &quot;have sex with target instead of eating their heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Solar XP is still a thing, maybe let that pay for &quot;Knacks&quot; along with Sorcery, Evocations, etc...since everyone wants their &quot;normal&quot; XP for Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though they were quite poorly organized and often had... strange requirements. Prey's Skin Disguise required Humble Mouse Shape, Towering Beast Form, and Many-Faced Moon Transformation (that edition's weaker version of Twin-Faced Hero) and Essence 3, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:36:58-07:00","id":224376,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Lunar prereqs have always been a shit-show. I'm sure I could find my 1e book and see that's the case; it's certainly the case in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:03:27-07:00","id":224390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224323#post224323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idealised and grounded interpretations of beasts are equally valid, and the game has no business favouring one over the other \u2013 that's for individual players to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh almost definitely. Probably actually better that it should do so.<br /> <br /> It's still just a bit how I feel about animal stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Still, there are probably other places where it can be disregarded; Animal Avatars, for instance, or the intelligent animals of Halta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:17:29-07:00","id":224402,"title":"","content":"The things you call Knacks, if they should be required at all, probably fit better under the Merits system, for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:19:03-07:00","id":224404,"title":"","content":"1e Lunars: in which you need Charisma 2 to have a totem shape, and Wits Charms lead to Stamina Charms lead to Manipulation Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:39:46-07:00","id":224420,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XeFxdkaFzRA\" target=\"_blank\">Now, we will hear true facts about the owl.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:44:16-07:00","id":224421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224402#post224402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things you call Knacks, if they should be required at all, probably fit better under the Merits system, for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Maybe the &quot;here's a bigger range of sizes you can turn into&quot; but some of the other stuff seems like solid Charm territory. Maybe combine some of the weaker effects into the same Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:48:50-07:00","id":224428,"title":"","content":"Is it strictly necessary to make the range of things you can turn into dependent on a Charm or Knack or Merit or whatever?<br /> <br /> Just for the sake of argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:51:18-07:00","id":224435,"title":"","content":"There can exist supernatural Merits; they've been around about as long as White Wolf has. <br /> <br /> Even excepting the ones that only expand the range of sizes or have no cost (I get the feeling that's more of the Knacks than not), only counting the ones with activations or costing motes, well\u2026 yeah, I'm fine with Deadly Beastman Transformation, Twin-Faced Hero, et cetera., being Charms. Hence why I said &quot;for the most part.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224428#post224428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it strictly necessary to make the range of things you can turn into dependent on a Charm or Knack or Merit or whatever?<br /> <br /> Just for the sake of argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I addressed <i>that</i>, too, y'know. The whole bit about <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026if they should be required at all\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-10-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:08:16-07:00","id":224462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224311#post224311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's kinda weird to think of a character and puzzle out, &quot;Now, how is his soul like an ocelot?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>He is uncannily good with prayer pieces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:04:28-07:00","id":224643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224304#post224304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also might help focus a bit more on what Lunars are; an owl as a spirit shape doesn't indicate wisdom, it's silent death on wings. The association with the No Moon Caste is because of the acute senses of sight and hearing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224316#post224316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait. You're saying the owl's acute senses (Perception) make it suitable for a high-Perception No Moon.<br /> <br /> Are you actually agreeing with me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually like an answer to this. How is what you just said different from what I said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-10-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:48:20-07:00","id":224673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223661#post223661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Moons have been described as shamans rather than sorcerers. No Moons suffered from an association with sorcery like none other, given that their anima was useless for anything else until 2e's Lunar manual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also an association with gods, spirits and priesthood, because the magical caste should obviously be the one dealing with gods, yeah?<br /> <br /> Never mind that gods are people, so dealing with them is a social action. Prayer? (Charisma + Performance). Persuasion, Bargaining, Intimidating? Social actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:58:36-07:00","id":224699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224357#post224357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes and no. Knacks were basically charms that did stuff to shapeshifting, and were separated for... different xp rates.<br /> <br /> ...the different xp cost might still be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also a way to break outside of the new insistence that Lunar Charm trees avoid crossing between Attributes, like they did wildly in First Edition.<br /> <br /> So long as Knacks had minimum Attribute requirements, being different from Lunar Charms excused a tree whereby a Strength Knack led into a Stamina Knack and then into an Intelligence Knack, as a theoretical example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T18:24:49-07:00","id":224718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224673#post224673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also an association with gods, spirits and priesthood, because the magical caste should obviously be the one dealing with gods, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for serious. They know what they're looking at and talking to, which for many spirits, is going to net you an awful lot of information about what buttons they have to push.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Never mind that gods are people, so dealing with them is a social action. Prayer? (Charisma + Performance). Persuasion, Bargaining, Intimidating? Social actions. </div> </div> </div>And much easier to engage in if you happen to know what bribes to use, or what constitutes a particularly effective threat to one. Hence, No Moons.<br /> <br /> But maybe we're going about this the wrong way, and the &quot;Warrior, Trickster, Shaman&quot; applies to all three Castes in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T18:29:12-07:00","id":224727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224402#post224402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things you call Knacks, if they should be required at all, probably fit better under the Merits system, for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure I agree with this. If my character concept is a master shapeshifter, and I want quick change charms, and more form acquisition charms, I'm not sure I want to be restricted in that way. Unless Merits can be purchased in game easily. Which I think they can be, in some cases. Which would mean I agree with you in many ways. Guess I figured it out by talking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T18:41:28-07:00","id":224741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224643#post224643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually like an answer to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is what you just said different from what I said?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I actually didn't think there was any difference at all, but now that I've looked back at what you said, it looks to me like you're still pushing at the idea that one has an owl totem because they already have high-Perception or whatever.<br /> <br /> That wasn't what I was getting at with the idea of owls being associated with the No Moon Caste, not least of which is that you'll have the spirit shape for a while before you're part of the Caste. I was actually just pointing at attributes of the actual owl that resonate with the Caste in a manner other than wisdom symbolism.<br /> <br /> You have gotten me onto an interesting line of thought, though... how much of a push between human form and beast form informs the nature of how your Caste is selected. Is it fitting that a person should be part of the No Moon Caste when they <i>only</i> survive, endure and dominate by their insight and mental speed when in their animal shape? Hmm, that gives me ideas about reconciling certain combinations of Caste and totem with the idea of a Lunar who, in their human form, opts to fight with means somewhat other than their powers (while their general attitude in how to fight and the desire to fight is still broadly informed by Caste and totem).<br /> <br /> I'd totally make a No Moon who is almost blind in human form and has extremely sharp senses as an owl. A kind of slightly modified Granny Weatherwax.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes the idea of a spirit shape selected according to terms of redressing your shortcomings in a human shape, of providing avenues to an idealized self, or of being a form suitable to surviving the event of one's Exaltation...<br /> <br /> A Northerner who was unusually thinly built by the standards of people in that clime, survives to early adulthood by uncommon leniency in their family, only for some disaster to strike in which the fierce determination to survive evokes the mighty and hardy body of a mammoth that is suited to the environment in every way that their human body was not, and so switches back and forth as needs and preference suits.<br /> <br /> Because the spirit shape is supposed to be a true form, is it not? Lunars are supposed to be versatile, yes? To confine the relationship to a direct symmetry would seem to go against the spirit of that, I think.<br /> <br /> And it can go the other way, as well; where the qualities you display in human shape define your Caste more than your totem does. This one is a mammoth because they needed to be to survive this blizzard, and all the blizzards (literal and figurative) to come, but they still survive by guile and beauty projected by their true human form, so they're a Changing Moon. After all, if Caste comes after Exaltation, why should it be limited by the symbolic connotations of the spirit shape?<br /> <br /> God, thank you; I'd been struggling to think of something that could fit the idea of a slight framed, physically weak person having a mammoth for a spirit shape that would amount to more than irony for its own sake, and this query led me straight into it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T19:03:01-07:00","id":224759,"title":"","content":"Mental note: devise Lunar character with dolphin spirit shape based on backstory in which they Exalted in the course of failing to save a loved one from drowning. Figure out all possible symbolic connotations or personality stereotypes for dolphins (except the desire to prevent people from drowning, I suppose...) and try to give them little to no presence in the character (although, that spirit shape is still useful and resonant even if they never really try to save anybody from drowning again...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T19:27:44-07:00","id":224773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224304#post224304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'm a little bit cold towards the idea of Lunar spirit shapes being informed by romantic or literary conceptions of animals, partially because I think it's a bit overdone, partially because I feel that Lunars are a bit more suited to being more unvarnished about beasts, partially because I think it limits the range of imagined totems a bit (there are some animals one might just be hard pressed to find symbolic meaning for). I'm guided in somewhat by Lea's idea that it would be better if Ma-Ha-Suchi had originally been a goat totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a conception of Lunars that makes them unsuitable for being werewolves is a good conception. Lunars don't <i>need</i> to be werewolves, but they should absolutely be the place you go to for a werewolf. And werewolves are all the way &quot;romantic or literary conceptions of animals&quot;. So I have to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T19:53:53-07:00","id":224780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224759#post224759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental note: devise Lunar character with dolphin spirit shape based on backstory in which they Exalted in the course of failing to save a loved one from drowning. Figure out all possible symbolic connotations or personality stereotypes for dolphins (except the desire to prevent people from drowning, I suppose...) and try to give them little to no presence in the character (although, that spirit shape is still useful and resonant even if they never really try to save anybody from drowning again...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Dolphins are actually horrible, horrible animals, so you have a lot more options than you might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:13:47-07:00","id":224786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224311#post224311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's kinda weird to think of a character and puzzle out, &quot;Now, how is his soul like an ocelot?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's titillated by oscillating his titalot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:55:21-07:00","id":224808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224741#post224741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd been struggling to think of something that could fit the idea of a slight framed, physically weak person having a mammoth for a spirit shape that would amount to more than irony for its own sake</div> </div> </div> </div>At least you're honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224741#post224741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes the idea of a spirit shape selected according to terms of redressing your shortcomings in a human shape, of providing avenues to an idealized self, or of being a form suitable to surviving the event of one's Exaltation...<br /> <br /> A Northerner who was unusually thinly built by the standards of people in that clime, survives to early adulthood by uncommon leniency in their family, only for some disaster to strike in which the fierce determination to survive evokes the mighty and hardy body of a mammoth that is suited to the environment in every way that their human body was not, and so switches back and forth as needs and preference suits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if that's what seems interesting to you, great. But I've really never heard of it being interpreted that way before. The spirit shape is the shape that represents your true nature. It's not the shape that represents something you <i>need</i> to be but <i>aren't;</i> it's the shape that represents what you <i>are.</i><br /> <br /> I mean, if you want to play that kind of scenario, with a Lunar whose spirit shape represents nothing more than whatever shape was needed to survive the event of his exaltation - say you needed to run really fast just then, so you have a cheetah or something for a spirit shape even though your reflexes are shit and you have no hunting instincts, etc. - I wish you the best of luck. But I think if you do that, you're really just denying yourself a lot of the fun of playing a Lunar. Because then, your spirit shape means nothing to you. It's not your true self. It's just another shape. It might as well just be a shape in your Heart's Blood library for all the significance and meaning it has for you. When you assume your spirit shape, you're not even assuming the shape of your spirit at all. What's the point of even having a spirit shape, then?<br /> <br /> Compare that with the Lunar whose spirit shape is a cheetah because he is, in his heart, in his soul, a hunter. A hunter of lawless men, a hitman, a brilliant investigator who hunts the guilty among the innocent and the truth among lies, whatever. Someone who lives for the chase and will not be put off the scent. Someone who only feels alive when closing on his quarry; a taste of blood on the wind, the closer he gets the sharper his instincts and the more active and focused his mind. Someone for whom life is just one chase after another. Whatever shape he takes, the shape of his spirit remains constant, the pure, refined essence of what he is.<br /> <br /> What exactly do you gain by throwing that away and saying you have a cheetah for a spirit shape because just before you exalted you were being chased by a claw strider and had to run really fast to get away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-11-2014, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:09:26-07:00","id":224814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224808#post224808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit shape is the shape that represents your true nature. It's not the shape that represents something you <i>need</i> to be, but <i>aren't;</i> it's the shape that represents what you <i>are.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems (at least potentially) problematic to me to tell a player (particularly a completely new player) something like &quot;think long and hard about what your character <i>is</i> on a very deep personal and emotional level, despite never having played a single IC scene with them, and from that meditation pick a spirit shape that's never going to change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me, I prefer &quot;pick a shape you think is cool for the character that you want to play, and see how that shape comes to define you and your personality over the course of the stories we tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> I view your way as front-loading a lot of deep character development that is hard to contextualize in the pregame vacuum, versus the player just picking what they want and seeing where it takes them. And I like the idea that even an underfed street girl (who might have shitty Physical stats pre-Exaltation, not that that really matters unless you start the game with a mortal build) still has the stubbornness of a rhinoceros and that that manifests as her spirit shape. That's the moment when the inner power flows forth, possibly even surprising that person with the animal form that represents them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:23:25-07:00","id":224838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224814#post224814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view your way as front-loading a lot of deep character development that is hard to contextualize in the pregame vacuum, versus the player just picking what they want and seeing where it takes them. And I like the idea that even an underfed street girl (who might have shitty Physical stats pre-Exaltation, not that that really matters unless you start the game with a mortal build) still has the stubbornness of a rhinoceros and that that manifests as her spirit shape. That's the moment when the inner power flows forth, possibly even surprising that person with the animal form that represents them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That is a fine idea. Because in that sense, the shape meaningfully reflects her nature. Maybe not in a physical sense but it's still a reflection of her in some way. And you might express her stubborness as high Willpower and Stamina (a small girl can still be impossible to dissuade and hard to knock down).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224814#post224814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems (at least potentially) problematic to me to tell a player (particularly a completely new player) something like &quot;think long and hard about what your character <i>is</i> on a very deep personal and emotional level, despite never having played a single IC scene with them, and from that meditation pick a spirit shape that's never going to change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me, I prefer &quot;pick a shape you think is cool for the character that you want to play, and see how that shape comes to define you and your personality over the course of the stories we tell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again yes, you're right there. Often you don't really know what the character is like until you've played him or her for a while. And it's usual in my group for people to change their character sheets a lot (including totems for Lunars) over the first several sessions as they figure the characters out better. Doesn't mean you shouldn't try to figure them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:45:34-07:00","id":224849,"title":"","content":"The main reason to put Charm-based barriers on the forms a Lunar can assume, is to help mitigate how frontloaded Lunars are. The Lunar Charmset having to be balanced against how much power and flexibility Lunars get for no XP investment means that even an ideal Lunar charmset has to look somewhat lackluster relative to other Celestials who don't get such an advantage. There are multiple ways to handle this, for instance sticking an XP cost on properly internalizing a shape gained by the hunt to make it usable, but a less restrictive method is just to gate off certain categories of form behind a Charm purchase. This hinders shapeshifting, but in return means that everything else about Lunars can be made stronger than would be allowable if unregulated shapeshifting was allowed at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T22:08:40-07:00","id":224859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224814#post224814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems (at least potentially) problematic to me to tell a player (particularly a completely new player) something like &quot;think long and hard about what your character <i>is</i> on a very deep personal and emotional level, despite never having played a single IC scene with them, and from that meditation pick a spirit shape that's never going to change.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me, I prefer &quot;pick a shape you think is cool for the character that you want to play, and see how that shape comes to define you and your personality over the course of the stories we tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> I view your way as front-loading a lot of deep character development that is hard to contextualize in the pregame vacuum, versus the player just picking what they want and seeing where it takes them. And I like the idea that even an underfed street girl (who might have shitty Physical stats pre-Exaltation, not that that really matters unless you start the game with a mortal build) still has the stubbornness of a rhinoceros and that that manifests as her spirit shape. That's the moment when the inner power flows forth, possibly even surprising that person with the animal form that represents them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... This line of thought pointed me in a direction I hadn't considered before. Wild alternative interpretation/vague speculation, away!<br /> <br /> With the gods going back to being more important to the choosing of their Chosen, I wonder if it's possible that <i>Luna</i> might have a hand in defining a spirit shape. Luna's rather perceptive, after all, and the gods have some strong understanding of the natures of their Chosen. She could reasonably pick one that strongly reflects the character as he is. She could also pick one that suits what she expects he will become after taking the Second Breath. Or even what he could potentially be and what she hopes to encourage -- said potential may be a big part of what stirred her heart and turned her head in the first place.* Hell, perhaps sometimes she picks something that seems right out of left field because she knows that, if something <i>should</i> be meaningful and <i>feels</i> meaningful to its recipient,** the recipient -- and others -- are going to try to come up with reasons <i>why</i> it is meaningful; whatever reason or reasons they reach will usually be persuasive, and she's very curious to see what they draw from it, how they see it defining themselves, and how they themselves define it. For similar reasons, she may also pick something deliberately against the grain of the sort of thing one would expect a character to receive, or one that otherwise carries with it some interesting lesson, to see how this person who has drawn her interest responds to the apparent incongruity.***<br /> <br /> Eh, again, mostly musing, here. It wouldn't need to happen for every Lunar Exalt -- I like the idea of not even Luna necessarily knowing what spirit shape one of her Chosen may posses until, well, her Chosen possesses it. Even if entirely untrue, I definitely think it's something that some Lunars might believe or speculate about.<br /> <br /> * For the purposes of this speculation, I'm not assuming the standard &quot;Lunars Exalt for surviving&quot; is as very definitely true as it was in 2e. Or even if it is, who Luna's likely to pick from among the survivors.<br /> <br /> ** I get the impression Lunars are as comfortable in their human forms as they are in their spirit shapes, feeling a continuity and significance that they really don't have in other forms (outside DBT). It doesn't have a mechanical impact in their skill with any shape (oh, aside a mote discount for assuming a true form?), but I still like the notion.<br /> <br /> *** And lo, did Terezin, blonde-maned king of Eresteba (better known as the Lion Province), widely spoken of for his courage and for his great leadership of all men and beasts, drew his Second Breath as a Chosen of Luna. With the spirit shape of a humble donkey. Perhaps he continues with it with as much courage and pride as before, such that even the beast of burden in time becomes symbolic of kingship and nobility. Perhaps it turns his thoughts and efforts more to the laborers and downtrodden of his lands, and becomes beloved by them for his compassion. Perhaps he feels humbled by this form, and becomes a less bold, but a considerably more thoughtful ruler. Perhaps Luna expected one of these, all of these, or none of these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T01:58:32-07:00","id":224938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dolphins are actually horrible, horrible animals</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, there are substantiated reports of bottlenose dolphins intervening for the purpose of saving human lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't think a conception of Lunars that makes them unsuitable for being werewolves is a good conception. Lunars don't </span></span></span><i>need</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to be werewolves, but they should absolutely be the place you go to for a werewolf. And werewolves are all the way &quot;romantic or literary conceptions of animals&quot;.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolf&quot; is about as broad a category as vampire, but I'd assume you mean in terms of the specific things in the mould of the Garou and such.<br /> <br /> Still, looking at some of the developer statements about what Lunars are like, I'd have to wonder; is a wolf-totem Lunar savage in the human form because of how they're influenced by the wolf, or savage in the wolf form because of how they're influenced by the human, with the actual selection of the spirit shape having been predicated on other factors?<br /> <br /> Owls may not actually be wise, and a Lunar might have the totem for factors that resonate more with literal owls, but a lot of Lunars are likely to be wise (for given values of the term) and might act in ways while in their other form that generate and perpetuate the stereotype.<br /> <br /> Yeees, it does feel fitting to me that there are times in which the animal form of a Lunar is distinguished and uncanny because it's acting a bit like a human; the totem snared in by resonance with literal qualities of the beast, but thereafter not limited to them because there is still a human inside, and the result feels rather strange.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-11-2014, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T03:28:38-07:00","id":224963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224808#post224808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit shape is the shape that represents your true nature. It's not the shape that represents something you <i>need</i> to be but <i>aren't;</i> it's the shape that represents what you <i>are.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing so much of a distinction between those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you want to play that kind of scenario, with a Lunar whose spirit shape represents nothing more than whatever shape was needed to survive the event of his exaltation - say you needed to run really fast just then, so you have a cheetah or something for a spirit shape even though your reflexes are shit and you have no hunting instincts, etc. - I wish you the best of luck. But I think if you do that, you're really just denying yourself a lot of the fun of playing a Lunar. Because then, your spirit shape means nothing to you. It's not your true self. It's just another shape. It might as well just be a shape in your Heart's Blood library for all the significance and meaning it has for you. When you assume your spirit shape, you're not even assuming the shape of your spirit at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if one assumes that the circumstances of Exaltation aren't a deeply defining event. Even a transformative one; the moment in which one Exalts might make one an entirely different person to what they were before, which also seems like it would muddy up an exacting need to define the spirit shape according to &quot;who you are&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare that with the Lunar whose spirit shape is a cheetah because he is, in his heart, in his soul, a hunter. A hunter of lawless men, a hitman, a brilliant investigator who hunts the guilty among the innocent and the truth among lies, whatever. Someone who lives for the chase and will not be put off the scent. Someone who only feels alive when closing on his quarry; a taste of blood on the wind, the closer he gets the sharper his instincts and the more active and focused his mind. Someone for whom life is just one chase after another. Whatever shape he takes, the shape of his spirit remains constant, the pure, refined essence of what he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's great as well, still having the capacity to have somebody whose cheetah like traits are non-obvious until they become capable of actually turning into a cheetah, <i>and</i> the person who always seemed like cheetah would be a suitable metaphor to them until it becomes literal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you gain by throwing that away and saying you have a cheetah for a spirit shape because just before you exalted you were being chased by a claw strider and had to run really fast to get away?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, more diverse options for one.<br /> <br /> Noho that's terrible, I'll come up with something more specific.<br /> <br /> At the heart of it, I'm just plain attached to the idea of things that don't really line up with the straightforward assumption or interpretation, with characteristics that don't seem like they should be married together but are, with that sometimes making sense when you look closer and see the connective tissue, but sometimes they're just distinct characteristics, because people are diverse, and don't readily adhere to literary themes.<br /> <br /> It's like the thing Lea once said about Castes, about adhering to archetype but not stereotype; I do so love to try and conceive <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">how far one can stretch the possibilities of Castes, to the point of making Solars who don't have a single dot in their Caste Abilities. This might be influenced a bit by how Lunar Castes seem to provide me with a lot less room for that.<br /> <br /> And I might be a bit biased by how much I've been absorbing Jenna Moran's games lately. Exalted is certainly not Nobilis, and especially not Chuubo's, but I think there can still be some useful lessons to draw from those, from the range of Anchors and Powers who aren't the stereotypes of their Estates and spells to turn somebody into a frog that have some fairly broad possible interpretations of &quot;frog&quot; depending on context or mood; in short, of things in which you have one theme, but multiple possible variations on it. It already works well for Caste, I don't see why it shouldn't have the same for &quot;Lunars have a totem animal they can turn into&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides, Lunars of all people seem as though they should have some decent inroads into not adhering strictly to obvious interpretations; people want Lunars to reference versatility, and they're often drawn from the uncanny, the outsider, the iconoclast, that seems like it should at least have people who subvert expectations every once in a while.<br /> <br /> So in that example, you might have somebody who only really knew who they were in their instinctual response to that crisis. Or somebody who was fiercely desperate to survive pushing through the limits of what they were into the possibilities of what they need to be; sure that's a principle that can apply to any shape, but the spirit shape has a special place as the <i>first</i> one where that feeling came through, the revelation of that inadequacy and, more importantly, achieving the power to overcome it, and it sets the tenor for all of the future challenges to be overcome. Or it could be that being chased down by claw striders is a common and noteworthy danger of the locality, and to be somebody who is defined by having transformed for the sake of surviving it makes one noteworthy and powerful within their region. Or it might be that, in a literal or broadly figurative sense, the inability to run away from things has been a bane of the person's life, and in this instance where it was a life or death thing that would probably end in death, the resulting surge of emotion and determination pushes them into making it through the event, and thereafter to overcoming every other thing that used to be beyond reach.<br /> <br /> Heh, all of my talk of subverting stereotypes, and yet I still keep fixating on &quot;if it's an event where you're fleeing from something and not chasing something, you should turn into a gazelle&quot;.<br /> <br /> .... Dear God I'm focusing a huge amount on framing the spirit shape in terms of the idea that you transform into it during the Exaltation, aren't I?<br /> <br /> Obviously the concept requires a bit of refinement...<br /> <br /> Hmmm, the dolphin one still seems to have the idea where totem is defined by deficiency despite the idea that the person necessarily did not turn into a dolphin in the course of the event.<br /> <br /> Still, at least it's got me thinking.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T07:13:09-07:00","id":225050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224859#post224859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the gods going back to being more important to the choosing of their Chosen, I wonder if it's possible that <i>Luna</i> might have a hand in defining a spirit shape. Luna's rather perceptive, after all, and the gods have some strong understanding of the natures of their Chosen. She could reasonably pick one that strongly reflects the character as he is. She could also pick one that suits what she expects he will become after taking the Second Breath. Or even what he could potentially be and what she hopes to encourage -- said potential may be a big part of what stirred her heart and turned her head in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is ever a detailed explanation for the nature of the spirit shape (and I certainly hope there isn't, because closing down many routes of interpretation for an author to hard-code their own vision is just terrible when you're talking about a game of mythic heroes) I hope this is not it. Which is not to say that I think this is an invalid interpretation, or not worth exploring. It just adds to much of an external element for my liking.<br /> <br /> It's a cool idea, mind, and certainly a Lunar IC might wonder &quot;why is my spirit shape a desert basilisk when I'm from Whitewall? WTF Luna?&quot; but I think the more you start pushing for NPCs (controlled by the ST) to have some degree of narrative control over a player character's self-expression, I start to worry a little. Perhaps for nothing, admittedly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224859#post224859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lo, did Terezin, blonde-maned king of Eresteba (better known as the Lion Province), widely spoken of for his courage and for his great leadership of all men and beasts, drew his Second Breath as a Chosen of Luna. With the spirit shape of a humble donkey. Perhaps he continues with it with as much courage and pride as before, such that even the beast of burden in time becomes symbolic of kingship and nobility. Perhaps it turns his thoughts and efforts more to the laborers and downtrodden of his lands, and becomes beloved by them for his compassion. Perhaps he feels humbled by this form, and becomes a less bold, but a considerably more thoughtful ruler. Perhaps Luna expected one of these, all of these, or none of these.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest worry is not that Terezin's player chose this as like...kind of subverting a trope or playing with an idea of character growth, but that they played through an Exaltation scene and the ST was like &quot;OK your Spirit Shape is a donkey lol.&quot; I mean no amount of rules will stop a terrible ST, granted. But even on a narrative level the idea that the spirit shape is being set for you from without, rather than being an expression from within, is problematic to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-11-2014, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T07:37:32-07:00","id":225070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224963#post224963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if one assumes that the circumstances of Exaltation aren't a deeply defining event. Even a transformative one; the moment in which one Exalts might make one an entirely different person to what they were before</div> </div> </div> </div>If being Exalted transformed you into an entirely different person than the one you were before, why were you Exalted at all?<br /> <br /> I mean that sounds fine for an Infernal Exalt, but Lunars aren't chosen for something they might have been, they're chosen for what they are. Strength of Many's backstory doesn't tell us that he was a cringing weakling, the most pitiful slave in the camp, hardly expected to survive, until one day Luna chose him and he became strong. He was the strongest man in the camp, possibly the strongest mortal in that part of the south, and when he used his great strength and fortitude to stand up for others, he received the blessing of Luna. The Lunar Exaltation didn't transform him into someone totally different, it empowered him because of who he already was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-11-2014, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:02:20-07:00","id":225087,"title":"","content":"They're chosen for what they are at the moment of exaltation. What they were five minutes before is potentially quite different. An exaltation can turn a coward's momentary spike of backbone into a sustained avalanche of spine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:07:42-07:00","id":225089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225050#post225050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is ever a detailed explanation for the nature of the spirit shape (and I certainly hope there isn't, because closing down many routes of interpretation for an author to hard-code their own vision is just terrible when you're talking about a game of mythic heroes) I hope this is not it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, we're in agreement that I'd rather things not be too detailed. I wouldn't personally mind the explanation, but I'd prefer things be left mostly unspecified. Were it to exist in canon at all, I wouldn't like it as more than just one in a series of possible speculations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is not to say that I think this is an invalid interpretation, or not worth exploring. It just adds to much of an external element for my liking.<br /> <br /> It's a cool idea, mind, and certainly a Lunar IC might wonder &quot;why is my spirit shape a desert basilisk when I'm from Whitewall? WTF Luna?&quot; but I think the more you start pushing for NPCs (controlled by the ST) to have some degree of narrative control over a player character's self-expression, I start to worry a little. Perhaps for nothing, admittedly. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, with all respect, I would see that as worrying for nothing. I mean, preference for external over internal I understand completely, I just don't see it impacting how things would proceed at a table. The spirit shape is such a significant factor in a character that the idea of removing it from the players' hands never once occurred to me, and still doesn't seem plausible. It'd be like the ST deciding to set a character's Caste or Favored Abilities/Attributes or starting Charms when they Exalt. Or deciding, &quot;Yeah, Luna/Sol/Whoever doesn't feel like Choosing you after all, despite that being kind of the premise.&quot; Technically possible, but not something I'd expect to be at all plausible. At least if it's not something the group had discussed beforehand, or if the game isn't going to break apart then and there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My biggest worry is not that Terezin's player chose this as like...kind of subverting a trope or playing with an idea of character growth, but that they played through an Exaltation scene and the ST was like &quot;OK your Spirit Shape is a donkey lol.&quot; I mean no amount of rules will stop a terrible ST, granted. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, again, it would be something completely IC. It's too important to put in the ST's hands, outside a game where the group had decided to put it there. Even then, that game that wouldn't last long if the ST had decided to be... well, an ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even on a narrative level the idea that the spirit shape is being set for you from without, rather than being an expression from within, is problematic to me. </div> </div> </div>I can see that. I guess I don't see as much of a concern there, though. Individual Chosen of the Unconquered Sun have the Castes they do because the Sun selected them to be one of his priests, warriors, diplomats, shadowed hands, or intellectual luminaries. Panther, for instance, had life experiences that would have left him quite without the skills of an archetypal priest, but potential was seen there for him to, well, grow into it. I would, in hindsight, probably walk back the &quot;pick something at random&quot; notion a bit; in this scenario, I imagine Luna's very carefully considering the individual in question. She appears to all her Chosen in person, and that clearly suggests she cares a great deal for them. The spirit shape would be a direct a result of who the character is, or who the character could be, as much as another type of character's bestowed Caste.<br /> <br /> It's also an idea that I imagine is particularly likely to be unpalatable if one already has a sour taste in one's mouth from the idea that the gods are directly choosing their Exalted. I get that, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweaking. 08-11-2014, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:15:53-07:00","id":225093,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Luna doesn't pick. Everyone on creation has a spirit-shape-in-potential and the exaltation just lets it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:17:04-07:00","id":225095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225070#post225070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If being Exalted transformed you into an entirely different person than the one you were before, why were you Exalted at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be able to tell stories about Exaltation (especially the circumstances and aftermath of it) unlocking your hidden potential.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:18:13-07:00","id":225097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225087#post225087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're chosen for what they are at the moment of exaltation. What they were five minutes before is potentially quite different. An exaltation can turn a coward's momentary spike of backbone into a sustained avalanche of spine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd post a link to the Devilman theme, but the TV series doesn't use that origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:28:15-07:00","id":225101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=223564#post223564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Melee Charms are mutually exclusive from Solar Archery. A Lunar applies pretty much all Strength and Dexterity Charms into either weapon with little to no exclusivity.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can also shapeshift more than once per battle. If he needs an Evocation this round, he shapeshifts back to human. If he doesn't need an Evocation this round, he reassumes or remains in DBT. This is essentially no different from a Solar switching out one magical sword for another magical weapon as the battle changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Martial and Marital Ready keywords, invented by the devs(Admittly, they could not be in this edd. But they are indicative of how the devs work and or think) show that it's not exactly true that they are mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 08-11-2014, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:30:02-07:00","id":225102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225087#post225087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're chosen for what they are at the moment of exaltation. What they were five minutes before is potentially quite different. An exaltation can turn a coward's momentary spike of backbone into a sustained avalanche of spine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any canon Lunars who could serve as an example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224859#post224859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... This line of thought pointed me in a direction I hadn't considered before. Wild alternative interpretation/vague speculation, away!<br /> <br /> With the gods going back to being more important to the choosing of their Chosen, I wonder if it's possible that <i>Luna</i> might have a hand in defining a spirit shape. Luna's rather perceptive, after all, and the gods have some strong understanding of the natures of their Chosen. She could reasonably pick one that strongly reflects the character as he is. She could also pick one that suits what she expects he will become after taking the Second Breath. Or even what he could potentially be and what she hopes to encourage -- said potential may be a big part of what stirred her heart and turned her head in the first place.* Hell, perhaps sometimes she picks something that seems right out of left field because she knows that, if something <i>should</i> be meaningful and <i>feels</i> meaningful to its recipient,** the recipient -- and others -- are going to try to come up with reasons <i>why</i> it is meaningful; whatever reason or reasons they reach will usually be persuasive, and she's very curious to see what they draw from it, how they see it defining themselves, and how they themselves define it. For similar reasons, she may also pick something deliberately against the grain of the sort of thing one would expect a character to receive, or one that otherwise carries with it some interesting lesson, to see how this person who has drawn her interest responds to the apparent incongruity.***<br /> <br /> Eh, again, mostly musing, here. It wouldn't need to happen for every Lunar Exalt -- I like the idea of not even Luna necessarily knowing what spirit shape one of her Chosen may posses until, well, her Chosen possesses it. Even if entirely untrue, I definitely think it's something that some Lunars might believe or speculate about.<br /> <br /> * For the purposes of this speculation, I'm not assuming the standard &quot;Lunars Exalt for surviving&quot; is as very definitely true as it was in 2e. Or even if it is, who Luna's likely to pick from among the survivors.<br /> <br /> ** I get the impression Lunars are as comfortable in their human forms as they are in their spirit shapes, feeling a continuity and significance that they really don't have in other forms (outside DBT). It doesn't have a mechanical impact in their skill with any shape (oh, aside a mote discount for assuming a true form?), but I still like the notion.<br /> <br /> *** And lo, did Terezin, blonde-maned king of Eresteba (better known as the Lion Province), widely spoken of for his courage and for his great leadership of all men and beasts, drew his Second Breath as a Chosen of Luna. With the spirit shape of a humble donkey. Perhaps he continues with it with as much courage and pride as before, such that even the beast of burden in time becomes symbolic of kingship and nobility. Perhaps it turns his thoughts and efforts more to the laborers and downtrodden of his lands, and becomes beloved by them for his compassion. Perhaps he feels humbled by this form, and becomes a less bold, but a considerably more thoughtful ruler. Perhaps Luna expected one of these, all of these, or none of these.</div> </div> </div> </div>It opens some opportunities for roleplaying, and I can see an ST doing it this way for a player who's interested. In-setting, I think letting the Fickle Lady decide your spirit shape... or anything about you, really... is kind of a terrifying prospect. I mean, she is not exactly the most consistent god/dess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-11-2014, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:23:34-07:00","id":225143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225102#post225102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there any canon Lunars who could serve as an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few Lunars had established Exaltation scenes prior to second edition, and many of the later ones seemed very similar to Solar Exaltations. First edition did note that there could definitely be formerly timid folk who manage to take the Second Breath, though. And that they would then basically end up like Akira from Devilman and turn into badasses who hunt and kill with their bare hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:31:12-07:00","id":225148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225087#post225087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're chosen for what they are at the moment of exaltation. What they were five minutes before is potentially quite different. An exaltation can turn a coward's momentary spike of backbone into a sustained avalanche of spine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sustained avalanche of spine...sounds like a cool Liminal Charm!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:48:25-07:00","id":225158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225095#post225095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should be able to tell stories about Exaltation (especially the circumstances and aftermath of it) unlocking your hidden potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And hidden potential, I think, is generally expressed as Attributes. Someone with Intelligence 3 is bright and would make a good scholar, though she's never learned to read. Someone with Stamina 4 has hidden reserves of endurance, though she's lived a pampered lifestyle and never worked a day in her life. Someone with Dexterity 4 has the reflexes and coordination of a cat, though he labors as a book-copyer and will probably never be taught to fight.<br /> <br /> But unlocking your hidden potential means learning to use something you already have. The intelligent girl teaches herself to read, studies thaumaturgy, makes pacts with gods and initiates herself into sorcery. The book-copyer draws a bead on the charging austrech and brings it down with a 'lucky' shot planted square between the eyes. The pampered princess is left to die, they thought they had finished her, but she is a long way from finished, it can be a long road between life and death, and her brother the orkhan will learn every inch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-11-2014, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:33:58-07:00","id":225182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225158#post225158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. And hidden potential, I think, is generally expressed as Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, hidden potential exists in all Exalted. It's what the French call a certain... I don't know what. As opposed to readily quantifiable properties such as how much you can lift, how many drinks it takes before you end up with a lampshade on your head, or how many people have taken the pains to record your likeness in a shrine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T12:25:00-07:00","id":225221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225143#post225143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very few Lunars had established Exaltation scenes prior to second edition, and many of the later ones seemed very similar to Solar Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always something that annoyed me about Lunars (and unfortunately, I don't think it's fixable without invalidating existing Lunar concepts, so there's nothing to be done about it.) Every type of Exalted has their own unique circumstances and rules for their Exaltation... except Lunars, which just sort of reuse the Solar one with a vague note about 'survivors' tacked on at the end:<br /> <br /> DBs inherit their Exaltations.<br /> Alchemicals are built.<br /> Abyssals are chosen at the moment of death and must choose to accept.<br /> Infernals are chosen at their moment of greatest failure, must choose to accept, and spend five days in a cocoon before emerging as their new selves.<br /> Sidereals are fated from the moment of their birth.<br /> <br /> Solars are people of excellence uplifted without warning.<br /> Lunars are... people of a very very subtly different <i>kind</i> of excellence, and are uplifted without warning.<br /> <br /> Surviving is just a kind of Excellence, isn't really necessary for Lunars, and doesn't actually tie in to their Exaltation narrative anyway, so it comes off as more of a suggestion than something that shapes what they are. You can infer that Solars tend to have been highly skilled while Lunars tend to have been highly... attribute-ed... but that's just crudely trying to retroactively apply their mechanics to their background, and it isn't really reflected in their thematics (see eg. Solar Hercules.)<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to try and come up with ideas for a new mechanism or narrative for Lunar Exaltation, even though realistically I recognize that it can't be changed at this point (because there are too many existing Lunar concepts that would be invalidated by changing the narrative under them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:05:22-07:00","id":225242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225070#post225070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If being Exalted transformed you into an entirely different person than the one you were before, why were you Exalted at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Light a fire under you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that sounds fine for an Infernal Exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>And a variety of Solars.<br /> <br /> There's a whole &quot;David was a farm boy until serendipity sent him against a giant Philistine&quot; thing one can draw on here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars aren't chosen for something they might have been, they're chosen for what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'd say a person could be considered to include the qualities of their own deficiencies or things that they want or need to be but aren't until a suitable circumstance brings it to the fore.<br /> <br /> It's not as if I'm suggesting that a character should have an Exaltation into something that hasn't the slightest thing to do with their persona whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength of Many's backstory doesn't tell us that he was a cringing weakling, the most pitiful slave in the camp, hardly expected to survive, until one day Luna chose him and he became strong. He was the strongest man in the camp, possibly the strongest mortal in that part of the south, and when he used his great strength and fortitude to stand up for others, he received the blessing of Luna. The Lunar Exaltation didn't transform him into someone totally different, it empowered him because of who he already was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, different characters sure are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:09:32-07:00","id":225244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225158#post225158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. And hidden potential, I think, is generally expressed as Attributes. Someone with Intelligence 3 is bright and would make a good scholar, though she's never learned to read. Someone with Stamina 4 has hidden reserves of endurance, though she's lived a pampered lifestyle and never worked a day in her life. Someone with Dexterity 4 has the reflexes and coordination of a cat, though he labors as a book-copyer and will probably never be taught to fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying it's possible for characters with no dots in Lore, Resistance and Martial Arts/Melee to have a hidden potential to learn those Abilities?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:41:35-07:00","id":225283,"title":"","content":"Why do Lunars have Spirit Shapes?<br /> <br /> At the advent of the ancient war, the Great Gods wove their weapons around a core of celestial fire, stolen from Heaven by Autochthon, whose body still bears the steel-scarring wounds of its capture. The Dragon was happy to devour its portion of the champion-soul, in the manner of a snake, and so seeded the race of humans with children whose blood ran thick with its power. Alas, its eagerness and greed and lust worked against it, and as the heavenly power rushed out it tore into five lethargic drakes, who fled to shed their skins in the corners of the world forevermore. The other Incarna saw this, and were more cautious - instead of taking the champion-soul onto themselves, they danced with it, working it with their light (this is the nature of souls).<br /> <br /> The Sun's light defines borders, searing night from day and real from unreal and virtue from injustice. He armoured the champion-soul in sunlight, and it shined apart and above from the world. Each was a halo that crowned itself, a token of world-enriching arrogance, all-conquering and too admirable to be tolerated. Soon even Sol was forced to uncup his hands and turn his eyes aside, the light of his children promoting itself to ever-greater brilliance, and the Solars were released into the world.<br /> <br /> The Star's light defines passage, linking moments in space and places in time. She-they strung the champion-soul across countless points of starlight, and it became a thread of as many strands. Each wove itself into the world, seeking to be sought, knowing all by inference and guessing at nothing with uncanny accuracy. In time even the Maidens lost track of their work, the light of their-her children concealing itself behind the shadows it cast, and the Sidereals made their way to the world.<br /> <br /> But the Moon's light defines nothing, dancing happily with impossibilities and nightmares. The champion-soul ignored it, as one brushes off a dream after waking, and there was nothing to be done. Instead, she turned to her lover, Gaia, whose light she shared (this is the nature of love). Understanding her distress, Gaia called on the first of each and every animal she had created, all the great ancestor-spirits of those beasts she bore, and gave them a task - to carry the Moon's light. The stag hung the Moon's light about its antlers like dripping jewelry, and the fish pooled it in its scales, and the tiger bore it in its terrible gaze, and on and on. Together they bore the Moon's light to the champion-soul, which could not ignore them, for they were real. It accepted their gifts, and itself became a thing that was only mostly real - but it remembered the great First Beasts, and ran free and strange as they did, and the Lunars made their way into the world.<br /> <br /> That's why Lunars have Spirit Shapes.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now, see, that took me ~10-15 minutes to type up, most of which was phrasing. It gives people a concrete reason there's spirit shapes, other than &quot;muh apocalypse&quot;, which can still be safely ignored as an old myth. It makes the spirit shape more than just the thing you get mutations for in your warform, and excises the &quot;I have earned the gaze of the gods, and so wield the power of... a golden retriever!&quot; aspect - now it's the legacy of an ancient, terrible and beautiful animal-spirit, with all the hooks and potential Charmtech that implies. It even gives Lunars a clear connection to the animal spirits they always seem to be associated with for no apparent reason beyond &quot;hey, I ate one of your dudes and can now wear his skin - we're automatically bros&quot;. Hell, it even opens up hooks for surviving Animal Avatars to have links to specific Lunars (i.e. PCs). And if you want, it can even become their unique method of Exaltation - an animal of the appropriate type carries their Exaltation to them, dissolving into moonlight as it does so, taking impossible paths to reach the Chosen. It can even be their spirit adviser.<br /> <br /> That took a quarter of an hour, it does all that, and <i>it's not even particularly good</i>. I don't even <i>like</i> the spirit shape as an idea. Fuck the last two editions for not even managing <i>that</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":605,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","user":"Revlid","date":". 08-11-2014, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:53:19-07:00","id":225292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225244#post225244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying it's possible for characters with no dots in Lore, Resistance and Martial Arts/Melee to have a hidden potential to learn those Abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that wasn't exactly my point. I'm saying they have innate potential to fight, to withstand injury and to master intellectual thought. And that potential is represented as their Attributes. From 2E core:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>STEP TWO: ATTRIBUTES<br /> The Attributes define your character\u2019s innate capabilities and aptitudes.<br /> <br /> STEP THREE: ABILITIES<br /> Abilities describe what your character knows and can do, what he\u2019s learned rather than his natural potential.</i></div>See also:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Physical Attributes define your character\u2019s physical potential\u2014how fast she runs, how much she can lift and how healthy she is.<br /> <br /> Social Attributes define your character\u2019s ability to interact with, relate to and manipulate others. Social Attributes affect first impressions, your character\u2019s ability to inspire or lead people and how attractive she is.<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes define your character\u2019s intellectual capacity\u2014how quickly she thinks, how keen her senses are and how smart she is.<br /> <br /> A character with no dots in an Ability is unskilled, and a character with no dots in an Attribute is crippled and incapable of actions requiring that Attribute.</i></div>Attributes are a character's innate talents, whether known or unknown. Abilities are his learned skills. So if a character has hidden, unknown potential for something, you should see it represented in the relevant Attribute.<br /> <br /> I've always thought that Lunars are probably the best type of Exalted for exploring a character's hidden potential, because other types' abilities are less about potential and more about skill. No one is ever born with Archery 5; it's something you have to train long and hard to achieve. But you might have been born with Dexterity 5 and Perception 5 still have no idea of your potential to be one of the finest duelists in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-11-2014, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T15:35:36-07:00","id":225353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225242#post225242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as if I'm suggesting that a character should have an Exaltation into something that hasn't the slightest thing to do with their persona whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you said,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=224963#post224963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the moment in which one Exalts might make one an entirely different person to what they were before, which also seems like it would muddy up an exacting need to define the spirit shape according to &quot;who you are&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like you're saying that your inner nature can change in a single moment to such an extent that your spirit shape doesn't fit with who you were before.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not even a bad idea, honestly. If you wanted that as a player, I'd say fine. It's just an inversion of how I'm used to thinking about it. If that's not what you're saying, I apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:21:10-07:00","id":225386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225158#post225158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. And hidden potential, I think, is generally expressed as Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's valid in some cases, but I'm resistant to hidden potential being something you can look up on a character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:33:04-07:00","id":225394,"title":"","content":"I think the discussion of hidden potential is odd.<br /> <br /> One dot in Lore means you're literate and can read a map. I'm rather sure that anyone who is old enough to exalt has the potential to learn to read. There's nothing 'hidden' about it. Unless you have a specific injuries or diseases, you can learn to fight with a melee weapon or unarmed. Again, that's not hidden potential, that's normal potential.<br /> <br /> When we talk about hidden potential, we mean someone who appears unlikely to master something can actually become great at it. Someone who is clumsy and out of shape becoming a fabulous dancer. That's not Grace, who has Dex 5 and Performance 0, getting Performance 2. That's Grace, who has Dex 2 and Performance 0, getting Performance 4.<br /> <br /> If Grace were already dexterous and had good balance, no one would be surprised if she became a great dancer. If Grace is strong and in good shape, no one is going to be surprised that she's a good athlete. If Grace is good-looking and pleasant to be around, no one is going to be surprised that she excels at public speaking.<br /> <br /> High attributes are obvious potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 08-11-2014, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:43:19-07:00","id":225403,"title":"","content":"Usually, I'd think of &quot;hidden potential&quot; as being less about capability and more about motivation and will. Like, being about how you do things and what you accomplish with it.<br /> <br /> There are lots of great public speakers, but only a few Martin Luther Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:53:44-07:00","id":225410,"title":"","content":"This isn't really relevant to the way Exalted does things, but I'd see potential less as your current stats and more as your trait maximums -- someone with hidden potential (emphasis on hidden) in Melee could, with training, raise it higher than the average person (for mortals this is already somewhat the case: regular mortals can seldom go above 4).<br /> <br /> It could be an interesting homebrew - modding the maximums of your traits to say something about the potential of your character, sacrificing flexibility for power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:56:08-07:00","id":225412,"title":"","content":"Martin Luther King entered college at the age of 15. Almost every report we have of him paints him as intelligent and charismatic, even at a young age.<br /> <br /> I don't see that as hidden potential because it's not hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:03:49-07:00","id":225419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225394#post225394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we talk about hidden potential, we mean someone who appears unlikely to master something can actually become great at it. Someone who is clumsy and out of shape becoming a fabulous dancer. That's not Grace, who has Dex 5 and Performance 0, getting Performance 2. That's Grace, who has Dex 2 and Performance 0, getting Performance 4.<br /> <br /> If Grace were already dexterous and had good balance, no one would be surprised that if she became a great dancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of how I'm seeing it, too. I don't generally take a high Attribute to mean a character has strong potential in something; I generally take it to mean a character has a lot of her broad capability in that area. Fox may have Intelligence 2 and nothing in Lore, Occult, or other thinky Abilities, but he may still have a natural way of thinking and approaching matters that might make a learned sage say, &quot;Study hard and train your mind, boy; with your natural approach, you have potential to be a brilliant scholar.&quot; Sara, meanwhile, may have only Strength and Dexterity 2 and Melee 1, but someone who knows what to look for sees she has the right build, bone structure, attitude, foundational instruction, or whatever else to become an impressive master of the blade. To me, it feels natural that the term &quot;you have potential&quot; implies the &quot;you&quot; there has yet to realize it, whether in terms of skill (Ability), general capability (Attribute), or both.<br /> <br /> I can kinda see how someone with Dex 5 and Melee 0 could be told he has potential to be amazing with an axe, because, well, yeah, he's deft and nimble with 5 whole dots of space to grow into that Ability. But I would raise an eyebrow if he was told, &quot;You have potential to be deft and nimble,&quot; because having Dex 5 generally means one <i>already is</i> deft and nimble. The other eyebrow would also go up if his potential skill with an axe was described as &quot;hidden potential,&quot; because, no, he's plainly very dextrous unless he deliberately plays it down, so the term there would be &quot;obvious potential.&quot; But yeah, the phrase &quot;potential&quot; in a vacuum? I generally presume it speaks of someone with neither high Abilities nor high Attributes in the area, but with some trait that isn't necessarily reflected anywhere on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm missing something with the &quot;Attributes as hidden potential&quot; idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:07:30-07:00","id":225423,"title":"","content":"It's also difficult to define anything that can be measured by numbers on a character sheet as &quot;hidden potential&quot; because...well, yes, a Cha 2 guy can spend the XP to get up to Performance 4, and it's not any harder for him than it is for the Cha 4 guy. It does take less training for the Cha 4 guy to get the same results before considering Charm prereqs, that is to say he only needs Performance 1 to have five dice and the Cha 2 guy needs Performance 3.<br /> <br /> But then, raw stats aren't potential either because the Cha 2 guy can also spend XP to get up to Cha 4. In the real world there are things like genetics that put limits on how strong/fast/tough/intelligent/handsome someone can be, and while there are ways to get around some of these limits they're largely unchangeable through training. In Exalted, the only thing stopping your character from being just as strong as any other strongman is that you don't have them spend XP on it. That's not even a function of being an Exalt, you can do it as a heroic mortal too. So clearly either everyone in Creation has equal levels of &quot;hidden potential&quot;, or stats aren't hidden potential. I tend to go with the latter.<br /> <br /> As for what is...I'm not sure there really is such a thing, mechanically speaking. You can see all the values on the character sheet, you can tell exactly what someone's capabilities and remaining potential in a given field are. Hidden potential is more about narrative, a character starting weak in something and then growing stronger in it. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221817-3rd-edition-xp-costs/\">We're having a lovely thread about how Exalted character creation makes this a bad idea for a story to tell</a>, but you can do it, and I think this is the closest you'll get to Gohan displaying lots of untapped power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:15:51-07:00","id":225448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225394#post225394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the discussion of hidden potential is odd.<br /> <br /> One dot in Lore means you're literate and can read a map. I'm rather sure that anyone who is old enough to exalt has the potential to learn to read. There's nothing 'hidden' about it. Unless you have a specific injuries or diseases, you can learn to fight with a melee weapon or unarmed. Again, that's not hidden potential, that's normal potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really what I was talking about either. I meant a peasant girl have the Intelligence required to be a master savant, but it may go unrecognized because she's never had the opportunity to learn to read. I didn't mean she had the hidden potential to learn to read. Obviously almost everyone has that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225394#post225394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Grace were already dexterous and had good balance, no one would be surprised if she became a great dancer. If Grace is strong and in good shape, no one is going to be surprised that she's a good athlete. If Grace is good-looking and pleasant to be around, no one is going to be surprised that she excels at public speaking.<br /> <br /> High attributes are obvious potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. You don't necessarily notice your natural talents that easily, and neither do people around you. You may think you have talents you don't have, and you may miss the ones you do. For instance if you have Stamina 4, you may never give any thought to the fact that you can't remember the last time you were ill, and maybe no one else has either. You may have Dexterity 4 or 5, yet live a boring life, so that it's never fully dawned on you just how quick your reflexes are. And if you've never handled a prayer piece (and most people haven't), you probably have no idea you have the makings of a master duelist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:20:27-07:00","id":225454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225244#post225244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying it's possible for characters with no dots in Lore, Resistance and Martial Arts/Melee to have a hidden potential to learn those Abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not? I would imagine that most people with hidden potential in a talent never realize that potential IRL. I mean, I think the implication is generally that your stats as a chargen Exalt are higher than they would have been at the moment of Exaltation, because those stats are <i>gonzo ridiculous</i>, and then you &quot;grew into them&quot; due to cosmic understanding opening all your chakras, or whatever the heck.<br /> <br /> Certainly, if your hidden potential in something was completely unrealized up until [whatever], there should be a <i>reason</i>, but that could be almost anything -- often it will be attributable to lifestyle factors, but it's totally in-genre for you just to have some sort of mental block that you suddenly plow through in a transcendent moment.<br /> <br /> I don't really think you can relate potential to your <i>current</i> traits, because those are about what you are, and potential is about what you could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:28:56-07:00","id":225462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225448#post225448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really what I was talking about either. I meant a peasant girl have the Intelligence required to be a master savant, but it may go unrecognized because she's never had the opportunity to learn to read. I didn't mean she had the hidden potential to learn to read. Obviously almost everyone has that.<br /> <br /> Eh. You don't necessarily notice your natural talents that easily, and neither do people around you. You may think you have talents you don't have, and you may miss the ones you do. For instance if you have Stamina 4, you may never give any thought to the fact that you can't remember the last time you were ill, and maybe no one else has either. You may have Dexterity 4 or 5, yet live a boring life, so that it's never fully dawned on you just how quick your reflexes are. And if you've never handled a prayer piece (and most people haven't), you probably have no idea you have the makings of a master duelist.</div> </div> </div> </div>And anyone that's the top of their field will have to have both a high Attribute and Ability. It applies to everyone. It isn't a Lunar-only thing. It can't be used as a &quot;Lunar gauge&quot;. You'd do better to look at how dedicated someone is to the sorts of Intimacies which Thousand Streams Defender or the Lunar version of Righteous Lion Defense reinforce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:25:55-07:00","id":225510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225423#post225423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also difficult to define anything that can be measured by numbers on a character sheet as &quot;hidden potential&quot; because...well, yes, a Cha 2 guy can spend the XP to get up to Performance 4, and it's not any harder for him than it is for the Cha 4 guy. It does take less training for the Cha 4 guy to get the same results before considering Charm prereqs, that is to say he only needs Performance 1 to have five dice and the Cha 2 guy needs Performance 3.<br /> <br /> But then, raw stats aren't potential either because the Cha 2 guy can also spend XP to get up to Cha 4. In the real world there are things like genetics that put limits on how strong/fast/tough/intelligent/handsome someone can be, and while there are ways to get around some of these limits they're largely unchangeable through training. In Exalted, the only thing stopping your character from being just as strong as any other strongman is that you don't have them spend XP on it. That's not even a function of being an Exalt, you can do it as a heroic mortal too. So clearly either everyone in Creation has equal levels of &quot;hidden potential&quot;, or stats aren't hidden potential. I tend to go with the latter.<br /> <br /> As for what is...I'm not sure there really is such a thing, mechanically speaking. You can see all the values on the character sheet, you can tell exactly what someone's capabilities and remaining potential in a given field are. Hidden potential is more about narrative, a character starting weak in something and then growing stronger in it. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221817-3rd-edition-xp-costs/\">We're having a lovely thread about how Exalted character creation makes this a bad idea for a story to tell</a>, but you can do it, and I think this is the closest you'll get to Gohan displaying lots of untapped power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, look. I quoted the 2E core book exactly. The words and concepts I'm using are the same the game system uses. In 2E, your Attributes are your innate talents and potential - whether you know you have them or not - and your Abilities are your learned skills. That is how they're defined. It may not make the most sense all the time, but that's the system in the most recent published form.<br /> <br /> If you need more quotes, here's the section from the 2E book that describes the game's core mechanic:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>POOLS AND DICE<br /> Whenever a character attempts an action where success and failure are both possible, her player rolls a number of dice equal to the dots the character has in the appropriate trait or traits. Most rolls couple an Attribute with an Ability,<b> representing the combination of innate potential and learned skill</b> that best applies to the situation.</i></div>Here's a quote from the Lunars book, about charms:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Lunars are naturally instinctive creatures. This is part of why their Charms focus on Attributes, their natural potential, instead of the training represented by Abilities.</i></div>I mean, we're talking about the core mechanic of the game here, Attribute+Ability and what they mean. It seems like quite often on this forum I find myself saying something that comes straight out of the books, and people respond as if they're hearing it for the first time and that I'm talking nonsense or just making things up. I must admit it gets exasperating to always have to defend my interpretation of things when all it is is the game exactly as it's written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:30:26-07:00","id":225513,"title":"","content":"I don't think Attributes representing &quot;potential&quot; is meant to imply that they imply some heights that the character might have going forward. A better term might be &quot;innate power&quot; though that doesn't really satisfy me either. But to me &quot;innate potential&quot; means something greater that the character does not possess yet, versus their current, existing natural prowess which is expressed by their current rating in an Attribute. Prowess, that's a good word for it!<br /> <br /> At the same time, here's what the book says about the spirit shape:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunars page 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Known as the spirit shape, this form is that of a specific animal representing the Lunar\u2019s inner nature and personality. A majestic warrior might acquire a sleek jaguar as his spirit shape, while a crafty street urchin takes the iconic shape of a sly fox.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u200b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Nowhere in the RAW does it imply &quot;your spirit shape has to somewhat reflect or be at all influenced by your character's human-form Attributes.&quot; The Lunars book may have issues but I kinda doubt they would write &quot;inner nature&quot; when they meant &quot;Attributes,&quot; which is a known system term used in the same book and all over the game line. If they really wanted to say &quot;Attributes,&quot; they would have said &quot;Attributes.&quot; So I think they're really referring to something intangible about the character, something wholly different from the dots on the sheet.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-11-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:48:31-07:00","id":225526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225513#post225513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, here's what the book says about the spirit shape:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Known as the spirit shape, this form is that of a specific animal representing the Lunar\u2019s inner nature and personality. A majestic warrior might acquire a sleek jaguar as his spirit shape, while a crafty street urchin takes the iconic shape of a sly fox.</span></span></div>Nowhere in the RAW does it imply &quot;your spirit shape has to somewhat reflect or be at all influenced by your character's human-form Attributes.&quot; The Lunars book may have issues but I kinda doubt they would write &quot;inner nature&quot; when they meant &quot;Attributes,&quot; which is a known system term used in the same book and all over the game line. If they really wanted to say &quot;Attributes,&quot; they would have said &quot;Attributes.&quot; So I think they're really referring to something intangible about the character, something wholly different from the dots on the sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. So what would a &quot;crafty&quot; street urchin's Attributes look like, in your opinion? Would you expect a particularly crafty character to have Wits 1, Intelligence 1 and Manipulation 1?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, forget what you would expect. Is it even possible, in Exalted, for a crafty street urchin to have Wits 1, Intelligence 1 and Manipulation 1?<br /> <br /> Because, read as written, according to the Attribute descriptions given in Chapter Three of the core rulebook, an urchin with those Attributes would be &quot;dull and stupid&quot;. And (I'm guessing) not even eligible for a license to urchin, let alone the &quot;sly fox&quot; spirit shape your quote suggests would be appropriate for an urchin who is crafty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225513#post225513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Attributes representing &quot;potential&quot; is meant to imply that they imply some heights that the character might have going forward. A better term might be &quot;innate power&quot; though that doesn't really satisfy me either. But to me &quot;innate potential&quot; means something greater that the character does not possess yet, versus their current, existing natural prowess which is expressed by their current rating in an Attribute. Prowess, that's a good word for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Innate potential&quot; doesn't refer to something you don't possess yet. It refers to what you do possess: your natural talents, capabilities, instincts and aptitudes. That's how the core book defines Attributes, and I've quoted the lines where it says just that. So basically you're saying exactly what I've been saying for a couple of pages now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-12-2014, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T07:51:52-07:00","id":225970,"title":"","content":"I was meaning to address this in the magic armour thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221490-magic-armor-problematic?p=221699#post221699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I can judge by prior works and writings. Were Shrikes a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was good but the execution was stifled due to coming into existence so late in the game line and alongside other attempts to make 2.0 combos more fun and less of a death trap. As another toy for Dawn Caste Solars who didn't need them they represented even more unnecessary bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> Had 3e not been approved and the developers been left to redevelop the existing splats for 2.5 it could have been interesting to see a revised Lunar Exalted who used reflexive attacks as a <i>replacement</i> for Extra-Action charms and (most) counter-attacks. In addition to giving them a more distinctive playstyle it'd help to make Attributes besides Dexterity more useful and be very in-keeping with certain themes (multiple attacks, particularly ones you build up from being attacked are a good mechanical shorthand for &quot;now I'm angry&quot;).<br /> <br /> At least that's how I'd do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T01:26:45-07:00","id":226841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=225970#post225970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was meaning to address this in the magic armour thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea was good but the execution was stifled due to coming into existence so late in the game line and alongside other attempts to make 2.0 combos more fun and less of a death trap. As another toy for Dawn Caste Solars who didn't need them they represented even more unnecessary bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> Had 3e not been approved and the developers been left to redevelop the existing splats for 2.5 it could have been interesting to see a revised Lunar Exalted who used reflexive attacks as a <i>replacement</i> for Extra-Action charms and (most) counter-attacks. In addition to giving them a more distinctive playstyle it'd help to make Attributes besides Dexterity more useful and be very in-keeping with certain themes (multiple attacks, particularly ones you build up from being attacked are a good mechanical shorthand for &quot;now I'm angry&quot;).<br /> <br /> At least that's how I'd do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...ok. I can admit, that could be intresting. The general thrust of how they existed, though, was kinda trash and shreaded the system. As a charm-tech replacment, though...that could have some merit. That's something to think on. Thank you.<br /> <br /> I still fool around with 2.5 due to a lack of anything to do. No promises, but if I manage to hack anything worthwhile out of it(God I seriously wish I was better at this sort of thing.), I'll share, promise!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 08-13-2014, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T05:08:45-07:00","id":228991,"title":"","content":"Is anybody else ever very mildly annoyed when the tattoos of a Lunar aren't consistent between illustrations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T07:14:42-07:00","id":229029,"title":"","content":"There should totally be charms/knacks that allow you to rearrange your Tattoos to lie about your Reknown / Succor / Mettle / [valor] / [temperance] or make them behave like Rorschach's mask.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, it would give artists a flimsy excuse to forget proper tattoo placement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T07:51:58-07:00","id":229053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=228991#post228991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anybody else ever very mildly annoyed when the tattoos of a Lunar aren't consistent between illustrations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I'm also annoyed by how tattoos are required or you go crazy, and how many stupid drawbacks they bring, and the very idea that an Exaltation designed to combat the enemies at the gates of Creation might be damaged by the area outside said gates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229029#post229029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should totally be charms/knacks that allow you to rearrange your Tattoos to lie about your Reknown / Succor / Mettle / [valor] / [temperance]</div> </div> </div> </div>The badly-transplanted, terribly-implemented Werewolf Renown system shit can stay out too.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To explain, I fucking <i>love </i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse. It's one of my favorite games to play and run, if not my favorite, and the only reason I don't play it more than Exalted is more of my gaming friends prefer the themes to Exalted over Werewolf. I like the Renown system in Werewolf just fine, and it works very well for its role in that game. That said, I don't think it has any good role, and even less good execution, for Lunars. A lot of the 1e Silver Pact stuff (which was largely pasted into 2e) was inspired heavily by the Garou Nation in OWoD Werewolf, and it shows - it just doesn't work for Lunars, because Exalted is not telling the same story as Werewolf, and the community of Lunars is not at all similar to the Garou Nation in purpose, outlook, goal or even theme (aside from being made up of shapeshifters). So just drop this part, because while it makes a lot of sense in Werewolf, it makes none for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-15-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T08:12:07-07:00","id":229058,"title":"","content":"Wyld'll damage exaltations if it wants to. Wyld don't give a fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:05:28-07:00","id":229104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=228991#post228991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anybody else ever very mildly annoyed when the tattoos of a Lunar aren't consistent between illustrations?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it may be one of the least annoying things about tattooed Lunars, because I always hated the tattoos in general. &quot;Hi, I'm a shapeshifter and trickster but you can always tell who I am unless I buy this charm. Oh, and if I buy that Charm to hide my tattoos, you can still spot my tell, unless I refuse to buy this entire tree of shapeshifting enhancements. So, better not. Also, I better not use very many Charms or I can't shapeshift, except for three forms... one of which I didn't buy because it would totally screw over my trickster shapeshifting. Why don't any other shapeshifters have a tell by the way? I mean, if every shapeshifter had a tell, that might be cool, but no, I guess its only me. You know, how I use my perfect shapeshifting to become something else but can never, ever, get rid of this oddly shaped eye. Well, at least unheroic mortals won't see through my Tell. I can generally interact with them without them screaming Lunar! and running away. Pity that heroic mortals sometimes do see through it, and Exalted generally see through it at the drop of a hat. Oh, and they screw up part of my sorcery, and they literally show my social history with other Lunars like a Facebook feed. All so that my anima power isn't as flexible anymore. Oh well, at least I won't turn into a slobbering Wyld nightmare. Just, you know, one more thing I can't turn into with tattoos.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, if Lunars are going to be shapeshifters, and that's there thing, let them do it! It's ok! Shapeshifting is BADASS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:08:45-07:00","id":229108,"title":"","content":"You'd think being casteless wasn't an option or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:19:13-07:00","id":229113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229053#post229053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the very idea that an Exaltation designed to combat the enemies at the gates of Creation might be damaged by the area outside said gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, even though I find myself doubting that what's wrong with the Lunars in the next Edition will be a condition of extensive exposure to the Wyld, I still find this logic a bit dubious.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I dislike looking on the Essences as something designed towards tactical or functional purposes; if design enters into it, it's design towards the kind of heroes that result.<br /> <br /> That and how the idea seems to have been that the Lunars had been continuously within the Wyld for an extremely long time.<br /> <br /> Really, while there's something worth keeping in the idea that the appropriate Essences can't be destroyed, the idea that it cannot be influenced or altered seems to cut off more than it safeguards. Why does it not extend to Abyssals and Infernals, and probably to Exigents (re dirty bomb Exaltations)?<br /> <br /> They shouldn't be <i>casually</i> affected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:27:25-07:00","id":229121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229108#post229108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd think being casteless wasn't an option or something...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, in many games, they are not. &quot;No, sorry, no chimeras in my game. Those aren't for PCs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:42:56-07:00","id":229134,"title":"","content":"Well that's just wrong. Stay out of the wyld and that's not even an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:45:19-07:00","id":229135,"title":"","content":"The Tell isn't necessarily an issue if you don't make it something blindingly obvious. The rules are that it can take any form, but usually represents something having to do with your spirit shape. <i>Usually.</i> But even if it does, you have room to play with it. The last Tell I used was the persistent scent of a certain plant. So hey, someone notices I smell like I've been outdoors or maybe am wearing perfume. Go figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:54:36-07:00","id":229170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229121#post229121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly, in many games, they are not. &quot;No, sorry, no chimeras in my game. Those aren't for PCs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what the Knacks do, chimerae aren't really for Lunars. Their themes demand not being a shoggoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:55:13-07:00","id":229171,"title":"","content":"The tell isn't a lunar detector. Someone beats it once, maybe they notice an odd distinctive feature. You have to show up again in a different form and <i>then</i> they notice this other guy/thing has the same distinct feature and maybe put two and two together. Even then they might dismiss the connection as a coincidence and even if they come to the conclusion that the two things are one and the same based on this one feature they might not know that this is a thing distinct to lunars. Probably isn't, actually. Luna's shapeshifting is noted to be perfect which implies most gods have something you can recognise them by.<br /> <br /> Point is some schmuck seeing the tell and going OMG LUNAR!!!!11! isn't an issue because THAT'S NOT HOW IT FUCKING WORKS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:21:26-07:00","id":229194,"title":"","content":"TSk, that's a reasonable response to the tell. Unfortunately, that is not how the tell works as written.<br /> <br /> First, the tell makes a magical social attack against every single person in the area against their MDV with 12 automatic successes. If you are in a true form, their MDV is doubled. Remember also that MDV is increased if the individual has a higher Appearance. Also, as a note for magical mental influence: &quot;Targets recognize the supernatural force behind the character\u2019s actions.&quot; That means, walking around in your true human form, every single person with an MDV of seven or higher automatically notices that you are a Lunar and that you are magically trying to make them not look at your tell. That's an MDV after modifications for Appearance, etc.<br /> <br /> If your character's motivation is something like &quot;Destroy the Anathema,&quot; the order to ignore the tell becomes an Unacceptable Order, with all the effects that entails. Admittedly, this is only in rare cases, like fanatical Wyld Hunt Dragon-Blooded. Of course, these are the people you most want to hide from.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you spend even one mote of Peripheral Essence, your tell becomes obvious. If someone has seen your tell before, that's a +2 to their MDV. If they know that the tell is a sign of Shapeshifters, that's an additional +1. If they know that the Tell is only a Lunar thing, that's an additional +2 (not stacking with the +1). Purchasing certain Knacks can also reduce the number of successes at the Tells attack, but we'll ignore those for now.<br /> <br /> This means that if someone spots you after having spent even 1 mote of Peripheral Essence, and wants to find you again, and you just happen to be in your true human or animal forms, and they know enough about Lunars to know what a Tell is, the MDV they require to see you is:<br /> <br /> 12/2 - 4 = 2. That's right, if by some chance you encounter a Wyld Hunt, spend some essence on trying to kill them, fail, and escape, if they even glance in your direction at a later date while you are hiding out, they will automatically see you, because your tell will scream at them &quot;I&quot;m right here!&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit, this is not because the Tell is a bad idea. It's because the social mechanics have a real problem, and the Tell should NOT be using them. Especially to attack anyone who sees you! That's just god-awful thinking.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the suggestions for the Tell are something like &quot;a fine mantle of down upon your shoulders in human form. &quot; So, many STs won't go for a scent. I think its reasonable, but even if they do let it go, that scent automatically triggers a &quot;Don't notice me effect!&quot; If they do notice it, they realize that the smell is creating a magical mental influence of 'Don't notice me!&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the Tell in concept, but I hate hate hate how it was implemented through the weakest part of the ruleset in Ex2. The Tell isn't even half the problem. The fact that Lunars have THREE things that screw over their shapeshifting is what bothers me. The Tell, the Tattoos, and the the inability to spend Essence while transformed. Add that to certain Knacks you just can't take (shapeshifting knacks that make your shapeshifting better but also screw over your shapeshifting), and it just... kinda sucks.<br /> <br /> End rant.<br /> <br /> Edit: TSk, I really, really wish that the Tell worked like you suggest. Most capable STs I know throw out the ENTIRE Tell system and homebrew something to take effect. There's just so much work to do to make Lunars what they should be, they don't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:31:55-07:00","id":229200,"title":"","content":"I guess I've never considered the social attack effect to mean, when someone notices your Tell, that they also notice there's a magical effect disguising it. That's never come up in a game for me. However I can see the logic of why an ST would rule it would.<br /> <br /> I've also never taken it to mean spotting a Tell means you recognize someone's a Lunar Exalt. I can't say that's not in the books, but if it is, that's silly, and surely we ignore it? After all, not everyone in Creation even knows what a Lunar Exalt is.<br /> <br /> As for the scent: forget the examples, the rules explicitly say the Tell can take any form, be it audio, visual, olfactory. So having a perpetually pine-fresh scent is a perfectly legit Tell.<br /> <br /> I agree with that it shouldn't rely on social attacks at all, or it should have way more automatic successes. And being forced to take Hide of the Cunning Hunter to hide your tattoos, which is stupid, surely that should be a free ability (I mean you already start with fewer free charms, it really sucks as a Lunar that the ones you have you have to waste on things like that and DBT, charms you basically have to take). I just think the Tell can be played in a way that prevents it being such a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-15-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:36:24-07:00","id":229228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229200#post229200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I've never considered the social attack effect to mean, when someone notices your Tell, that they also notice there's a magical effect disguising it. That's never come up in a game for me.<br /> <br /> I've also never taken it to mean spotting a Tell means you recognize someone's a Lunar Exalt. I can't say that's not in the books, but if it is, that's silly, and surely we ignore it? After all, not everyone in Creation even knows what a Lunar Exalt is.<br /> <br /> As for the scent: forget the examples, the rules explicitly say the Tell can take any form, be it audio, visual, olfactory. So having a perpetually pine-fresh scent is a perfectly legit Tell.<br /> <br /> I agree with that it shouldn't rely on social attacks at all, or it should have way more automatic successes. And being forced to take Hide of the Cunning Hunter to hide your tattoos, which is stupid, surely that should be a free ability (I mean you already start with fewer free charms, it really sucks as a Lunar that the ones you have you have to waste on things like that and DBT, charms you basically have to take). I just think the Tell can be played in a way that prevents it being such a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, it can be played that way, sure. It just isn't written that way. I think one of the big problems is that the Tell makes a magical mental attack, and in the Core Book it says someone subjected to a Magical Mental Attack automatically understands that it is unnatural mental influence. I'm guessing you guys fudged a little bit when it came to the Social Combat rules as well? My group through that whole thing out as well, because garbage.<br /> <br /> I would always allow a Tell of any sort, so long as it isn't too gratuitous. So did one of my STs. The other however, did not. I couldn't walk into a room in my true form without someone spotting me, because 'Rules as Written.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:48:22-07:00","id":229234,"title":"","content":"I think I'm just going to go and have a Diet Coke until I cool down a bit. I love Lunars so much, and lay a Celtic template on them for Storytelling purposes, and they become so interesting. Just the ruleset doesn't support them. It makes me sad. <br /> <br /> Last note: Why do Lunars have such a small Personal Essence pool if Shapeshifting costs motes and you can't Shapeshift if you've spent very much Peripheral. Especially with such big Peripheral pools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:48:33-07:00","id":229235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229194#post229194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your character's motivation is something like &quot;Destroy the Anathema,&quot; the order to ignore the tell becomes an Unacceptable Order, with all the effects that entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring magic, only explicit orders for suicide are Unacceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:52:08-07:00","id":229241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229228#post229228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it can be played that way, sure. It just isn't written that way. I think one of the big problems is that the Tell makes a magical mental attack, and in the Core Book it says someone subjected to a Magical Mental Attack automatically understands that it is unnatural mental influence. I'm guessing you guys fudged a little bit when it came to the Social Combat rules as well? My group through that whole thing out as well, because garbage.<br /> <br /> I would always allow a Tell of any sort, so long as it isn't too gratuitous. So did one of my STs. The other however, did not. I couldn't walk into a room in my true form without someone spotting me, because 'Rules as Written.'</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, it's not considered UMI. Lunars p.130 says: &quot;The Lunar radiates a powerful and unnoticeable mental influence on people who perceive the Lunar in any form, commanding them to ignore the Tell. This counts as natural mental influence, despite its obviously magical nature.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:55:16-07:00","id":229244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229104#post229104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hi, I'm a shapeshifter and trickster but you can always tell who I am unless I buy this charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point where the tattoos become impossible to hide by clothing and otherwise explicit as the accoutrements of a Lunar, i.e. the point where your Anima is flaring a fair bit, that cat is already out of the bag regardless of shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't any other shapeshifters have a tell by the way? I mean, if every shapeshifter had a tell, that might be cool, but no, I guess its only me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, making the Tell a specific, mechanically heavy thing reserved for Lunars, as opposed to something like how Five Days Darkness has inky black eyes regardless of his shape, isn't really the best.<br /> <br /> The Tell is a decent idea, but I think it needs to be less overthought and overdesigned.<br /> <br /> And personally, I'm not averse to the idea that beings like, say, Lucien are better at turning into other beings than Lunars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:27:15-07:00","id":229276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229235#post229235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Barring magic, only explicit orders for suicide are Unacceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but many characters will have that sort of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:36:01-07:00","id":229314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229241#post229241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, it's not considered UMI. Lunars p.130 says: &quot;The Lunar radiates a powerful and unnoticeable mental influence on people who perceive the Lunar in any form, commanding them to ignore the Tell. This counts as natural mental influence, despite its obviously magical nature.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, must of have missed that line where it specifically says this magic is not magical, despite being magic. Honestly, it shows that they understood that the rules that they were writing were problematic at best. Catching that line in game. My bad, and I accept the correction. I still maintain that the mechanical heavy rules around the Tell is garbage. Also I forgot to note the point where if you have an Intimacy or Motivation regarding Anathema you get bonus MDV to spotting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:37:25-07:00","id":229317,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a natural influence. If you spot it and it lights up like a christmas tree then the storyteller is doing it <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>WRONG.</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:45:00-07:00","id":229321,"title":"","content":"The tell is...problematic, yes. It's an NMI effect that acts like UMI, and both calls and pushes away attention from itself at the SAME TIME. Plus the whole problem of there's no true way to negate it, so if someone has an illusion negator, so much for being the best shapeshifter in the setting...Luna's got you beat, and you can't ever equal her ever. Plus, as you noted, everything else that has such effects. That eclipse that just got a shift-charm from a spirit? No tell. And so on.<br /> <br /> As to why the tiny personal pool, when Perif modlock? Bad system design, flat out. The shapeshifting system from 1ed on has been garbage. Hell, there was...I forget who, but someone on staff once qouted as &quot;Well, why should we bother with good animal rules? Only one splat really interacts with them that way.&quot; It...becomes REALLY problematic when that one splat that does? It's kiiinda their main damn thing. (Ignoring debates on if that should or shouldn't be, for the moment it is, and that's kinda...yeah.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:45:03-07:00","id":229322,"title":"","content":"It could be improved, yeah. The number of automatic successes is way too low, or the MDV modifiers are too high. But it looks like your ST's misreading of the rules was really crippling your experience there. You should not have had to deal with that crap as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> And (IIRC, this may not be canonically correct) if you don't go like Marena from KOC and make your Tell something obvious like a pair of fox ears and a tail, even someone who notices it doesn't necessarily think there's anything supernatural about it. They just notice something about you they might recognize in another form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:50:53-07:00","id":229349,"title":"","content":"No, you're not wrong there. Nothing about the tell explicity says: LUNAR HERE. There's mutants and such in setting, so it's not impossible to be mistaken for one of those...but that does have it's own problems and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:53:46-07:00","id":229354,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's entirely possible that the character is a descendent of a beastman, or of a bestial god / demon / elemental, or was otherwise endowed by some such god, etc.<br /> Though I gotta admit, I also missed that part where it's actually NMI, my circle always played it as UMI (though honestly 1e Lunar tell rules were a lot more usable imo. Spending motes on an Integrity Excellency should not auto-detect the tell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 08-15-2014, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:56:16-07:00","id":229357,"title":"","content":"Which is all sorts of ironic, really. SOMETHING of 1ed Lunars being better then 2ed!? I think that's the only thing!<br /> <br /> (Fucking charmclouds still give me nightmares)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:57:36-07:00","id":229360,"title":"","content":"Personally I found 1e's DBT rules much more fun than picking out a few Mutations. It was broken for sure, but hella fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:02:22-07:00","id":229365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229360#post229360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I found 1e's DBT rules much more fun than picking out a few Mutations. It was broken for sure, but hella fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, honistly, I agree. It was super fun. But for people that never played it, we really have to say HOW broken. It was triveal to make a never-die lunar.<br /> <br /> Which is why I have to keep it in the box of doesn't work as well as 2ed, sadly enough. Plus, yanno, it was also super-mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:03:21-07:00","id":229367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229113#post229113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know, even though I find myself doubting that what's wrong with the Lunars in the next Edition will be a condition of extensive exposure to the Wyld, I still find this logic a bit dubious.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I dislike looking on the Essences as something designed towards tactical or functional purposes; if design enters into it, it's design towards the kind of heroes that result.<br /> <br /> That and how the idea seems to have been that the Lunars had been continuously within the Wyld for an extremely long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my problem is how suspension of disbelief is affected when you have a splat that has something that works like IPP or CRP (and IIRC Lunars do - though I could very well be misremembering). If Solars can start with IPP and can use it every day, and if Lunars have a similar effect, it doesn't make sense to me why all Lunars wouldn't develop that ability and constantly use it while in the Wyld. Obviously the notion of IPP-as-written has its own very deep problems (an E1 Charm shutting down an entire category of challenges) but if it's there but isn't used, that's nonsensical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229321#post229321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tell is...problematic, yes. It's an NMI effect that acts like UMI, and both calls and pushes away attention from itself at the SAME TIME. Plus the whole problem of there's no true way to negate it, so if someone has an illusion negator, so much for being the best shapeshifter in the setting...Luna's got you beat, and you can't ever equal her ever. Plus, as you noted, everything else that has such effects. That eclipse that just got a shift-charm from a spirit? No tell. And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even know why 2e decided to use the terrible social mechanics for the Tell. You're right, it comes across as just too complicated and overwrought. On top of everything Ejtaka said, there's also the fact that if you take the DBT enhancement Knack, it becomes even easier to spot your Tell. Ugh. Why they didn't just go for a Stealth/Awareness route over &quot;magical social attack&quot; is beyond me. That makes more sense. Also the Air-Breathing Mermaid design process proceeding into &quot;buy this Charm to hide your basically required tattoos&quot; sends me into a rage. I <i>hate</i> Air-Breathing Mermaid effects; hiding your tattoos should be a baseline power of the tattoos, because why would elder Lunars be so stupid as to say &quot;hey we need these tattoos to not go crazy and turn into piles of goo, but they're also going to be super fucking obvious to everyone, so instead of building in functionality to make them less obvious, here's a Charm you can learn for it.&quot; UGHHHHH this design","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:10:51-07:00","id":229378,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I...remember the DBT problem with the tell. It left such a bad taste in my mouth that I frankly assumed that everyone would remember it, and thus no one needed to bring it up. Better for everyone. (Compare Beast-power Concentration, that leaves you humanoid, but lowers the Tell Threshold. That is both thematic and FUN, as so far as the tell can be fun.)<br /> <br /> Just be glad that the damn tattoo charm had it's cost reduced in 2ed. 1ed? It could cost you FIFTEEN fucking XP to buy the goddamn thing.<br /> <br /> Let me repeat that. FIFTEEN. 15. XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:10:59-07:00","id":229379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229354#post229354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I gotta admit, I also missed that part where it's actually NMI, my circle always played it as UMI (though honestly 1e Lunar tell rules were a lot more usable imo. Spending motes on an Integrity Excellency should not auto-detect the tell).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is UMI, but it counts as NMI. And I'd forgotten about that line too, until I looked it up. I've always treated it as different from other UMI, but I guess I forgot the reason.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I don't think you can use an Integrity Excellency to detect the Tell. Because the mental attack is unnoticeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-15-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:15:51-07:00","id":229385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229379#post229379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And I don't think you can use an Integrity Excellency to detect the Tell. Because the mental attack is unnoticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's actually the case, the Tell itself creates a <i>ton</i> of fundamental system transparency issues that the core rules go out of their way to prevent in the combat/social combat steps process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:22:20-07:00","id":229396,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the tell fucks you over even in the metagame sense. It's a very special mechanic, that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:36:19-07:00","id":229431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229367#post229367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Solars can start with IPP and can use it every day, and if Lunars have a similar effect, it doesn't make sense to me why all Lunars wouldn't develop that ability and constantly use it while in the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have it that not even a Solar who had spent several decades or centuries in the Wyld without respite would not come away from that unscathed. Integrity-Protecting Prana is how such a scenario is even possible in the first place, as opposed to sublimating into unanchored abstractions within a few months. Such extreme exposure is operating on a level of plot just a few steps below the Great Curse, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:39:00-07:00","id":229439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229379#post229379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think you can use an Integrity Excellency to detect the Tell. Because the mental attack is unnoticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you/your ST reads the rules, and what your tell appears as -- if your character's tell is a toothy croco-smirk, complete with scales and crocodile teeth, a Solar using an integrity Exc. to bypass the MI will instantly notice it (and well, being NPCs, the ST decides that they figure out the Lunarness right away, because weird UMI/NMI rules).<br /> <br /> TL;DR: what Revan said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:40:25-07:00","id":229441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229378#post229378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I...remember the DBT problem with the tell. It left such a bad taste in my mouth that I frankly assumed that everyone would remember it, and thus no one needed to bring it up. Better for everyone. (Compare Beast-power Concentration, that leaves you humanoid, but lowers the Tell Threshold. That is both thematic and FUN, as so far as the tell can be fun.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tell can indeed be fun. The Lunar I was talking about, with the scent-Tell, this was/is his anima:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://s29.postimg.org/pvh832rhz/pedunculata.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And his Tell is its scent. I'm still playing that Lunar in a couple of games. I like being able to say the scent of moonflowers fills the room when his anima glows; I like being able to fly off in hawk shape, trailing flower-scent. The Tell can be both thematic and fun. You just need to put some consideration into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:47:24-07:00","id":229447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229385#post229385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's actually the case, the Tell itself creates a <i>ton</i> of fundamental system transparency issues that the core rules go out of their way to prevent in the combat/social combat steps process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, he's got a point. I mean, it's one thing to use, say, an Awareness Excellency on a roll to detect an unexpected attack, but the Tell is a passive thing acting against a static value. It's not even a matter of telling players they need to roll in order to see something, it would be more like &quot;hey, something's happening here, but your MDV is too low to see through it, d'you wanna spend some motes to boost it up?&quot;, which... I don't know, it would feel weirdly abrupt in a way that calling for a roll would not to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:52:03-07:00","id":229449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229441#post229441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tell can indeed be fun. The Lunar I was talking about, with the scent-Tell, this was/is his anima:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://s29.postimg.org/pvh832rhz/pedunculata.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And his Tell is its scent. I'm still playing that Lunar in a couple of games. I like being able to say the scent of moonflowers fills the room when his anima glows; I like being able to fly off in hawk shape, trailing flower-scent. The Tell can be both thematic and fun. You just need to put some consideration into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy that you've been able to enjoy it, I really am. To me, the tell is just a massive headache that's been a constant reminder of how Lunars have just been a mechanical pile of garbage in 1ed, then have no real setting place in 2ed, along with being just weak, silver solars.<br /> <br /> To call out how each part of the Tell can be mapped to other lunar problems: It's a mechanical mess(1ed reminders FUCK YOU CHARM CLOUDS) that violates a few basic system assumptions(Exaltation being involdate, their own charm of Laughing into the Teeth of Madness breaking their Exaltation), that both poorly hide themselves and try to scream out to be noticed(Both 1ed and 2ed fluff intergration. You can yank lunars and basically nothing changes, but they try hard to pretend they have an impact)<br /> <br /> As such...it's...honistly not fun for me. Just makes me wince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 08-15-2014, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:57:26-07:00","id":229455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229441#post229441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tell can indeed be fun. The Lunar I was talking about, with the scent-Tell, this was/is his anima:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://s29.postimg.org/pvh832rhz/pedunculata.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And his Tell is its scent. I'm still playing that Lunar in a couple of games. I like being able to say the scent of moonflowers fills the room when his anima glows; I like being able to fly off in hawk shape, trailing flower-scent. The Tell can be both thematic and fun. You just need to put some consideration into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I agree. The problem is when you get an ST that doesn't, and then insists to sticking with the worst interpretation of the rules possible.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is in the way MDV, Excellencies and the Tell interact. Excellencies are reflexive, and sort of instinctual, so the characters themselves don't necessarily need to be aware of the thing they're defending against for the excellency to use get used, because &quot;That zenith is just so good at integrity that nothing gets past him, his Essence invokes it automatically, blah blah&quot;. Or, at least that what ended up being argued at that point.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree with that last part (edit: of what I said, not of your post; the excellencies thing), but again, ST fiat and rules interpretation. I'd like for the Tell rules, if any, to be as fool-proof as possible when it's a defining feature of a splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 08-15-2014, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:00:01-07:00","id":229458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229447#post229447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, he's got a point. I mean, it's one thing to use, say, an Awareness Excellency on a roll to detect an unexpected attack, but the Tell is a passive thing acting against a static value. It's not even a matter of telling players they need to roll in order to see something, it would be more like &quot;hey, something's happening here, but your MDV is too low to see through it, d'you wanna spend some motes to boost it up?&quot;, which... I don't know, it would feel weirdly abrupt in a way that calling for a roll would not to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is problematic on the metagame level with the kind of system transparency the core rules have built in.<br /> <br /> It's fine to not allow a Charm or a roll to try and detect it, but that is going agains the system transparency RAW.<br /> <br /> That is a problem. It's fine if you run the game with less system transparency, but that's a deliberate choice away from the baseline rules on transparency. Either those rules need to be reworked (and I do believe this to be the case, because I think too much transparency can ruin IC moments where you shouldn't know what is going on but the rules say that OOC you have every right to know, which produces weird metagame reading-OOC-knowledge-into-IC issues) or the Tell should conform to the existing system transparency RAW, rather than providing a notable (perhaps THE notable) exception to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:42:48-07:00","id":229577,"title":"","content":"Excellencies represent deliberate charm use. My understanding is you can't use them in a passive sense, to defend against attacks of which you're not aware. Against an unnoticeable/unexpected attack (such as the Tell), you're forced to rely solely on static defenses and charms that explicitly allow you to use them in that situation.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's a problem. Lots of times ingame, the storyteller privately determines whether you notice something or not. If you don't notice it, he says nothing. That's one of the factors that makes a game interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:26:36-07:00","id":229628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229360#post229360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I found 1e's DBT rules much more fun than picking out a few Mutations. It was broken for sure, but hella fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Worth a reminder, a lot of mutations in 1e were also broken, straight up. Tough gave you natural lethal soak equal to your full Stamina, added on two dots of Strength and one dot of Stamina, and gave you health levels. After the player's guide came out, you didn't even need to worry about limiting your Essence from taking it, you could just spend four bonus points to get it. Get that and inexhaustible for another four bonus points, you could easily start out with natural ratings of Strength 7 and Stamina 8. It was the only way to get a significant amount of soak from Armor-Forming Technique (capped at additional lethal soak equal to half the Lunar's Stamina, making it like a limited Excellency-type effect in 2e terms)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:55:32-07:00","id":229700,"title":"","content":"Part of the core rules include the notion that if you're being affected by some power, then OOC you are aware of it so that you can choose to spend resources to resist it. You are aware when a surprise attack launches, so that your character can reflexively (and instinctively) activate a surprise-negator to protect himself. The notion is the same with social attacks - you are aware of it OOC when brainwashing magic is used, even before you have your character spend Willpower or use a perfect, because the effect can affect your character and by the RAW you have a right to counter it (though framing social interaction in the attack/defense parlance of combat - that should have been the first sign that the whole notion was fucked, when you approach making friends or persuading people in some similar manner as to sticking a knife in them. Digression).<br /> <br /> So in the game you have &quot;secret&quot; effects which can be used on your character (surprise attacks, traps, written social attacks delivered through Letter-Within-a-Letter Technique or through Charms that make the social attack a surprise), which the player is allowed <i>if not required</i> to be aware of, in order to be able to respond if they choose to do so. <br /> <br /> Unless you're not allowed to be aware of them in certain fringe cases that seem quite arbitrarily chosen. It's these cases that make statements against the core rules, which themselves are either good or ill, but value judgments aside <i>they're still the core rules </i>and for consistency's sake you should either say &quot;unless it's Obvious you have no way of knowing there is magic in that request or attack and you have to respond as you choose - usually with maximum paranoia&quot; or &quot;you know OOC everything about the attack, and if you're not worried about it IC then of course you can ignore it but the player is explicitly required to be allowed to make that decision for the character, not have a result imposed on him.&quot; The latter is the baseline rule. Except when it isn't, for arbitrary reasons.<br /> <br /> The Tell therefore wants to use the existing social combat mechanics, except it also wants to negate the portions of them that require the defender to be informed of the effects bearing down on him. Which is really fucked up: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, p. 173</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, social attacks follow the same 10 steps as normal attacks, with slight changes appropriate to the nature of such encounters. These differences are explained here, with steps not listed following the exact rules of physical combat. <br /> 1) Declare Attack: The attacker must decide the traits used for the attack. . . The declaration should also indicate the desired effect of the attack so the defender knows how to respond.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, p. 145</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Declaration of Attack: The attacker\u2019s player states that the character is attacking and what Charms (if any) he will activate to enhance the attack, excepting reroll effects. If the attack cannot be stopped by a particular mode of defense (dodge or parry), the attacker\u2019s player must include this information in the declaration.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look, I don't particularly care for the extent of these rules, but they exist. I would prefer that the OOC rules tend towards more &quot;wow, I have no idea if there's a Charm in that attack or not, so I'm gonna have to risk not deploying my own Charms to counter it&quot; (this is assuming a 3e where perfects are not spammable and are either once-a-scene type things or have a cool down) over &quot;I know everything about this attack so meh, my (M)DV can handle it.&quot; But we're talking 2e mechanics, which do require that social attacks follow the same rules. So, ok, an DMDV of &lt;12 always misses the tell...oh wait, if you're in human shape, that drops, if it's the Wyld Hunt or people alerted by the Wyld Hunt and/or who have previously seen the Lunar, it drops more...the Tell starts out by violating core transparency rules, and then it's completely shit against the people you actually might want to hide from, so it's terrible on both ends of the spectrum. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229577#post229577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellencies represent deliberate charm use. My understanding is you can't use them in a passive sense, to defend against attacks of which you're not aware. Against an unnoticeable/unexpected attack (such as the Tell), you're forced to rely solely on static defenses and charms that explicitly allow you to use them in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This requires the ST to declare &quot;something unknown is affecting you, do you want to try and counter it? It's considered surprise&quot; to which most players will say &quot;what do I need to do? I have surprise negators for physical and social combat and also perfects for physical and social effects.&quot; So you pop a Charm that negates social surprise, and then either activate a social perfect or use an Excellency, and that is that. That's the draw of transparency, <i>and I hate it</i>, but swinging on the pendulum too far the other way means your characters are killed from surprise or secretly convinced to give up their goals and live in huts, and that's bad too.<br /> <br /> Sure, you as an ST can just have notes from your players' sheets and know their capabilities, and maybe only tell them if you know they have a chance of beating it. That's not a bad idea though I think some players would really resent the rules being used that way.<br /> <br /> And deliberate use IC is completely governed by OOC decisions, which must be allowed to be informed. Characters are explicitly unaware of unexpected attacks unless their player negates surprise; however the player has a right to know they're being attacked from surprise, even if they can't or don't counter the surprise. This is a great example of the problem with couching a &quot;this thing about me resists being seen&quot; in social combat terms, because Exalted explicitly have Charms to get around that and players will use them given the chance, and that just kills everything about Lunars being able to blend in.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:38:03-07:00","id":229768,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting and unfamiliar take on the situation. I've never thought that a surprise-negating charm or a perfect defense would have any effect against the Tell, because the Tell's magical effect isn't merely surprising; it's explicitly unnoticeable.<br /> <br /> If I may ask, how do you deal with this? As a player or storyteller, when you encounter a Lunar in-game? What process do you go through, step by step?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-15-2014, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:44:09-07:00","id":229772,"title":"","content":"And that more or less sums of my hatred of the tell as a limitation on Lunars that they can't ever deflect. Because it's one big screw you to what's meant to be their biggest power, and the reason why they get so few nice things.<br /> <br /> And it works SO badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:47:25-07:00","id":229773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229700#post229700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tell therefore wants to use the existing social combat mechanics, except it also wants to negate the portions of them that require the defender to be informed of the effects bearing down on him. Which is really fucked up:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what happens when you go from trying to actually get people to spot the Tell in 1e (with Awareness rolls) and try to shoehorn in social combat resolution. The impetus behind this decision is still rather baffling. While resisting Arcane Fate with Integrity instead of Occult sort of makes sense, trying to spot a magical feature that hides itself isn't really something that lines up quite so well, as shown by the numerous exceptions to the rules that Tells have in order to function. It would probably be better to simply go back to 1e Tell mechanics, which would be quite simplified in 2e on account of DBT not being a multiple purchase affair, or amazingly overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:59:37-07:00","id":229781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229768#post229768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never thought that a surprise-negating charm or a perfect defense would have any effect against the Tell, because the Tell's magical effect isn't merely surprising; it's explicitly unnoticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's...even worse in a way. Solars (and indeed, all Celestial splats) are supposed to have Charmsets that contain a Charm-based counter for every possible negative eventuality described by the rules (Crippling, Poison, Compulsion, social attacks, etc). If you can negate surprise, but not this quality of &quot;unnoticeable,&quot; then why aren't there offensive one-shotting Charms that exploit this &quot;unnoticeable&quot; paradigm? (Personally I view that &quot;unnoticeable&quot; term as being written by someone who didn't understand Exalted's complex lexicon of terms of art).<br /> <br /> At the same time, if the Tell is so easily exploited by a social surprise negator + social perfect (which can be declared as soon as the social attack is), it really <i>really</i> sucks at its job.<br /> <br /> yeah this kind of meta-thinking is mostly inapplicable when we're talking about a Lunar PC sneaking through the Blessed Isle unless you have Peleps Deled walking around with huge passive Awareness and MDV boosting Charms on looking for hidden Anathema. The real issue it pops up is when you have a non-Lunar PC, and a Lunar PC or NPC who is trying to hide their Lunar status from them, and how trivially easy it should be to see through the Tell using the normal rules for social attacks, but also how bullshit it is for the Tell to circumvent those normal rules in a way that the system wasn't holistically designed to handle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229768#post229768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask, how do you deal with this? As a player or storyteller, when you encounter a Lunar in-game? What process do you go through, step by step?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, the only way I've ever been able to deal with it in a good way is with a degree of handwaving. Mortals can't see through the Tell even when the Lunar is in a true form, and it's come up so rarely otherwise that I've basically just had the Tell succeed or fail in a manner that would be most plot-relevant or create the most interesting scene (no, I didn't always fuck over the player, but I did intentionally cause tense situations because those should be fun - guaranteed success stops being fun after a few iterations of it and guaranteed failure is only cool if the consequences of failure are themselves fun, which is not usually the case).<br /> <br /> It's just that the mechanics as presented are such a clusterfuck that making the Tell interact as-intended within the scope of the existing rules is very difficult as it touches on the (broken) foundations of the system.<br /> <br /> As a person who enjoys simulationism (Exalted definition, as well as Forgite), and really enjoys seeing a good ruleset interact with itself (I like to play with moving parts), feeling like handwaving is <i>necessary</i> (versus doing it when I feel like it might add to the game - as a supplement to the RAW rather than as a replacement for them) is extremely unsatisfying to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:31:33-07:00","id":229804,"title":"","content":"From what I can gather, the Tell was originally supposed to be about something that you could be recognised by across forms, rather than something that gave you away as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> I mean, depending on what it was, it would possibly give you away as <i>weird</i>. But Creation is full of weird; Eos and Osseia have a guy who has white scales and red eyes and can swim super fast because he drank the blood of a certain kind of big eel. That doesn't mean you won't draw attention, or even scorn, but maybe not always a Wyld Hunt, I think. Not until somebody sees about three different animals who all have a similar uncanny trait.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if Lunars are about shaping perceptions of themselves... I wonder about them having a Charm that does a thing like in that first chapter of Harry Potter; people see an animal doing a thing that animals obviously don't do, and they dismiss that first impression because animals don't do that.<br /> <br /> Probably helps get people to overlook an animal with tattoos at least. Either that or lead people to the conclusion that some awful person tattooed an animal...<br /> <br /> Hmm, if Solars have a Bureaucracy Charm to give people the impression that they're a good merchant when they are, is it too Silver Solar for Lunars to have a Manipulation or Appearance Charm that gives people the impression that they're a good merchant whether they are or not? I dunno, it seems like it would fit with the ideas of shaping perceptions of themselves, of being tricksters, and contrasting Attribute Charms with Ability ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:37:23-07:00","id":229806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229781#post229781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's...even worse in a way. Solars (and indeed, all Celestial splats) are supposed to have Charmsets that contain a Charm-based counter for every possible negative eventuality described by the rules (Crippling, Poison, Compulsion, social attacks, etc). If you can negate surprise, but not this quality of &quot;unnoticeable,&quot; then why aren't there offensive one-shotting Charms that exploit this &quot;unnoticeable&quot; paradigm? (Personally I view that &quot;unnoticeable&quot; term as being written by someone who didn't understand Exalted's complex lexicon of terms of art).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for a start, the Tell isn't really all that hard to spot. If a Lunar is in one of her true forms, the base MDV needed to spot it is 6. Most starting characters can manage that without charms. If the person observing the Lunar is actually looking for Lunars, the base MDV is 4. It's considerably harder to notice the Tell if the Lunar is in a false shape, of course, but even then, there are applicable modifiers.<br /> <br /> Also, you can use charms to counteract it. Any charm that raises your MDV for a scene, for example, would help you spot a Tell. Also magical perception charms, like All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight, would help, depending on ST ruling. But a perfect defense or a surprise-negating charm, I've never thought those would help at all, by themselves or together, because the Tell itself isn't just a surprise attack. It's an unnoticeable effect unless you have a high enough MDV or some other magic that lets you detect it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229781#post229781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the only way I've ever been able to deal with it in a good way is with a degree of handwaving. Mortals can't see through the Tell even when the Lunar is in a true form, and it's come up so rarely otherwise that I've basically just had the Tell succeed or fail in a manner that would be most plot-relevant or create the most interesting scene (no, I didn't always fuck over the player, but I did intentionally cause tense situations because those should be fun - guaranteed success stops being fun after a few iterations of it and guaranteed failure is only cool if the consequences of failure are themselves fun, which is not usually the case).<br /> <br /> It's just that the mechanics as presented are such a clusterfuck that making the Tell interact as-intended within the scope of the existing rules is very difficult as it touches on the (broken) foundations of the system.<br /> <br /> As a person who enjoys simulationism (Exalted definition, as well as Forgite), and really enjoys seeing a good ruleset interact with itself (I like to play with moving parts), feeling like handwaving is <i>necessary</i> (versus doing it when I feel like it might add to the game - as a supplement to the RAW rather than as a replacement for them) is extremely unsatisfying to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just look at the MDV and any applicable modifiers, really. If it's not high enough, they don't see anything. But isn't that part of the fun? For me it is, as a player. I like to know there's stuff going on I don't know about. And it just makes it feel more rewarding later, when I suddenly notice there's more here than meets the eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:40:32-07:00","id":229809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revan058</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229772#post229772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's one big screw you to what's meant to be their biggest power...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Their biggest power&quot; is <i>Exaltation</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:45:06-07:00","id":229815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229804#post229804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can gather, the Tell was originally supposed to be about something that you could be recognised by across forms, rather than something that gave you away as a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's been my reading of it. As just another little detail that makes your character feel more personal and unique. The main purpose being to give your Lunar some interesting personal flavor. Not really to fuck with your shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T18:47:52-07:00","id":229818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229809#post229809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Their biggest power&quot; is <i>Exaltation</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the shapeshifter Exalted. The biggest draw of said Exaltation, that was so &quot;powerful&quot; it was demed that every other thing they could do would have to be crippled because of it. That greatest power that left them do do jack SHIT in the setting for a good 10,000 or so years, other then suck and die.<br /> <br /> What a wonderful, amazing power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","user":"Revan058","date":". 08-15-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T19:35:40-07:00","id":229872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229815#post229815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's been my reading of it. As just another little detail that makes your character feel more personal and unique. The main purpose being to give your Lunar some interesting personal flavor. Not really to fuck with your shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... from what I gather, the idea in the original book's outline was that if a Lunar stayed in the same area for a long enough time, people would become familiar with their true forms, and it would inform suspicions about or observations for them in other forms.<br /> <br /> That has its place in preventing shapeshifting from being an overpowered disguise power (particularly considering that they can get a diverse range of shapes basically for free), but I think it's mostly just about resonating with shapeshifter and similar folklore and mythology. Like noticing that somebody has a sixth finger or a monobrow and realising that they're a werewolf. Probably some other stuff that I can't recall or was unfamiliar with.<br /> <br /> How people respond to that might depend on how the Lunar has been acting, or impressions cultivated by Charms; sometimes to see a beast bearing the sign of a Lunar is a good omen, and sometimes it's a mark of dark times coming. The Haslanti are supposed to be familiar with how to recognise Gerd, and to do so is a comforting thing. It's an additional distinct way for Lunars to relate to people and be perceived; there's something about trying to read a person through the body language of an animal. And I'd be inclined to think that many Lunars assume animal forms just for the sake of it, as an expression of a certain sense of alienation, while still sometimes being close to people.<br /> <br /> And sometimes it serves as a logical way to explain why Lunars who venture too far into Realm-controlled lands for too long still need to be wary of the Wyld Hunt, despite how every one of them has notable disguise powers. And even <i>that</i> is dependent on the idea of Lunars who did something that drew enough attention for people to note down your details that they could draw later patterns from.<br /> <br /> Which might explain why more Lunars don't rampage upon the Blessed Isle; a Lunar who operates in the heart of the Realm is one whose Tell is not known, and a Lunar whose Tell is not known is one who didn't take the opportunity while in the heart of the Realm to do something that large numbers of the enemy would notice. You can't charge straight into a manse like a bull in a china shop, but you can do more subtle, careful, long term things.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't even really think of it as a balancing trade off for how easily they can shapeshift; it just shapes narratives and play experiences in a manner that fits inspiration sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:35:00-07:00","id":229899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229872#post229872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... from what I gather, the idea in the original book's outline was that if a Lunar stayed in the same area for a long enough time, people would become familiar with their true forms, and it would inform suspicions about or observations for them in other forms.<br /> <br /> That has its place in preventing shapeshifting from being an overpowered disguise power (particularly considering that they can get a diverse range of shapes basically for free), but I think it's mostly just about resonating with shapeshifter and similar folklore and mythology. Like noticing that somebody has a sixth finger or a monobrow and realising that they're a werewolf. Probably some other stuff that I can't recall or was unfamiliar with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune stories. In Japanese folk tales, foxes can take human form, but their disguise isn't perfect. Oftentimes the fox is startled by a dog, or scalded with water, and her concentration slips so that someone notices she has a tail, or something.<br /> <br /> I think your analysis is pretty spot on. It's as much a narrative gimmick as a shapeshifting mechanic. I think it's intended to help as much as it takes away.<br /> <br /> Although from a simulationist perspective, I doubt Immaculates would have much luck keeping careful record of different Lunars' Tells. Just because, I mean, it'd be like UFO sightings. False reports of anathema sightings in the Threshold must outnumber accurate ones dozens to one. Actually, Lunars themselves could easily manipulate their records if they wanted to, by staging false sightings to fill their reports with misleading information. Then the next time a particular Lunar went down to Realm territory, it'd be, &quot;Vicesh the Needle? Don't be silly. Everyone knows the Needle's eyes are bright red, and mine, as you can see, are blue.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-15-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T07:04:54-07:00","id":230152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229806#post229806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for a start, the Tell isn't really all that hard to spot. If a Lunar is in one of her true forms, the base MDV needed to spot it is 6. Most starting characters can manage that without charms. If the person observing the Lunar is actually looking for Lunars, the base MDV is 4. It's considerably harder to notice the Tell if the Lunar is in a false shape, of course, but even then, there are applicable modifiers.<br /> <br /> Also, you can use charms to counteract it. Any charm that raises your MDV for a scene, for example, would help you spot a Tell. Also magical perception charms, like All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight, would help, depending on ST ruling. But a perfect defense or a surprise-negating charm, I've never thought those would help at all, by themselves or together, because the Tell itself isn't just a surprise attack. It's an unnoticeable effect unless you have a high enough MDV or some other magic that lets you detect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It troubles me when this is basically the only &quot;unnoticeable effect&quot; in the entire game that doesn't interact with any of the given mechanics except for MDV. It's clearly making a social attack. &quot;Unnoticeable&quot; isn't a mechanical term of art in Exalted, or if it is, there's no counter, meaning a lot of &quot;unnoticeable&quot; Charm tech should have been developed because clearly it's a competency hole that does exist and can/should be exploited. <br /> <br /> And it troubles me that a Lunar walking around in human form can be spotted as supernatural so easily. If they've taken the Knack to have more DBT mutations (and why wouldn't you?), then the MDV only has to be 4 for you to be spotted. That is <i>pathetic</i>.<br /> <br /> Basically the Tell is a rules-exception, but it's also quite shitty at its own job. It sucks from both ends. It's really quite mystifying that so much suck could be fit into one effect, but there you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T07:43:01-07:00","id":230211,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think I see an easy enough fix. You know when it says the tell gets 12 auto successes? Scratch that. It gets 36.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T07:59:19-07:00","id":230218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230211#post230211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think I see an easy enough fix. You know when it says the tell gets 12 auto successes? Scratch that. It gets 36.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. That doesn't fix its weird interaction with system transparency and its non-use of clearly-established Exalted &quot;magic effect&quot; terminology though. I find that to be more problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T12:10:42-07:00","id":230415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229899#post229899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kitsune stories. In Japanese folk tales, foxes can take human form, but their disguise isn't perfect. Oftentimes the fox is startled by a dog, or scalded with water, and her concentration slips so that someone notices she has a tail, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a part of some Sun Wukong tales. No matter what form he took he always had a tail. Even when that form was Architecture.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:43:00-07:00","id":230490,"title":"","content":"So if it is natural mental influence, it can simply be negated by spending one Willpower point, right? Also, I wasn't able to find it, but there is no such thing as an 'unexpected' social attack that neutralizes your DV, is there? I sincerely hope not, because that would be extremely silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:05:00-07:00","id":230528,"title":"","content":"Spending a willpower point is a concious thing. You can't do it to negate an influence you don't know is occurring. <br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, you see [description]&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm. I spend a willpower&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;On what?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:11:49-07:00","id":230533,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like I said. The tell fucks you on a META level, it's so horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:26:34-07:00","id":230556,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that a snake with antlers is silly, and antlers on a deer should be unremarkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:30:19-07:00","id":230559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230556#post230556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that a snake with antlers is silly...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unktehi\" target=\"_blank\">Did you say something?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:38:36-07:00","id":230566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230556#post230556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that a snake with antlers is silly</div> </div> </div> </div>For all the problems with the Second Edition Tell, the book is fairly clear that details like that would be represented by markings or similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">antlers on a deer should be unremarkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I was never quite up on how physical feature Tells were supposed to intersect with the spirit shape.<br /> <br /> I assume that it's a trade off made by the fact that the spirit shape is supposed to be one upon which the tattoos are still evident.<br /> <br /> Although personally, I've got an idea for a snow leopard-totem Lunar whose Tell is in her hair; in human form, the natural white colour has streaks and speckles of black, and in leopard form you've got an animal that is actually snowy white as opposed to the mild grey colour of a natural one.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that would make more of an impression with a polar bear; a Lunar who looks like a Cocal Cola advertisement, as opposed to that mildly yellowed colour of real life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:39:41-07:00","id":230568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230559#post230559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unktehi\" target=\"_blank\">Did you say something?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That wiki is incomplete as there are numerous Chinese myths and stories about great horned serpents, although in many of those it is also an albino or white serpent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:42:46-07:00","id":230569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229053#post229053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The badly-transplanted, terribly-implemented Werewolf Renown system shit can stay out too.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To explain, I fucking <i>love </i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse. It's one of my favorite games to play and run, if not my favorite, and the only reason I don't play it more than Exalted is more of my gaming friends prefer the themes to Exalted over Werewolf. I like the Renown system in Werewolf just fine, and it works very well for its role in that game. That said, I don't think it has any good role, and even less good execution, for Lunars. A lot of the 1e Silver Pact stuff (which was largely pasted into 2e) was inspired heavily by the Garou Nation in OWoD Werewolf, and it shows - it just doesn't work for Lunars, because Exalted is not telling the same story as Werewolf, and the community of Lunars is not at all similar to the Garou Nation in purpose, outlook, goal or even theme (aside from being made up of shapeshifters). So just drop this part, because while it makes a lot of sense in Werewolf, it makes none for Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the core problem that there are, maybe, 300-400 Lunars, tops, scattered around the <i>entire world</i>. That sort of makes the idea of a formal renown system a bit silly. A lot of Exalted books have had problems with this -- Cult of the Illuminated was written as though there was this constant influx of huge numbers of Solars into the cult, say.<br /> <br /> (Although my favorite error here was the part in 1e Lunars where the Storyteller chapter warns you that if a Lunar lives in a city, their children will probably not Exalt as Lunars. Technically true!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-16-2014, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:25:32-07:00","id":230615,"title":"","content":"The Renown concept is poorly executed, but I think there's something salvageable in the idea that Lunars utilise their tattoos as a way of conveying their life story to other Lunars, as a straightforward and distinct way for them to compare where they stand and get an idea out of what this Lunar in front of you might have to offer.<br /> <br /> The idea that when somebody looks at Leviathan, they're looking at a hundred feet of exposition about how he's wrecked some folks shit up, and that somebody is a Lunar who might want to make a deal with Leviathan...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:27:48-07:00","id":230617,"title":"","content":"Not just Renown, but Rank! They just called it Face.<br /> <br /> And required all Attributes at 3 or 4 dots at higher levels. This put lie to the desire to &quot;not want to hose ugly Lunars&quot; though having Appearance-based Charms. You want to make it to higher Face? Sorry, you just aren't pretty enough. Come back when you're the biggest, strongest, and prettiest. Then you can be the Baus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230568#post230568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wiki is incomplete as there are numerous Chinese myths and stories about great horned serpents, although in many of those it is also an albino or white serpent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without that additional support, I believe that the point is made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T16:38:56-07:00","id":230693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230617#post230617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This put lie to the desire to &quot;not want to hose ugly Lunars&quot; though having Appearance-based Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember: it wasn't about ugly Lunars, only Lunars with ugly <i>totems</i>.<br /> ...Yeah.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:12:26-07:00","id":230706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230693#post230693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember: it wasn't about ugly Lunars, only Lunars with ugly <i>totems</i>.<br /> ...Yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DMnM_cQu6Fo\" data-code=\"DMnM_cQu6Fo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DMnM_cQu6Fo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:29:19-07:00","id":230721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=228991#post228991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anybody else ever very mildly annoyed when the tattoos of a Lunar aren't consistent between illustrations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've houseruled in the past that they actually do change over time, as a kind of weird arcane poetry that writes and rewrites itself.<br /> <br /> The Face thing is useful if you're particularly well-known. For instance, a starting character whose last incarnation was famous. Other Lunars and various gods might know you before you know them. But without actual mechanics to support it, it's entirely a narrative effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:07:36-07:00","id":230820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=230569#post230569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the core problem that there are, maybe, 300-400 Lunars, tops, scattered around the <i>entire world</i>. That sort of makes the idea of a formal renown system a bit silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, that was part of my point. Maybe I should have said so explicitly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:03:23-07:00","id":231714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=229317#post229317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a natural influence. If you spot it and it lights up like a christmas tree then the storyteller is doing it <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>WRONG.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean I shouldn't play a Lunar whose spirit form is a caribou and whose tell is a shiny red nose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T12:21:39-07:00","id":231859,"title":"","content":"Lighting up like a headlight is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:25:39-07:00","id":234122,"title":"","content":"So, discussion point.<br /> <br /> Recently, John mentioned that while there would be 300 Solars and 100 Sidereals, there were <i>around</i> 400 Lunars. <br /> <br /> What implications does this have? If the number of Exaltations is variable, perhaps Lunar Exalts do not reincarnate in the same way as their fellow Celestials, and are Exalted through some other means, or perhaps there were more and an unknown number of them have been irretrievably lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:32:05-07:00","id":234129,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Solar Deliberative just never got around to counting them, or they did and the records went missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:59:34-07:00","id":234148,"title":"","content":"Or they conducted an Exalted census every ten years and the numbers fluctuated so much with Lunars that they finally asked Luna and her only response was trollface.jpg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:51:44-07:00","id":234249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234122#post234122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recently, John mentioned that while there would be 300 Solars and 100 Sidereals, there were <i>around</i> 400 Lunars.<br /> <br /> What implications does this have? If the number of Exaltations is variable</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this question:<br /> <br /> How would you ever know when the maximum number of Exalted possible are in existence at the same time?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:43:51-07:00","id":234296,"title":"","content":"Maybe the census they took on Lunars was so protean and fluid that even after taking it they couldn't figure out what the hell they just wrote down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:46:54-07:00","id":234318,"title":"","content":"Maybe there are exactly 423 lunar exaltations, but the amount of them that were flies/plants during the census made it hard to count them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:10:18-07:00","id":234350,"title":"","content":"I just see Luna telling her Chosen that a census was coming and offering an award to anyone who could dodge it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:28:10-07:00","id":234373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234122#post234122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, discussion point.<br /> <br /> Recently, John mentioned that while there would be 300 Solars and 100 Sidereals, there were <i>around</i> 400 Lunars.<br /> <br /> What implications does this have? If the number of Exaltations is variable, perhaps Lunar Exalts do not reincarnate in the same way as their fellow Celestials, and are Exalted through some other means, or perhaps there were more and an unknown number of them have been irretrievably lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that there's about 400 Lunars. Maybe 397, maybe 412, exact number isn't important. I wouldn't read anything metaphysically significant into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:41:27-07:00","id":234443,"title":"","content":"Why not? That's the fun part.<br /> <br /> For example: There's Exactly the same number of Lunars as Third Circle Demons. Nobody knows why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:47:04-07:00","id":234453,"title":"","content":"Wait, are there really 300 Solars? Or is it 150 Solars, 100 Abyssals and 50 Infernals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:50:34-07:00","id":234462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234453#post234453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are there really 300 Solars? Or is it 150 Solars, 100 Abyssals and 50 Infernals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they mean originally, pre-prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:18:18-07:00","id":234526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234453#post234453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are there really 300 Solars? Or is it 150 Solars, 100 Abyssals and 50 Infernals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The numbers I see from 2nd Ed is there are exactly 150 Solars, 100 Abyssals, 50 Infernals, 100 Sidereals, 300 Lunars, and a variable number of Dragon-Blooded somewhere between 10,000 and more than 10,000. The Solars, Abyssals, Infernals, and Sidereals are all equally divided between the five castes. Which, honestly, seems a bit silly when you think that the Abyssals and Infernals were grabbed randomly from the Jade prison, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:35:02-07:00","id":234538,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think it's ever implied that those numbers are exact. TED asked for a flat 50 because he thought the whole thing would go tits up, and the yozis would probably want an equal share each, so there probably are 10 of each type of infernal. Abyssals get the rest of whatever they nabbed, which was about a half of either what was in the prison or slightly more so it was half of the total number, it never really specifies. <br /> <br /> In practice the make up is whatever is required to make the exact combination of exalts that show up in your game possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:46:15-07:00","id":234600,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't normally make anything of the numbers being inexact, I always assumed that they were. It's only that the phrasing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hatewheel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are slightly more Dragon-Blooded. Not a lot. 100 Sids and 300 Solars, and around 400 Lunars. Exigents have similarly low numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>...suggests that of the Solars, Sidereals and Lunars, only Lunars now have inexact numbers. I'm sure I'm reading too much into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:59:52-07:00","id":234615,"title":"","content":"It feels like an interesting point. Personally, I drew more from how the number of Lunars is now (approximately) equal to the numbers of Sids plus the number of Solars. A little broad speculation went on around <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/221412-exalted-ask-the-developers-thread-on-rpg-net/page2\">here</a>, if you're curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:20:32-07:00","id":234639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234600#post234600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...suggests that of the Solars, Sidereals and Lunars, only Lunars now have inexact numbers. I'm sure I'm reading too much into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think that's accurate. 100 Sids, 300 Solars, ~400 Lunars (but the actual number is irrelevant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:37:37-07:00","id":234730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234538#post234538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think it's ever implied that those numbers are exact. TED asked for a flat 50 because he thought the whole thing would go tits up, and the yozis would probably want an equal share each, so there probably are 10 of each type of infernal. Abyssals get the rest of whatever they nabbed, which was about a half of either what was in the prison or slightly more so it was half of the total number, it never really specifies.<br /> <br /> In practice the make up is whatever is required to make the exact combination of exalts that show up in your game possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, no, its never implied... just the number repeated constantly with no suggestion that they aren't exact numbers. It's like how the Enterprise in TNG ALWAYS has exactly 1014 people on board, despite crew members with families transferring around fro ship to ship and stuff. My Creation is different than canon Creation. Always has been, always will be. When the books always say though, that there is a number of Solars, and it never changes or suggests that the number is unknown, I'm going to go out on a limb and say that in canon, they are an exact number. Maybe they aren't active all the time. Maybe some are 'missing' for whatever reason (like that guy who got stuck in Elsewhere). But canon, in 2E, was exact numbers. 1E was different (I think). 3E, hard to guess. Will there be 300 exactly, or about 300 original Solar Exaltations? Or are there roughly 300 now, meaning there were more like 700 back in the day? Just one more thing to wait to find out about in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:55:12-07:00","id":234744,"title":"","content":"That there were 300 original Solar Exaltations in 2e is indeed definite. That there were exactly 50 Infernal Exaltations in 2e is also definite. But the 2e numbers of Abyssals was presented as the Deathlords grabbing <i>around</i> half of the Solars, and then giving 50 to the Yozis, leaving about 150 Solars and 100 Abyssals. I'm sure there are places in 2e where the numbers are said to be exact. I'm inclined to discount those in favor of the ones where they're approximate. At least in 2e, the seizing of the Exaltations from the Jade Prison has never been presented as a precision affair.<br /> <br /> As for EX3, I'm not <i>discounting</i> the possibility that it's 300 Solars today out of however many originals. But yeah, &quot;300 original Solars, roughly 150 now, roughly 100 Abyssals, exactly/roughly 50 Infernals&quot; still strikes me as most likely. We'll see!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ha, my post actually <i>says</i> #666, Holden! I shall lord this over you! Literally! Both in the sense of being higher on the page and, y'know, as nalak42 notes, hamster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"Holden. 08-19-2014, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:08:59-07:00","id":234749,"title":"","content":"666 reply of the beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:42:19-07:00","id":234802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234749#post234749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">666 reply of the beast</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony being that it was said by a hamster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:26:51-07:00","id":234972,"title":"","content":"Eh, that's a mistranslation - IIRC, the real number is 6<i>1</i>6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:16:40-07:00","id":235143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234972#post234972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, that's a mistranslation - IIRC, the real number is 6<i>1</i>6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually just watching a video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UkZqFtYtqaI\" target=\"_blank\">about this very topic.</a> 666 has an interesting history. 616 is referenced towards the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:25:27-07:00","id":235145,"title":"","content":"So, the primary Marvel comics universe is the Antichrist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:48:12-07:00","id":235155,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:39:16-07:00","id":235564,"title":"","content":"That nomenclature was the doing of Alan Moore, wasn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:41:34-07:00","id":235565,"title":"","content":"666 and 616 are just the numbers you get from different spellings of Emperor Nero's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:00:30-07:00","id":235743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234749#post234749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">666 reply of the beast</div> </div> </div> </div>Your look like #661 to me. Oriares is the true devil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:16:02-07:00","id":235931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=234453#post234453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are there really 300 Solars? Or is it 150 Solars, 100 Abyssals and 50 Infernals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I take it as a shorthand for everything related to the Solars, partially because playing up that connection seems to be in the works, and partially because John vocally dislikes the term &quot;Solaroid&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Lunars, I wonder if there being more of them than Solars hints that their connection and duality is a thing of their own making, rather than a design purpose of Luna. Hence, their number is an independently derived matter.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it might suggest different qualities to what a god who has not turned away from an Age of Sorrows might contrive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T13:59:08-07:00","id":236906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1109-lunars-thread?p=235743#post235743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your look like #661 to me. Oriares is the true devil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I accept that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:12:19-07:00","id":238197,"title":"","content":"","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 08-23-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}